window.AZ305_DATA = {"version":"2026-09-23.v1","title":"AZ-305 CBT","source":"https://examcademy.com/exams/microsoft/az305","scrapedAt":"2026-09-23","questionCount":285,"translated":0,"topics":[{"en":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","ko":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","weight":[25,30],"count":93},{"en":"Design data storage solutions","ko":"데이터 저장소 설계","weight":[20,25],"count":69},{"en":"Design infrastructure solutions","ko":"인프라 설계","weight":[30,35],"count":89},{"en":"Design business continuity solutions","ko":"업무 연속성 설계","weight":[15,20],"count":34}],"questions":[{"n":1,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You have an Azure subscription.\n\nYou plan to deploy a monitoring solution that will include the following:\n\n- Azure Monitor Network Insights\n- Application Insights\n- Microsoft Sentinel\n- VM insights\n\nA single team will manage the monitoring solution.\n\nWhat is the minimum number of Azure Monitor workspaces that are required?","stemKo":"You have an Azure subscription.\n\nYou plan to deploy a monitoring solution that will include the following:\n\n- Azure Monitor Network Insights\n- Application Insights\n- Microsoft Sentinel\n- VM insights\n\nA single team will manage the monitoring solution.\n\nWhat is the minimum number of Azure Monitor workspaces that are required?","explanationEn":"A single Log Analytics workspace can collect Azure Monitor data and also support Microsoft Sentinel. Workspace-based Application Insights stores its telemetry in a Log Analytics workspace, and VM insights requires one; these services can share the same workspace when no isolation or other design constraint requires separate workspaces.\n\n**Learn more:** [Design a Log Analytics workspace architecture](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-monitor/logs/workspace-design) · [Create and configure Application Insights resources](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-monitor/app/create-workspace-resource)","explanationKo":"A single Log Analytics workspace can collect Azure Monitor data and also support Microsoft Sentinel. Workspace-based Application Insights stores its telemetry in a Log Analytics workspace, and VM insights requires one; these services can share the same workspace when no isolation or other design constraint requires separate workspaces.\n\n**Learn more:** [Design a Log Analytics workspace architecture](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-monitor/logs/workspace-design) · [Create and configure Application Insights resources](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-monitor/app/create-workspace-resource)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"1","ko":"1"},{"label":"B","en":"2","ko":"2"},{"label":"C","en":"3","ko":"3"},{"label":"D","en":"4","ko":"4"}],"answers":["A"]},{"n":2,"id":null,"type":"dropdown","topic":"Design data storage solutions","topicKo":"데이터 저장소 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"Your on-premises network contains a file server named Server1 that stores 500 GB of data.\n\nYou need to use Azure Data Factory to copy the data from Server1 to Azure Storage. You add a new data factory.\n\nWhat should you do next?","stemKo":"Your on-premises network contains a file server named Server1 that stores 500 GB of data.\n\nYou need to use Azure Data Factory to copy the data from Server1 to Azure Storage. You add a new data factory.\n\nWhat should you do next?","explanationEn":"A self-hosted integration runtime enables Azure Data Factory to connect to an on-premises file system and transfer data to cloud storage. A pipeline containing a Copy activity then orchestrates the transfer. Azure File Sync, File Server Resource Manager, Azure Import/Export, and Azure-SSIS integration runtime do not provide the required Data Factory copy path.\n\n**Learn more:** [Create and configure a self-hosted integration runtime](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/data-factory/create-self-hosted-integration-runtime) · [Copy activity in Azure Data Factory](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/data-factory/copy-activity-overview)","explanationKo":"A self-hosted integration runtime enables Azure Data Factory to connect to an on-premises file system and transfer data to cloud storage. A pipeline containing a Copy activity then orchestrates the transfer. Azure File Sync, File Server Resource Manager, Azure Import/Export, and Azure-SSIS integration runtime do not provide the required Data Factory copy path.\n\n**Learn more:** [Create and configure a self-hosted integration runtime](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/data-factory/create-self-hosted-integration-runtime) · [Copy activity in Azure Data Factory](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/data-factory/copy-activity-overview)","learnMore":[],"blanks":[{"id":"server1","labelEn":"From Server1:","labelKo":"From Server1:","options":[{"en":"Install an Azure File Sync agent.","ko":"Install an Azure File Sync agent."},{"en":"Install a self-hosted integration runtime.","ko":"Install a self-hosted integration runtime."},{"en":"Install the File Server Resource Manager role service.","ko":"Install the File Server Resource Manager role service."}],"answer":"Install a self-hosted integration runtime."},{"id":"data_factory","labelEn":"From the data factory:","labelKo":"From the data factory:","options":[{"en":"Create a pipeline.","ko":"Create a pipeline."},{"en":"Create an Azure Import/Export job.","ko":"Create an Azure Import/Export job."},{"en":"Provision an Azure-SQL Server Integration Services (SSIS) integration runtime.","ko":"Provision an Azure-SQL Server Integration Services (SSIS) integration runtime."}],"answer":"Create a pipeline."}],"template":""},{"n":3,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You have an Azure subscription. The subscription contains a tiered app named App1 that is distributed across multiple containers hosted in Azure Container Instances.\n\nYou need to deploy an Azure Monitor monitoring solution for App. The solution must meet the following requirements:\n\n- Support synthetic transaction monitoring for traffic between the App1 components.\n- Minimize development effort.\n\nWhat should you include in the solution?","stemKo":"You have an Azure subscription. The subscription contains a tiered app named App1 that is distributed across multiple containers hosted in Azure Container Instances.\n\nYou need to deploy an Azure Monitor monitoring solution for App. The solution must meet the following requirements:\n\n- Support synthetic transaction monitoring for traffic between the App1 components.\n- Minimize development effort.\n\nWhat should you include in the solution?","explanationEn":"Application Insights provides availability tests for synthetic monitoring. These tests issue recurring web requests to application endpoints to verify availability and responsiveness, and they do not require modifications to the tested application or website. This supports monitoring component interactions while minimizing development effort.\n\n**Learn more:** [Application Insights availability tests - Azure Monitor](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-monitor/app/availability)","explanationKo":"Application Insights provides availability tests for synthetic monitoring. These tests issue recurring web requests to application endpoints to verify availability and responsiveness, and they do not require modifications to the tested application or website. This supports monitoring component interactions while minimizing development effort.\n\n**Learn more:** [Application Insights availability tests - Azure Monitor](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-monitor/app/availability)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Network insights","ko":"Network insights"},{"label":"B","en":"Application Insights","ko":"Application Insights"},{"label":"C","en":"Container insights","ko":"Container insights"},{"label":"D","en":"Log Analytics Workspace insights","ko":"Log Analytics Workspace insights"}],"answers":["B"]},{"n":4,"id":null,"type":"dropdown","topic":"Design infrastructure solutions","topicKo":"인프라 설계","koMissing":true,"images":["assets/1785751601509-xbztjf2u.jpg"],"stemEn":"You deploy several Azure SQL Database instances. You plan to configure the Diagnostics settings on the databases as shown in the following exhibit.\n\n[[IMG1]]","stemKo":"You deploy several Azure SQL Database instances. You plan to configure the Diagnostics settings on the databases as shown in the following exhibit.\n\n[[IMG1]]","explanationEn":"The enabled SQLInsights log category has a 90-day retention policy and is archived to the storage account. Log Analytics workspace analytics retention can be configured for up to 730 days.\n\n**Learn more:** [Configure data retention for a Log Analytics workspace in Microsoft Azure](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/troubleshoot/azure/azure-monitor/log-analytics/billing/configure-data-retention) · [Set up diagnostic logs via the Azure Monitor REST API](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/data-factory/monitor-logs-rest)","explanationKo":"The enabled SQLInsights log category has a 90-day retention policy and is archived to the storage account. Log Analytics workspace analytics retention can be configured for up to 730 days.\n\n**Learn more:** [Configure data retention for a Log Analytics workspace in Microsoft Azure](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/troubleshoot/azure/azure-monitor/log-analytics/billing/configure-data-retention) · [Set up diagnostic logs via the Azure Monitor REST API](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/data-factory/monitor-logs-rest)","learnMore":[],"blanks":[{"id":"blob_retention","labelEn":"항목 blob_retention","labelKo":"항목 blob_retention","options":[{"en":"30 days","ko":"30 days"},{"en":"90 days","ko":"90 days"},{"en":"730 days","ko":"730 days"},{"en":"indefinite","ko":"indefinite"}],"answer":"90 days"},{"id":"log_analytics_max","labelEn":"항목 log_analytics_max","labelKo":"항목 log_analytics_max","options":[{"en":"30 days","ko":"30 days"},{"en":"90 days","ko":"90 days"},{"en":"730 days","ko":"730 days"},{"en":"indefinite","ko":"indefinite"}],"answer":"730 days"}],"template":"The amount of time that SQLInsights data will be stored in blob storage is {{blob_retention}}.\n\nThe maximum amount of time that SQLInsights data can be stored in Azure Log Analytics is {{log_analytics_max}}."},{"n":5,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design data storage solutions","topicKo":"데이터 저장소 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You have an Azure subscription that includes an Azure Blob Storage account named store1.\n\nYou have an on-premises file server named Server1 that runs Windows Server 2016. Server1 stores 500 GB of company files.\n\nYou need to store a copy of the company files from Server1 in store1.\n\nWhich two Azure services could accomplish this goal? Each correct answer provides a complete solution.\n\n**NOTE:** Each correct selection is worth one point.","stemKo":"You have an Azure subscription that includes an Azure Blob Storage account named store1.\n\nYou have an on-premises file server named Server1 that runs Windows Server 2016. Server1 stores 500 GB of company files.\n\nYou need to store a copy of the company files from Server1 in store1.\n\nWhich two Azure services could accomplish this goal? Each correct answer provides a complete solution.\n\n**NOTE:** Each correct selection is worth one point.","explanationEn":"Azure Import/Export supports importing data into Azure Blob Storage by transferring prepared disk drives to an Azure datacenter. Azure Data Factory Copy activity supports copying files from an on-premises file system to Azure Blob Storage when a self-hosted integration runtime provides access to the on-premises source.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure Import/Export service overview](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/import-export/storage-import-export-service) · [Copy activity in Azure Data Factory and Azure Synapse Analytics](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/data-factory/copy-activity-overview)","explanationKo":"Azure Import/Export supports importing data into Azure Blob Storage by transferring prepared disk drives to an Azure datacenter. Azure Data Factory Copy activity supports copying files from an on-premises file system to Azure Blob Storage when a self-hosted integration runtime provides access to the on-premises source.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure Import/Export service overview](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/import-export/storage-import-export-service) · [Copy activity in Azure Data Factory and Azure Synapse Analytics](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/data-factory/copy-activity-overview)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"an Azure Logic Apps integration account","ko":"an Azure Logic Apps integration account"},{"label":"B","en":"an Azure Import/Export job","ko":"an Azure Import/Export job"},{"label":"C","en":"Azure Data Factory","ko":"Azure Data Factory"},{"label":"D","en":"an Azure Analysis services On-premises data gateway","ko":"an Azure Analysis services On-premises data gateway"},{"label":"E","en":"an Azure Batch account","ko":"an Azure Batch account"}],"answers":["BC"]},{"n":6,"id":null,"type":"drag_drop","topic":"Design data storage solutions","topicKo":"데이터 저장소 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You need to design an architecture that captures user creation and role assignments. The captured data must be stored in Azure Cosmos DB.\n\nWhich services should be included in the design?\n\nEach service may be used once, more than once, or not at all.","stemKo":"You need to design an architecture that captures user creation and role assignments. The captured data must be stored in Azure Cosmos DB.\n\nWhich services should be included in the design?\n\nEach service may be used once, more than once, or not at all.","explanationEn":"Microsoft Entra ID audit logs can be streamed to Azure Event Hubs through diagnostic settings. An Azure Function triggered by Event Hubs can process each audit event and write it to Azure Cosmos DB using a Cosmos DB output binding or SDK.\n\n**Learn more:** [How to stream activity logs to an event hub](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity/monitoring-health/howto-stream-logs-to-event-hub) · [Azure Event Hubs trigger for Azure Functions](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-functions/functions-bindings-event-hubs-trigger)","explanationKo":"Microsoft Entra ID audit logs can be streamed to Azure Event Hubs through diagnostic settings. An Azure Function triggered by Event Hubs can process each audit event and write it to Azure Cosmos DB using a Cosmos DB output binding or SDK.\n\n**Learn more:** [How to stream activity logs to an event hub](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity/monitoring-health/howto-stream-logs-to-event-hub) · [Azure Event Hubs trigger for Azure Functions](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-functions/functions-bindings-event-hubs-trigger)","learnMore":[],"items":[{"en":"Azure Event Grid","ko":"Azure Event Grid"},{"en":"Azure Event Hubs","ko":"Azure Event Hubs"},{"en":"Azure Functions","ko":"Azure Functions"},{"en":"Azure Monitor Logs","ko":"Azure Monitor Logs"},{"en":"Azure Notification Hubs","ko":"Azure Notification Hubs"}],"slots":[{"id":"slot1","labelEn":"항목 slot1","labelKo":"항목 slot1","answer":"Azure Event Hubs"},{"id":"slot2","labelEn":"항목 slot2","labelKo":"항목 slot2","answer":"Azure Functions"}],"reuse":true},{"n":7,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You have an application used by 6,000 users to validate their vacation requests. The application maintains its own credential store.\n\nUsers must provide a username and password to access the application. The application does **NOT** support identity providers.\n\nYou plan to upgrade the application to use single sign-on (SSO) authentication by using an Azure Active Directory (Azure AD) application registration.\n\nWhich SSO method should you use?","stemKo":"You have an application used by 6,000 users to validate their vacation requests. The application maintains its own credential store.\n\nUsers must provide a username and password to access the application. The application does **NOT** support identity providers.\n\nYou plan to upgrade the application to use single sign-on (SSO) authentication by using an Azure Active Directory (Azure AD) application registration.\n\nWhich SSO method should you use?","explanationEn":"Password-based SSO uses the application's existing username-and-password authentication process. Microsoft Entra ID securely stores the application credentials and supplies them during sign-in, making it suitable for an application that does not support SAML or OpenID Connect federation with an identity provider.\n\n**Learn more:** [Add password-based single sign-on to an application](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity/enterprise-apps/configure-password-single-sign-on-non-gallery-applications)","explanationKo":"Password-based SSO uses the application's existing username-and-password authentication process. Microsoft Entra ID securely stores the application credentials and supplies them during sign-in, making it suitable for an application that does not support SAML or OpenID Connect federation with an identity provider.\n\n**Learn more:** [Add password-based single sign-on to an application](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity/enterprise-apps/configure-password-single-sign-on-non-gallery-applications)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"header-based","ko":"header-based"},{"label":"B","en":"SAML","ko":"SAML"},{"label":"C","en":"password-based","ko":"password-based"},{"label":"D","en":"OpenID Connect","ko":"OpenID Connect"}],"answers":["C"]},{"n":8,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You need to recommend a solution for generating a monthly report of all new Azure Resource Manager (ARM) resource deployments in your Azure subscription.\n\nWhat should the recommendation include?","stemKo":"You need to recommend a solution for generating a monthly report of all new Azure Resource Manager (ARM) resource deployments in your Azure subscription.\n\nWhat should the recommendation include?","explanationEn":"Azure Activity Log captures subscription-level control-plane operations performed through Azure Resource Manager, including resource create, update, delete, and deployment-related operations. It can therefore be filtered to identify new deployments during each month and used as the source for the report.\n\n**Learn more:** [Activity log in Azure Monitor](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-monitor/platform/activity-log) · [Azure Activity Log event schema](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-monitor/platform/activity-log-schema)","explanationKo":"Azure Activity Log captures subscription-level control-plane operations performed through Azure Resource Manager, including resource create, update, delete, and deployment-related operations. It can therefore be filtered to identify new deployments during each month and used as the source for the report.\n\n**Learn more:** [Activity log in Azure Monitor](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-monitor/platform/activity-log) · [Azure Activity Log event schema](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-monitor/platform/activity-log-schema)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Azure Activity Log","ko":"Azure Activity Log"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure Advisor","ko":"Azure Advisor"},{"label":"C","en":"Azure Analysis Services","ko":"Azure Analysis Services"},{"label":"D","en":"Azure Monitor action groups","ko":"Azure Monitor action groups"}],"answers":["A"]},{"n":9,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design infrastructure solutions","topicKo":"인프라 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You have an on-premises Microsoft SQL Server named SQL1 that hosts 50 databases.\n\nYou plan to migrate SQL1 to Azure SQL Managed Instance.\n\nYou need to carry out an offline migration of SQL1. The solution must minimize administrative effort.\n\nWhat should you include in the solution?","stemKo":"You have an on-premises Microsoft SQL Server named SQL1 that hosts 50 databases.\n\nYou plan to migrate SQL1 to Azure SQL Managed Instance.\n\nYou need to carry out an offline migration of SQL1. The solution must minimize administrative effort.\n\nWhat should you include in the solution?","explanationEn":"Azure Database Migration Service supports offline migration from SQL Server to Azure SQL Managed Instance and centrally orchestrates the migration process, reducing the administrative work required to move many databases.\n\n**Learn more:** [Migration overview: SQL Server to Azure SQL Managed Instance](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/data-migration/sql-server/managed-instance/overview) · [What is Azure Database Migration Service?](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/dms/dms-overview)","explanationKo":"Azure Database Migration Service supports offline migration from SQL Server to Azure SQL Managed Instance and centrally orchestrates the migration process, reducing the administrative work required to move many databases.\n\n**Learn more:** [Migration overview: SQL Server to Azure SQL Managed Instance](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/data-migration/sql-server/managed-instance/overview) · [What is Azure Database Migration Service?](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/dms/dms-overview)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Azure Migrate","ko":"Azure Migrate"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure Database Migration Service","ko":"Azure Database Migration Service"},{"label":"C","en":"SQL Server Migration Assistant (SSMA)","ko":"SQL Server Migration Assistant (SSMA)"},{"label":"D","en":"Data Migration Assistant (DMA)","ko":"Data Migration Assistant (DMA)"}],"answers":["B"]},{"n":10,"id":null,"type":"dropdown","topic":"Design data storage solutions","topicKo":"데이터 저장소 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You are designing a data pipeline to integrate large amounts of data from multiple on-premises Microsoft SQL Server databases into an Azure analytics platform. The pipeline will include these actions:\n\n- Database updates will be exported periodically to a staging area in Azure Blob storage.\n- Data from blob storage will be cleansed and transformed by a highly parallelized load process.\n- The transformed data will be loaded into a data warehouse.\n- Each update batch will refresh an online analytical processing (OLAP) model in a managed serving layer.\n- The managed serving layer will serve thousands of end users.\n\nYou need to implement the data warehouse and serving layers. What should you use?","stemKo":"You are designing a data pipeline to integrate large amounts of data from multiple on-premises Microsoft SQL Server databases into an Azure analytics platform. The pipeline will include these actions:\n\n- Database updates will be exported periodically to a staging area in Azure Blob storage.\n- Data from blob storage will be cleansed and transformed by a highly parallelized load process.\n- The transformed data will be loaded into a data warehouse.\n- Each update batch will refresh an online analytical processing (OLAP) model in a managed serving layer.\n- The managed serving layer will serve thousands of end users.\n\nYou need to implement the data warehouse and serving layers. What should you use?","explanationEn":"An Azure Synapse Analytics dedicated SQL pool provides reserved, distributed SQL compute for data stored in SQL tables and is intended for enterprise data-warehousing workloads. Azure Analysis Services is a fully managed service for tabular semantic data models and supports elastic user concurrency, making it suitable for an OLAP serving layer used by thousands of users.\n\n**Learn more:** [What is Azure Synapse Analytics?](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/synapse-analytics/overview-what-is) · [What is Azure Analysis Services?](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/analysis-services/azure-analysis-services/analysis-services-overview?view=sql-analysis-services-2025)","explanationKo":"An Azure Synapse Analytics dedicated SQL pool provides reserved, distributed SQL compute for data stored in SQL tables and is intended for enterprise data-warehousing workloads. Azure Analysis Services is a fully managed service for tabular semantic data models and supports elastic user concurrency, making it suitable for an OLAP serving layer used by thousands of users.\n\n**Learn more:** [What is Azure Synapse Analytics?](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/synapse-analytics/overview-what-is) · [What is Azure Analysis Services?](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/analysis-services/azure-analysis-services/analysis-services-overview?view=sql-analysis-services-2025)","learnMore":[],"blanks":[{"id":"data_warehouse","labelEn":"To implement the data warehouse:","labelKo":"To implement the data warehouse:","options":[{"en":"An Apache Spark pool in Azure Synapse Analytics","ko":"An Apache Spark pool in Azure Synapse Analytics"},{"en":"An Azure Synapse Analytics dedicated SQL pool","ko":"An Azure Synapse Analytics dedicated SQL pool"},{"en":"Azure Data Lake Analytics","ko":"Azure Data Lake Analytics"}],"answer":"An Azure Synapse Analytics dedicated SQL pool"},{"id":"serving_layer","labelEn":"To implement the serving layer:","labelKo":"To implement the serving layer:","options":[{"en":"Azure Analysis Services","ko":"Azure Analysis Services"},{"en":"An Apache Spark pool Azure Synapse Analytics","ko":"An Apache Spark pool Azure Synapse Analytics"},{"en":"An Azure Synapse Analytics dedicated SQL pool","ko":"An Azure Synapse Analytics dedicated SQL pool"}],"answer":"Azure Analysis Services"}],"template":""},{"n":11,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design data storage solutions","topicKo":"데이터 저장소 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You have 12 on-premises data sources containing customer information, consisting of Microsoft SQL Server, MySQL, and Oracle databases.\n\nYou have an Azure subscription.\n\nYou plan to create an Azure Data Lake Storage account to consolidate the customer information for analysis and reporting.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that automatically copies new information from the data sources to the Data Lake Storage account by using extract, transform, and load (ETL). The solution must minimize administrative effort.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","stemKo":"You have 12 on-premises data sources containing customer information, consisting of Microsoft SQL Server, MySQL, and Oracle databases.\n\nYou have an Azure subscription.\n\nYou plan to create an Azure Data Lake Storage account to consolidate the customer information for analysis and reporting.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that automatically copies new information from the data sources to the Data Lake Storage account by using extract, transform, and load (ETL). The solution must minimize administrative effort.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","explanationEn":"Azure Data Factory is a managed cloud data-integration service that orchestrates scheduled ETL pipelines. Its Copy activity can move data from supported on-premises database sources through a self-hosted integration runtime to Azure Data Lake Storage, and its pipelines can apply transformations and incremental-load logic with minimal infrastructure administration.\n\n**Learn more:** [Copy activity in Azure Data Factory](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/data-factory/copy-activity-overview) · [Copy and transform data to and from SQL Server using Azure Data Factory](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/data-factory/connector-sql-server)","explanationKo":"Azure Data Factory is a managed cloud data-integration service that orchestrates scheduled ETL pipelines. Its Copy activity can move data from supported on-premises database sources through a self-hosted integration runtime to Azure Data Lake Storage, and its pipelines can apply transformations and incremental-load logic with minimal infrastructure administration.\n\n**Learn more:** [Copy activity in Azure Data Factory](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/data-factory/copy-activity-overview) · [Copy and transform data to and from SQL Server using Azure Data Factory](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/data-factory/connector-sql-server)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Azure Data Factory","ko":"Azure Data Factory"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure Data Explorer","ko":"Azure Data Explorer"},{"label":"C","en":"Azure Data Share","ko":"Azure Data Share"},{"label":"D","en":"Azure Data Studio","ko":"Azure Data Studio"}],"answers":["A"]},{"n":12,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You need to recommend a solution that generates a monthly report of every new Azure Resource Manager (ARM) resource deployment in your Azure subscription.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","stemKo":"You need to recommend a solution that generates a monthly report of every new Azure Resource Manager (ARM) resource deployment in your Azure subscription.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","explanationEn":"Azure Log Analytics can store exported Azure activity-log data in the `AzureActivity` table and query it with KQL. The activity log captures Azure Resource Manager control-plane operations, including resource creation and deployment-related operations, enabling a monthly deployment report.\n\n**Learn more:** [Activity log in Azure Monitor](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-monitor/platform/activity-log) · [Monitor Azure Resource Manager](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-resource-manager/management/monitor-resource-manager)","explanationKo":"Azure Log Analytics can store exported Azure activity-log data in the `AzureActivity` table and query it with KQL. The activity log captures Azure Resource Manager control-plane operations, including resource creation and deployment-related operations, enabling a monthly deployment report.\n\n**Learn more:** [Activity log in Azure Monitor](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-monitor/platform/activity-log) · [Monitor Azure Resource Manager](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-resource-manager/management/monitor-resource-manager)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Azure Log Analytics","ko":"Azure Log Analytics"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure Analysis Services","ko":"Azure Analysis Services"},{"label":"C","en":"Azure Monitor metrics","ko":"Azure Monitor metrics"},{"label":"D","en":"Azure Monitor action groups","ko":"Azure Monitor action groups"}],"answers":["A"]},{"n":13,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design infrastructure solutions","topicKo":"인프라 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You have 100 Microsoft SQL Server Integration Services (SSIS) packages configured to use 10 on-premises SQL Server databases as their destinations.\n\nYou plan to migrate the 10 on-premises databases to Azure SQL Database.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution to create Azure-SQL Server Integration Services (SSIS) packages. The solution must ensure that the packages can target the SQL Database instances as their destinations.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","stemKo":"You have 100 Microsoft SQL Server Integration Services (SSIS) packages configured to use 10 on-premises SQL Server databases as their destinations.\n\nYou plan to migrate the 10 on-premises databases to Azure SQL Database.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution to create Azure-SQL Server Integration Services (SSIS) packages. The solution must ensure that the packages can target the SQL Database instances as their destinations.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","explanationEn":"Azure Data Factory provides Azure-SSIS Integration Runtime for deploying and running SSIS packages in Azure. It supports SSISDB hosted on Azure SQL Database and connections to Azure SQL Database server endpoints, enabling the packages to use Azure SQL Database instances as destinations.\n\n**Learn more:** [Create an Azure-SSIS integration runtime in Azure Data Factory](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/data-factory/create-azure-ssis-integration-runtime) · [Deploy SSIS packages in Azure Data Factory](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/data-factory/create-azure-ssis-integration-runtime-deploy-packages)","explanationKo":"Azure Data Factory provides Azure-SSIS Integration Runtime for deploying and running SSIS packages in Azure. It supports SSISDB hosted on Azure SQL Database and connections to Azure SQL Database server endpoints, enabling the packages to use Azure SQL Database instances as destinations.\n\n**Learn more:** [Create an Azure-SSIS integration runtime in Azure Data Factory](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/data-factory/create-azure-ssis-integration-runtime) · [Deploy SSIS packages in Azure Data Factory](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/data-factory/create-azure-ssis-integration-runtime-deploy-packages)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Data Migration Assistant (DMA)","ko":"Data Migration Assistant (DMA)"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure Data Factory","ko":"Azure Data Factory"},{"label":"C","en":"Azure Data Catalog","ko":"Azure Data Catalog"},{"label":"D","en":"SQL Server Migration Assistant (SSMA)","ko":"SQL Server Migration Assistant (SSMA)"}],"answers":["B"]},{"n":14,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design data storage solutions","topicKo":"데이터 저장소 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You are designing an app that will use Azure Cosmos DB to aggregate sales from multiple countries.\n\nYou need to recommend an API for the app. The solution must meet these requirements:\n\n- Support SQL queries.\n- Support geo-replication.\n- Store and access data relationally.\n\nWhich API should you recommend?","stemKo":"You are designing an app that will use Azure Cosmos DB to aggregate sales from multiple countries.\n\nYou need to recommend an API for the app. The solution must meet these requirements:\n\n- Support SQL queries.\n- Support geo-replication.\n- Store and access data relationally.\n\nWhich API should you recommend?","explanationEn":"Azure Cosmos DB for PostgreSQL is a managed, distributed SQL database based on PostgreSQL. It stores data in relational tables and supports SQL queries, while its distributed architecture supports geographically distributed deployments. The other listed APIs use non-relational data models.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure Cosmos DB for PostgreSQL documentation](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/cosmos-db/postgresql/)","explanationKo":"Azure Cosmos DB for PostgreSQL is a managed, distributed SQL database based on PostgreSQL. It stores data in relational tables and supports SQL queries, while its distributed architecture supports geographically distributed deployments. The other listed APIs use non-relational data models.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure Cosmos DB for PostgreSQL documentation](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/cosmos-db/postgresql/)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Apache Cassandra","ko":"Apache Cassandra"},{"label":"B","en":"PostgreSQL","ko":"PostgreSQL"},{"label":"C","en":"MongoDB","ko":"MongoDB"},{"label":"D","en":"NoSQL","ko":"NoSQL"}],"answers":["B"]},{"n":15,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design data storage solutions","topicKo":"데이터 저장소 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You plan to deploy an application named App1 that will run in containers on Azure Kubernetes Service (AKS) clusters. The AKS clusters will be located across four Azure regions.\n\nYou need to recommend a storage solution that ensures updated container images are automatically replicated to every Azure region that hosts the AKS clusters.\n\nWhich storage solution should you recommend?","stemKo":"You plan to deploy an application named App1 that will run in containers on Azure Kubernetes Service (AKS) clusters. The AKS clusters will be located across four Azure regions.\n\nYou need to recommend a storage solution that ensures updated container images are automatically replicated to every Azure region that hosts the AKS clusters.\n\nWhich storage solution should you recommend?","explanationEn":"Azure Container Registry geo-replication automatically synchronizes pushed container-image content to replicas in the selected Azure regions. Geo-replication is available on the Premium Azure Container Registry SKU, enabling regional AKS deployments to pull images from a nearby registry replica.\n\n**Learn more:** [Geo-replication in Azure Container Registry](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/container-registry/container-registry-geo-replication)","explanationKo":"Azure Container Registry geo-replication automatically synchronizes pushed container-image content to replicas in the selected Azure regions. Geo-replication is available on the Premium Azure Container Registry SKU, enabling regional AKS deployments to pull images from a nearby registry replica.\n\n**Learn more:** [Geo-replication in Azure Container Registry](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/container-registry/container-registry-geo-replication)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"geo-redundant storage (GRS) accounts","ko":"geo-redundant storage (GRS) accounts"},{"label":"B","en":"Premium SKU Azure Container Registry","ko":"Premium SKU Azure Container Registry"},{"label":"C","en":"Azure Content Delivery Network (CDN)","ko":"Azure Content Delivery Network (CDN)"},{"label":"D","en":"Azure Cache for Redis","ko":"Azure Cache for Redis"}],"answers":["B"]},{"n":16,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design infrastructure solutions","topicKo":"인프라 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You must recommend a solution that satisfies App1's data requirements.\n\nWhat should be deployed to every availability zone that hosts an App1 instance?","stemKo":"You must recommend a solution that satisfies App1's data requirements.\n\nWhat should be deployed to every availability zone that hosts an App1 instance?","explanationEn":"Azure Cosmos DB multi-region writes provides active-active writes and reads across the configured regions, so application instances can use a local writable database endpoint while Cosmos DB replicates the data globally. GZRS is a replication setting for one Azure Storage account, not a separate data service deployed into each availability zone.\n\n**Learn more:** [Distribute Data Globally - Azure Cosmos DB](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/cosmos-db/distribute-data-globally) · [Data redundancy - Azure Storage](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/common/storage-redundancy)","explanationKo":"Azure Cosmos DB multi-region writes provides active-active writes and reads across the configured regions, so application instances can use a local writable database endpoint while Cosmos DB replicates the data globally. GZRS is a replication setting for one Azure Storage account, not a separate data service deployed into each availability zone.\n\n**Learn more:** [Distribute Data Globally - Azure Cosmos DB](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/cosmos-db/distribute-data-globally) · [Data redundancy - Azure Storage](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/common/storage-redundancy)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"an Azure Cosmos DB that uses multi-region writes","ko":"an Azure Cosmos DB that uses multi-region writes"},{"label":"B","en":"an Azure Data Lake store that uses geo-zone-redundant storage (GZRS)","ko":"an Azure Data Lake store that uses geo-zone-redundant storage (GZRS)"},{"label":"C","en":"an Azure Storage account that uses geo-zone-redundant storage (GZRS)","ko":"an Azure Storage account that uses geo-zone-redundant storage (GZRS)"}],"answers":["A"]},{"n":17,"id":null,"type":"dropdown","topic":"Design infrastructure solutions","topicKo":"인프라 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You are building a multi-tier application named App1 to run on Azure virtual machines. App1 reaches peak utilization from 8 AM to 9 AM and from 4 PM to 5 PM on weekdays.\n\nDeploy infrastructure for App1 that meets these requirements:\n\n- Support virtual machines deployed across four availability zones in two Azure regions.\n- Reduce costs by accumulating CPU credits during low-utilization periods.\n\nWhat is the minimum number of virtual networks to deploy, and which virtual machine size should be used?","stemKo":"You are building a multi-tier application named App1 to run on Azure virtual machines. App1 reaches peak utilization from 8 AM to 9 AM and from 4 PM to 5 PM on weekdays.\n\nDeploy infrastructure for App1 that meets these requirements:\n\n- Support virtual machines deployed across four availability zones in two Azure regions.\n- Reduce costs by accumulating CPU credits during low-utilization periods.\n\nWhat is the minimum number of virtual networks to deploy, and which virtual machine size should be used?","explanationEn":"A virtual network and its subnets span availability zones within one Azure region, so deployment in two regions requires at least two virtual networks. Azure B-series VMs accrue CPU credits below the base CPU performance threshold and use them for higher CPU demand, making them suitable for intermittent peaks.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure virtual network overview](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/virtual-network/virtual-networks-overview) · [B family VM size series](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/virtual-machines/sizes/general-purpose/b-family)","explanationKo":"A virtual network and its subnets span availability zones within one Azure region, so deployment in two regions requires at least two virtual networks. Azure B-series VMs accrue CPU credits below the base CPU performance threshold and use them for higher CPU demand, making them suitable for intermittent peaks.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure virtual network overview](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/virtual-network/virtual-networks-overview) · [B family VM size series](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/virtual-machines/sizes/general-purpose/b-family)","learnMore":[],"blanks":[{"id":"virtual_networks","labelEn":"Number of virtual networks:","labelKo":"Number of virtual networks:","options":[{"en":"1","ko":"1"},{"en":"2","ko":"2"},{"en":"3","ko":"3"},{"en":"4","ko":"4"}],"answer":"2"},{"id":"virtual_machine_size","labelEn":"Virtual machine size:","labelKo":"Virtual machine size:","options":[{"en":"A-Series","ko":"A-Series"},{"en":"B-Series","ko":"B-Series"},{"en":"D-Series","ko":"D-Series"},{"en":"M-Series","ko":"M-Series"}],"answer":"B-Series"}],"template":""},{"n":18,"id":null,"type":"dropdown","topic":"Design business continuity solutions","topicKo":"업무 연속성 설계","koMissing":true,"images":["assets/1783707853768-wvkhqvnf.png"],"stemEn":"You have an Azure web app named App1 and an Azure key vault named KV1. App1 stores database connection strings in KV1.\n\nApp1 performs these request types against KV1:\n\n- Get\n- List\n- Wrap\n- Delete\n- Unwrap\n\n[[IMG1]]\n\n- Backup\n- Decrypt\n- Encrypt\n\nYou are evaluating service continuity for App1. If the Azure region hosting KV1 becomes unavailable, identify:\n\n- Where KV1 will fail over\n- Which request type will be unavailable during the failover","stemKo":"You have an Azure web app named App1 and an Azure key vault named KV1. App1 stores database connection strings in KV1.\n\nApp1 performs these request types against KV1:\n\n- Get\n- List\n- Wrap\n- Delete\n- Unwrap\n\n[[IMG1]]\n\n- Backup\n- Decrypt\n- Encrypt\n\nYou are evaluating service continuity for App1. If the Azure region hosting KV1 becomes unavailable, identify:\n\n- Where KV1 will fail over\n- Which request type will be unavailable during the failover","explanationEn":"Azure Key Vault replicates supported vaults to the Azure paired region and Microsoft can initiate a regional failover. Following failover, the vault is read-only. Supported operations include Get, List, Wrap, Unwrap, Backup, Decrypt, and Encrypt; Delete is unavailable.\n\n**Learn more:** [Reliability in Azure Key Vault](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/reliability/reliability-key-vault)","explanationKo":"Azure Key Vault replicates supported vaults to the Azure paired region and Microsoft can initiate a regional failover. Following failover, the vault is read-only. Supported operations include Get, List, Wrap, Unwrap, Backup, Decrypt, and Encrypt; Delete is unavailable.\n\n**Learn more:** [Reliability in Azure Key Vault](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/reliability/reliability-key-vault)","learnMore":[],"blanks":[{"id":"failover_destination","labelEn":"To where will KV1 fail over?","labelKo":"To where will KV1 fail over?","options":[{"en":"A server in the same availability set","ko":"A server in the same availability set"},{"en":"A server in the same fault domain","ko":"A server in the same fault domain"},{"en":"A server in the paired region","ko":"A server in the paired region"},{"en":"A virtual machine in a scale set","ko":"A virtual machine in a scale set"}],"answer":"A server in the paired region"},{"id":"unavailable_request","labelEn":"During the failover, which request type will be unavailable?","labelKo":"During the failover, which request type will be unavailable?","options":[{"en":"Get","ko":"Get"},{"en":"List","ko":"List"},{"en":"Wrap","ko":"Wrap"},{"en":"Delete","ko":"Delete"},{"en":"Unwrap","ko":"Unwrap"},{"en":"Backup","ko":"Backup"},{"en":"Decrypt","ko":"Decrypt"},{"en":"Encrypt","ko":"Encrypt"}],"answer":"Delete"}],"template":""},{"n":19,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design data storage solutions","topicKo":"데이터 저장소 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You are designing an application that aggregates content for users.\n\nYou need to recommend a database solution for the application. The solution must satisfy these requirements:\n\n- Support SQL commands.\n- Support multi-master writes.\n- Guarantee low-latency read operations.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","stemKo":"You are designing an application that aggregates content for users.\n\nYou need to recommend a database solution for the application. The solution must satisfy these requirements:\n\n- Support SQL commands.\n- Support multi-master writes.\n- Guarantee low-latency read operations.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","explanationEn":"Azure Cosmos DB SQL API provides SQL-like querying for JSON data, supports multi-region active-active writes, and replicates data across regions so reads can be served with low latency near users.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure Cosmos DB overview](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/cosmos-db/overview) · [Configure multi-region writes in applications that use Azure Cosmos DB](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/cosmos-db/how-to-multi-master)","explanationKo":"Azure Cosmos DB SQL API provides SQL-like querying for JSON data, supports multi-region active-active writes, and replicates data across regions so reads can be served with low latency near users.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure Cosmos DB overview](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/cosmos-db/overview) · [Configure multi-region writes in applications that use Azure Cosmos DB](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/cosmos-db/how-to-multi-master)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Azure Cosmos DB SQL API","ko":"Azure Cosmos DB SQL API"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure SQL Database that uses active geo-replication","ko":"Azure SQL Database that uses active geo-replication"},{"label":"C","en":"Azure SQL Database Hyperscale","ko":"Azure SQL Database Hyperscale"},{"label":"D","en":"Azure Database for PostgreSQL","ko":"Azure Database for PostgreSQL"}],"answers":["A"]},{"n":20,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You have an Azure Active Directory (Azure AD) tenant that is synchronized with an on-premises Active Directory domain.\n\nYou have an internal web app named WebApp1 that is hosted on-premises. WebApp1 uses Integrated Windows authentication.\n\nSome users work remotely and do **NOT** have VPN access to the on-premises network.\n\nYou need to give the remote users single sign-on (SSO) access to WebApp1.\n\nWhich two features should you include in the solution? Each correct answer presents part of the solution.\n\n**NOTE:** Each correct selection is worth one point.","stemKo":"You have an Azure Active Directory (Azure AD) tenant that is synchronized with an on-premises Active Directory domain.\n\nYou have an internal web app named WebApp1 that is hosted on-premises. WebApp1 uses Integrated Windows authentication.\n\nSome users work remotely and do **NOT** have VPN access to the on-premises network.\n\nYou need to give the remote users single sign-on (SSO) access to WebApp1.\n\nWhich two features should you include in the solution? Each correct answer presents part of the solution.\n\n**NOTE:** Each correct selection is worth one point.","explanationEn":"Azure AD Application Proxy securely publishes an on-premises web application for remote access without a VPN. For applications that use Integrated Windows Authentication, Application Proxy supports SSO through Kerberos Constrained Delegation. The published application is created, configured, and assigned to users as an Azure AD enterprise application.\n\n**Learn more:** [Microsoft Entra application proxy](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity/app-proxy/overview-what-is-app-proxy) · [Kerberos Constrained Delegation for SSO to apps with Application Proxy](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity/app-proxy/how-to-configure-sso-with-kcd)","explanationKo":"Azure AD Application Proxy securely publishes an on-premises web application for remote access without a VPN. For applications that use Integrated Windows Authentication, Application Proxy supports SSO through Kerberos Constrained Delegation. The published application is created, configured, and assigned to users as an Azure AD enterprise application.\n\n**Learn more:** [Microsoft Entra application proxy](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity/app-proxy/overview-what-is-app-proxy) · [Kerberos Constrained Delegation for SSO to apps with Application Proxy](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity/app-proxy/how-to-configure-sso-with-kcd)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Azure AD Application Proxy","ko":"Azure AD Application Proxy"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure AD Privileged Identity Management (PIM)","ko":"Azure AD Privileged Identity Management (PIM)"},{"label":"C","en":"Conditional Access policies","ko":"Conditional Access policies"},{"label":"D","en":"Azure Arc","ko":"Azure Arc"},{"label":"E","en":"Azure AD enterprise applications","ko":"Azure AD enterprise applications"},{"label":"F","en":"Azure Application Gateway","ko":"Azure Application Gateway"}],"answers":["AE"]},{"n":21,"id":null,"type":"dropdown","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You are designing an app hosted on Azure virtual machines that run Ubuntu. The app will use a third-party email service to send email messages to users. The email service requires the app to authenticate by using an API key.\n\nYou need to recommend an Azure Key Vault solution for storing and accessing the API key while minimizing administrative effort.\n\nWhat should you recommend using to store and access the key?","stemKo":"You are designing an app hosted on Azure virtual machines that run Ubuntu. The app will use a third-party email service to send email messages to users. The email service requires the app to authenticate by using an API key.\n\nYou need to recommend an Azure Key Vault solution for storing and accessing the API key while minimizing administrative effort.\n\nWhat should you recommend using to store and access the key?","explanationEn":"Azure Key Vault secrets are for sensitive string values such as API keys. A managed identity assigned to an Azure VM can obtain Microsoft Entra tokens without the app managing credentials; grant it permission to read the Key Vault secret.\n\n**Learn more:** [About Azure Key Vault secrets](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/key-vault/secrets/about-secrets) · [What is managed identities for Azure resources?](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity/managed-identities-azure-resources/overview)","explanationKo":"Azure Key Vault secrets are for sensitive string values such as API keys. A managed identity assigned to an Azure VM can obtain Microsoft Entra tokens without the app managing credentials; grant it permission to read the Key Vault secret.\n\n**Learn more:** [About Azure Key Vault secrets](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/key-vault/secrets/about-secrets) · [What is managed identities for Azure resources?](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity/managed-identities-azure-resources/overview)","learnMore":[],"blanks":[{"id":"storage","labelEn":"Storage:","labelKo":"Storage:","options":[{"en":"Certificate","ko":"Certificate"},{"en":"Key","ko":"Key"},{"en":"Secret","ko":"Secret"}],"answer":"Secret"},{"id":"access","labelEn":"Access:","labelKo":"Access:","options":[{"en":"An API token","ko":"An API token"},{"en":"A managed service identity (MSI)","ko":"A managed service identity (MSI)"},{"en":"A service principal","ko":"A service principal"}],"answer":"A managed service identity (MSI)"}],"template":""},{"n":22,"id":null,"type":"dropdown","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You have an Azure subscription containing a virtual network named VNET1 and 10 virtual machines connected to VNET1.\n\nDesign a solution to manage the virtual machines from the internet that meets these requirements:\n\n- Authenticate incoming connections with Azure Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA) before network connectivity is permitted.\n- Use TLS for incoming connections and TCP port 443.\n- Support both RDP and SSH.\n\nWhat should the solution include?","stemKo":"You have an Azure subscription containing a virtual network named VNET1 and 10 virtual machines connected to VNET1.\n\nDesign a solution to manage the virtual machines from the internet that meets these requirements:\n\n- Authenticate incoming connections with Azure Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA) before network connectivity is permitted.\n- Use TLS for incoming connections and TCP port 443.\n- Support both RDP and SSH.\n\nWhat should the solution include?","explanationEn":"Azure Bastion provides RDP and SSH access to VMs through TLS over TCP 443 while avoiding direct public exposure of RDP and SSH ports. A Conditional Access policy targeting Microsoft Azure Management can require MFA for Azure management access, including initiating Bastion sessions. The Azure Windows VM Sign-In app is specific to Microsoft Entra authentication to Windows VMs, so it does not satisfy a solution that must also support SSH.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure Bastion RDP connections](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/bastion/bastion-connect-vm-rdp-windows) · [Require MFA for Azure management with Conditional Access](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity/conditional-access/policy-old-require-mfa-azure-mgmt)","explanationKo":"Azure Bastion provides RDP and SSH access to VMs through TLS over TCP 443 while avoiding direct public exposure of RDP and SSH ports. A Conditional Access policy targeting Microsoft Azure Management can require MFA for Azure management access, including initiating Bastion sessions. The Azure Windows VM Sign-In app is specific to Microsoft Entra authentication to Windows VMs, so it does not satisfy a solution that must also support SSH.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure Bastion RDP connections](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/bastion/bastion-connect-vm-rdp-windows) · [Require MFA for Azure management with Conditional Access](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity/conditional-access/policy-old-require-mfa-azure-mgmt)","learnMore":[],"blanks":[{"id":"vm_access","labelEn":"To provide access to virtual machines on VNET1, use:","labelKo":"To provide access to virtual machines on VNET1, use:","options":[{"en":"Azure Bastion","ko":"Azure Bastion"},{"en":"Just-in-time (JIT) VM access","ko":"Just-in-time (JIT) VM access"},{"en":"Azure Web Application Firewall (WAF) in Azure Front Door","ko":"Azure Web Application Firewall (WAF) in Azure Front Door"}],"answer":"Azure Bastion"},{"id":"mfa","labelEn":"To enforce Azure MFA, use:","labelKo":"To enforce Azure MFA, use:","options":[{"en":"An Azure Identity Governance access package","ko":"An Azure Identity Governance access package"},{"en":"A Conditional Access policy that has the Cloud apps assignment set to Azure Windows VM Sign-In","ko":"A Conditional Access policy that has the Cloud apps assignment set to Azure Windows VM Sign-In"},{"en":"A Conditional Access policy that has the Cloud apps assignment set to Microsoft Azure Management","ko":"A Conditional Access policy that has the Cloud apps assignment set to Microsoft Azure Management"}],"answer":"A Conditional Access policy that has the Cloud apps assignment set to Microsoft Azure Management"}],"template":""},{"n":23,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design infrastructure solutions","topicKo":"인프라 설계","koMissing":true,"images":["assets/1783707864292-x5ydxlmp.png"],"stemEn":"You are designing an Azure order-processing system that will contain the Azure resources shown in the following table.\n\n[[IMG1]]\n\nThe order-processing system will use the following transaction flow:\n\n- A customer will place an order by using App1.\n- When the order is received, App1 will generate a message to check product availability at vendor 1 and vendor 2.\n- An integration component will process the message and then trigger either Function1 or Function2, depending on the order type.\n- When a vendor confirms product availability, Function1 or Function2 will generate a status message for App1.\n- All transaction steps will be logged to storage1.\n\nWhich resource type should you recommend for the integration component?","stemKo":"You are designing an Azure order-processing system that will contain the Azure resources shown in the following table.\n\n[[IMG1]]\n\nThe order-processing system will use the following transaction flow:\n\n- A customer will place an order by using App1.\n- When the order is received, App1 will generate a message to check product availability at vendor 1 and vendor 2.\n- An integration component will process the message and then trigger either Function1 or Function2, depending on the order type.\n- When a vendor confirms product availability, Function1 or Function2 will generate a status message for App1.\n- All transaction steps will be logged to storage1.\n\nWhich resource type should you recommend for the integration component?","explanationEn":"An Azure Data Factory pipeline is a logical grouping of activities that can implement the branching logic the scenario requires: it can inspect the order type and use a conditional (If Condition/Switch) activity to invoke either Function1 or Function2 via the Azure Function activity, and it can log each transaction step's outcome as part of the same orchestrated pipeline. Azure Service Bus, Event Grid, and Event Hubs Capture are all messaging or ingestion mechanisms, but none of them natively performs the type-based branching and multi-step orchestration that an integration component doing this routing and invocation logic needs.\n\n**Learn more:** [Pipelines and activities in Azure Data Factory](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/data-factory/concepts-pipelines-activities) · [Azure Function activity in Azure Data Factory](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/data-factory/control-flow-azure-function-activity)","explanationKo":"An Azure Data Factory pipeline is a logical grouping of activities that can implement the branching logic the scenario requires: it can inspect the order type and use a conditional (If Condition/Switch) activity to invoke either Function1 or Function2 via the Azure Function activity, and it can log each transaction step's outcome as part of the same orchestrated pipeline. Azure Service Bus, Event Grid, and Event Hubs Capture are all messaging or ingestion mechanisms, but none of them natively performs the type-based branching and multi-step orchestration that an integration component doing this routing and invocation logic needs.\n\n**Learn more:** [Pipelines and activities in Azure Data Factory](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/data-factory/concepts-pipelines-activities) · [Azure Function activity in Azure Data Factory](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/data-factory/control-flow-azure-function-activity)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"an Azure Service Bus queue","ko":"an Azure Service Bus queue"},{"label":"B","en":"an Azure Data Factory pipeline","ko":"an Azure Data Factory pipeline"},{"label":"C","en":"an Azure Event Grid domain","ko":"an Azure Event Grid domain"},{"label":"D","en":"an Azure Event Hubs capture","ko":"an Azure Event Hubs capture"}],"answers":["B"]},{"n":24,"id":null,"type":"statements","topic":"Design infrastructure solutions","topicKo":"인프라 설계","koMissing":true,"images":["assets/1783706907793-618v3p1r.png","assets/1783706912996-v8wzw484.jpg"],"stemEn":"Your company develops a web service deployed to an Azure virtual machine named VM1. The web service enables an API to access real-time data from VM1. The current virtual-machine deployment is shown in the Deployment exhibit.\n\n[[IMG1]]\n\nThe chief technology officer (CTO) sends this email message: “Our developers have deployed the web service to a virtual machine named VM1. Testing has confirmed that the API is accessible from VM1 and VM2. Our partners must be able to connect to the API over the Internet. Partners will use this data in applications that they develop.”\n\nYou deploy an Azure API Management (APIM) service. The relevant API Management configuration is shown in the API exhibit.\n\n[[IMG2]]\n\nFor each of the following statements, select Yes if the statement is true. Otherwise, select No.","stemKo":"Your company develops a web service deployed to an Azure virtual machine named VM1. The web service enables an API to access real-time data from VM1. The current virtual-machine deployment is shown in the Deployment exhibit.\n\n[[IMG1]]\n\nThe chief technology officer (CTO) sends this email message: “Our developers have deployed the web service to a virtual machine named VM1. Testing has confirmed that the API is accessible from VM1 and VM2. Our partners must be able to connect to the API over the Internet. Partners will use this data in applications that they develop.”\n\nYou deploy an Azure API Management (APIM) service. The relevant API Management configuration is shown in the API exhibit.\n\n[[IMG2]]\n\nFor each of the following statements, select Yes if the statement is true. Otherwise, select No.","explanationEn":"In external virtual-network mode, API Management endpoints are accessible from the public Internet and the gateway can access resources in the virtual network. Azure routes traffic between subnets in the same virtual network by default. Therefore, APIM can reach VM1 and partners can use APIM’s public endpoint without a VPN gateway.\n\n**Learn more:** [Use a virtual network to secure inbound or outbound traffic for Azure API Management](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/api-management/virtual-network-concepts) · [Tutorial: Route network traffic with a route table](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/virtual-network/tutorial-create-route-table)","explanationKo":"In external virtual-network mode, API Management endpoints are accessible from the public Internet and the gateway can access resources in the virtual network. Azure routes traffic between subnets in the same virtual network by default. Therefore, APIM can reach VM1 and partners can use APIM’s public endpoint without a VPN gateway.\n\n**Learn more:** [Use a virtual network to secure inbound or outbound traffic for Azure API Management](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/api-management/virtual-network-concepts) · [Tutorial: Route network traffic with a route table](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/virtual-network/tutorial-create-route-table)","learnMore":[],"statements":[{"en":"The API is available to partners over the internet.","ko":"The API is available to partners over the internet.","answer":"Yes"},{"en":"The APIM instance can access real-time data from VM1.","ko":"The APIM instance can access real-time data from VM1.","answer":"Yes"},{"en":"A VPN gateway is required for partner access.","ko":"A VPN gateway is required for partner access.","answer":"No"}],"columns":["Yes","No"]},{"n":25,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design infrastructure solutions","topicKo":"인프라 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You are developing a sales application that will include several Azure cloud services and manage different transaction components. Different cloud services will process customer orders, billing, payment, inventory, and shipping.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that lets the cloud services asynchronously exchange transaction information by using XML messages.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","stemKo":"You are developing a sales application that will include several Azure cloud services and manage different transaction components. Different cloud services will process customer orders, billing, payment, inventory, and shipping.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that lets the cloud services asynchronously exchange transaction information by using XML messages.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","explanationEn":"Azure Service Bus is a managed enterprise message broker that decouples cloud services through durable queues and publish/subscribe topics, enabling asynchronous transaction processing. Service Bus messages can contain structured data encoded as XML.\n\n**Learn more:** [What is Azure Service Bus?](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/service-bus-messaging/service-bus-messaging-overview) · [Service Bus queues, topics, and subscriptions](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/service-bus-messaging/service-bus-queues-topics-subscriptions)","explanationKo":"Azure Service Bus is a managed enterprise message broker that decouples cloud services through durable queues and publish/subscribe topics, enabling asynchronous transaction processing. Service Bus messages can contain structured data encoded as XML.\n\n**Learn more:** [What is Azure Service Bus?](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/service-bus-messaging/service-bus-messaging-overview) · [Service Bus queues, topics, and subscriptions](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/service-bus-messaging/service-bus-queues-topics-subscriptions)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Azure Service Fabric","ko":"Azure Service Fabric"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure Data Lake","ko":"Azure Data Lake"},{"label":"C","en":"Azure Service Bus","ko":"Azure Service Bus"},{"label":"D","en":"Azure Application Gateway","ko":"Azure Application Gateway"}],"answers":["C"]},{"n":26,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design infrastructure solutions","topicKo":"인프라 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You have an Azure subscription.\n\nYou need to deploy an Azure Kubernetes Service (AKS) solution that uses Windows Server 2019 nodes. The solution must meet these requirements:\n\n- Minimize the time required to provision compute resources during scale-out operations.\n- Support autoscaling for Windows Server containers.\n\nWhich scaling option should you recommend?","stemKo":"You have an Azure subscription.\n\nYou need to deploy an Azure Kubernetes Service (AKS) solution that uses Windows Server 2019 nodes. The solution must meet these requirements:\n\n- Minimize the time required to provision compute resources during scale-out operations.\n- Support autoscaling for Windows Server containers.\n\nWhich scaling option should you recommend?","explanationEn":"Virtual nodes provide rapid pod provisioning through Azure Container Instances, avoiding the wait for the Kubernetes cluster autoscaler to deploy VM compute nodes. For Windows Server containers, Kubernetes version 1.20.2 or later is a prerequisite for this capability; it is not itself a scaling option.\n\n**Learn more:** [Use virtual nodes with Azure Kubernetes Service (AKS)](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/aks/virtual-nodes) · [Create Windows Server node pools with containerd in Azure Kubernetes Service (AKS)](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/aks/windows-containerd)","explanationKo":"Virtual nodes provide rapid pod provisioning through Azure Container Instances, avoiding the wait for the Kubernetes cluster autoscaler to deploy VM compute nodes. For Windows Server containers, Kubernetes version 1.20.2 or later is a prerequisite for this capability; it is not itself a scaling option.\n\n**Learn more:** [Use virtual nodes with Azure Kubernetes Service (AKS)](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/aks/virtual-nodes) · [Create Windows Server node pools with containerd in Azure Kubernetes Service (AKS)](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/aks/windows-containerd)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"horizontal pod autoscaler","ko":"horizontal pod autoscaler"},{"label":"B","en":"Virtual nodes","ko":"Virtual nodes"},{"label":"C","en":"Kubernetes version 1.20.2 or newer","ko":"Kubernetes version 1.20.2 or newer"},{"label":"D","en":"cluster autoscaler","ko":"cluster autoscaler"}],"answers":["B"]},{"n":27,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design infrastructure solutions","topicKo":"인프라 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You are planning to migrate App1 to Azure.\n\nYou need to recommend a network-connectivity solution for the Azure Storage account that will store the App1 data. The solution must satisfy the security and compliance requirements.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","stemKo":"You are planning to migrate App1 to Azure.\n\nYou need to recommend a network-connectivity solution for the Azure Storage account that will store the App1 data. The solution must satisfy the security and compliance requirements.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","explanationEn":"An Azure private endpoint maps the Azure Storage service to a private IP address in the virtual network, allowing traffic to reach the specific storage resource through Azure Private Link rather than its public endpoint. This provides maximum network isolation and strong protection against data exfiltration, making it appropriate for security and compliance requirements.\n\n**Learn more:** [Private access to Azure PaaS services](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/networking/design-guide/private-platform-as-a-service) · [What is a private endpoint? - Azure Private Link](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/private-link/private-endpoint-overview)","explanationKo":"An Azure private endpoint maps the Azure Storage service to a private IP address in the virtual network, allowing traffic to reach the specific storage resource through Azure Private Link rather than its public endpoint. This provides maximum network isolation and strong protection against data exfiltration, making it appropriate for security and compliance requirements.\n\n**Learn more:** [Private access to Azure PaaS services](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/networking/design-guide/private-platform-as-a-service) · [What is a private endpoint? - Azure Private Link](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/private-link/private-endpoint-overview)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Microsoft peering for an ExpressRoute circuit","ko":"Microsoft peering for an ExpressRoute circuit"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure public peering for an ExpressRoute circuit","ko":"Azure public peering for an ExpressRoute circuit"},{"label":"C","en":"a service endpoint that has a service endpoint policy","ko":"a service endpoint that has a service endpoint policy"},{"label":"D","en":"a private endpoint","ko":"a private endpoint"}],"answers":["D"]},{"n":28,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design infrastructure solutions","topicKo":"인프라 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"Solution: You use Azure Front Door to enable access to the app.\n\nDoes this achieve the goal?","stemKo":"Solution: You use Azure Front Door to enable access to the app.\n\nDoes this achieve the goal?","explanationEn":"Azure Front Door provides global load balancing across healthy origins and can route traffic to an alternative origin when one becomes unavailable, supporting regional-outage resiliency. Azure Front Door WAF also supports rate-limit rules to limit requests from clients.\n\n**Learn more:** [Accelerate and Secure Your Web Application with Azure Front Door](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/frontdoor/scenarios) · [WAF Rate Limiting for Azure Front Door](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/web-application-firewall/afds/waf-front-door-rate-limit)","explanationKo":"Azure Front Door provides global load balancing across healthy origins and can route traffic to an alternative origin when one becomes unavailable, supporting regional-outage resiliency. Azure Front Door WAF also supports rate-limit rules to limit requests from clients.\n\n**Learn more:** [Accelerate and Secure Your Web Application with Azure Front Door](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/frontdoor/scenarios) · [WAF Rate Limiting for Azure Front Door](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/web-application-firewall/afds/waf-front-door-rate-limit)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Yes","ko":"Yes"},{"label":"B","en":"No","ko":"No"}],"answers":["A"]},{"n":29,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design infrastructure solutions","topicKo":"인프라 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"Solution: You use Azure Traffic Manager to provide access to the app.\n\nDoes this achieve the goal?","stemKo":"Solution: You use Azure Traffic Manager to provide access to the app.\n\nDoes this achieve the goal?","explanationEn":"Azure Traffic Manager can distribute traffic across endpoints and route users to healthy endpoints when a regional endpoint becomes unavailable, but it does not enforce request rate limits. Therefore, it cannot satisfy the required rate-limiting, load-balancing, and regional-outage requirements as a complete solution.\n\n**Learn more:** [Traffic Manager routing methods](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/traffic-manager/traffic-manager-routing-methods) · [Control Azure App Service traffic with Azure Traffic Manager](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/app-service/web-sites-traffic-manager)","explanationKo":"Azure Traffic Manager can distribute traffic across endpoints and route users to healthy endpoints when a regional endpoint becomes unavailable, but it does not enforce request rate limits. Therefore, it cannot satisfy the required rate-limiting, load-balancing, and regional-outage requirements as a complete solution.\n\n**Learn more:** [Traffic Manager routing methods](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/traffic-manager/traffic-manager-routing-methods) · [Control Azure App Service traffic with Azure Traffic Manager](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/app-service/web-sites-traffic-manager)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Yes","ko":"Yes"},{"label":"B","en":"No","ko":"No"}],"answers":["B"]},{"n":30,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design infrastructure solutions","topicKo":"인프라 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"Solution: Use Azure Load Balancer to provide access to the app.\n\nDoes this satisfy the goal?","stemKo":"Solution: Use Azure Load Balancer to provide access to the app.\n\nDoes this satisfy the goal?","explanationEn":"Azure Load Balancer operates at Layer 4 for TCP and UDP traffic and does not provide application-layer rate limiting. A Global Load Balancer can balance traffic across regions and support regional failover, but it cannot by itself satisfy the required rate-limiting capability.\n\n**Learn more:** [Troubleshoot Azure Load Balancer limitations](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/troubleshoot/azure/load-balancer/troubleshoot-load-balancer-platform-limitations) · [Global load balancer - Azure Load Balancer](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/load-balancer/cross-region-overview)","explanationKo":"Azure Load Balancer operates at Layer 4 for TCP and UDP traffic and does not provide application-layer rate limiting. A Global Load Balancer can balance traffic across regions and support regional failover, but it cannot by itself satisfy the required rate-limiting capability.\n\n**Learn more:** [Troubleshoot Azure Load Balancer limitations](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/troubleshoot/azure/load-balancer/troubleshoot-load-balancer-platform-limitations) · [Global load balancer - Azure Load Balancer](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/load-balancer/cross-region-overview)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Yes","ko":"Yes"},{"label":"B","en":"No","ko":"No"}],"answers":["B"]},{"n":31,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design infrastructure solutions","topicKo":"인프라 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"Solution: You use Azure Application Gateway to provide access to the app.\n\nDoes this achieve the goal?","stemKo":"Solution: You use Azure Application Gateway to provide access to the app.\n\nDoes this achieve the goal?","explanationEn":"Azure Application Gateway v2 is a single-region service, so it becomes unavailable if its region has an outage. Multi-region resiliency requires separate regional gateways and a global load-balancing service to route and fail over traffic between them. Application Gateway WAF v2 can support rate limiting, but that does not satisfy the regional-outage requirement by itself.\n\n**Learn more:** [Reliability in Azure Application Gateway v2](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/reliability/reliability-application-gateway-v2) · [Create rate limiting custom rules for Application Gateway WAF v2](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/web-application-firewall/ag/rate-limiting-configure)","explanationKo":"Azure Application Gateway v2 is a single-region service, so it becomes unavailable if its region has an outage. Multi-region resiliency requires separate regional gateways and a global load-balancing service to route and fail over traffic between them. Application Gateway WAF v2 can support rate limiting, but that does not satisfy the regional-outage requirement by itself.\n\n**Learn more:** [Reliability in Azure Application Gateway v2](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/reliability/reliability-application-gateway-v2) · [Create rate limiting custom rules for Application Gateway WAF v2](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/web-application-firewall/ag/rate-limiting-configure)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Yes","ko":"Yes"},{"label":"B","en":"No","ko":"No"}],"answers":["B"]},{"n":32,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design business continuity solutions","topicKo":"업무 연속성 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You have an Azure web app that uses an Azure key vault named KeyVault1 in the West US Azure region.\n\nYou are designing a disaster recovery plan for KeyVault1 and plan to back up its keys.\n\nYou need to determine where the backup can be restored.\n\nWhat should you identify?","stemKo":"You have an Azure web app that uses an Azure key vault named KeyVault1 in the West US Azure region.\n\nYou are designing a disaster recovery plan for KeyVault1 and plan to back up its keys.\n\nYou need to determine where the backup can be restored.\n\nWhat should you identify?","explanationEn":"A backed-up Azure Key Vault key may be restored to a different key vault, provided that the target vault is in the same Azure subscription and in an Azure region within the same geography. A backup from the US geography cannot be restored to a vault in a different geography.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure Key Vault security worlds and geographic boundaries](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/key-vault/general/overview-security-worlds) · [Restore-AzKeyVaultKey](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/powershell/module/az.keyvault/restore-azkeyvaultkey?view=azps-15.5.0)","explanationKo":"A backed-up Azure Key Vault key may be restored to a different key vault, provided that the target vault is in the same Azure subscription and in an Azure region within the same geography. A backup from the US geography cannot be restored to a vault in a different geography.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure Key Vault security worlds and geographic boundaries](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/key-vault/general/overview-security-worlds) · [Restore-AzKeyVaultKey](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/powershell/module/az.keyvault/restore-azkeyvaultkey?view=azps-15.5.0)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"any region worldwide","ko":"any region worldwide"},{"label":"B","en":"the same region only","ko":"the same region only"},{"label":"C","en":"KeyVault1 only","ko":"KeyVault1 only"},{"label":"D","en":"the same geography only","ko":"the same geography only"}],"answers":["D"]},{"n":33,"id":null,"type":"drag_drop","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"Each role may be used once, more than once, or not at all.","stemKo":"Each role may be used once, more than once, or not at all.","explanationEn":"A User Administrator scoped to MarketingAU can manage user accounts within that administrative unit, including creating them. A Helpdesk Administrator scoped to MarketingAU can reset passwords for non-administrative users in that unit. Assigning either tenant-level role would provide broader permissions than necessary.\n\n**Learn more:** [Assign Microsoft Entra roles](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity/role-based-access-control/manage-roles-portal) · [How to create or delete users in Microsoft Entra ID](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/fundamentals/how-to-create-delete-users)","explanationKo":"A User Administrator scoped to MarketingAU can manage user accounts within that administrative unit, including creating them. A Helpdesk Administrator scoped to MarketingAU can reset passwords for non-administrative users in that unit. Assigning either tenant-level role would provide broader permissions than necessary.\n\n**Learn more:** [Assign Microsoft Entra roles](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity/role-based-access-control/manage-roles-portal) · [How to create or delete users in Microsoft Entra ID](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/fundamentals/how-to-create-delete-users)","learnMore":[],"items":[{"en":"Helpdesk Administrator for MarketingAU","ko":"Helpdesk Administrator for MarketingAU"},{"en":"Helpdesk Administrator for the tenant","ko":"Helpdesk Administrator for the tenant"},{"en":"User Administrator for MarketingAU","ko":"User Administrator for MarketingAU"},{"en":"User Administrator for the tenant","ko":"User Administrator for the tenant"}],"slots":[{"id":"user1","labelEn":"User1:","labelKo":"User1:","answer":"User Administrator for MarketingAU"},{"id":"user2","labelEn":"User2:","labelKo":"User2:","answer":"Helpdesk Administrator for MarketingAU"}],"reuse":true},{"n":34,"id":null,"type":"dropdown","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You must ensure that users who manage the production environment are registered for Azure MFA and must use Azure MFA when signing in to the Azure portal. The solution must meet the authentication and authorization requirements.\n\nWhat should you do?","stemKo":"You must ensure that users who manage the production environment are registered for Azure MFA and must use Azure MFA when signing in to the Azure portal. The solution must meet the authentication and authorization requirements.\n\nWhat should you do?","explanationEn":"Azure AD Identity Protection's MFA registration policy requires selected users to register for Azure MFA. A Conditional Access policy enforces MFA through its grant controls by requiring multifactor authentication; session controls and a sign-in risk policy do not provide that general Azure portal MFA requirement.\n\n**Learn more:** [Configure the multifactor authentication registration policy](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/id-protection/howto-identity-protection-configure-mfa-policy) · [How to Configure Grant Controls in Microsoft Entra](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity/conditional-access/concept-conditional-access-grant)","explanationKo":"Azure AD Identity Protection's MFA registration policy requires selected users to register for Azure MFA. A Conditional Access policy enforces MFA through its grant controls by requiring multifactor authentication; session controls and a sign-in risk policy do not provide that general Azure portal MFA requirement.\n\n**Learn more:** [Configure the multifactor authentication registration policy](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/id-protection/howto-identity-protection-configure-mfa-policy) · [How to Configure Grant Controls in Microsoft Entra](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity/conditional-access/concept-conditional-access-grant)","learnMore":[],"blanks":[{"id":"registration","labelEn":"To register the users for Azure MFA, use:","labelKo":"To register the users for Azure MFA, use:","options":[{"en":"Azure AD Identity Protection","ko":"Azure AD Identity Protection"},{"en":"Security defaults in Azure AD","ko":"Security defaults in Azure AD"},{"en":"Azure AD authentication methods policy","ko":"Azure AD authentication methods policy"}],"answer":"Azure AD Identity Protection"},{"id":"enforcement","labelEn":"To enforce Azure MFA authentication, configure:","labelKo":"To enforce Azure MFA authentication, configure:","options":[{"en":"Grant control in capolicy1","ko":"Grant control in capolicy1"},{"en":"Session control in capolicy1","ko":"Session control in capolicy1"},{"en":"Sign-in risk policy in Azure AD Identity Protection for the Litware.com.tenant","ko":"Sign-in risk policy in Azure AD Identity Protection for the Litware.com.tenant"}],"answer":"Grant control in capolicy1"}],"template":""},{"n":35,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design data storage solutions","topicKo":"데이터 저장소 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You intend to use an Azure Storage account to store data assets.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that satisfies these requirements:\n\n- Supports immutable storage\n- Prevents anonymous access to the storage account\n- Supports access control list (ACL)-based Azure AD permissions\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","stemKo":"You intend to use an Azure Storage account to store data assets.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that satisfies these requirements:\n\n- Supports immutable storage\n- Prevents anonymous access to the storage account\n- Supports access control list (ACL)-based Azure AD permissions\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","explanationEn":"Azure Data Lake Storage provides hierarchical namespace-based ACLs for Microsoft Entra ID users, groups, service principals, and managed identities. It also supports container-level immutable WORM policies, while anonymous blob access can be disabled at the underlying storage-account level.\n\n**Learn more:** [Access control model in Azure Data Lake Storage](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/blobs/data-lake-storage-access-control-model) · [Overview of immutable storage for blob data](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/blobs/immutable-storage-overview)","explanationKo":"Azure Data Lake Storage provides hierarchical namespace-based ACLs for Microsoft Entra ID users, groups, service principals, and managed identities. It also supports container-level immutable WORM policies, while anonymous blob access can be disabled at the underlying storage-account level.\n\n**Learn more:** [Access control model in Azure Data Lake Storage](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/blobs/data-lake-storage-access-control-model) · [Overview of immutable storage for blob data](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/blobs/immutable-storage-overview)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Azure Files","ko":"Azure Files"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure Data Lake Storage","ko":"Azure Data Lake Storage"},{"label":"C","en":"Azure NetApp Files","ko":"Azure NetApp Files"},{"label":"D","en":"Azure Blob Storage","ko":"Azure Blob Storage"}],"answers":["B"]},{"n":36,"id":null,"type":"drag_drop","topic":"Design infrastructure solutions","topicKo":"인프라 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You plan to deploy an infrastructure solution with the following configurations:\n\n- External users will access the infrastructure by using Azure Front Door.\n- Azure API Management will control external-user access to the backend APIs hosted in Azure Kubernetes Service (AKS).\n- External users will authenticate through an Azure AD B2C tenant that uses OpenID Connect-based federation with a third-party identity provider.\n\nWhich function does each service provide? Each function may be used once, more than once, or not at all.","stemKo":"You plan to deploy an infrastructure solution with the following configurations:\n\n- External users will access the infrastructure by using Azure Front Door.\n- Azure API Management will control external-user access to the backend APIs hosted in Azure Kubernetes Service (AKS).\n- External users will authenticate through an Azure AD B2C tenant that uses OpenID Connect-based federation with a third-party identity provider.\n\nWhich function does each service provide? Each function may be used once, more than once, or not at all.","explanationEn":"Azure Front Door WAF provides managed protection against common web and API vulnerabilities, including OWASP rules. Azure API Management can use the `validate-jwt` policy to enforce the existence and validity of JWTs issued by Azure AD B2C before requests reach AKS-hosted backend APIs.\n\n**Learn more:** [Web Application Firewall (WAF) on Azure Front Door](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/frontdoor/web-application-firewall) · [Azure API Management policy reference - validate-jwt](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/api-management/validate-jwt-policy)","explanationKo":"Azure Front Door WAF provides managed protection against common web and API vulnerabilities, including OWASP rules. Azure API Management can use the `validate-jwt` policy to enforce the existence and validity of JWTs issued by Azure AD B2C before requests reach AKS-hosted backend APIs.\n\n**Learn more:** [Web Application Firewall (WAF) on Azure Front Door](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/frontdoor/web-application-firewall) · [Azure API Management policy reference - validate-jwt](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/api-management/validate-jwt-policy)","learnMore":[],"items":[{"en":"Protection against Open Web Application Security Project (OWASP) vulnerabilities","ko":"Protection against Open Web Application Security Project (OWASP) vulnerabilities"},{"en":"IP filtering on a per-API level","ko":"IP filtering on a per-API level"},{"en":"Validation of Azure B2C JSON Web Tokens (JWTs)","ko":"Validation of Azure B2C JSON Web Tokens (JWTs)"}],"slots":[{"id":"front_door","labelEn":"Front Door:","labelKo":"Front Door:","answer":"Protection against Open Web Application Security Project (OWASP) vulnerabilities"},{"id":"api_management","labelEn":"API Management:","labelKo":"API Management:","answer":"Validation of Azure B2C JSON Web Tokens (JWTs)"}],"reuse":true},{"n":37,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design infrastructure solutions","topicKo":"인프라 설계","koMissing":true,"images":["assets/1783708076038-t2wxlutj.png"],"stemEn":"You are designing a solution that computes 3D geometry from height-map data.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that meets these requirements:\n\n- Performs calculations in Azure.\n- Ensures each node can communicate data with every other node.\n- Maximizes the number of nodes calculating multiple scenes as quickly as possible.\n- Minimizes implementation effort.\n\n[[IMG1]]\n\nWhich two actions should be included in the recommendation? Each correct answer presents part of the solution.\n\nNOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.","stemKo":"You are designing a solution that computes 3D geometry from height-map data.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that meets these requirements:\n\n- Performs calculations in Azure.\n- Ensures each node can communicate data with every other node.\n- Maximizes the number of nodes calculating multiple scenes as quickly as possible.\n- Minimizes implementation effort.\n\n[[IMG1]]\n\nWhich two actions should be included in the recommendation? Each correct answer presents part of the solution.\n\nNOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.","explanationEn":"Azure Batch provides managed pools of compute nodes for parallel workloads and supports inter-node communication within a pool. Enabling parallel task execution allows multiple tasks to run concurrently on each compute node; Microsoft specifically identifies this as a way to mitigate the node limit that applies when inter-node communication is required, increasing the number of tasks that can run simultaneously while avoiding the effort of building and managing a custom render farm.\n\n**Learn more:** [Run tasks concurrently to maximize usage of Batch compute nodes](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/batch/batch-parallel-node-tasks) · [Nodes and pools in Azure Batch](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/batch/nodes-and-pools)","explanationKo":"Azure Batch provides managed pools of compute nodes for parallel workloads and supports inter-node communication within a pool. Enabling parallel task execution allows multiple tasks to run concurrently on each compute node; Microsoft specifically identifies this as a way to mitigate the node limit that applies when inter-node communication is required, increasing the number of tasks that can run simultaneously while avoiding the effort of building and managing a custom render farm.\n\n**Learn more:** [Run tasks concurrently to maximize usage of Batch compute nodes](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/batch/batch-parallel-node-tasks) · [Nodes and pools in Azure Batch](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/batch/nodes-and-pools)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Enable parallel file systems on Azure.","ko":"Enable parallel file systems on Azure."},{"label":"B","en":"Create a render farm that uses virtual machines.","ko":"Create a render farm that uses virtual machines."},{"label":"C","en":"Create a render farm that uses virtual machine scale sets.","ko":"Create a render farm that uses virtual machine scale sets."},{"label":"D","en":"Create a render farm that uses Azure Batch.","ko":"Create a render farm that uses Azure Batch."},{"label":"E","en":"Enable parallel task execution on compute nodes.","ko":"Enable parallel task execution on compute nodes."}],"answers":["DE"]},{"n":38,"id":null,"type":"dropdown","topic":"Design infrastructure solutions","topicKo":"인프라 설계","koMissing":true,"images":["assets/1785751117837-08jk3zan.png"],"stemEn":"You plan to deploy the backup policy shown in the following exhibit.\n\n[[IMG1]]\n\nUse the drop-down menus to choose the answer that completes each statement based on the information in the graphic.","stemKo":"You plan to deploy the backup policy shown in the following exhibit.\n\n[[IMG1]]\n\nUse the drop-down menus to choose the answer that completes each statement based on the information in the graphic.","explanationEn":"Azure VM Backup policies define daily, weekly, monthly, and yearly retention points. The enabled monthly retention period is 36 months, which is the longest recovery period configured. A standard daily backup schedule creates one scheduled recovery point per day, so the minimum RPO is one day.\n\n**Learn more:** [Quickstart - Back up a VM with the Azure portal by using Azure Backup](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/backup/quick-backup-vm-portal) · [FAQ - Backing up Azure VMs](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/backup/backup-azure-vm-backup-faq)","explanationKo":"Azure VM Backup policies define daily, weekly, monthly, and yearly retention points. The enabled monthly retention period is 36 months, which is the longest recovery period configured. A standard daily backup schedule creates one scheduled recovery point per day, so the minimum RPO is one day.\n\n**Learn more:** [Quickstart - Back up a VM with the Azure portal by using Azure Backup](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/backup/quick-backup-vm-portal) · [FAQ - Backing up Azure VMs](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/backup/backup-azure-vm-backup-faq)","learnMore":[],"blanks":[{"id":"retention","labelEn":"Virtual machines that are backed up by using the policy can be recovered for up to a maximum of [answer choice]:","labelKo":"Virtual machines that are backed up by using the policy can be recovered for up to a maximum of [answer choice]:","options":[{"en":"90 days","ko":"90 days"},{"en":"26 weeks","ko":"26 weeks"},{"en":"36 months","ko":"36 months"},{"en":"45 months","ko":"45 months"}],"answer":"36 months"},{"id":"rpo","labelEn":"The minimum recovery point objective (RPO) for virtual machines that are backed up by using the policy is [answer choice]:","labelKo":"The minimum recovery point objective (RPO) for virtual machines that are backed up by using the policy is [answer choice]:","options":[{"en":"1 hour","ko":"1 hour"},{"en":"1 day","ko":"1 day"},{"en":"1 week","ko":"1 week"},{"en":"1 month","ko":"1 month"},{"en":"1 year","ko":"1 year"}],"answer":"1 day"}],"template":""},{"n":39,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design data storage solutions","topicKo":"데이터 저장소 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You are designing an application that aggregates content for users.\n\nYou need to recommend a database solution for the application. The solution must meet these requirements:\n\n- Support SQL commands.\n- Support multi-master writes.\n- Guarantee low-latency read operations.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","stemKo":"You are designing an application that aggregates content for users.\n\nYou need to recommend a database solution for the application. The solution must meet these requirements:\n\n- Support SQL commands.\n- Support multi-master writes.\n- Guarantee low-latency read operations.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","explanationEn":"Azure Cosmos DB for NoSQL provides a SQL-like query language for JSON data, supports writes in multiple Azure regions, and offers an SLA-backed single-digit-millisecond latency guarantee for reads at the 99th percentile.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure Cosmos DB for NoSQL overview](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/cosmos-db/overview) · [Multi-region writes in Azure Cosmos DB](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/cosmos-db/multi-region-writes)","explanationKo":"Azure Cosmos DB for NoSQL provides a SQL-like query language for JSON data, supports writes in multiple Azure regions, and offers an SLA-backed single-digit-millisecond latency guarantee for reads at the 99th percentile.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure Cosmos DB for NoSQL overview](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/cosmos-db/overview) · [Multi-region writes in Azure Cosmos DB](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/cosmos-db/multi-region-writes)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Azure Cosmos DB for NoSQL","ko":"Azure Cosmos DB for NoSQL"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure SQL Database that uses active geo-replication","ko":"Azure SQL Database that uses active geo-replication"},{"label":"C","en":"Azure SQL Database Hyperscale","ko":"Azure SQL Database Hyperscale"},{"label":"D","en":"Azure Cosmos DB for PostgreSQL","ko":"Azure Cosmos DB for PostgreSQL"}],"answers":["A"]},{"n":40,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design infrastructure solutions","topicKo":"인프라 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You are designing a microservices architecture to be hosted in an Azure Kubernetes Service (AKS) cluster. Applications that consume the microservices will run on Azure virtual machines. The virtual machines and the AKS cluster will be located in the same virtual network.\n\nYou need to design a solution that exposes the microservices to the consumer applications. The solution must meet these requirements:\n\n- Ingress access to the microservices must be limited to one private IP address and secured by using mutual TLS authentication.\n- The number of incoming microservice calls must be rate-limited.\n- Costs must be minimized.\n\nWhat should you include in the solution?","stemKo":"You are designing a microservices architecture to be hosted in an Azure Kubernetes Service (AKS) cluster. Applications that consume the microservices will run on Azure virtual machines. The virtual machines and the AKS cluster will be located in the same virtual network.\n\nYou need to design a solution that exposes the microservices to the consumer applications. The solution must meet these requirements:\n\n- Ingress access to the microservices must be limited to one private IP address and secured by using mutual TLS authentication.\n- The number of incoming microservice calls must be rate-limited.\n- Costs must be minimized.\n\nWhat should you include in the solution?","explanationEn":"Azure API Management Premium tier can be connected to a virtual network in internal mode so its gateway is reached through a private IP address. API Management supports mutual TLS client-certificate validation and rate-limit policies, allowing the gateway to enforce both authentication and call throttling. The Standard tier’s service-endpoint connectivity does not provide the required private inbound gateway exposure; the Premium virtual-network deployment is therefore the option that satisfies all requirements.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure API Management with an Azure virtual network](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/api-management/virtual-network-concepts?tabs=stv2) · [Secure APIs using client certificate authentication in API Management](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/api-management/api-management-howto-mutual-certificates-for-clients)","explanationKo":"Azure API Management Premium tier can be connected to a virtual network in internal mode so its gateway is reached through a private IP address. API Management supports mutual TLS client-certificate validation and rate-limit policies, allowing the gateway to enforce both authentication and call throttling. The Standard tier’s service-endpoint connectivity does not provide the required private inbound gateway exposure; the Premium virtual-network deployment is therefore the option that satisfies all requirements.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure API Management with an Azure virtual network](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/api-management/virtual-network-concepts?tabs=stv2) · [Secure APIs using client certificate authentication in API Management](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/api-management/api-management-howto-mutual-certificates-for-clients)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Azure App Gateway with Azure Web Application Firewall (WAF)","ko":"Azure App Gateway with Azure Web Application Firewall (WAF)"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure API Management Standard tier with a service endpoint","ko":"Azure API Management Standard tier with a service endpoint"},{"label":"C","en":"Azure Front Door with Azure Web Application Firewall (WAF)","ko":"Azure Front Door with Azure Web Application Firewall (WAF)"},{"label":"D","en":"Azure API Management Premium tier with virtual network connection","ko":"Azure API Management Premium tier with virtual network connection"}],"answers":["D"]},{"n":41,"id":null,"type":"dropdown","topic":"Design data storage solutions","topicKo":"데이터 저장소 설계","koMissing":true,"images":["assets/1783706874506-pj4vnm6b.png","assets/1783706876779-vkp0d27r.png"],"stemEn":"HOTSPOT -\n\nYou have an Azure subscription containing the storage accounts shown in the following table.\n\n[[IMG1]]\n\nYou plan to implement two new apps with the requirements in the following table.\n\n[[IMG2]]\n\nWhich storage accounts should you recommend for each app?","stemKo":"HOTSPOT -\n\nYou have an Azure subscription containing the storage accounts shown in the following table.\n\n[[IMG1]]\n\nYou plan to implement two new apps with the requirements in the following table.\n\n[[IMG2]]\n\nWhich storage accounts should you recommend for each app?","explanationEn":"Blob lifecycle management can tier block blobs in standard general-purpose v2 and BlobStorage accounts, which makes storage1 and storage3 suitable for App1. Azure Files is available in general-purpose v2 and FileStorage accounts, so storage1, storage2, and storage4 satisfy App2's Azure file-share requirement.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure Blob Storage lifecycle management overview](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/blobs/lifecycle-management-overview) · [Azure Files deployment planning](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/files/storage-files-planning)","explanationKo":"Blob lifecycle management can tier block blobs in standard general-purpose v2 and BlobStorage accounts, which makes storage1 and storage3 suitable for App1. Azure Files is available in general-purpose v2 and FileStorage accounts, so storage1, storage2, and storage4 satisfy App2's Azure file-share requirement.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure Blob Storage lifecycle management overview](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/blobs/lifecycle-management-overview) · [Azure Files deployment planning](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/files/storage-files-planning)","learnMore":[],"blanks":[{"id":"app1","labelEn":"App1:","labelKo":"App1:","options":[{"en":"Storage1 and storage2 only","ko":"Storage1 and storage2 only"},{"en":"Storage1 and storage3 only","ko":"Storage1 and storage3 only"},{"en":"Storage1, storage2, and storage3 only","ko":"Storage1, storage2, and storage3 only"},{"en":"Storage1, storage2, storage3, and storage4","ko":"Storage1, storage2, storage3, and storage4"}],"answer":"Storage1 and storage3 only"},{"id":"app2","labelEn":"App2:","labelKo":"App2:","options":[{"en":"Storage4 only","ko":"Storage4 only"},{"en":"Storage1 and storage4 only","ko":"Storage1 and storage4 only"},{"en":"Storage1, storage2, and storage4 only","ko":"Storage1, storage2, and storage4 only"},{"en":"Storage1, storage2, storage3, and storage4","ko":"Storage1, storage2, storage3, and storage4"}],"answer":"Storage1, storage2, and storage4 only"}],"template":""},{"n":42,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design infrastructure solutions","topicKo":"인프라 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You are building a sales application that will include several Azure cloud services and manage different parts of a transaction. Separate cloud services will process customer orders, billing, payment, inventory, and shipping.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that lets the cloud services asynchronously exchange transaction information by using XML messages.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","stemKo":"You are building a sales application that will include several Azure cloud services and manage different parts of a transaction. Separate cloud services will process customer orders, billing, payment, inventory, and shipping.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that lets the cloud services asynchronously exchange transaction information by using XML messages.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","explanationEn":"Azure Service Bus is a managed enterprise message broker that decouples applications and services through durable queues and publish/subscribe topics. It supports asynchronous communication and can carry structured data encoded as XML, making it suitable for exchanging transaction data among independently operating services.\n\n**Learn more:** [What is Azure Service Bus?](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/service-bus-messaging/service-bus-messaging-overview) · [Asynchronous messaging patterns and high availability](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/service-bus-messaging/service-bus-async-messaging)","explanationKo":"Azure Service Bus is a managed enterprise message broker that decouples applications and services through durable queues and publish/subscribe topics. It supports asynchronous communication and can carry structured data encoded as XML, making it suitable for exchanging transaction data among independently operating services.\n\n**Learn more:** [What is Azure Service Bus?](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/service-bus-messaging/service-bus-messaging-overview) · [Asynchronous messaging patterns and high availability](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/service-bus-messaging/service-bus-async-messaging)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Azure Notification Hubs","ko":"Azure Notification Hubs"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure Data Lake","ko":"Azure Data Lake"},{"label":"C","en":"Azure Service Bus","ko":"Azure Service Bus"},{"label":"D","en":"Azure Blob Storage","ko":"Azure Blob Storage"}],"answers":["C"]},{"n":43,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design data storage solutions","topicKo":"데이터 저장소 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You have an app called App1 that uses an Azure Blob Storage container named app1data.\n\nApp1 uploads a cumulative transaction-log file named File1.txt to a block blob in app1data every hour. File1.txt contains transaction data only for the current day.\n\nYou must ensure that the final uploaded version of File1.txt from any day can be restored for up to 30 days after it is overwritten. The solution must use the least possible storage space.\n\nWhat should the solution include?","stemKo":"You have an app called App1 that uses an Azure Blob Storage container named app1data.\n\nApp1 uploads a cumulative transaction-log file named File1.txt to a block blob in app1data every hour. File1.txt contains transaction data only for the current day.\n\nYou must ensure that the final uploaded version of File1.txt from any day can be restored for up to 30 days after it is overwritten. The solution must use the least possible storage space.\n\nWhat should the solution include?","explanationEn":"A blob snapshot can be taken once per day to preserve that day’s final state and retained for 30 days. Snapshots are billed for unique blocks, so they provide the required daily recovery points without retaining every hourly overwrite. Blob soft delete and blob versioning automatically retain data for each overwrite, creating unnecessary hourly recovery states and using more storage.\n\n**Learn more:** [Blob snapshots - Azure Storage](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/blobs/snapshots-overview) · [Choosing between blob soft delete and blob versioning](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/blobs/soft-delete-vs-versioning-options)","explanationKo":"A blob snapshot can be taken once per day to preserve that day’s final state and retained for 30 days. Snapshots are billed for unique blocks, so they provide the required daily recovery points without retaining every hourly overwrite. Blob soft delete and blob versioning automatically retain data for each overwrite, creating unnecessary hourly recovery states and using more storage.\n\n**Learn more:** [Blob snapshots - Azure Storage](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/blobs/snapshots-overview) · [Choosing between blob soft delete and blob versioning](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/blobs/soft-delete-vs-versioning-options)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"container soft delete","ko":"container soft delete"},{"label":"B","en":"blob snapshots","ko":"blob snapshots"},{"label":"C","en":"blob soft delete","ko":"blob soft delete"},{"label":"D","en":"blob versioning","ko":"blob versioning"}],"answers":["B"]},{"n":44,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"What should the identity-management strategy contain to support the intended changes?","stemKo":"What should the identity-management strategy contain to support the intended changes?","explanationEn":"An existing Active Directory Domain Services domain can be extended into Azure by deploying additional domain controllers as Azure virtual machines in an Azure virtual network. This preserves the existing `corp.fabrikam.com` domain while providing directory and authentication services for Azure-based resources; it does not require moving all existing domain controllers or creating a separate Microsoft Entra tenant.\n\n**Learn more:** [Install Active Directory Domain Services on an Azure virtual machine](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows-server/identity/ad-ds/deploy/virtual-dc/adds-on-azure-vm) · [Deploy and manage Azure IaaS Active Directory domain controllers in Azure](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/deploy-manage-azure-iaas-active-directory-domain-controllers-azure/)","explanationKo":"An existing Active Directory Domain Services domain can be extended into Azure by deploying additional domain controllers as Azure virtual machines in an Azure virtual network. This preserves the existing `corp.fabrikam.com` domain while providing directory and authentication services for Azure-based resources; it does not require moving all existing domain controllers or creating a separate Microsoft Entra tenant.\n\n**Learn more:** [Install Active Directory Domain Services on an Azure virtual machine](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows-server/identity/ad-ds/deploy/virtual-dc/adds-on-azure-vm) · [Deploy and manage Azure IaaS Active Directory domain controllers in Azure](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/deploy-manage-azure-iaas-active-directory-domain-controllers-azure/)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Deploy domain controllers for corp.fabrikam.com to virtual networks in Azure.","ko":"Deploy domain controllers for corp.fabrikam.com to virtual networks in Azure."},{"label":"B","en":"Move all the domain controllers from corp.fabrikam.com to virtual networks in Azure.","ko":"Move all the domain controllers from corp.fabrikam.com to virtual networks in Azure."},{"label":"C","en":"Deploy a new Azure AD tenant for the authentication of new R&D projects.","ko":"Deploy a new Azure AD tenant for the authentication of new R&D projects."},{"label":"D","en":"Deploy domain controllers for the rd.fabrikam.com forest to virtual networks in Azure.","ko":"Deploy domain controllers for the rd.fabrikam.com forest to virtual networks in Azure."}],"answers":["A"]},{"n":45,"id":null,"type":"dropdown","topic":"Design infrastructure solutions","topicKo":"인프라 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You need to recommend a solution to integrate Azure Cosmos DB and Azure Synapse. The solution must meet these requirements:\n\n- Traffic from an Azure Synapse workspace to the Azure Cosmos DB account must use the Microsoft backbone network.\n- Traffic from the Azure Synapse workspace to the Azure Cosmos DB account must not be routed across the internet.\n- Implementation effort must be minimized.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","stemKo":"You need to recommend a solution to integrate Azure Cosmos DB and Azure Synapse. The solution must meet these requirements:\n\n- Traffic from an Azure Synapse workspace to the Azure Cosmos DB account must use the Microsoft backbone network.\n- Traffic from the Azure Synapse workspace to the Azure Cosmos DB account must not be routed across the internet.\n- Implementation effort must be minimized.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","explanationEn":"A Synapse managed virtual network is managed by Azure Synapse, reducing the need to deploy and maintain networking infrastructure. A managed private endpoint connects Synapse resources privately to Azure Cosmos DB through Azure Private Link, rather than exposing the data path to public internet access. Firewall rules and service endpoint policies do not create this managed private endpoint connection.\n\n**Learn more:** [Analytics with Azure Synapse Link - Azure Cosmos DB](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/cosmos-db/synapse-link) · [Create a Managed private endpoint to your data source - Azure Synapse Analytics](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/synapse-analytics/security/how-to-create-managed-private-endpoints)","explanationKo":"A Synapse managed virtual network is managed by Azure Synapse, reducing the need to deploy and maintain networking infrastructure. A managed private endpoint connects Synapse resources privately to Azure Cosmos DB through Azure Private Link, rather than exposing the data path to public internet access. Firewall rules and service endpoint policies do not create this managed private endpoint connection.\n\n**Learn more:** [Analytics with Azure Synapse Link - Azure Cosmos DB](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/cosmos-db/synapse-link) · [Create a Managed private endpoint to your data source - Azure Synapse Analytics](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/synapse-analytics/security/how-to-create-managed-private-endpoints)","learnMore":[],"blanks":[{"id":"synapse_workspace","labelEn":"When provisioning the Azure Synapse workspace:","labelKo":"When provisioning the Azure Synapse workspace:","options":[{"en":"Configure a dedicated managed virtual network.","ko":"Configure a dedicated managed virtual network."},{"en":"Disable public network access to the workspace endpoints.","ko":"Disable public network access to the workspace endpoints."},{"en":"Enable the use of the Azure AD authentication.","ko":"Enable the use of the Azure AD authentication."}],"answer":"Configure a dedicated managed virtual network."},{"id":"cosmos_account","labelEn":"When configuring the Azure Cosmos DB account, enable:","labelKo":"When configuring the Azure Cosmos DB account, enable:","options":[{"en":"Managed private endpoints","ko":"Managed private endpoints"},{"en":"Server-level firewall rules","ko":"Server-level firewall rules"},{"en":"Service endpoint policies","ko":"Service endpoint policies"}],"answer":"Managed private endpoints"}],"template":""},{"n":46,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design business continuity solutions","topicKo":"업무 연속성 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You must design a highly available Azure SQL database that meets these requirements:\n\n- Failover between database replicas must take place with no data loss.\n- The database must stay available if an availability zone goes down.\n- Costs must be kept to a minimum.\n\nWhich deployment option should you choose?","stemKo":"You must design a highly available Azure SQL database that meets these requirements:\n\n- Failover between database replicas must take place with no data loss.\n- The database must stay available if an availability zone goes down.\n- Costs must be kept to a minimum.\n\nWhich deployment option should you choose?","explanationEn":"Azure SQL Database Business Critical tier uses multiple synchronous high-availability replicas based on availability groups. When zone redundancy is enabled, replicas are distributed across availability zones, providing zero recovery point objective (RPO) for committed data during single-zone failures and synchronous failover with no data loss. This tier directly meets all three requirements (no data loss, zone availability, cost-efficiency) without additional replication infrastructure.","explanationKo":"Azure SQL Database Business Critical tier uses multiple synchronous high-availability replicas based on availability groups. When zone redundancy is enabled, replicas are distributed across availability zones, providing zero recovery point objective (RPO) for committed data during single-zone failures and synchronous failover with no data loss. This tier directly meets all three requirements (no data loss, zone availability, cost-efficiency) without additional replication infrastructure.","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Azure SQL Database Serverless","ko":"Azure SQL Database Serverless"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure SQL Managed Instance General Purpose","ko":"Azure SQL Managed Instance General Purpose"},{"label":"C","en":"Azure SQL Database Basic","ko":"Azure SQL Database Basic"},{"label":"D","en":"Azure SQL Database Business Critical","ko":"Azure SQL Database Business Critical"}],"answers":["D"]},{"n":47,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design business continuity solutions","topicKo":"업무 연속성 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You must design a highly available Azure SQL database that satisfies these requirements:\n\n- Failover between database replicas must take place without data loss.\n- The database must stay available if an availability zone experiences an outage.\n- Costs must be kept to a minimum.\n\nWhich deployment option should you choose?","stemKo":"You must design a highly available Azure SQL database that satisfies these requirements:\n\n- Failover between database replicas must take place without data loss.\n- The database must stay available if an availability zone experiences an outage.\n- Costs must be kept to a minimum.\n\nWhich deployment option should you choose?","explanationEn":"A zone-redundant Azure SQL Database Premium deployment distributes synchronized replicas across availability zones. Synchronous replication provides zero loss of committed data during zone failover, and Premium does not incur an additional charge for enabling zone redundancy. Basic does not support zone redundancy; Hyperscale can require additional high-availability replicas and is not the lowest-cost option for these requirements.\n\n**Learn more:** [Reliability in Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/reliability/reliability-sql-database)","explanationKo":"A zone-redundant Azure SQL Database Premium deployment distributes synchronized replicas across availability zones. Synchronous replication provides zero loss of committed data during zone failover, and Premium does not incur an additional charge for enabling zone redundancy. Basic does not support zone redundancy; Hyperscale can require additional high-availability replicas and is not the lowest-cost option for these requirements.\n\n**Learn more:** [Reliability in Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/reliability/reliability-sql-database)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Azure SQL Database Hyperscale","ko":"Azure SQL Database Hyperscale"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure SQL Database Premium","ko":"Azure SQL Database Premium"},{"label":"C","en":"Azure SQL Database Basic","ko":"Azure SQL Database Basic"},{"label":"D","en":"Azure SQL Managed Instance General Purpose","ko":"Azure SQL Managed Instance General Purpose"}],"answers":["B"]},{"n":48,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design infrastructure solutions","topicKo":"인프라 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You are building a sales application that will contain several Azure cloud services and manage different parts of a transaction. Different cloud services will process customer orders, billing, payment, inventory, and shipping.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that lets the cloud services communicate transaction information asynchronously by using XML messages.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","stemKo":"You are building a sales application that will contain several Azure cloud services and manage different parts of a transaction. Different cloud services will process customer orders, billing, payment, inventory, and shipping.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that lets the cloud services communicate transaction information asynchronously by using XML messages.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","explanationEn":"Azure Queue Storage provides message queues that decouple distributed application components, allowing one service to place transaction messages in a queue for another service to process asynchronously. Queue messages must be compatible with UTF-8 XML requests; XML markup carried as message content must be Base64-encoded.\n\n**Learn more:** [Introduction to Azure Queue Storage](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/queues/storage-queues-introduction) · [Put Message (Azure Queue Storage REST API)](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/rest/api/storageservices/put-message)","explanationKo":"Azure Queue Storage provides message queues that decouple distributed application components, allowing one service to place transaction messages in a queue for another service to process asynchronously. Queue messages must be compatible with UTF-8 XML requests; XML markup carried as message content must be Base64-encoded.\n\n**Learn more:** [Introduction to Azure Queue Storage](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/queues/storage-queues-introduction) · [Put Message (Azure Queue Storage REST API)](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/rest/api/storageservices/put-message)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Azure Notification Hubs","ko":"Azure Notification Hubs"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure Queue Storage","ko":"Azure Queue Storage"},{"label":"C","en":"Azure Blob Storage","ko":"Azure Blob Storage"},{"label":"D","en":"Azure Application Gateway","ko":"Azure Application Gateway"}],"answers":["B"]},{"n":49,"id":null,"type":"dropdown","topic":"Design data storage solutions","topicKo":"데이터 저장소 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You have an app that generates 50,000 events each day.\n\nYou plan to stream the events to an Azure event hub and use Event Hubs Capture to implement cold-path processing. A reporting system will consume the Event Hubs Capture output.\n\nIdentify the Azure storage type that must be provisioned and the inbound data format the reporting system must support.","stemKo":"You have an app that generates 50,000 events each day.\n\nYou plan to stream the events to an Azure event hub and use Event Hubs Capture to implement cold-path processing. A reporting system will consume the Event Hubs Capture output.\n\nIdentify the Azure storage type that must be provisioned and the inbound data format the reporting system must support.","explanationEn":"Azure Event Hubs Capture supports Azure Data Lake Storage Gen2 as a capture destination. Capture writes event data as Avro files, so the downstream reporting system must support Avro.\n\n**Learn more:** [Capture events through Azure Event Hubs in Azure Blob Storage or Azure Data Lake Storage](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/event-hubs/event-hubs-capture-overview)","explanationKo":"Azure Event Hubs Capture supports Azure Data Lake Storage Gen2 as a capture destination. Capture writes event data as Avro files, so the downstream reporting system must support Avro.\n\n**Learn more:** [Capture events through Azure Event Hubs in Azure Blob Storage or Azure Data Lake Storage](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/event-hubs/event-hubs-capture-overview)","learnMore":[],"blanks":[{"id":"storage_type","labelEn":"Storage type:","labelKo":"Storage type:","options":[{"en":"Azure Data Lake Storage Gen2","ko":"Azure Data Lake Storage Gen2"},{"en":"Premium block blobs","ko":"Premium block blobs"},{"en":"Premium file shares","ko":"Premium file shares"}],"answer":"Azure Data Lake Storage Gen2"},{"id":"data_format","labelEn":"Data format:","labelKo":"Data format:","options":[{"en":"Apache Parquet","ko":"Apache Parquet"},{"en":"Avro","ko":"Avro"},{"en":"JSON","ko":"JSON"}],"answer":"Avro"}],"template":""},{"n":50,"id":null,"type":"drag_drop","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"Which blade should be used to modify each app registration? Each blade can be used once, more than once, or not at all.","stemKo":"Which blade should be used to modify each app registration? Each blade can be used once, more than once, or not at all.","explanationEn":"App1 exposes the Writer application role through App roles. App2, as the client calling App1, requests and receives that application permission through API permissions. Assigned application roles are emitted in the access token's `roles` claim.\n\n**Learn more:** [appRole resource type](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/graph/api/resources/approle?view=graph-rest-1.0) · [Expose scopes in a protected web API](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity-platform/scenario-protected-web-api-expose-scopes)","explanationKo":"App1 exposes the Writer application role through App roles. App2, as the client calling App1, requests and receives that application permission through API permissions. Assigned application roles are emitted in the access token's `roles` claim.\n\n**Learn more:** [appRole resource type](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/graph/api/resources/approle?view=graph-rest-1.0) · [Expose scopes in a protected web API](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity-platform/scenario-protected-web-api-expose-scopes)","learnMore":[],"items":[{"en":"API permissions","ko":"API permissions"},{"en":"App roles","ko":"App roles"},{"en":"Token configuration","ko":"Token configuration"}],"slots":[{"id":"app1","labelEn":"App1:","labelKo":"App1:","answer":"App roles"},{"id":"app2","labelEn":"App2:","labelKo":"App2:","answer":"API permissions"}],"reuse":true},{"n":51,"id":null,"type":"drag_drop","topic":"Design business continuity solutions","topicKo":"업무 연속성 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You intend to use Azure Storage for data assets.\n\nYou need to determine the procedure for failing over a general-purpose v2 account as part of a disaster-recovery plan. The solution must satisfy these requirements:\n\n- Apps must be able to access the storage account following a failover.\n- You must be able to fail the storage account back to its original location.\n- Downtime must be minimized.\n\nWhich three actions should you take, in sequence?","stemKo":"You intend to use Azure Storage for data assets.\n\nYou need to determine the procedure for failing over a general-purpose v2 account as part of a disaster-recovery plan. The solution must satisfy these requirements:\n\n- Apps must be able to access the storage account following a failover.\n- You must be able to fail the storage account back to its original location.\n- Downtime must be minimized.\n\nWhich three actions should you take, in sequence?","explanationEn":"GRS replicates data to a secondary geographic region and is required for an account failover. Azure updates the storage service endpoints during failover so they point to the new primary region. After an unplanned failover, the account becomes LRS and loses geo-redundancy; configuring GRS again replicates data to the original region and enables a later failback. ZRS does not provide cross-region replication.\n\n**Learn more:** [Initiate a storage account failover](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/common/storage-initiate-account-failover) · [Azure Storage failover FAQ: scenarios, limitations, and best practices](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/common/storage-failover-faq)","explanationKo":"GRS replicates data to a secondary geographic region and is required for an account failover. Azure updates the storage service endpoints during failover so they point to the new primary region. After an unplanned failover, the account becomes LRS and loses geo-redundancy; configuring GRS again replicates data to the original region and enables a later failback. ZRS does not provide cross-region replication.\n\n**Learn more:** [Initiate a storage account failover](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/common/storage-initiate-account-failover) · [Azure Storage failover FAQ: scenarios, limitations, and best practices](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/common/storage-failover-faq)","learnMore":[],"items":[{"en":"After a failover, configure geo-redundant storage (GRS) replication for the storage account.","ko":"After a failover, configure geo-redundant storage (GRS) replication for the storage account."},{"en":"Initiate a failover.","ko":"Initiate a failover."},{"en":"Before a failover, configure zone-redundant storage (ZRS) replication for the storage account.","ko":"Before a failover, configure zone-redundant storage (ZRS) replication for the storage account."},{"en":"Before a failover, configure geo-redundant storage (GRS) replication for the storage account.","ko":"Before a failover, configure geo-redundant storage (GRS) replication for the storage account."},{"en":"After a failover, configure zone-redundant storage (ZRS) replication for the storage account.","ko":"After a failover, configure zone-redundant storage (ZRS) replication for the storage account."}],"slots":[{"id":"step1","labelEn":"항목 step1","labelKo":"항목 step1","answer":"Before a failover, configure geo-redundant storage (GRS) replication for the storage account."},{"id":"step2","labelEn":"항목 step2","labelKo":"항목 step2","answer":"Initiate a failover."},{"id":"step3","labelEn":"항목 step3","labelKo":"항목 step3","answer":"After a failover, configure geo-redundant storage (GRS) replication for the storage account."}],"reuse":false},{"n":52,"id":null,"type":"dropdown","topic":"Design data storage solutions","topicKo":"데이터 저장소 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"Contoso, Ltd. has an Azure subscription containing:\n\n- An Azure Synapse Analytics workspace named `contosoworkspace1`\n- An Azure Data Lake Storage account named `contosolake1`\n- An Azure SQL database named `contososql1`\n\nContoso product data is copied from `contososql1` to `contosolake1`.\n\nIts partner, Fabrikam Inc., has an Azure subscription containing:\n\n- A virtual machine named `FabrikamVM1` that runs Microsoft SQL Server 2019\n- An Azure Storage account named `fabrikamsa1`\n\nContoso plans to upload research data from `FabrikamVM1` to `contosolake1`. During upload, the research data must be transformed into the formats used by Contoso. The data in `contosolake1` will be analyzed by using `contosoworkspace1`.\n\nRecommend a solution that meets these requirements:\n\n- Upload and transform the research data from `FabrikamVM1`.\n- Provide Fabrikam restricted access to snapshots of the data in `contosoworkspace1`.\n\nWhat should you recommend for each requirement?","stemKo":"Contoso, Ltd. has an Azure subscription containing:\n\n- An Azure Synapse Analytics workspace named `contosoworkspace1`\n- An Azure Data Lake Storage account named `contosolake1`\n- An Azure SQL database named `contososql1`\n\nContoso product data is copied from `contososql1` to `contosolake1`.\n\nIts partner, Fabrikam Inc., has an Azure subscription containing:\n\n- A virtual machine named `FabrikamVM1` that runs Microsoft SQL Server 2019\n- An Azure Storage account named `fabrikamsa1`\n\nContoso plans to upload research data from `FabrikamVM1` to `contosolake1`. During upload, the research data must be transformed into the formats used by Contoso. The data in `contosolake1` will be analyzed by using `contosoworkspace1`.\n\nRecommend a solution that meets these requirements:\n\n- Upload and transform the research data from `FabrikamVM1`.\n- Provide Fabrikam restricted access to snapshots of the data in `contosoworkspace1`.\n\nWhat should you recommend for each requirement?","explanationEn":"Azure Synapse pipelines can copy data from SQL Server and use mapping data flows to transform it before it is written to Azure Data Lake Storage. Azure Data Share supports securely sharing data snapshots with external organizations and Azure subscriptions.\n\n**Learn more:** [Copy and transform data to and from SQL Server by using Azure Data Factory or Azure Synapse Analytics](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/data-factory/connector-sql-server) · [Share and receive data from Azure Blob Storage and Azure Data Lake Storage](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/data-share/how-to-share-from-storage)","explanationKo":"Azure Synapse pipelines can copy data from SQL Server and use mapping data flows to transform it before it is written to Azure Data Lake Storage. Azure Data Share supports securely sharing data snapshots with external organizations and Azure subscriptions.\n\n**Learn more:** [Copy and transform data to and from SQL Server by using Azure Data Factory or Azure Synapse Analytics](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/data-factory/connector-sql-server) · [Share and receive data from Azure Blob Storage and Azure Data Lake Storage](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/data-share/how-to-share-from-storage)","learnMore":[],"blanks":[{"id":"upload_transform","labelEn":"Upload and transform the data:","labelKo":"Upload and transform the data:","options":[{"en":"Azure Data Box Gateway","ko":"Azure Data Box Gateway"},{"en":"Azure Data Share","ko":"Azure Data Share"},{"en":"Azure Synapse pipelines","ko":"Azure Synapse pipelines"}],"answer":"Azure Synapse pipelines"},{"id":"restricted_access","labelEn":"Provide restricted access:","labelKo":"Provide restricted access:","options":[{"en":"Azure Data Box Gateway","ko":"Azure Data Box Gateway"},{"en":"Azure Data Share","ko":"Azure Data Share"},{"en":"Azure Synapse pipelines","ko":"Azure Synapse pipelines"}],"answer":"Azure Data Share"}],"template":""},{"n":53,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design infrastructure solutions","topicKo":"인프라 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You plan to automate the deployment of resources to Azure subscriptions.\n\nWhat is one difference between using Azure Blueprints and Azure Resource Manager (ARM) templates?","stemKo":"You plan to automate the deployment of resources to Azure subscriptions.\n\nWhat is one difference between using Azure Blueprints and Azure Resource Manager (ARM) templates?","explanationEn":"Azure Blueprints retain the relationship between a blueprint definition and its deployed assignment, which supports ongoing tracking and auditing. ARM templates do not remain actively connected to the resources after deployment.\n\n**Learn more:** [What is Azure Blueprints (Preview)?](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/governance/blueprints/overview)","explanationKo":"Azure Blueprints retain the relationship between a blueprint definition and its deployed assignment, which supports ongoing tracking and auditing. ARM templates do not remain actively connected to the resources after deployment.\n\n**Learn more:** [What is Azure Blueprints (Preview)?](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/governance/blueprints/overview)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"ARM templates remain connected to the deployed resources.","ko":"ARM templates remain connected to the deployed resources."},{"label":"B","en":"Only blueprints can contain policy definitions.","ko":"Only blueprints can contain policy definitions."},{"label":"C","en":"Only ARM templates can contain policy definitions.","ko":"Only ARM templates can contain policy definitions."},{"label":"D","en":"Blueprints remain connected to the deployed resources.","ko":"Blueprints remain connected to the deployed resources."}],"answers":["D"]},{"n":54,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You need to recommend a solution for generating a monthly report of all new Azure Resource Manager (ARM) resource deployments in your Azure subscription.\n\nWhat should the recommendation include?","stemKo":"You need to recommend a solution for generating a monthly report of all new Azure Resource Manager (ARM) resource deployments in your Azure subscription.\n\nWhat should the recommendation include?","explanationEn":"Azure Activity Log captures subscription-level control-plane events, including resource creation and Azure Resource Manager deployment operations. It provides the audit data needed to identify and report new deployments over a monthly period.\n\n**Learn more:** [Activity log in Azure Monitor](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-monitor/platform/activity-log)","explanationKo":"Azure Activity Log captures subscription-level control-plane events, including resource creation and Azure Resource Manager deployment operations. It provides the audit data needed to identify and report new deployments over a monthly period.\n\n**Learn more:** [Activity log in Azure Monitor](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-monitor/platform/activity-log)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Azure Activity Log","ko":"Azure Activity Log"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure Arc","ko":"Azure Arc"},{"label":"C","en":"Azure Analysis Services","ko":"Azure Analysis Services"},{"label":"D","en":"Azure Monitor metrics","ko":"Azure Monitor metrics"}],"answers":["A"]},{"n":55,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design business continuity solutions","topicKo":"업무 연속성 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You must design a highly available Azure SQL database that satisfies these requirements:\n\n- Failover between database replicas must happen with no data loss.\n- The database must stay available if an availability zone fails.\n- Costs must be kept to a minimum.\n\nWhich deployment option should you use?","stemKo":"You must design a highly available Azure SQL database that satisfies these requirements:\n\n- Failover between database replicas must happen with no data loss.\n- The database must stay available if an availability zone fails.\n- Costs must be kept to a minimum.\n\nWhich deployment option should you use?","explanationEn":"The Business Critical service tier maintains multiple synchronous database replicas and supports zone redundancy, which distributes replicas across availability zones. A synchronized replica can become primary after a zone failure, with no expected committed-data loss. Basic and Standard do not support zone redundancy; Business Critical also has no extra charge to enable zone redundancy because it already provides multiple replicas.\n\n**Learn more:** [Reliability in Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/reliability/reliability-sql-database)","explanationKo":"The Business Critical service tier maintains multiple synchronous database replicas and supports zone redundancy, which distributes replicas across availability zones. A synchronized replica can become primary after a zone failure, with no expected committed-data loss. Basic and Standard do not support zone redundancy; Business Critical also has no extra charge to enable zone redundancy because it already provides multiple replicas.\n\n**Learn more:** [Reliability in Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/reliability/reliability-sql-database)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Azure SQL Database Serverless","ko":"Azure SQL Database Serverless"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure SQL Database Business Critical","ko":"Azure SQL Database Business Critical"},{"label":"C","en":"Azure SQL Database Basic","ko":"Azure SQL Database Basic"},{"label":"D","en":"Azure SQL Database Standard","ko":"Azure SQL Database Standard"}],"answers":["B"]},{"n":56,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design data storage solutions","topicKo":"데이터 저장소 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You are planning a storage solution. The solution must satisfy these requirements:\n\n- Support at least 500 requests per second.\n- Support large image, video, and audio streams.\n\nWhich type of Azure Storage account should you provision?","stemKo":"You are planning a storage solution. The solution must satisfy these requirements:\n\n- Support at least 500 requests per second.\n- Support large image, video, and audio streams.\n\nWhich type of Azure Storage account should you provision?","explanationEn":"A standard general-purpose v2 account supports Azure Blob Storage, which is designed for streaming video and audio. Its block blobs support objects up to approximately 190.7 TiB and have a target rate of up to 3,000 requests per second per blob, satisfying both the large-stream and 500-requests-per-second requirements. Premium block blob accounts are primarily recommended when high transaction rates, smaller objects, or consistently low latency specifically require premium performance.\n\n**Learn more:** [Introduction to Azure Blob Storage](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/blobs/storage-blobs-introduction) · [Scalability and performance targets for Blob storage](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/blobs/scalability-targets)","explanationKo":"A standard general-purpose v2 account supports Azure Blob Storage, which is designed for streaming video and audio. Its block blobs support objects up to approximately 190.7 TiB and have a target rate of up to 3,000 requests per second per blob, satisfying both the large-stream and 500-requests-per-second requirements. Premium block blob accounts are primarily recommended when high transaction rates, smaller objects, or consistently low latency specifically require premium performance.\n\n**Learn more:** [Introduction to Azure Blob Storage](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/blobs/storage-blobs-introduction) · [Scalability and performance targets for Blob storage](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/blobs/scalability-targets)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"standard general-purpose v2","ko":"standard general-purpose v2"},{"label":"B","en":"premium block blobs","ko":"premium block blobs"},{"label":"C","en":"premium page blobs","ko":"premium page blobs"},{"label":"D","en":"premium file shares","ko":"premium file shares"}],"answers":["A"]},{"n":57,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design infrastructure solutions","topicKo":"인프라 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You are developing a sales application that will include several Azure cloud services and process different parts of a transaction. Different cloud services will handle customer orders, billing, payment, inventory, and shipping.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that enables the cloud services to communicate transaction information asynchronously by using XML messages.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","stemKo":"You are developing a sales application that will include several Azure cloud services and process different parts of a transaction. Different cloud services will handle customer orders, billing, payment, inventory, and shipping.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that enables the cloud services to communicate transaction information asynchronously by using XML messages.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","explanationEn":"Azure Service Bus provides durable queues and publish-subscribe topics for reliable asynchronous communication between decoupled services. Its message payloads can contain structured data such as XML, making it suitable for exchanging transaction information among order, billing, payment, inventory, and shipping services.\n\n**Learn more:** [What is Azure Service Bus?](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/service-bus-messaging/service-bus-messaging-overview) · [Asynchronous messaging patterns and high availability](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/service-bus-messaging/service-bus-async-messaging)","explanationKo":"Azure Service Bus provides durable queues and publish-subscribe topics for reliable asynchronous communication between decoupled services. Its message payloads can contain structured data such as XML, making it suitable for exchanging transaction information among order, billing, payment, inventory, and shipping services.\n\n**Learn more:** [What is Azure Service Bus?](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/service-bus-messaging/service-bus-messaging-overview) · [Asynchronous messaging patterns and high availability](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/service-bus-messaging/service-bus-async-messaging)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Azure Service Bus","ko":"Azure Service Bus"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure Blob Storage","ko":"Azure Blob Storage"},{"label":"C","en":"Azure Notification Hubs","ko":"Azure Notification Hubs"},{"label":"D","en":"Azure Application Gateway","ko":"Azure Application Gateway"}],"answers":["A"]},{"n":58,"id":null,"type":"dropdown","topic":"Design data storage solutions","topicKo":"데이터 저장소 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"HOTSPOT\n\nYou intend to use Azure SQL as a database platform.\n\nYou must recommend an Azure SQL product and service tier that meet these requirements:\n\n- Automatically scale compute resources according to workload demand\n- Offer per-second billing\n\nWhat should you recommend?","stemKo":"HOTSPOT\n\nYou intend to use Azure SQL as a database platform.\n\nYou must recommend an Azure SQL product and service tier that meet these requirements:\n\n- Automatically scale compute resources according to workload demand\n- Offer per-second billing\n\nWhat should you recommend?","explanationEn":"Azure SQL Database serverless automatically scales compute based on workload demand and bills compute use per second. It is available in the General Purpose service tier, so a single Azure SQL database with General Purpose meets both requirements.\n\n**Learn more:** [Serverless compute tier - Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/database/serverless-tier-overview?view=azuresql)","explanationKo":"Azure SQL Database serverless automatically scales compute based on workload demand and bills compute use per second. It is available in the General Purpose service tier, so a single Azure SQL database with General Purpose meets both requirements.\n\n**Learn more:** [Serverless compute tier - Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/database/serverless-tier-overview?view=azuresql)","learnMore":[],"blanks":[{"id":"azure_sql_product","labelEn":"Azure SQL product:","labelKo":"Azure SQL product:","options":[{"en":"A single Azure SQL database","ko":"A single Azure SQL database"},{"en":"An Azure SQL Database elastic pool","ko":"An Azure SQL Database elastic pool"},{"en":"Azure SQL Managed Instance","ko":"Azure SQL Managed Instance"}],"answer":"A single Azure SQL database"},{"id":"service_tier","labelEn":"Service tier:","labelKo":"Service tier:","options":[{"en":"Basic","ko":"Basic"},{"en":"Business Critical","ko":"Business Critical"},{"en":"General Purpose","ko":"General Purpose"},{"en":"Hyperscale","ko":"Hyperscale"},{"en":"Standard","ko":"Standard"}],"answer":"General Purpose"}],"template":""},{"n":59,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design data storage solutions","topicKo":"데이터 저장소 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You are designing an Azure IoT Hub solution that will contain 50,000 IoT devices.\n\nEach device will stream data that includes temperature, device ID, and time data. About 50,000 records will be written per second. The data must be visualized in near real time.\n\nYou need to recommend a service for storing and querying the data.\n\nWhich two services can you recommend? Each correct answer presents a complete solution.\n\n**NOTE:** Each correct selection is worth one point.","stemKo":"You are designing an Azure IoT Hub solution that will contain 50,000 IoT devices.\n\nEach device will stream data that includes temperature, device ID, and time data. About 50,000 records will be written per second. The data must be visualized in near real time.\n\nYou need to recommend a service for storing and querying the data.\n\nWhich two services can you recommend? Each correct answer presents a complete solution.\n\n**NOTE:** Each correct selection is worth one point.","explanationEn":"For 50,000 IoT devices streaming 50,000 records per second with near-real-time visualization, two services meet all requirements: Azure Cosmos DB SQL API provides horizontally scalable storage and SQL-based querying for high-volume telemetry, while Azure Time Series Insights was purpose-built to ingest, store, query, and visualize time-series IoT data in near real-time. Azure Table Storage (A) cannot handle the throughput, and Azure Event Grid (B) is only a broker without storage or query capabilities.","explanationKo":"For 50,000 IoT devices streaming 50,000 records per second with near-real-time visualization, two services meet all requirements: Azure Cosmos DB SQL API provides horizontally scalable storage and SQL-based querying for high-volume telemetry, while Azure Time Series Insights was purpose-built to ingest, store, query, and visualize time-series IoT data in near real-time. Azure Table Storage (A) cannot handle the throughput, and Azure Event Grid (B) is only a broker without storage or query capabilities.","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Azure Table Storage","ko":"Azure Table Storage"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure Event Grid","ko":"Azure Event Grid"},{"label":"C","en":"Azure Cosmos DB SQL API","ko":"Azure Cosmos DB SQL API"},{"label":"D","en":"Azure Time Series Insights","ko":"Azure Time Series Insights"}],"answers":["CD"]},{"n":60,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You have an Azure subscription.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that enables developers to provision Azure virtual machines. The solution must meet these requirements:\n\n- Allow virtual machines to be created only in specified regions.\n- Allow only specified virtual machine sizes to be created.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","stemKo":"You have an Azure subscription.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that enables developers to provision Azure virtual machines. The solution must meet these requirements:\n\n- Allow virtual machines to be created only in specified regions.\n- Allow only specified virtual machine sizes to be created.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","explanationEn":"Azure Policy provides deny-based governance controls for resource deployments. The built-in Allowed locations policy restricts deployment to specified regions, and the Allowed virtual machine size SKUs policy restricts the VM SKUs that can be deployed.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure Policy overview](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/governance/policy/overview) · [Built-in policy definitions for Azure Virtual Machines](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/virtual-machines/policy-reference)","explanationKo":"Azure Policy provides deny-based governance controls for resource deployments. The built-in Allowed locations policy restricts deployment to specified regions, and the Allowed virtual machine size SKUs policy restricts the VM SKUs that can be deployed.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure Policy overview](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/governance/policy/overview) · [Built-in policy definitions for Azure Virtual Machines](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/virtual-machines/policy-reference)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Attribute-based access control (ABAC)","ko":"Attribute-based access control (ABAC)"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure Policy","ko":"Azure Policy"},{"label":"C","en":"Conditional Access policies","ko":"Conditional Access policies"},{"label":"D","en":"role-based access control (RBAC)","ko":"role-based access control (RBAC)"}],"answers":["B"]},{"n":61,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design infrastructure solutions","topicKo":"인프라 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"Your company hosts 300 virtual machines in a VMware environment. The virtual machines differ in size and have varying utilization levels.\n\nYou plan to migrate all the virtual machines to Azure.\n\nYou need to recommend the number and sizes of Azure virtual machines required to migrate the existing workloads to Azure. The solution must minimize administrative effort.\n\nWhat should you use to make the recommendation?","stemKo":"Your company hosts 300 virtual machines in a VMware environment. The virtual machines differ in size and have varying utilization levels.\n\nYou plan to migrate all the virtual machines to Azure.\n\nYou need to recommend the number and sizes of Azure virtual machines required to migrate the existing workloads to Azure. The solution must minimize administrative effort.\n\nWhat should you use to make the recommendation?","explanationEn":"Azure Migrate Discovery and Assessment evaluates VMware workloads and can use collected CPU, memory, disk, and network performance data to produce right-sized Azure VM recommendations. This supports sizing the migrated estate according to actual utilization while minimizing manual assessment work.\n\n**Learn more:** [Overview of Azure Migrate assessment types](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/migrate/concepts-assessment-overview?view=migrate) · [Performance vs. as-is on-premises assessments](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/migrate/target-right-sizing?view=migrate)","explanationKo":"Azure Migrate Discovery and Assessment evaluates VMware workloads and can use collected CPU, memory, disk, and network performance data to produce right-sized Azure VM recommendations. This supports sizing the migrated estate according to actual utilization while minimizing manual assessment work.\n\n**Learn more:** [Overview of Azure Migrate assessment types](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/migrate/concepts-assessment-overview?view=migrate) · [Performance vs. as-is on-premises assessments](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/migrate/target-right-sizing?view=migrate)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Azure Pricing calculator","ko":"Azure Pricing calculator"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure Advisor","ko":"Azure Advisor"},{"label":"C","en":"Azure Migrate","ko":"Azure Migrate"},{"label":"D","en":"Azure Cost Management","ko":"Azure Cost Management"}],"answers":["C"]},{"n":62,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You have an Azure Active Directory (Azure AD) tenant synchronized with an on-premises Active Directory domain.\n\nYour company has an internally developed line-of-business (LOB) application.\n\nYou need to implement SAML single sign-on (SSO) and require multi-factor authentication (MFA) when users try to access the application from an unknown location.\n\nWhich two features should be included in the solution? Each correct answer represents part of the solution.\n\nNOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.","stemKo":"You have an Azure Active Directory (Azure AD) tenant synchronized with an on-premises Active Directory domain.\n\nYour company has an internally developed line-of-business (LOB) application.\n\nYou need to implement SAML single sign-on (SSO) and require multi-factor authentication (MFA) when users try to access the application from an unknown location.\n\nWhich two features should be included in the solution? Each correct answer represents part of the solution.\n\nNOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.","explanationEn":"Azure AD enterprise applications provide the SAML SSO configuration for an application integrated with Azure AD. Conditional Access policies can target the application, evaluate network/location conditions, and require MFA for access outside trusted or named locations.\n\n**Learn more:** [Enable SAML single sign-on for an enterprise application](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity/enterprise-apps/add-application-portal-setup-sso) · [Require MFA for all users with Conditional Access](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity/conditional-access/policy-all-users-mfa-strength)","explanationKo":"Azure AD enterprise applications provide the SAML SSO configuration for an application integrated with Azure AD. Conditional Access policies can target the application, evaluate network/location conditions, and require MFA for access outside trusted or named locations.\n\n**Learn more:** [Enable SAML single sign-on for an enterprise application](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity/enterprise-apps/add-application-portal-setup-sso) · [Require MFA for all users with Conditional Access](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity/conditional-access/policy-all-users-mfa-strength)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Azure AD Privileged Identity Management (PIM)","ko":"Azure AD Privileged Identity Management (PIM)"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure Application Gateway","ko":"Azure Application Gateway"},{"label":"C","en":"Azure AD enterprise applications","ko":"Azure AD enterprise applications"},{"label":"D","en":"Azure AD Identity Protection","ko":"Azure AD Identity Protection"},{"label":"E","en":"Conditional Access policies","ko":"Conditional Access policies"}],"answers":["CE"]},{"n":63,"id":null,"type":"dropdown","topic":"Design data storage solutions","topicKo":"데이터 저장소 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You are designing a data-storage solution to support reporting.\n\nThe solution will ingest high volumes of JSON data by using Azure Event Hubs. As data arrives, Event Hubs will write it to storage. The solution must meet these requirements:\n\n- Organize data into directories by date and time.\n- Allow stored data to be queried directly, transformed into summarized tables, and then saved in a data warehouse.\n- Ensure that the data warehouse can store 50 TB of relational data and support between 200 and 300 concurrent read operations.\n\nWhich service should you recommend for each type of data store?","stemKo":"You are designing a data-storage solution to support reporting.\n\nThe solution will ingest high volumes of JSON data by using Azure Event Hubs. As data arrives, Event Hubs will write it to storage. The solution must meet these requirements:\n\n- Organize data into directories by date and time.\n- Allow stored data to be queried directly, transformed into summarized tables, and then saved in a data warehouse.\n- Ensure that the data warehouse can store 50 TB of relational data and support between 200 and 300 concurrent read operations.\n\nWhich service should you recommend for each type of data store?","explanationEn":"Azure Data Lake Storage Gen2 supplies a hierarchical namespace for directory-based storage and is supported as an Azure Event Hubs Capture destination. Azure SQL Database Hyperscale supports databases up to 128 TB, up to 30,000 concurrent sessions, and read scale-out through secondary replicas, meeting the relational-capacity and concurrent-read requirements.\n\n**Learn more:** [Configure Event Hubs Capture to Azure Data Lake Storage Gen2](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/event-hubs/event-hubs-capture-enable-through-portal) · [Azure SQL Database single-database vCore resource limits](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/database/resource-limits-vcore-single-databases?view=azuresql)","explanationKo":"Azure Data Lake Storage Gen2 supplies a hierarchical namespace for directory-based storage and is supported as an Azure Event Hubs Capture destination. Azure SQL Database Hyperscale supports databases up to 128 TB, up to 30,000 concurrent sessions, and read scale-out through secondary replicas, meeting the relational-capacity and concurrent-read requirements.\n\n**Learn more:** [Configure Event Hubs Capture to Azure Data Lake Storage Gen2](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/event-hubs/event-hubs-capture-enable-through-portal) · [Azure SQL Database single-database vCore resource limits](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/database/resource-limits-vcore-single-databases?view=azuresql)","learnMore":[],"blanks":[{"id":"ingested_data","labelEn":"Data store for the ingested data:","labelKo":"Data store for the ingested data:","options":[{"en":"Azure Blob Storage","ko":"Azure Blob Storage"},{"en":"Azure Data Lake Storage Gen2","ko":"Azure Data Lake Storage Gen2"},{"en":"Azure Files","ko":"Azure Files"},{"en":"Azure NetApp Files","ko":"Azure NetApp Files"}],"answer":"Azure Data Lake Storage Gen2"},{"id":"data_warehouse","labelEn":"Data store for the data warehouse:","labelKo":"Data store for the data warehouse:","options":[{"en":"Azure Cosmos DB Cassandra API","ko":"Azure Cosmos DB Cassandra API"},{"en":"Azure Cosmos DB SQL API","ko":"Azure Cosmos DB SQL API"},{"en":"Azure SQL Database Hyperscale","ko":"Azure SQL Database Hyperscale"},{"en":"Azure Synapse Analytics dedicated SQL pools","ko":"Azure Synapse Analytics dedicated SQL pools"}],"answer":"Azure SQL Database Hyperscale"}],"template":""},{"n":64,"id":null,"type":"dropdown","topic":"Design infrastructure solutions","topicKo":"인프라 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You intend to deploy a containerized web app across five Azure Kubernetes Service (AKS) clusters, with each cluster located in a separate Azure region.\n\nInternet access to the app must meet these requirements:\n\n- Route incoming HTTPS requests to the cluster with the lowest network latency.\n- Route HTTPS traffic to individual pods through an ingress controller.\n- Minimize failover time if an AKS cluster becomes unavailable.\n\nWhat should be included in the solution?","stemKo":"You intend to deploy a containerized web app across five Azure Kubernetes Service (AKS) clusters, with each cluster located in a separate Azure region.\n\nInternet access to the app must meet these requirements:\n\n- Route incoming HTTPS requests to the cluster with the lowest network latency.\n- Route HTTPS traffic to individual pods through an ingress controller.\n- Minimize failover time if an AKS cluster becomes unavailable.\n\nWhat should be included in the solution?","explanationEn":"Azure Front Door performs global Layer 7 HTTP/HTTPS routing using health probes and latency-based origin selection, directing requests to the lowest-latency healthy regional origin and failing over when an origin is unhealthy. Azure Application Gateway, integrated with AKS through Application Gateway Ingress Controller (AGIC), provides HTTP/HTTPS ingress routing to AKS workloads and their pods.\n\n**Learn more:** [Traffic routing methods to origin - Azure Front Door](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/frontdoor/routing-methods) · [Add health probes to your AKS pods](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/application-gateway/ingress-controller-add-health-probes)","explanationKo":"Azure Front Door performs global Layer 7 HTTP/HTTPS routing using health probes and latency-based origin selection, directing requests to the lowest-latency healthy regional origin and failing over when an origin is unhealthy. Azure Application Gateway, integrated with AKS through Application Gateway Ingress Controller (AGIC), provides HTTP/HTTPS ingress routing to AKS workloads and their pods.\n\n**Learn more:** [Traffic routing methods to origin - Azure Front Door](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/frontdoor/routing-methods) · [Add health probes to your AKS pods](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/application-gateway/ingress-controller-add-health-probes)","learnMore":[],"blanks":[{"id":"global_load_balancing","labelEn":"For global load balancing:","labelKo":"For global load balancing:","options":[{"en":"Azure Front Door","ko":"Azure Front Door"},{"en":"Azure Traffic Manager","ko":"Azure Traffic Manager"},{"en":"Cross-region load balancing in Azure","ko":"Cross-region load balancing in Azure"},{"en":"Standard Load Balancer","ko":"Standard Load Balancer"}],"answer":"Azure Front Door"},{"id":"ingress_controller","labelEn":"As the ingress controller:","labelKo":"As the ingress controller:","options":[{"en":"Azure Application Gateway","ko":"Azure Application Gateway"},{"en":"Azure Standard Load Balancer","ko":"Azure Standard Load Balancer"},{"en":"Basic Azure Load Balancer","ko":"Basic Azure Load Balancer"}],"answer":"Azure Application Gateway"}],"template":""},{"n":65,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"After migrating App1 to Azure, you must enforce the data-modification requirements to satisfy the security and compliance requirements.\n\nWhat should you do?","stemKo":"After migrating App1 to Azure, you must enforce the data-modification requirements to satisfy the security and compliance requirements.\n\nWhat should you do?","explanationEn":"An Azure Blob Storage immutability policy provides write-once, read-many (WORM) protection, preventing protected blob data from being modified or deleted for the configured retention period or while a legal hold applies. It is configured through the blob/container access policy settings and is intended for regulatory and compliance retention requirements.\n\n**Learn more:** [Overview of immutable storage for blob data - Azure Storage](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/blobs/immutable-storage-overview) · [Configure immutability policies for blob versions - Azure Storage](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/blobs/immutable-policy-configure-version-scope)","explanationKo":"An Azure Blob Storage immutability policy provides write-once, read-many (WORM) protection, preventing protected blob data from being modified or deleted for the configured retention period or while a legal hold applies. It is configured through the blob/container access policy settings and is intended for regulatory and compliance retention requirements.\n\n**Learn more:** [Overview of immutable storage for blob data - Azure Storage](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/blobs/immutable-storage-overview) · [Configure immutability policies for blob versions - Azure Storage](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/blobs/immutable-policy-configure-version-scope)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Create an access policy for the blob service.","ko":"Create an access policy for the blob service."},{"label":"B","en":"Implement Azure resource locks.","ko":"Implement Azure resource locks."},{"label":"C","en":"Create Azure RBAC assignments.","ko":"Create Azure RBAC assignments."},{"label":"D","en":"Modify the access level of the blob service.","ko":"Modify the access level of the blob service."}],"answers":["A"]},{"n":66,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design data storage solutions","topicKo":"데이터 저장소 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You need to recommend a data-storage strategy for WebApp1.\n\nWhat should the recommendation include?","stemKo":"You need to recommend a data-storage strategy for WebApp1.\n\nWhat should the recommendation include?","explanationEn":"A vCore-based Azure SQL Database provides a PaaS database service and supports Azure Hybrid Benefit for SQL Server, allowing eligible existing SQL Server licenses to reduce database costs. The vCore model also provides independent selection of compute and storage resources.\n\n**Learn more:** [Purchasing models and service tiers - Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/database/purchasing-models?view=azuresql)","explanationKo":"A vCore-based Azure SQL Database provides a PaaS database service and supports Azure Hybrid Benefit for SQL Server, allowing eligible existing SQL Server licenses to reduce database costs. The vCore model also provides independent selection of compute and storage resources.\n\n**Learn more:** [Purchasing models and service tiers - Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/database/purchasing-models?view=azuresql)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"an Azure virtual machine that runs SQL Server","ko":"an Azure virtual machine that runs SQL Server"},{"label":"B","en":"a fixed-size DTU Azure SQL database","ko":"a fixed-size DTU Azure SQL database"},{"label":"C","en":"an Azure SQL Database elastic pool","ko":"an Azure SQL Database elastic pool"},{"label":"D","en":"a vCore-based Azure SQL database","ko":"a vCore-based Azure SQL database"}],"answers":["D"]},{"n":67,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design infrastructure solutions","topicKo":"인프라 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You need to recommend an App Service architecture that fulfills the requirements for App1. The solution must minimize costs.\n\nWhat should you recommend?","stemKo":"You need to recommend an App Service architecture that fulfills the requirements for App1. The solution must minimize costs.\n\nWhat should you recommend?","explanationEn":"An App Service plan is created in a region, and multiple apps in the same plan share the plan’s compute resources. App Service Environments provide dedicated isolation and require the Isolated v2 tier, making them more expensive than the multitenant App Service offering. Availability-zone resilience is configured by distributing plan instances across zones within a region, rather than by creating a plan for each zone.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure App Service plans](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/app-service/overview-hosting-plans) · [App Service Environment v3 and multitenant comparison](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/app-service/environment/ase-multi-tenant-comparison)","explanationKo":"An App Service plan is created in a region, and multiple apps in the same plan share the plan’s compute resources. App Service Environments provide dedicated isolation and require the Isolated v2 tier, making them more expensive than the multitenant App Service offering. Availability-zone resilience is configured by distributing plan instances across zones within a region, rather than by creating a plan for each zone.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure App Service plans](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/app-service/overview-hosting-plans) · [App Service Environment v3 and multitenant comparison](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/app-service/environment/ase-multi-tenant-comparison)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"one App Service Environment (ASE) per availability zone","ko":"one App Service Environment (ASE) per availability zone"},{"label":"B","en":"one App Service Environment (ASE) per region","ko":"one App Service Environment (ASE) per region"},{"label":"C","en":"one App Service plan per region","ko":"one App Service plan per region"},{"label":"D","en":"one App Service plan per availability zone","ko":"one App Service plan per availability zone"}],"answers":["C"]},{"n":68,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You have an Azure subscription containing 1,000 resources.\n\nYou need to produce compliance reports for the subscription. The solution must allow the resources to be grouped by department.\n\nWhat should you use to organize the resources?","stemKo":"You have an Azure subscription containing 1,000 resources.\n\nYou need to produce compliance reports for the subscription. The solution must allow the resources to be grouped by department.\n\nWhat should you use to organize the resources?","explanationEn":"Azure Policy assesses resource compliance and provides compliance data and reporting for a subscription. Tags are key-value metadata that categorize resources by organizational attributes such as department, and Azure Policy can enforce consistent tag use at scale.\n\n**Learn more:** [Overview of Azure Policy](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/governance/policy/overview) · [Use tags to organize your Azure resources and management hierarchy](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-resource-manager/management/tag-resources)","explanationKo":"Azure Policy assesses resource compliance and provides compliance data and reporting for a subscription. Tags are key-value metadata that categorize resources by organizational attributes such as department, and Azure Policy can enforce consistent tag use at scale.\n\n**Learn more:** [Overview of Azure Policy](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/governance/policy/overview) · [Use tags to organize your Azure resources and management hierarchy](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-resource-manager/management/tag-resources)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"application groups and quotas","ko":"application groups and quotas"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure Policy and tags","ko":"Azure Policy and tags"},{"label":"C","en":"administrative units and Azure Lighthouse","ko":"administrative units and Azure Lighthouse"},{"label":"D","en":"resource groups and role assignments","ko":"resource groups and role assignments"}],"answers":["B"]},{"n":69,"id":null,"type":"dropdown","topic":"Design infrastructure solutions","topicKo":"인프라 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"Your company has offices in New York City, Sydney, Paris, and Johannesburg.\n\nThe company has an Azure subscription.\n\nYou plan to deploy a new Azure networking solution that meets these requirements:\n\n- Connect to ExpressRoute circuits in the Azure regions of East US, Southeast Asia, North Europe, and South Africa\n- Minimize latency by supporting connections in three regions\n- Support site-to-site VPN connections\n- Minimize costs\n\nYou need to determine the minimum number of Azure Virtual WAN hubs to deploy and the virtual WAN SKU to use.","stemKo":"Your company has offices in New York City, Sydney, Paris, and Johannesburg.\n\nThe company has an Azure subscription.\n\nYou plan to deploy a new Azure networking solution that meets these requirements:\n\n- Connect to ExpressRoute circuits in the Azure regions of East US, Southeast Asia, North Europe, and South Africa\n- Minimize latency by supporting connections in three regions\n- Support site-to-site VPN connections\n- Minimize costs\n\nYou need to determine the minimum number of Azure Virtual WAN hubs to deploy and the virtual WAN SKU to use.","explanationEn":"A Virtual WAN hub connects to an ExpressRoute circuit in the same Azure region, so four hubs are needed for the circuits in East US, Southeast Asia, North Europe, and South Africa. The Standard virtual WAN SKU supports both ExpressRoute and site-to-site VPN; the Basic SKU supports site-to-site VPN but not ExpressRoute.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure Virtual WAN FAQ](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/virtual-wan/virtual-wan-faq) · [Virtual WAN settings](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/virtual-wan/virtual-wan-about#virtual-wan-types)","explanationKo":"A Virtual WAN hub connects to an ExpressRoute circuit in the same Azure region, so four hubs are needed for the circuits in East US, Southeast Asia, North Europe, and South Africa. The Standard virtual WAN SKU supports both ExpressRoute and site-to-site VPN; the Basic SKU supports site-to-site VPN but not ExpressRoute.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure Virtual WAN FAQ](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/virtual-wan/virtual-wan-faq) · [Virtual WAN settings](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/virtual-wan/virtual-wan-about#virtual-wan-types)","learnMore":[],"blanks":[{"id":"number_of_virtual_wan_hubs","labelEn":"Number of Virtual WAN hubs:","labelKo":"Number of Virtual WAN hubs:","options":[{"en":"1","ko":"1"},{"en":"2","ko":"2"},{"en":"3","ko":"3"},{"en":"4","ko":"4"}],"answer":"4"},{"id":"virtual_wan_sku","labelEn":"Virtual WAN SKU:","labelKo":"Virtual WAN SKU:","options":[{"en":"Basic","ko":"Basic"},{"en":"Standard","ko":"Standard"}],"answer":"Standard"}],"template":""},{"n":70,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design business continuity solutions","topicKo":"업무 연속성 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You have SQL Server running on an Azure virtual machine. The databases receive writes nightly as part of a batch process.\n\nYou need to recommend a disaster recovery solution for the data. The solution must meet these requirements:\n\n- Provide the ability to recover from a regional outage.\n- Support a recovery time objective (RTO) of 15 minutes.\n- Support a recovery point objective (RPO) of 24 hours.\n- Support automated recovery.\n- Minimize costs.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","stemKo":"You have SQL Server running on an Azure virtual machine. The databases receive writes nightly as part of a batch process.\n\nYou need to recommend a disaster recovery solution for the data. The solution must meet these requirements:\n\n- Provide the ability to recover from a regional outage.\n- Support a recovery time objective (RTO) of 15 minutes.\n- Support a recovery point objective (RPO) of 24 hours.\n- Support automated recovery.\n- Minimize costs.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","explanationEn":"Azure Site Recovery replicates Azure virtual machines to a target region for regional disaster recovery and can orchestrate failover through recovery plans. For SQL Server workloads, Microsoft documents an expected Site Recovery RTO of typically less than 15 minutes; its asynchronous replication can meet a 24-hour RPO while avoiding the cost of a continuously active secondary SQL Server deployment.\n\n**Learn more:** [Set up disaster recovery for SQL Server with Azure Site Recovery](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/site-recovery/site-recovery-sql) · [Reliability in Azure Site Recovery](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/reliability/reliability-site-recovery)","explanationKo":"Azure Site Recovery replicates Azure virtual machines to a target region for regional disaster recovery and can orchestrate failover through recovery plans. For SQL Server workloads, Microsoft documents an expected Site Recovery RTO of typically less than 15 minutes; its asynchronous replication can meet a 24-hour RPO while avoiding the cost of a continuously active secondary SQL Server deployment.\n\n**Learn more:** [Set up disaster recovery for SQL Server with Azure Site Recovery](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/site-recovery/site-recovery-sql) · [Reliability in Azure Site Recovery](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/reliability/reliability-site-recovery)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Azure virtual machine availability sets","ko":"Azure virtual machine availability sets"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure Disk Backup","ko":"Azure Disk Backup"},{"label":"C","en":"an Always On availability group","ko":"an Always On availability group"},{"label":"D","en":"Azure Site Recovery","ko":"Azure Site Recovery"}],"answers":["D"]},{"n":71,"id":null,"type":"dropdown","topic":"Design data storage solutions","topicKo":"데이터 저장소 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You are designing a data analytics solution using Azure Synapse and Azure Data Lake Storage Gen2.\n\nRecommend Azure Synapse pools that meet these requirements:","stemKo":"You are designing a data analytics solution using Azure Synapse and Azure Data Lake Storage Gen2.\n\nRecommend Azure Synapse pools that meet these requirements:","explanationEn":"Dedicated SQL pools support hash-distributed tables and ingestion from the data lake. Apache Spark pools support creating, querying, and modifying Delta Lake tables; serverless SQL pools can query Delta data but cannot modify synchronized lake tables.\n\n**Learn more:** [Synapse SQL architecture](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/synapse-analytics/sql/overview-architecture) · [Access lake databases using serverless SQL pool](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/synapse-analytics/metadata/database)","explanationKo":"Dedicated SQL pools support hash-distributed tables and ingestion from the data lake. Apache Spark pools support creating, querying, and modifying Delta Lake tables; serverless SQL pools can query Delta data but cannot modify synchronized lake tables.\n\n**Learn more:** [Synapse SQL architecture](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/synapse-analytics/sql/overview-architecture) · [Access lake databases using serverless SQL pool](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/synapse-analytics/metadata/database)","learnMore":[],"blanks":[{"id":"ingest_hash","labelEn":"Ingest data from Data Lake Storage into hash-distributed tables:","labelKo":"Ingest data from Data Lake Storage into hash-distributed tables:","options":[{"en":"A dedicated SQL pool","ko":"A dedicated SQL pool"},{"en":"A serverless Apache Spark pool","ko":"A serverless Apache Spark pool"},{"en":"A serverless SQL pool","ko":"A serverless SQL pool"}],"answer":"A dedicated SQL pool"},{"id":"delta_update","labelEn":"Implement, query, and update data in Delta Lake:","labelKo":"Implement, query, and update data in Delta Lake:","options":[{"en":"A dedicated SQL pool","ko":"A dedicated SQL pool"},{"en":"A serverless Apache Spark pool","ko":"A serverless Apache Spark pool"},{"en":"A serverless SQL pool","ko":"A serverless SQL pool"}],"answer":"A serverless Apache Spark pool"}],"template":""},{"n":72,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design infrastructure solutions","topicKo":"인프라 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You are developing a sales application that will include several Azure cloud services and handle different parts of a transaction. Different cloud services will process customer orders, billing, payment, inventory, and shipping.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that enables the cloud services to communicate transaction information asynchronously by using XML messages.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","stemKo":"You are developing a sales application that will include several Azure cloud services and handle different parts of a transaction. Different cloud services will process customer orders, billing, payment, inventory, and shipping.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that enables the cloud services to communicate transaction information asynchronously by using XML messages.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","explanationEn":"Azure Service Bus is a fully managed enterprise message broker that decouples applications and services through queues and publish-subscribe topics. It supports asynchronous, store-and-forward communication, and its message payloads can carry structured data such as XML.\n\n**Learn more:** [What is Azure Service Bus?](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-gb/azure/service-bus-messaging/service-bus-messaging-overview) · [Asynchronous messaging patterns and high availability](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/service-bus-messaging/service-bus-async-messaging)","explanationKo":"Azure Service Bus is a fully managed enterprise message broker that decouples applications and services through queues and publish-subscribe topics. It supports asynchronous, store-and-forward communication, and its message payloads can carry structured data such as XML.\n\n**Learn more:** [What is Azure Service Bus?](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-gb/azure/service-bus-messaging/service-bus-messaging-overview) · [Asynchronous messaging patterns and high availability](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/service-bus-messaging/service-bus-async-messaging)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Azure Service Bus","ko":"Azure Service Bus"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure Data Lake","ko":"Azure Data Lake"},{"label":"C","en":"Azure Application Gateway","ko":"Azure Application Gateway"},{"label":"D","en":"Azure Notification Hubs","ko":"Azure Notification Hubs"}],"answers":["A"]},{"n":73,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design business continuity solutions","topicKo":"업무 연속성 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You intend to deploy 10 applications to Azure. The applications will be deployed across two Azure Kubernetes Service (AKS) clusters, with each cluster located in a separate Azure region.\n\nThe application deployment must satisfy the following requirements:\n\n- Ensure that the applications stay available if one AKS cluster fails.\n- Ensure that internet connection traffic is encrypted by using SSL, without needing to configure SSL on every container.\n\nWhich service should be included in the recommendation?","stemKo":"You intend to deploy 10 applications to Azure. The applications will be deployed across two Azure Kubernetes Service (AKS) clusters, with each cluster located in a separate Azure region.\n\nThe application deployment must satisfy the following requirements:\n\n- Ensure that the applications stay available if one AKS cluster fails.\n- Ensure that internet connection traffic is encrypted by using SSL, without needing to configure SSL on every container.\n\nWhich service should be included in the recommendation?","explanationEn":"Azure Front Door is a global Layer 7 load balancer that monitors origin health and can fail over traffic from an unavailable AKS cluster to an alternate regional cluster. It also supports TLS/SSL termination (SSL offload) at the edge, avoiding SSL configuration on each application container.\n\n**Learn more:** [Accelerate and secure your web application with Azure Front Door](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/frontdoor/scenarios) · [Azure Front Door best practices](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/frontdoor/best-practices)","explanationKo":"Azure Front Door is a global Layer 7 load balancer that monitors origin health and can fail over traffic from an unavailable AKS cluster to an alternate regional cluster. It also supports TLS/SSL termination (SSL offload) at the edge, avoiding SSL configuration on each application container.\n\n**Learn more:** [Accelerate and secure your web application with Azure Front Door](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/frontdoor/scenarios) · [Azure Front Door best practices](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/frontdoor/best-practices)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Azure Front Door","ko":"Azure Front Door"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure Traffic Manager","ko":"Azure Traffic Manager"},{"label":"C","en":"AKS ingress controller","ko":"AKS ingress controller"},{"label":"D","en":"Azure Load Balancer","ko":"Azure Load Balancer"}],"answers":["A"]},{"n":74,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design infrastructure solutions","topicKo":"인프라 설계","koMissing":true,"images":["assets/1783706725971-2qots6h6.png"],"stemEn":"You have an Azure subscription containing a Basic Azure virtual WAN named VirtualWAN1 and the virtual hubs shown in the following table.\n\n[[IMG1]]\n\nYou have an ExpressRoute circuit in the US East Azure region.\n\nYou need to create an ExpressRoute association with VirtualWAN1.\n\nWhat should you do first?","stemKo":"You have an Azure subscription containing a Basic Azure virtual WAN named VirtualWAN1 and the virtual hubs shown in the following table.\n\n[[IMG1]]\n\nYou have an ExpressRoute circuit in the US East Azure region.\n\nYou need to create an ExpressRoute association with VirtualWAN1.\n\nWhat should you do first?","explanationEn":"A Basic Azure virtual WAN supports only site-to-site VPN. Upgrading it to Standard upgrades its hubs to Standard hubs, which support ExpressRoute and allow deployment of an ExpressRoute gateway for the circuit association. An ExpressRoute premium add-on is not inherently required, and the existing US East hub is the appropriate regional hub.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure Virtual WAN overview](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/virtual-wan/virtual-wan-about) · [Upgrade a virtual WAN from Basic to Standard](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/virtual-wan/upgrade-virtual-wan)","explanationKo":"A Basic Azure virtual WAN supports only site-to-site VPN. Upgrading it to Standard upgrades its hubs to Standard hubs, which support ExpressRoute and allow deployment of an ExpressRoute gateway for the circuit association. An ExpressRoute premium add-on is not inherently required, and the existing US East hub is the appropriate regional hub.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure Virtual WAN overview](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/virtual-wan/virtual-wan-about) · [Upgrade a virtual WAN from Basic to Standard](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/virtual-wan/upgrade-virtual-wan)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Upgrade VirtualWAN1 to Standard.","ko":"Upgrade VirtualWAN1 to Standard."},{"label":"B","en":"Create a gateway on Hub1.","ko":"Create a gateway on Hub1."},{"label":"C","en":"Enable the ExpressRoute premium add-on.","ko":"Enable the ExpressRoute premium add-on."},{"label":"D","en":"Create a hub virtual network in US East.","ko":"Create a hub virtual network in US East."}],"answers":["A"]},{"n":75,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You are planning a large Azure environment that will include many subscriptions.\n\nYou intend to use Azure Policy as part of a governance solution.\n\nTo which three scopes can Azure Policy definitions be assigned? Each correct answer provides a complete solution.\n\n**NOTE:** Each correct selection is worth one point.","stemKo":"You are planning a large Azure environment that will include many subscriptions.\n\nYou intend to use Azure Policy as part of a governance solution.\n\nTo which three scopes can Azure Policy definitions be assigned? Each correct answer provides a complete solution.\n\n**NOTE:** Each correct selection is worth one point.","explanationEn":"Azure Policy assignments can be applied at management group, subscription, and resource group scopes, with inheritance to contained resources. Management groups are particularly suited to governing multiple subscriptions consistently.\n\n**Learn more:** [Overview of Azure Policy](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/governance/policy/overview)","explanationKo":"Azure Policy assignments can be applied at management group, subscription, and resource group scopes, with inheritance to contained resources. Management groups are particularly suited to governing multiple subscriptions consistently.\n\n**Learn more:** [Overview of Azure Policy](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/governance/policy/overview)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Azure Active Directory (Azure AD) administrative units","ko":"Azure Active Directory (Azure AD) administrative units"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure Active Directory (Azure AD) tenants","ko":"Azure Active Directory (Azure AD) tenants"},{"label":"C","en":"subscriptions","ko":"subscriptions"},{"label":"D","en":"compute resources","ko":"compute resources"},{"label":"E","en":"resource groups","ko":"resource groups"},{"label":"F","en":"management groups","ko":"management groups"}],"answers":["CEF"]},{"n":76,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You have an Azure subscription containing 10 web apps. The apps are integrated with Azure AD and are accessed by users from different project teams.\n\nUsers frequently move between projects.\n\nYou need to recommend an access-management solution for the web apps. The solution must meet these requirements:\n\n- Users must have access only to the app for the project to which they are currently assigned.\n- Project managers must verify which users can access their project’s app and remove users who are no longer assigned to that project.\n- Every 30 days, project managers must automatically be prompted to verify which users are assigned to their projects.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","stemKo":"You have an Azure subscription containing 10 web apps. The apps are integrated with Azure AD and are accessed by users from different project teams.\n\nUsers frequently move between projects.\n\nYou need to recommend an access-management solution for the web apps. The solution must meet these requirements:\n\n- Users must have access only to the app for the project to which they are currently assigned.\n- Project managers must verify which users can access their project’s app and remove users who are no longer assigned to that project.\n- Every 30 days, project managers must automatically be prompted to verify which users are assigned to their projects.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","explanationEn":"Microsoft Entra ID Governance provides access reviews for applications. Designated reviewers, such as project managers, can periodically review application assignments and recertify or deny users’ continued access; review outcomes can automatically remove users who no longer require access. Recurring reviews can be scheduled every 30 days.\n\n**Learn more:** [Plan a Microsoft Entra access reviews deployment](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/id-governance/deploy-access-reviews) · [Manage user and guest user access with access reviews](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/id-governance/manage-access-review)","explanationKo":"Microsoft Entra ID Governance provides access reviews for applications. Designated reviewers, such as project managers, can periodically review application assignments and recertify or deny users’ continued access; review outcomes can automatically remove users who no longer require access. Recurring reviews can be scheduled every 30 days.\n\n**Learn more:** [Plan a Microsoft Entra access reviews deployment](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/id-governance/deploy-access-reviews) · [Manage user and guest user access with access reviews](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/id-governance/manage-access-review)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Azure AD Identity Protection","ko":"Azure AD Identity Protection"},{"label":"B","en":"Microsoft Defender for Identity","ko":"Microsoft Defender for Identity"},{"label":"C","en":"Microsoft Entra Permissions Management","ko":"Microsoft Entra Permissions Management"},{"label":"D","en":"Azure AD Identity Governance","ko":"Azure AD Identity Governance"}],"answers":["D"]},{"n":77,"id":null,"type":"dropdown","topic":"Design data storage solutions","topicKo":"데이터 저장소 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You have an on-premises file server that contains 2 TB of data files. You plan to move the data files to Azure Blob Storage in the West Europe Azure region.\n\nYou need to recommend a storage account type for the data files and a replication solution for the storage account. The solution must meet these requirements:\n\n- Remain available if a single Azure datacenter fails.\n- Support storage tiers.\n- Minimize cost.\n\nWhat should you recommend?","stemKo":"You have an on-premises file server that contains 2 TB of data files. You plan to move the data files to Azure Blob Storage in the West Europe Azure region.\n\nYou need to recommend a storage account type for the data files and a replication solution for the storage account. The solution must meet these requirements:\n\n- Remain available if a single Azure datacenter fails.\n- Support storage tiers.\n- Minimize cost.\n\nWhat should you recommend?","explanationEn":"Standard general-purpose v2 accounts support Azure Blob Storage access tiers. ZRS replicates data synchronously across three Azure availability zones in the primary region, so a single datacenter or zone failure does not make the data unavailable. It meets that requirement without the additional cross-region replication cost of GRS or RA-GRS; LRS does not protect against a datacenter failure.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure storage account overview](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/common/storage-account-overview) · [Azure Storage redundancy](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/common/storage-redundancy)","explanationKo":"Standard general-purpose v2 accounts support Azure Blob Storage access tiers. ZRS replicates data synchronously across three Azure availability zones in the primary region, so a single datacenter or zone failure does not make the data unavailable. It meets that requirement without the additional cross-region replication cost of GRS or RA-GRS; LRS does not protect against a datacenter failure.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure storage account overview](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/common/storage-account-overview) · [Azure Storage redundancy](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/common/storage-redundancy)","learnMore":[],"blanks":[{"id":"storage_account_type","labelEn":"Storage Account type:","labelKo":"Storage Account type:","options":[{"en":"Premium block blobs","ko":"Premium block blobs"},{"en":"Standard general-purpose v1","ko":"Standard general-purpose v1"},{"en":"Standard general-purpose v2","ko":"Standard general-purpose v2"}],"answer":"Standard general-purpose v2"},{"id":"redundancy","labelEn":"Redundancy:","labelKo":"Redundancy:","options":[{"en":"Geo-redundant storage (GRS)","ko":"Geo-redundant storage (GRS)"},{"en":"Zone-redundant storage (ZRS)","ko":"Zone-redundant storage (ZRS)"},{"en":"Locally-redundant storage (LRS)","ko":"Locally-redundant storage (LRS)"},{"en":"Read-access geo-redundant storage (RA-GRS)","ko":"Read-access geo-redundant storage (RA-GRS)"}],"answer":"Zone-redundant storage (ZRS)"}],"template":""},{"n":78,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design data storage solutions","topicKo":"데이터 저장소 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You intend to deploy an app that will use an Azure Storage account.\n\nYou must deploy the storage account. It must meet these requirements:\n\n- Store data for multiple users.\n- Encrypt each user's data with a separate key.\n- Encrypt all data in the storage account by using customer-managed keys.\n\nWhat should you deploy?","stemKo":"You intend to deploy an app that will use an Azure Storage account.\n\nYou must deploy the storage account. It must meet these requirements:\n\n- Store data for multiple users.\n- Encrypt each user's data with a separate key.\n- Encrypt all data in the storage account by using customer-managed keys.\n\nWhat should you deploy?","explanationEn":"Blob Storage encryption scopes create separate encryption boundaries for data belonging to different customers or users. Each scope can use a customer-managed key from Azure Key Vault or Managed HSM and can be applied to a container or individual blob. A general-purpose v2 storage account supports Blob Storage and customer-managed keys for account encryption.\n\n**Learn more:** [Encryption scopes for Blob storage - Azure Storage](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/blobs/encryption-scope-overview) · [Azure Storage encryption for data at rest](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/common/storage-service-encryption)","explanationKo":"Blob Storage encryption scopes create separate encryption boundaries for data belonging to different customers or users. Each scope can use a customer-managed key from Azure Key Vault or Managed HSM and can be applied to a container or individual blob. A general-purpose v2 storage account supports Blob Storage and customer-managed keys for account encryption.\n\n**Learn more:** [Encryption scopes for Blob storage - Azure Storage](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/blobs/encryption-scope-overview) · [Azure Storage encryption for data at rest](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/common/storage-service-encryption)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"files in a premium file share storage account","ko":"files in a premium file share storage account"},{"label":"B","en":"blobs in a general purpose v2 storage account","ko":"blobs in a general purpose v2 storage account"},{"label":"C","en":"blobs in an Azure Data Lake Storage Gen2 account","ko":"blobs in an Azure Data Lake Storage Gen2 account"},{"label":"D","en":"files in a general purpose v2 storage account","ko":"files in a general purpose v2 storage account"}],"answers":["B"]},{"n":79,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design data storage solutions","topicKo":"데이터 저장소 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You need to recommend an Azure Storage solution that meets these requirements:\n\n- The storage must support 1 PB of data.\n- Data must be stored in blob storage.\n- The storage must support three levels of subfolders.\n- The storage must support access control lists (ACLs).\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","stemKo":"You need to recommend an Azure Storage solution that meets these requirements:\n\n- The storage must support 1 PB of data.\n- Data must be stored in blob storage.\n- The storage must support three levels of subfolders.\n- The storage must support access control lists (ACLs).\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","explanationEn":"A general-purpose v2 storage account with hierarchical namespace enabled provides Azure Data Lake Storage capabilities: real nested directories and POSIX-compliant ACLs for blob data. Hierarchical namespace support preserves object-storage scalability, so it meets the 1 PB requirement.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure Data Lake Storage hierarchical namespace](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/blobs/data-lake-storage-namespace) · [Use the Azure portal to manage ACLs in Azure Data Lake Storage](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/blobs/data-lake-storage-acl-azure-portal)","explanationKo":"A general-purpose v2 storage account with hierarchical namespace enabled provides Azure Data Lake Storage capabilities: real nested directories and POSIX-compliant ACLs for blob data. Hierarchical namespace support preserves object-storage scalability, so it meets the 1 PB requirement.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure Data Lake Storage hierarchical namespace](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/blobs/data-lake-storage-namespace) · [Use the Azure portal to manage ACLs in Azure Data Lake Storage](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/blobs/data-lake-storage-acl-azure-portal)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"a premium storage account that is configured for block blobs","ko":"a premium storage account that is configured for block blobs"},{"label":"B","en":"a general purpose v2 storage account that has hierarchical namespace enabled","ko":"a general purpose v2 storage account that has hierarchical namespace enabled"},{"label":"C","en":"a premium storage account that is configured for page blobs","ko":"a premium storage account that is configured for page blobs"},{"label":"D","en":"a premium storage account that is configured for file shares and supports large file shares","ko":"a premium storage account that is configured for file shares and supports large file shares"}],"answers":["B"]},{"n":80,"id":null,"type":"dropdown","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You are designing a software as a service (SaaS) application that enables Azure Active Directory (Azure AD) users to create and publish online surveys. The SaaS application has a front-end web app and a back-end web API. The web app relies on the web API to process updates to customer surveys.\n\nDesign an authorization flow that meets these requirements:\n\n- To access the back-end web API, the web app must authenticate by using OAuth 2 bearer tokens.\n- The web app must authenticate by using the identities of individual users.\n\nWhat should the solution include?","stemKo":"You are designing a software as a service (SaaS) application that enables Azure Active Directory (Azure AD) users to create and publish online surveys. The SaaS application has a front-end web app and a back-end web API. The web app relies on the web API to process updates to customer surveys.\n\nDesign an authorization flow that meets these requirements:\n\n- To access the back-end web API, the web app must authenticate by using OAuth 2 bearer tokens.\n- The web app must authenticate by using the identities of individual users.\n\nWhat should the solution include?","explanationEn":"Azure AD acts as the authorization server and issues an access token after authenticating the individual user. The web API is the protected resource; it validates the token and checks the delegated scopes or roles to authorize the requested operation.\n\n**Learn more:** [Access tokens in the Microsoft identity platform](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity-platform/access-tokens) · [Implement authorization in web APIs with Microsoft.Identity.Web](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/msidweb/authentication/authorization)","explanationKo":"Azure AD acts as the authorization server and issues an access token after authenticating the individual user. The web API is the protected resource; it validates the token and checks the delegated scopes or roles to authorize the requested operation.\n\n**Learn more:** [Access tokens in the Microsoft identity platform](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity-platform/access-tokens) · [Implement authorization in web APIs with Microsoft.Identity.Web](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/msidweb/authentication/authorization)","learnMore":[],"blanks":[{"id":"token_generator","labelEn":"The access tokens will be generated by:","labelKo":"The access tokens will be generated by:","options":[{"en":"Azure AD","ko":"Azure AD"},{"en":"A web app","ko":"A web app"},{"en":"A web API","ko":"A web API"}],"answer":"Azure AD"},{"id":"authorization_decisions","labelEn":"Authorization decisions will be performed by:","labelKo":"Authorization decisions will be performed by:","options":[{"en":"Azure AD","ko":"Azure AD"},{"en":"A web app","ko":"A web app"},{"en":"A web API","ko":"A web API"}],"answer":"A web API"}],"template":""},{"n":81,"id":null,"type":"dropdown","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"What should be implemented to satisfy the identity requirements?","stemKo":"What should be implemented to satisfy the identity requirements?","explanationEn":"Microsoft Entra ID Governance (formerly Azure AD Identity Governance) includes access reviews, which support recurring review and recertification of access to groups, enterprise applications, and privileged roles.\n\n**Learn more:** [Microsoft Entra ID Governance documentation](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/id-governance/identity-governance-overview) · [Access reviews overview](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/id-governance/access-reviews-overview)","explanationKo":"Microsoft Entra ID Governance (formerly Azure AD Identity Governance) includes access reviews, which support recurring review and recertification of access to groups, enterprise applications, and privileged roles.\n\n**Learn more:** [Microsoft Entra ID Governance documentation](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/id-governance/identity-governance-overview) · [Access reviews overview](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/id-governance/access-reviews-overview)","learnMore":[],"blanks":[{"id":"service","labelEn":"Service:","labelKo":"Service:","options":[{"en":"Azure AD Identity Governance","ko":"Azure AD Identity Governance"},{"en":"Azure AD Identity Protection","ko":"Azure AD Identity Protection"},{"en":"Azure AD Privilege Access Management (PIM)","ko":"Azure AD Privilege Access Management (PIM)"},{"en":"Azure Automation","ko":"Azure Automation"}],"answer":"Azure AD Identity Governance"},{"id":"feature","labelEn":"Feature:","labelKo":"Feature:","options":[{"en":"Access packages","ko":"Access packages"},{"en":"Access reviews","ko":"Access reviews"},{"en":"Approvals","ko":"Approvals"},{"en":"Runbooks","ko":"Runbooks"}],"answer":"Access reviews"}],"template":""},{"n":82,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You must recommend a solution for generating a monthly report of every new Azure Resource Manager (ARM) resource deployment in your Azure subscription.\n\nWhat should the recommendation include?","stemKo":"You must recommend a solution for generating a monthly report of every new Azure Resource Manager (ARM) resource deployment in your Azure subscription.\n\nWhat should the recommendation include?","explanationEn":"Azure Activity Log captures subscription-level Azure Resource Manager control-plane operations, including resource creation and deployment-related events. Its administrative events can be reviewed or filtered to identify new resource deployments over a monthly reporting period.\n\n**Learn more:** [Activity log in Azure Monitor](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-monitor/platform/activity-log) · [Azure Activity Log event schema](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-monitor/platform/activity-log-schema)","explanationKo":"Azure Activity Log captures subscription-level Azure Resource Manager control-plane operations, including resource creation and deployment-related events. Its administrative events can be reviewed or filtered to identify new resource deployments over a monthly reporting period.\n\n**Learn more:** [Activity log in Azure Monitor](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-monitor/platform/activity-log) · [Azure Activity Log event schema](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-monitor/platform/activity-log-schema)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Application Insights","ko":"Application Insights"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure Analysis Services","ko":"Azure Analysis Services"},{"label":"C","en":"Azure Advisor","ko":"Azure Advisor"},{"label":"D","en":"Azure Activity Log","ko":"Azure Activity Log"}],"answers":["D"]},{"n":83,"id":null,"type":"dropdown","topic":"Design data storage solutions","topicKo":"데이터 저장소 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You need to design a storage solution for an app that will store large quantities of frequently accessed data. The solution must meet these requirements:\n\n- Maximize data throughput.\n- Prevent data modifications for one year.\n- Minimize read and write latency.\n\nWhich Azure Storage account type and storage service should you recommend?","stemKo":"You need to design a storage solution for an app that will store large quantities of frequently accessed data. The solution must meet these requirements:\n\n- Maximize data throughput.\n- Prevent data modifications for one year.\n- Minimize read and write latency.\n\nWhich Azure Storage account type and storage service should you recommend?","explanationEn":"A premium BlockBlobStorage account is optimized for low-latency, high-throughput block blob workloads. Azure Blob Storage supports immutable (WORM) policies that prevent modification or deletion for the configured retention period, such as one year.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure Blob Storage immutable storage for legal hold and time-based retention policies](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/blobs/immutable-storage-overview) · [Azure premium block blob storage](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/blobs/storage-blob-block-blob-premium)","explanationKo":"A premium BlockBlobStorage account is optimized for low-latency, high-throughput block blob workloads. Azure Blob Storage supports immutable (WORM) policies that prevent modification or deletion for the configured retention period, such as one year.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure Blob Storage immutable storage for legal hold and time-based retention policies](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/blobs/immutable-storage-overview) · [Azure premium block blob storage](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/blobs/storage-blob-block-blob-premium)","learnMore":[],"blanks":[{"id":"storage_account_type","labelEn":"Storage account type:","labelKo":"Storage account type:","options":[{"en":"BlobStorage","ko":"BlobStorage"},{"en":"BlockBlobStorage","ko":"BlockBlobStorage"},{"en":"FileStorage","ko":"FileStorage"},{"en":"StorageV2 with Premium performance","ko":"StorageV2 with Premium performance"},{"en":"StorageV2 with Standard performance","ko":"StorageV2 with Standard performance"}],"answer":"BlockBlobStorage"},{"id":"storage_service","labelEn":"Storage service:","labelKo":"Storage service:","options":[{"en":"Blob","ko":"Blob"},{"en":"File","ko":"File"},{"en":"Table","ko":"Table"}],"answer":"Blob"}],"template":""},{"n":84,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design data storage solutions","topicKo":"데이터 저장소 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You have an on-premises storage solution.\n\nYou need to migrate the solution to Azure. The solution must support the Hadoop Distributed File System (HDFS).\n\nWhat should you use?","stemKo":"You have an on-premises storage solution.\n\nYou need to migrate the solution to Azure. The solution must support the Hadoop Distributed File System (HDFS).\n\nWhat should you use?","explanationEn":"Azure Data Lake Storage Gen2 provides a hierarchical namespace and Hadoop-compatible file-system access, enabling data to be managed through HDFS-compatible interfaces and the ABFS driver.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure Data Lake Storage Gen2 overview in HDInsight](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/hdinsight/overview-data-lake-storage-gen2) · [Using the HDFS CLI with Azure Data Lake Storage](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/blobs/data-lake-storage-use-hdfs-data-lake-storage)","explanationKo":"Azure Data Lake Storage Gen2 provides a hierarchical namespace and Hadoop-compatible file-system access, enabling data to be managed through HDFS-compatible interfaces and the ABFS driver.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure Data Lake Storage Gen2 overview in HDInsight](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/hdinsight/overview-data-lake-storage-gen2) · [Using the HDFS CLI with Azure Data Lake Storage](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/blobs/data-lake-storage-use-hdfs-data-lake-storage)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Azure Data Lake Storage Gen2","ko":"Azure Data Lake Storage Gen2"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure NetApp Files","ko":"Azure NetApp Files"},{"label":"C","en":"Azure Data Share","ko":"Azure Data Share"},{"label":"D","en":"Azure Table storage","ko":"Azure Table storage"}],"answers":["A"]},{"n":85,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design infrastructure solutions","topicKo":"인프라 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You have an Azure Functions microservice app named App1, hosted in the Consumption plan. App1 uses an Azure Queue Storage trigger.\n\nYou plan to migrate App1 to an Azure Kubernetes Service (AKS) cluster.\n\nYou need to ready the AKS cluster to support App1. The solution must meet these requirements:\n\n- Use the same scaling mechanism as the existing deployment.\n- Support kubenet and Azure Container Networking Interface (CNI) networking.\n\nWhich two actions should you perform? Each correct answer presents part of the solution.\n\nNOTE: Each correct answer is worth one point.","stemKo":"You have an Azure Functions microservice app named App1, hosted in the Consumption plan. App1 uses an Azure Queue Storage trigger.\n\nYou plan to migrate App1 to an Azure Kubernetes Service (AKS) cluster.\n\nYou need to ready the AKS cluster to support App1. The solution must meet these requirements:\n\n- Use the same scaling mechanism as the existing deployment.\n- Support kubenet and Azure Container Networking Interface (CNI) networking.\n\nWhich two actions should you perform? Each correct answer presents part of the solution.\n\nNOTE: Each correct answer is worth one point.","explanationEn":"KEDA provides event-driven autoscaling for Azure Functions containers on Kubernetes and supports Azure Storage Queue triggers. It feeds external event metrics to the Kubernetes Horizontal Pod Autoscaler (HPA), which scales the function pods. This preserves the Consumption-plan-style, queue-driven scaling model and does not depend on virtual nodes, which are unsupported with kubenet.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure Functions on Kubernetes with KEDA](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-functions/functions-kubernetes-keda) · [Kubernetes Event-driven Autoscaling (KEDA) on AKS](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/aks/keda-about)","explanationKo":"KEDA provides event-driven autoscaling for Azure Functions containers on Kubernetes and supports Azure Storage Queue triggers. It feeds external event metrics to the Kubernetes Horizontal Pod Autoscaler (HPA), which scales the function pods. This preserves the Consumption-plan-style, queue-driven scaling model and does not depend on virtual nodes, which are unsupported with kubenet.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure Functions on Kubernetes with KEDA](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-functions/functions-kubernetes-keda) · [Kubernetes Event-driven Autoscaling (KEDA) on AKS](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/aks/keda-about)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Configure the horizontal pod autoscaler.","ko":"Configure the horizontal pod autoscaler."},{"label":"B","en":"Install Virtual Kubelet.","ko":"Install Virtual Kubelet."},{"label":"C","en":"Configure the AKS cluster autoscaler.","ko":"Configure the AKS cluster autoscaler."},{"label":"D","en":"Configure the virtual node add-on.","ko":"Configure the virtual node add-on."},{"label":"E","en":"Install Kubernetes-based Event Driven Autoscaling (KEDA).","ko":"Install Kubernetes-based Event Driven Autoscaling (KEDA)."}],"answers":["AE"]},{"n":86,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design business continuity solutions","topicKo":"업무 연속성 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You must design a highly available Azure SQL database that satisfies these requirements:\n\n- Failover between database replicas must take place without data loss.\n- The database must stay available if a zone outage occurs.\n- Costs must be kept to a minimum.\n\nWhich deployment option should you use?","stemKo":"You must design a highly available Azure SQL database that satisfies these requirements:\n\n- Failover between database replicas must take place without data loss.\n- The database must stay available if a zone outage occurs.\n- Costs must be kept to a minimum.\n\nWhich deployment option should you use?","explanationEn":"Azure SQL Database Premium supports zone redundancy, which distributes synchronous replicas across availability zones. This provides resilience to an availability-zone outage with no expected loss of committed data. The Basic tier does not support zone redundancy, and Azure SQL Managed Instance Business Critical is a more costly option for these requirements.\n\n**Learn more:** [Reliability in Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/reliability/reliability-sql-database) · [Enable zone redundancy for Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/database/enable-zone-redundancy?view=azuresql)","explanationKo":"Azure SQL Database Premium supports zone redundancy, which distributes synchronous replicas across availability zones. This provides resilience to an availability-zone outage with no expected loss of committed data. The Basic tier does not support zone redundancy, and Azure SQL Managed Instance Business Critical is a more costly option for these requirements.\n\n**Learn more:** [Reliability in Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/reliability/reliability-sql-database) · [Enable zone redundancy for Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/database/enable-zone-redundancy?view=azuresql)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Azure SQL Managed Instance Business Critical","ko":"Azure SQL Managed Instance Business Critical"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure SQL Database Premium","ko":"Azure SQL Database Premium"},{"label":"C","en":"Azure SQL Database Basic","ko":"Azure SQL Database Basic"},{"label":"D","en":"Azure SQL Managed Instance General Purpose","ko":"Azure SQL Managed Instance General Purpose"}],"answers":["B"]},{"n":87,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design data storage solutions","topicKo":"데이터 저장소 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"Web access-log data is stored in Azure Blob Storage.\n\nYou plan to create monthly reports from the access logs.\n\nYou need to recommend an automated process that uploads the data to Azure SQL Database each month.\n\nWhat should the recommendation include?","stemKo":"Web access-log data is stored in Azure Blob Storage.\n\nYou plan to create monthly reports from the access logs.\n\nYou need to recommend an automated process that uploads the data to Azure SQL Database each month.\n\nWhat should the recommendation include?","explanationEn":"Azure Data Factory can orchestrate a scheduled monthly pipeline and use a Copy activity to load data from Azure Blob Storage into Azure SQL Database. Microsoft Learn documents this Blob Storage-to-Azure SQL Database pipeline pattern.\n\n**Learn more:** [Copy data from Azure Blob to Azure SQL Database using Azure Data Factory](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/data-factory/tutorial-copy-data-dot-net)","explanationKo":"Azure Data Factory can orchestrate a scheduled monthly pipeline and use a Copy activity to load data from Azure Blob Storage into Azure SQL Database. Microsoft Learn documents this Blob Storage-to-Azure SQL Database pipeline pattern.\n\n**Learn more:** [Copy data from Azure Blob to Azure SQL Database using Azure Data Factory](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/data-factory/tutorial-copy-data-dot-net)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Microsoft SQL Server Migration Assistant (SSMA)","ko":"Microsoft SQL Server Migration Assistant (SSMA)"},{"label":"B","en":"Data Migration Assistant (DMA)","ko":"Data Migration Assistant (DMA)"},{"label":"C","en":"AzCopy","ko":"AzCopy"},{"label":"D","en":"Azure Data Factory","ko":"Azure Data Factory"}],"answers":["D"]},{"n":88,"id":null,"type":"statements","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":["assets/1783707674258-dkea0ktc.png"],"stemEn":"HOTSPOT -\n\nYou have an Azure subscription containing the resources shown in the following table.\n\n[[IMG1]]\n\nYou create an Azure SQL database named DB1 that is hosted in the East US Azure region.\n\nYou add a diagnostic setting named Settings1 to DB1. Settings1 archives SQLInsights to storage1 and sends SQLInsights to Workspace1.\n\nFor each of the following statements, select **Yes** if the statement is true. Otherwise, select **No**.","stemKo":"HOTSPOT -\n\nYou have an Azure subscription containing the resources shown in the following table.\n\n[[IMG1]]\n\nYou create an Azure SQL database named DB1 that is hosted in the East US Azure region.\n\nYou add a diagnostic setting named Settings1 to DB1. Settings1 archives SQLInsights to storage1 and sends SQLInsights to Workspace1.\n\nFor each of the following statements, select **Yes** if the statement is true. Otherwise, select **No**.","explanationEn":"Azure SQL Database diagnostic telemetry can be sent to Azure Storage, Azure Event Hubs, or a Log Analytics workspace. Multiple parallel diagnostic settings are supported. Storage2 is a supported general-purpose v2 account, and the regional storage and Event Hubs destinations are in the same East US region as DB1. Thus, each proposed destination can be used by an additional diagnostic setting.\n\n**Learn more:** [Configure streaming export of metrics and resource logs for Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/database/metrics-diagnostic-telemetry-logging-streaming-export-configure?view=azuresql) · [Diagnostic settings in Azure Monitor](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-monitor/essentials/diagnostic-settings)","explanationKo":"Azure SQL Database diagnostic telemetry can be sent to Azure Storage, Azure Event Hubs, or a Log Analytics workspace. Multiple parallel diagnostic settings are supported. Storage2 is a supported general-purpose v2 account, and the regional storage and Event Hubs destinations are in the same East US region as DB1. Thus, each proposed destination can be used by an additional diagnostic setting.\n\n**Learn more:** [Configure streaming export of metrics and resource logs for Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/database/metrics-diagnostic-telemetry-logging-streaming-export-configure?view=azuresql) · [Diagnostic settings in Azure Monitor](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-monitor/essentials/diagnostic-settings)","learnMore":[],"statements":[{"en":"You can add a new diagnostic setting that archives SQLInsights logs to storage2.","ko":"You can add a new diagnostic setting that archives SQLInsights logs to storage2.","answer":"Yes"},{"en":"You can add a new diagnostic setting that sends SQLInsights logs to Workspace2.","ko":"You can add a new diagnostic setting that sends SQLInsights logs to Workspace2.","answer":"Yes"},{"en":"You can add a new diagnostic setting that sends SQLInsights logs to Hub1.","ko":"You can add a new diagnostic setting that sends SQLInsights logs to Hub1.","answer":"Yes"}],"columns":["Yes","No"]},{"n":89,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You need to recommend a solution that generates a monthly report of all new Azure Resource Manager (ARM) resource deployments in your Azure subscription.\n\nWhat should the recommendation include?","stemKo":"You need to recommend a solution that generates a monthly report of all new Azure Resource Manager (ARM) resource deployments in your Azure subscription.\n\nWhat should the recommendation include?","explanationEn":"Azure activity logs capture Azure Resource Manager control-plane operations, including resource creation and deployment-related events. Sending the activity log to a Log Analytics workspace allows the events to be queried with KQL for a monthly report.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure Monitor activity log](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-monitor/platform/activity-log) · [Monitor Azure Resource Manager](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-resource-manager/management/monitor-resource-manager)","explanationKo":"Azure activity logs capture Azure Resource Manager control-plane operations, including resource creation and deployment-related events. Sending the activity log to a Log Analytics workspace allows the events to be queried with KQL for a monthly report.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure Monitor activity log](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-monitor/platform/activity-log) · [Monitor Azure Resource Manager](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-resource-manager/management/monitor-resource-manager)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Application Insights","ko":"Application Insights"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure Arc","ko":"Azure Arc"},{"label":"C","en":"Azure Log Analytics","ko":"Azure Log Analytics"},{"label":"D","en":"Azure Monitor metrics","ko":"Azure Monitor metrics"}],"answers":["C"]},{"n":90,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"What should you recommend to satisfy the monitoring requirements for App2?","stemKo":"What should you recommend to satisfy the monitoring requirements for App2?","explanationEn":"Azure Application Insights provides application performance monitoring by collecting and analyzing application telemetry, including availability, failures, dependencies, and performance data.\n\n**Learn more:** [Application Insights OpenTelemetry observability overview - Azure Monitor](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-monitor/app/app-insights-overview)","explanationKo":"Azure Application Insights provides application performance monitoring by collecting and analyzing application telemetry, including availability, failures, dependencies, and performance data.\n\n**Learn more:** [Application Insights OpenTelemetry observability overview - Azure Monitor](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-monitor/app/app-insights-overview)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"VM insights","ko":"VM insights"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure Application Insights","ko":"Azure Application Insights"},{"label":"C","en":"Microsoft Sentinel","ko":"Microsoft Sentinel"},{"label":"D","en":"Container insights","ko":"Container insights"}],"answers":["B"]},{"n":91,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design infrastructure solutions","topicKo":"인프라 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"Your company operates offices in North America and Europe.\n\nYou plan to migrate to Azure.\n\nYou need to recommend a networking solution for the new Azure infrastructure. The solution must meet these requirements:\n\n- Point-to-Site (P2S) VPN connections for mobile users must automatically connect to the nearest Azure region.\n- Offices in each region must connect to their local Azure region by using an ExpressRoute circuit.\n- Transitive routing between virtual networks and on-premises networks must be supported.\n- Network traffic between virtual networks must be filtered by using FQDNs.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","stemKo":"Your company operates offices in North America and Europe.\n\nYou plan to migrate to Azure.\n\nYou need to recommend a networking solution for the new Azure infrastructure. The solution must meet these requirements:\n\n- Point-to-Site (P2S) VPN connections for mobile users must automatically connect to the nearest Azure region.\n- Offices in each region must connect to their local Azure region by using an ExpressRoute circuit.\n- Transitive routing between virtual networks and on-premises networks must be supported.\n- Network traffic between virtual networks must be filtered by using FQDNs.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","explanationEn":"Azure Virtual WAN provides regional virtual hubs with P2S and ExpressRoute gateway connectivity and managed transitive routing among connected virtual networks and on-premises networks. Its global User VPN profile directs a user to the closest Virtual WAN hub. A secured virtual hub integrates Azure Firewall for traffic inspection between virtual networks; Azure Firewall application rules support FQDN-based filtering.\n\n**Learn more:** [Download global and hub VPN profiles for User VPN clients](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/virtual-wan/global-hub-profile) · [Azure Virtual WAN overview](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/virtual-wan/virtual-wan-about)","explanationKo":"Azure Virtual WAN provides regional virtual hubs with P2S and ExpressRoute gateway connectivity and managed transitive routing among connected virtual networks and on-premises networks. Its global User VPN profile directs a user to the closest Virtual WAN hub. A secured virtual hub integrates Azure Firewall for traffic inspection between virtual networks; Azure Firewall application rules support FQDN-based filtering.\n\n**Learn more:** [Download global and hub VPN profiles for User VPN clients](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/virtual-wan/global-hub-profile) · [Azure Virtual WAN overview](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/virtual-wan/virtual-wan-about)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Azure Virtual WAN with a secured virtual hub","ko":"Azure Virtual WAN with a secured virtual hub"},{"label":"B","en":"virtual network peering and application security groups","ko":"virtual network peering and application security groups"},{"label":"C","en":"virtual network gateways and network security groups (NSGs)","ko":"virtual network gateways and network security groups (NSGs)"},{"label":"D","en":"Azure Route Server and Azure Network Function Manager","ko":"Azure Route Server and Azure Network Function Manager"}],"answers":["A"]},{"n":92,"id":null,"type":"statements","topic":"Design data storage solutions","topicKo":"데이터 저장소 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You are assessing the components of an Azure migration that require provisioning an Azure Storage account. For each statement, select Yes when it is true; otherwise, select No.","stemKo":"You are assessing the components of an Azure migration that require provisioning an Azure Storage account. For each statement, select Yes when it is true; otherwise, select No.","explanationEn":"Backup-based SQL Server migrations use an Azure Blob Storage account as intermediate storage for database backup files. Azure Storage supports hosting static website content. Database metrics are collected and monitored by Azure Monitor, so a Storage account is not required solely for metric monitoring.\n\n**Learn more:** [Prepare environment for a SQL VM migration](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/sql/sql-server/azure-arc/migration-sql-vm-prepare?view=sql-server-ver17) · [Static website hosting in Azure Storage](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/blobs/storage-blob-static-website)","explanationKo":"Backup-based SQL Server migrations use an Azure Blob Storage account as intermediate storage for database backup files. Azure Storage supports hosting static website content. Database metrics are collected and monitored by Azure Monitor, so a Storage account is not required solely for metric monitoring.\n\n**Learn more:** [Prepare environment for a SQL VM migration](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/sql/sql-server/azure-arc/migration-sql-vm-prepare?view=sql-server-ver17) · [Static website hosting in Azure Storage](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/blobs/storage-blob-static-website)","learnMore":[],"statements":[{"en":"You must provision an Azure Storage account for the SQL Server database migration.","ko":"You must provision an Azure Storage account for the SQL Server database migration.","answer":"Yes"},{"en":"You must provision an Azure Storage account for the Web site content storage.","ko":"You must provision an Azure Storage account for the Web site content storage.","answer":"Yes"},{"en":"You must provision an Azure Storage account for the Database metric monitoring.","ko":"You must provision an Azure Storage account for the Database metric monitoring.","answer":"No"}],"columns":["Yes","No"]},{"n":93,"id":null,"type":"dropdown","topic":"Design data storage solutions","topicKo":"데이터 저장소 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You are developing an Azure web app that will store employees’ Personally Identifiable Information (PII).\n\nYou need to recommend an Azure SQL Database solution for the web app. The solution must satisfy these requirements:\n\n- Preserve availability if a single datacenter fails.\n- Enable encryption for particular columns containing PII.\n- Scale up automatically during payroll processing.\n- Keep costs to a minimum.\n\nWhat should the recommendations include?","stemKo":"You are developing an Azure web app that will store employees’ Personally Identifiable Information (PII).\n\nYou need to recommend an Azure SQL Database solution for the web app. The solution must satisfy these requirements:\n\n- Preserve availability if a single datacenter fails.\n- Enable encryption for particular columns containing PII.\n- Scale up automatically during payroll processing.\n- Keep costs to a minimum.\n\nWhat should the recommendations include?","explanationEn":"A zone-redundant General Purpose Azure SQL Database is resilient to an availability-zone/datacenter outage. Serverless compute automatically scales based on workload demand and can auto-pause during inactivity, reducing cost. Always Encrypted protects selected sensitive columns, whereas TDE encrypts the database at rest.\n\n**Learn more:** [Serverless compute tier - Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/database/serverless-tier-overview?view=azuresql) · [Reliability in Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/reliability/reliability-sql-database)","explanationKo":"A zone-redundant General Purpose Azure SQL Database is resilient to an availability-zone/datacenter outage. Serverless compute automatically scales based on workload demand and can auto-pause during inactivity, reducing cost. Always Encrypted protects selected sensitive columns, whereas TDE encrypts the database at rest.\n\n**Learn more:** [Serverless compute tier - Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/database/serverless-tier-overview?view=azuresql) · [Reliability in Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/reliability/reliability-sql-database)","learnMore":[],"blanks":[{"id":"service_tier","labelEn":"Service tier and computer tier:","labelKo":"Service tier and computer tier:","options":[{"en":"Business Critical service tier and Serverless computer tier","ko":"Business Critical service tier and Serverless computer tier"},{"en":"General Purpose service tier and Serverless computer tier","ko":"General Purpose service tier and Serverless computer tier"},{"en":"Hyperscale service tier and Provisioned compute tier","ko":"Hyperscale service tier and Provisioned compute tier"}],"answer":"General Purpose service tier and Serverless computer tier"},{"id":"encryption","labelEn":"Encryption method:","labelKo":"Encryption method:","options":[{"en":"Always Encrypted","ko":"Always Encrypted"},{"en":"Microsoft SQL Server and database encryption keys","ko":"Microsoft SQL Server and database encryption keys"},{"en":"Transparent Data Encryption (TDE)","ko":"Transparent Data Encryption (TDE)"}],"answer":"Always Encrypted"}],"template":""},{"n":94,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design infrastructure solutions","topicKo":"인프라 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You have an Azure virtual machine named VM1 that runs Windows Server 2019 and stores 500 GB of data files.\n\nYou are designing a solution that will use Azure Data Factory to transform the data files and then load them into Azure Data Lake Storage.\n\nWhat should you deploy on VM1 to support this design?","stemKo":"You have an Azure virtual machine named VM1 that runs Windows Server 2019 and stores 500 GB of data files.\n\nYou are designing a solution that will use Azure Data Factory to transform the data files and then load them into Azure Data Lake Storage.\n\nWhat should you deploy on VM1 to support this design?","explanationEn":"A self-hosted integration runtime provides Azure Data Factory with compute and connectivity for data stores in a private network, including an Azure IaaS virtual machine. Installing it on VM1 lets Data Factory access and process the files before loading them to Azure Data Lake Storage.\n\n**Learn more:** [Integration runtime in Azure Data Factory](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/data-factory/concepts-integration-runtime) · [Create and configure a self-hosted integration runtime](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/data-factory/create-self-hosted-integration-runtime)","explanationKo":"A self-hosted integration runtime provides Azure Data Factory with compute and connectivity for data stores in a private network, including an Azure IaaS virtual machine. Installing it on VM1 lets Data Factory access and process the files before loading them to Azure Data Lake Storage.\n\n**Learn more:** [Integration runtime in Azure Data Factory](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/data-factory/concepts-integration-runtime) · [Create and configure a self-hosted integration runtime](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/data-factory/create-self-hosted-integration-runtime)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"the On-premises data gateway","ko":"the On-premises data gateway"},{"label":"B","en":"the Azure Pipelines agent","ko":"the Azure Pipelines agent"},{"label":"C","en":"the self-hosted integration runtime","ko":"the self-hosted integration runtime"},{"label":"D","en":"the Azure File Sync agent","ko":"the Azure File Sync agent"}],"answers":["C"]},{"n":95,"id":null,"type":"dropdown","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You have two Azure AD tenants, contoso.com and fabrikam.com. Each tenant is associated with 50 Azure subscriptions. Contoso.com has two users, User1 and User2.\n\nYou must meet these requirements:\n\n- Ensure User1 can change the Azure AD tenant associated with particular Azure subscriptions.\n- When an Azure subscription is associated with a new Azure AD tenant and no available Azure AD accounts have full subscription-level permissions, elevate User2's access to that subscription.\n\nThe solution must follow the principle of least privilege.\n\nWhich role should be assigned to each user?","stemKo":"You have two Azure AD tenants, contoso.com and fabrikam.com. Each tenant is associated with 50 Azure subscriptions. Contoso.com has two users, User1 and User2.\n\nYou must meet these requirements:\n\n- Ensure User1 can change the Azure AD tenant associated with particular Azure subscriptions.\n- When an Azure subscription is associated with a new Azure AD tenant and no available Azure AD accounts have full subscription-level permissions, elevate User2's access to that subscription.\n\nThe solution must follow the principle of least privilege.\n\nWhich role should be assigned to each user?","explanationEn":"The Service Administrator can change a subscription’s directory association, whereas a Co-administrator cannot. An Owner has full access at subscription scope and is sufficient to restore full subscription-level permissions after the subscription is moved; it avoids giving User2 the additional directory-association permission of the Service Administrator role.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure roles, Microsoft Entra roles, and classic subscription administrator roles](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/role-based-access-control/rbac-and-directory-admin-roles) · [Associate or add an Azure subscription to your Microsoft Entra tenant](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/active-directory/fundamentals/how-subscriptions-associated-directory)","explanationKo":"The Service Administrator can change a subscription’s directory association, whereas a Co-administrator cannot. An Owner has full access at subscription scope and is sufficient to restore full subscription-level permissions after the subscription is moved; it avoids giving User2 the additional directory-association permission of the Service Administrator role.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure roles, Microsoft Entra roles, and classic subscription administrator roles](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/role-based-access-control/rbac-and-directory-admin-roles) · [Associate or add an Azure subscription to your Microsoft Entra tenant](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/active-directory/fundamentals/how-subscriptions-associated-directory)","learnMore":[],"blanks":[{"id":"user1","labelEn":"User1:","labelKo":"User1:","options":[{"en":"Co-administrator","ko":"Co-administrator"},{"en":"Owner","ko":"Owner"},{"en":"Service administrator","ko":"Service administrator"}],"answer":"Service administrator"},{"id":"user2","labelEn":"User2:","labelKo":"User2:","options":[{"en":"Co-administrator","ko":"Co-administrator"},{"en":"Owner","ko":"Owner"},{"en":"Service administrator","ko":"Service administrator"}],"answer":"Owner"}],"template":""},{"n":96,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design data storage solutions","topicKo":"데이터 저장소 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You must recommend a storage solution for the records of a mission-critical application. The solution must provide a Service Level Agreement (SLA) for write-operation latency and throughput.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","stemKo":"You must recommend a storage solution for the records of a mission-critical application. The solution must provide a Service Level Agreement (SLA) for write-operation latency and throughput.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","explanationEn":"Azure Cosmos DB provides SLA-backed write latency and guaranteed provisioned throughput, making it suitable for mission-critical workloads that require predictable performance. Its SLAs cover latency, throughput, consistency, and availability.\n\n**Learn more:** [Reliability in Azure Cosmos DB](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/reliability/reliability-cosmos-db) · [Optimize provisioned throughput cost in Azure Cosmos DB](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/cosmos-db/optimize-cost-throughput)","explanationKo":"Azure Cosmos DB provides SLA-backed write latency and guaranteed provisioned throughput, making it suitable for mission-critical workloads that require predictable performance. Its SLAs cover latency, throughput, consistency, and availability.\n\n**Learn more:** [Reliability in Azure Cosmos DB](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/reliability/reliability-cosmos-db) · [Optimize provisioned throughput cost in Azure Cosmos DB](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/cosmos-db/optimize-cost-throughput)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Azure Data Lake Storage Gen2","ko":"Azure Data Lake Storage Gen2"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure Blob Storage","ko":"Azure Blob Storage"},{"label":"C","en":"Azure SQL","ko":"Azure SQL"},{"label":"D","en":"Azure Cosmos DB","ko":"Azure Cosmos DB"}],"answers":["D"]},{"n":97,"id":null,"type":"drag_drop","topic":"Design data storage solutions","topicKo":"데이터 저장소 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You are designing a virtual machine that will run Microsoft SQL Server and include two data disks. The first data disk will store log files, and the second will store data. Both disks are P40 managed disks.\n\nYou need to recommend a host caching method for each disk. The method must provide the best overall virtual-machine performance while preserving the integrity of the SQL data and logs.\n\nWhich host caching method should you recommend for each disk?\n\nEach method may be used once, more than once, or not at all.","stemKo":"You are designing a virtual machine that will run Microsoft SQL Server and include two data disks. The first data disk will store log files, and the second will store data. Both disks are P40 managed disks.\n\nYou need to recommend a host caching method for each disk. The method must provide the best overall virtual-machine performance while preserving the integrity of the SQL data and logs.\n\nWhich host caching method should you recommend for each disk?\n\nEach method may be used once, more than once, or not at all.","explanationEn":"Use None for the SQL Server transaction-log disk because log I/O is sequential and write-heavy, so ReadOnly caching offers no benefit. Use ReadOnly for the SQL Server data disk to improve read latency, IOPS, and throughput. Do not use ReadWrite caching for SQL Server data or log disks.\n\n**Learn more:** [Storage performance best practices for SQL Server on Azure VMs](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/virtual-machines/windows/performance-guidelines-best-practices-storage?view=azuresql)","explanationKo":"Use None for the SQL Server transaction-log disk because log I/O is sequential and write-heavy, so ReadOnly caching offers no benefit. Use ReadOnly for the SQL Server data disk to improve read latency, IOPS, and throughput. Do not use ReadWrite caching for SQL Server data or log disks.\n\n**Learn more:** [Storage performance best practices for SQL Server on Azure VMs](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/virtual-machines/windows/performance-guidelines-best-practices-storage?view=azuresql)","learnMore":[],"items":[{"en":"None","ko":"None"},{"en":"ReadOnly","ko":"ReadOnly"},{"en":"ReadWrite","ko":"ReadWrite"}],"slots":[{"id":"log","labelEn":"Log:","labelKo":"Log:","answer":"None"},{"id":"data","labelEn":"Data:","labelKo":"Data:","answer":"ReadOnly"}],"reuse":true},{"n":98,"id":null,"type":"drag_drop","topic":"Design infrastructure solutions","topicKo":"인프라 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You have an on-premises datacenter named Site1. Site1 includes a VMware vSphere cluster named Cluster1, which hosts 100 virtual machines. Cluster1 is managed by VMware vCenter.\n\nYou have an Azure subscription named Sub1.\n\nYou plan to migrate the virtual machines from Cluster1 to Sub1.\n\nYou need to identify the resources required to run the virtual machines in Azure while minimizing administrative effort.\n\nWhat should you configure?\n\nEach resource may be used once, more than once, or not at all.","stemKo":"You have an on-premises datacenter named Site1. Site1 includes a VMware vSphere cluster named Cluster1, which hosts 100 virtual machines. Cluster1 is managed by VMware vCenter.\n\nYou have an Azure subscription named Sub1.\n\nYou plan to migrate the virtual machines from Cluster1 to Sub1.\n\nYou need to identify the resources required to run the virtual machines in Azure while minimizing administrative effort.\n\nWhat should you configure?\n\nEach resource may be used once, more than once, or not at all.","explanationEn":"Azure VMware Solution deploys a VMware private cloud in an Azure subscription and supplies the VMware host capacity on which its vSphere clusters run workloads. Azure Migrate components support discovery, assessment, and migration, rather than providing the post-migration VMware compute environment.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure VMware Solution private cloud and cluster concepts](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-vmware/architecture-private-clouds) · [What is Azure VMware Solution?](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-vmware/introduction)","explanationKo":"Azure VMware Solution deploys a VMware private cloud in an Azure subscription and supplies the VMware host capacity on which its vSphere clusters run workloads. Azure Migrate components support discovery, assessment, and migration, rather than providing the post-migration VMware compute environment.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure VMware Solution private cloud and cluster concepts](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-vmware/architecture-private-clouds) · [What is Azure VMware Solution?](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-vmware/introduction)","learnMore":[],"items":[{"en":"An Azure Migrate appliance","ko":"An Azure Migrate appliance"},{"en":"An Azure Migrate project","ko":"An Azure Migrate project"},{"en":"An Azure VMware Solution private cloud","ko":"An Azure VMware Solution private cloud"},{"en":"An Azure VMware Solution host","ko":"An Azure VMware Solution host"}],"slots":[{"id":"sub1","labelEn":"Sub1:","labelKo":"Sub1:","answer":"An Azure VMware Solution private cloud"},{"id":"cluster1","labelEn":"Cluster1:","labelKo":"Cluster1:","answer":"An Azure VMware Solution host"}],"reuse":true},{"n":99,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design data storage solutions","topicKo":"데이터 저장소 설계","koMissing":true,"images":["assets/1783709421550-kgxixp0f.png"],"stemEn":"You have the resources shown in the following table.\n\n[[IMG1]]\n\nCDB1 contains a container that stores operational data updated continuously.\n\nYou are designing a solution that uses AS1 to analyze the operational data each day.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that analyzes the data without affecting the performance of the operational data store.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","stemKo":"You have the resources shown in the following table.\n\n[[IMG1]]\n\nCDB1 contains a container that stores operational data updated continuously.\n\nYou are designing a solution that uses AS1 to analyze the operational data each day.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that analyzes the data without affecting the performance of the operational data store.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","explanationEn":"Azure Synapse Link for Azure Cosmos DB enables Azure Synapse Analytics to query the Cosmos DB analytical store, which is a separately maintained, isolated column store. This supports analytics over continuously updated operational data without consuming the transactional workload’s provisioned throughput or affecting its performance.\n\n**Learn more:** [What is Azure Synapse Link for Azure Cosmos DB?](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/cosmos-db/synapse-link) · [What is Azure Cosmos DB analytical store?](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/cosmos-db/analytical-store-introduction)","explanationKo":"Azure Synapse Link for Azure Cosmos DB enables Azure Synapse Analytics to query the Cosmos DB analytical store, which is a separately maintained, isolated column store. This supports analytics over continuously updated operational data without consuming the transactional workload’s provisioned throughput or affecting its performance.\n\n**Learn more:** [What is Azure Synapse Link for Azure Cosmos DB?](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/cosmos-db/synapse-link) · [What is Azure Cosmos DB analytical store?](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/cosmos-db/analytical-store-introduction)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Azure Data Factory with Azure Cosmos DB and Azure Synapse Analytics connectors","ko":"Azure Data Factory with Azure Cosmos DB and Azure Synapse Analytics connectors"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure Synapse Analytics with PolyBase data loading","ko":"Azure Synapse Analytics with PolyBase data loading"},{"label":"C","en":"Azure Synapse Link for Azure Cosmos DB","ko":"Azure Synapse Link for Azure Cosmos DB"},{"label":"D","en":"Azure Cosmos DB change feed","ko":"Azure Cosmos DB change feed"}],"answers":["C"]},{"n":100,"id":null,"type":"dropdown","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You plan to build an Azure environment containing a root management group and 10 child management groups. Each child management group will contain five Azure subscriptions, and each subscription will have between 10 and 30 resource groups.\n\nYou need to design an Azure governance solution that meets these requirements:\n\n- Use Azure Blueprints to control governance across every subscription and resource group.\n- Ensure Blueprint-based configurations remain consistent across all subscriptions and resource groups.\n- Minimize the number of blueprint definitions and assignments.\n\nWhat should the solution include?","stemKo":"You plan to build an Azure environment containing a root management group and 10 child management groups. Each child management group will contain five Azure subscriptions, and each subscription will have between 10 and 30 resource groups.\n\nYou need to design an Azure governance solution that meets these requirements:\n\n- Use Azure Blueprints to control governance across every subscription and resource group.\n- Ensure Blueprint-based configurations remain consistent across all subscriptions and resource groups.\n- Minimize the number of blueprint definitions and assignments.\n\nWhat should the solution include?","explanationEn":"A blueprint definition saved at the root management group can be used by subscriptions throughout its management-group hierarchy, so a single definition maintains a common configuration. Blueprint assignments target subscriptions; assigning at a management group does not automatically deploy the blueprint to all descendant subscriptions. Create an assignment for each subscription.\n\n**Learn more:** [Overview of Azure Blueprints](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/governance/blueprints/overview) · [Quickstart: Define and assign a blueprint in the portal](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/governance/blueprints/create-blueprint-portal)","explanationKo":"A blueprint definition saved at the root management group can be used by subscriptions throughout its management-group hierarchy, so a single definition maintains a common configuration. Blueprint assignments target subscriptions; assigning at a management group does not automatically deploy the blueprint to all descendant subscriptions. Create an assignment for each subscription.\n\n**Learn more:** [Overview of Azure Blueprints](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/governance/blueprints/overview) · [Quickstart: Define and assign a blueprint in the portal](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/governance/blueprints/create-blueprint-portal)","learnMore":[],"blanks":[{"id":"definitions","labelEn":"Level at which to define the blueprints:","labelKo":"Level at which to define the blueprints:","options":[{"en":"The child management groups","ko":"The child management groups"},{"en":"The root management group","ko":"The root management group"},{"en":"The subscriptions","ko":"The subscriptions"}],"answer":"The root management group"},{"id":"assignments","labelEn":"Level at which to create the blueprint assignments:","labelKo":"Level at which to create the blueprint assignments:","options":[{"en":"The child management groups","ko":"The child management groups"},{"en":"The root management group","ko":"The root management group"},{"en":"The subscriptions","ko":"The subscriptions"}],"answer":"The subscriptions"}],"template":""},{"n":101,"id":null,"type":"dropdown","topic":"Design data storage solutions","topicKo":"데이터 저장소 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You have an Azure subscription.\n\nYou plan to deploy five storage accounts for block blobs and five storage accounts for file shares. The file shares will be accessed by using the SMB protocol.\n\nYou need to recommend an access-authorization solution for the storage accounts. The solution must meet these requirements:\n\n- Maximize security.\n- Prevent use of shared keys.\n- Whenever possible, support time-limited access.\n\nWhat should the solution include?","stemKo":"You have an Azure subscription.\n\nYou plan to deploy five storage accounts for block blobs and five storage accounts for file shares. The file shares will be accessed by using the SMB protocol.\n\nYou need to recommend an access-authorization solution for the storage accounts. The solution must meet these requirements:\n\n- Maximize security.\n- Prevent use of shared keys.\n- Whenever possible, support time-limited access.\n\nWhat should the solution include?","explanationEn":"A user delegation SAS for Blob Storage is signed with a user delegation key obtained through Microsoft Entra ID, avoiding shared-key authorization while allowing a defined validity period. Stored access policies are not supported for user delegation SAS tokens. Azure Files accessed through SMB uses identity-based authentication and authorization with Azure AD credentials rather than shared keys.\n\n**Learn more:** [Create a user delegation SAS](https://learn.microsoft.com/fil-ph/rest/api/storageservices/create-user-delegation-sas) · [Overview of Azure Files authorization and access control](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/files/storage-files-authorization-overview)","explanationKo":"A user delegation SAS for Blob Storage is signed with a user delegation key obtained through Microsoft Entra ID, avoiding shared-key authorization while allowing a defined validity period. Stored access policies are not supported for user delegation SAS tokens. Azure Files accessed through SMB uses identity-based authentication and authorization with Azure AD credentials rather than shared keys.\n\n**Learn more:** [Create a user delegation SAS](https://learn.microsoft.com/fil-ph/rest/api/storageservices/create-user-delegation-sas) · [Overview of Azure Files authorization and access control](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/files/storage-files-authorization-overview)","learnMore":[],"blanks":[{"id":"blobs","labelEn":"For the blobs:","labelKo":"For the blobs:","options":[{"en":"A user delegation shared access signature (SAS) only","ko":"A user delegation shared access signature (SAS) only"},{"en":"A shared access signature (SAS) and a stored access policy","ko":"A shared access signature (SAS) and a stored access policy"},{"en":"A user delegation shared access signature (SAS) and a stored access policy","ko":"A user delegation shared access signature (SAS) and a stored access policy"}],"answer":"A user delegation shared access signature (SAS) only"},{"id":"file_shares","labelEn":"For the file shares:","labelKo":"For the file shares:","options":[{"en":"Azure AD credentials","ko":"Azure AD credentials"},{"en":"A user delegation shared access signature (SAS) only","ko":"A user delegation shared access signature (SAS) only"},{"en":"A user delegation shared access signature (SAS) and a stored access policy","ko":"A user delegation shared access signature (SAS) and a stored access policy"}],"answer":"Azure AD credentials"}],"template":""},{"n":102,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You have an Azure Active Directory (Azure AD) tenant.\n\nYou intend to deploy Azure Cosmos DB databases that use the SQL API.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that gives specified Azure AD user accounts read access to the Cosmos DB databases.\n\nWhat should the recommendation include?","stemKo":"You have an Azure Active Directory (Azure AD) tenant.\n\nYou intend to deploy Azure Cosmos DB databases that use the SQL API.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that gives specified Azure AD user accounts read access to the Cosmos DB databases.\n\nWhat should the recommendation include?","explanationEn":"Azure Cosmos DB SQL API resource tokens are generated from permission resources and can be restricted to read-only access for a specific resource and time period. An Access control (IAM) role assignment is used to assign Azure resource-management permissions to specified Microsoft Entra ID principals. This combination supports scoped Cosmos DB access for selected directory users.\n\n**Learn more:** [Access control in the Azure Cosmos DB SQL API](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/rest/api/cosmos-db/access-control-on-cosmosdb-resources) · [Add and assign user roles for Azure Cosmos DB for NoSQL](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/cosmos-db/how-to-add-assign-user-roles)","explanationKo":"Azure Cosmos DB SQL API resource tokens are generated from permission resources and can be restricted to read-only access for a specific resource and time period. An Access control (IAM) role assignment is used to assign Azure resource-management permissions to specified Microsoft Entra ID principals. This combination supports scoped Cosmos DB access for selected directory users.\n\n**Learn more:** [Access control in the Azure Cosmos DB SQL API](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/rest/api/cosmos-db/access-control-on-cosmosdb-resources) · [Add and assign user roles for Azure Cosmos DB for NoSQL](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/cosmos-db/how-to-add-assign-user-roles)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"shared access signatures (SAS) and Conditional Access policies","ko":"shared access signatures (SAS) and Conditional Access policies"},{"label":"B","en":"certificates and Azure Key Vault","ko":"certificates and Azure Key Vault"},{"label":"C","en":"master keys and Azure Information Protection policies","ko":"master keys and Azure Information Protection policies"},{"label":"D","en":"a resource token and an Access control (IAM) role assignment","ko":"a resource token and an Access control (IAM) role assignment"}],"answers":["D"]},{"n":103,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design business continuity solutions","topicKo":"업무 연속성 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You need to design a highly available Azure SQL database that meets these requirements:\n\n- Failover between database replicas must occur with no data loss.\n- The database must stay available during an availability-zone outage.\n- Costs must be minimized.\n\nWhich deployment option should you choose?","stemKo":"You need to design a highly available Azure SQL database that meets these requirements:\n\n- Failover between database replicas must occur with no data loss.\n- The database must stay available during an availability-zone outage.\n- Costs must be minimized.\n\nWhich deployment option should you choose?","explanationEn":"Azure SQL Database Business Critical uses synchronously replicated high-availability replicas. When configured for zone redundancy, replicas are distributed across availability zones, providing zero loss of committed data on failover and resilience to a single-zone outage. It meets these requirements without the additional managed-instance deployment cost.\n\n**Learn more:** [Reliability in Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/reliability/reliability-sql-database) · [vCore purchasing model - Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/database/service-tiers-sql-database-vcore?view=azuresql)","explanationKo":"Azure SQL Database Business Critical uses synchronously replicated high-availability replicas. When configured for zone redundancy, replicas are distributed across availability zones, providing zero loss of committed data on failover and resilience to a single-zone outage. It meets these requirements without the additional managed-instance deployment cost.\n\n**Learn more:** [Reliability in Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/reliability/reliability-sql-database) · [vCore purchasing model - Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/database/service-tiers-sql-database-vcore?view=azuresql)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Azure SQL Managed Instance Business Critical","ko":"Azure SQL Managed Instance Business Critical"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure SQL Managed Instance General Purpose","ko":"Azure SQL Managed Instance General Purpose"},{"label":"C","en":"Azure SQL Database Business Critical","ko":"Azure SQL Database Business Critical"},{"label":"D","en":"Azure SQL Database Serverless","ko":"Azure SQL Database Serverless"}],"answers":["C"]},{"n":104,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You need to recommend a solution for generating a monthly report of all new Azure Resource Manager (ARM) resource deployments in your Azure subscription.\n\nWhat should the recommendation include?","stemKo":"You need to recommend a solution for generating a monthly report of all new Azure Resource Manager (ARM) resource deployments in your Azure subscription.\n\nWhat should the recommendation include?","explanationEn":"Azure Activity Log records subscription-level Azure Resource Manager control-plane events, including resource creation and other administrative operations. Those events provide the data needed to identify new deployments over a monthly reporting period.\n\n**Learn more:** [Activity log in Azure Monitor](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-monitor/platform/activity-log) · [Azure Activity Log event schema](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-monitor/platform/activity-log-schema)","explanationKo":"Azure Activity Log records subscription-level Azure Resource Manager control-plane events, including resource creation and other administrative operations. Those events provide the data needed to identify new deployments over a monthly reporting period.\n\n**Learn more:** [Activity log in Azure Monitor](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-monitor/platform/activity-log) · [Azure Activity Log event schema](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-monitor/platform/activity-log-schema)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Azure Activity Log","ko":"Azure Activity Log"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure Arc","ko":"Azure Arc"},{"label":"C","en":"Azure Analysis Services","ko":"Azure Analysis Services"},{"label":"D","en":"Azure Monitor action groups","ko":"Azure Monitor action groups"}],"answers":["A"]},{"n":105,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design infrastructure solutions","topicKo":"인프라 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You are building a sales application that will include several Azure cloud services and manage different transaction components. Separate cloud services will process customer orders, billing, payment, inventory, and shipping.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that lets the cloud services asynchronously exchange transaction information by using XML messages.\n\nWhat should be included in the recommendation?","stemKo":"You are building a sales application that will include several Azure cloud services and manage different transaction components. Separate cloud services will process customer orders, billing, payment, inventory, and shipping.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that lets the cloud services asynchronously exchange transaction information by using XML messages.\n\nWhat should be included in the recommendation?","explanationEn":"Azure Service Bus provides durable asynchronous messaging that decouples cloud services through queues or topics and subscriptions. Its messages can carry structured data encoded as XML, making it suitable for exchanging transactional order, billing, payment, inventory, and shipping information.\n\n**Learn more:** [What is Azure Service Bus?](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/service-bus-messaging/service-bus-messaging-overview) · [Asynchronous messaging patterns and high availability](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/service-bus-messaging/service-bus-async-messaging)","explanationKo":"Azure Service Bus provides durable asynchronous messaging that decouples cloud services through queues or topics and subscriptions. Its messages can carry structured data encoded as XML, making it suitable for exchanging transactional order, billing, payment, inventory, and shipping information.\n\n**Learn more:** [What is Azure Service Bus?](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/service-bus-messaging/service-bus-messaging-overview) · [Asynchronous messaging patterns and high availability](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/service-bus-messaging/service-bus-async-messaging)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Azure Notification Hubs","ko":"Azure Notification Hubs"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure Application Gateway","ko":"Azure Application Gateway"},{"label":"C","en":"Azure Service Bus","ko":"Azure Service Bus"},{"label":"D","en":"Azure Traffic Manager","ko":"Azure Traffic Manager"}],"answers":["C"]},{"n":106,"id":null,"type":"dropdown","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You have five Azure subscriptions. Each subscription is linked to a separate Azure AD tenant and contains virtual machines running Windows Server 2022.\n\nYou plan to gather Windows security events from the virtual machines and send them to one Log Analytics workspace.\n\nRecommend a solution that meets these requirements:\n\n- Collect event logs from multiple subscriptions.\n- Support data collection rules (DCRs) that define the events to collect.\n\nWhat should you recommend for each requirement?","stemKo":"You have five Azure subscriptions. Each subscription is linked to a separate Azure AD tenant and contains virtual machines running Windows Server 2022.\n\nYou plan to gather Windows security events from the virtual machines and send them to one Log Analytics workspace.\n\nRecommend a solution that meets these requirements:\n\n- Collect event logs from multiple subscriptions.\n- Support data collection rules (DCRs) that define the events to collect.\n\nWhat should you recommend for each requirement?","explanationEn":"Azure Lighthouse enables delegated management of subscriptions and resources across separate Microsoft Entra tenants. The Azure Monitor agent collects Windows event logs from virtual machines through data collection rules, which define the Windows events to collect and their Log Analytics destination.\n\n**Learn more:** [Onboard a customer to Azure Lighthouse](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/lighthouse/how-to/onboard-customer) · [Collect Windows events from virtual machines with Azure Monitor Agent](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-monitor/vm/data-collection-windows-events)","explanationKo":"Azure Lighthouse enables delegated management of subscriptions and resources across separate Microsoft Entra tenants. The Azure Monitor agent collects Windows event logs from virtual machines through data collection rules, which define the Windows events to collect and their Log Analytics destination.\n\n**Learn more:** [Onboard a customer to Azure Lighthouse](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/lighthouse/how-to/onboard-customer) · [Collect Windows events from virtual machines with Azure Monitor Agent](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-monitor/vm/data-collection-windows-events)","learnMore":[],"blanks":[{"id":"collect_event_logs","labelEn":"To collect the event logs:","labelKo":"To collect the event logs:","options":[{"en":"Azure Event Grid","ko":"Azure Event Grid"},{"en":"Azure Lighthouse","ko":"Azure Lighthouse"},{"en":"Azure Purview","ko":"Azure Purview"}],"answer":"Azure Lighthouse"},{"id":"support_dcrs","labelEn":"To support the DCRs:","labelKo":"To support the DCRs:","options":[{"en":"The Log Analytics agent","ko":"The Log Analytics agent"},{"en":"The Azure Monitor agent","ko":"The Azure Monitor agent"},{"en":"The Azure Connected Machine agent","ko":"The Azure Connected Machine agent"}],"answer":"The Azure Monitor agent"}],"template":""},{"n":107,"id":null,"type":"answer_reveal","topic":"Design business continuity solutions","topicKo":"업무 연속성 설계","koMissing":true,"images":["assets/1788032507104-g9b53ivu.jpg"],"stemEn":"HOTSPOT –\n\nYou plan to migrate DB1 and DB2 to Azure.\n\nYou must ensure that the Azure database and service tier satisfy the resiliency and business requirements.\n\nWhat should you configure?\n\n[[IMG1]]","stemKo":"HOTSPOT –\n\nYou plan to migrate DB1 and DB2 to Azure.\n\nYou must ensure that the Azure database and service tier satisfy the resiliency and business requirements.\n\nWhat should you configure?\n\n[[IMG1]]","explanationEn":"DB1 and DB2 are two separate application databases being lifted into the Azure SQL Database PaaS platform, and the business requirements call for minimizing cost and administrative effort. An elastic pool lets DB1 and DB2 share one pool of compute/storage resources under a single per-pool price instead of provisioning and managing two independent instances, which is the cheapest, lowest-effort way to host two databases with related usage patterns.\n\nFor the resiliency requirement — remain available if two availability zones in the region fail, fail over automatically, and minimize I/O latency — the service tier must support zone redundancy with a local-storage (not remote-storage) architecture. Business Critical uses the local-storage/Always On availability-group model: a primary replica plus up to three synchronously-updated secondary replicas with data on directly attached SSDs. When zone redundancy is enabled, those replicas (and the triplicated gateway ring) are spread across the region's availability zones, and Azure Service Fabric automatically fails over to a synchronized secondary in a surviving zone — all with the lowest read/write I/O latency Azure SQL Database offers, because storage is local to the compute node rather than remote network storage. General Purpose (remote-storage model, storage on Azure Blob Storage) also supports zone redundancy today, but it has materially higher I/O latency and does not provide the built-in readable secondary replicas that Business Critical offers, so it does not meet the 'minimize I/O latency' requirement as well as Business Critical does. Basic/Standard tiers don't support zone redundancy at all.\n\nA single Azure SQL Database (not pooled) is technically zone-redundant-capable too, but it does not address the cost/administrative-effort requirement for hosting two related databases, and the case study's wording ('a single … elastic pool') points at pooling both DB1 and DB2 together. Azure SQL Managed Instance can also be configured for zone redundancy today, but it is a heavier, instance-scoped (and more expensive) deployment model with no stated need in this scenario for instance-only features (SQL Agent, cross-database queries, linked servers, etc.), so it does not better satisfy the stated cost/effort requirement than an elastic pool does.\n\n**Learn more:** [Manage Multiple Databases with Elastic Pools - Azure SQL Database | Microsoft Learn](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/database/elastic-pool-overview?view=azuresql) · [Availability Through Local and Zone Redundancy - Azure SQL Database | Microsoft Learn](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/database/high-availability-sla-local-zone-redundancy?view=azuresql)","explanationKo":"DB1 and DB2 are two separate application databases being lifted into the Azure SQL Database PaaS platform, and the business requirements call for minimizing cost and administrative effort. An elastic pool lets DB1 and DB2 share one pool of compute/storage resources under a single per-pool price instead of provisioning and managing two independent instances, which is the cheapest, lowest-effort way to host two databases with related usage patterns.\n\nFor the resiliency requirement — remain available if two availability zones in the region fail, fail over automatically, and minimize I/O latency — the service tier must support zone redundancy with a local-storage (not remote-storage) architecture. Business Critical uses the local-storage/Always On availability-group model: a primary replica plus up to three synchronously-updated secondary replicas with data on directly attached SSDs. When zone redundancy is enabled, those replicas (and the triplicated gateway ring) are spread across the region's availability zones, and Azure Service Fabric automatically fails over to a synchronized secondary in a surviving zone — all with the lowest read/write I/O latency Azure SQL Database offers, because storage is local to the compute node rather than remote network storage. General Purpose (remote-storage model, storage on Azure Blob Storage) also supports zone redundancy today, but it has materially higher I/O latency and does not provide the built-in readable secondary replicas that Business Critical offers, so it does not meet the 'minimize I/O latency' requirement as well as Business Critical does. Basic/Standard tiers don't support zone redundancy at all.\n\nA single Azure SQL Database (not pooled) is technically zone-redundant-capable too, but it does not address the cost/administrative-effort requirement for hosting two related databases, and the case study's wording ('a single … elastic pool') points at pooling both DB1 and DB2 together. Azure SQL Managed Instance can also be configured for zone redundancy today, but it is a heavier, instance-scoped (and more expensive) deployment model with no stated need in this scenario for instance-only features (SQL Agent, cross-database queries, linked servers, etc.), so it does not better satisfy the stated cost/effort requirement than an elastic pool does.\n\n**Learn more:** [Manage Multiple Databases with Elastic Pools - Azure SQL Database | Microsoft Learn](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/database/elastic-pool-overview?view=azuresql) · [Availability Through Local and Zone Redundancy - Azure SQL Database | Microsoft Learn](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/database/high-availability-sla-local-zone-redundancy?view=azuresql)","learnMore":[],"answerImages":[],"answerTextEn":"**Database:** An Azure SQL Database elastic pool\n\n**Service tier:** Business Critical","answerTextKo":"**Database:** An Azure SQL Database elastic pool\n\n**Service tier:** Business Critical"},{"n":108,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design infrastructure solutions","topicKo":"인프라 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You are building a sales application that will include several Azure cloud services and manage different parts of a transaction. Separate cloud services will process customer orders, billing, payment, inventory, and shipping.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that lets the cloud services communicate transaction information asynchronously by using XML messages.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","stemKo":"You are building a sales application that will include several Azure cloud services and manage different parts of a transaction. Separate cloud services will process customer orders, billing, payment, inventory, and shipping.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that lets the cloud services communicate transaction information asynchronously by using XML messages.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","explanationEn":"Azure Service Bus provides durable queues and publish/subscribe topics for asynchronous communication between decoupled cloud services. Its messages can contain structured payloads such as XML, making it suitable for reliably transferring transaction data among order, billing, payment, inventory, and shipping components.\n\n**Learn more:** [What is Azure Service Bus?](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/service-bus-messaging/service-bus-messaging-overview) · [Asynchronous messaging patterns and high availability](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/service-bus-messaging/service-bus-async-messaging)","explanationKo":"Azure Service Bus provides durable queues and publish/subscribe topics for asynchronous communication between decoupled cloud services. Its messages can contain structured payloads such as XML, making it suitable for reliably transferring transaction data among order, billing, payment, inventory, and shipping components.\n\n**Learn more:** [What is Azure Service Bus?](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/service-bus-messaging/service-bus-messaging-overview) · [Asynchronous messaging patterns and high availability](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/service-bus-messaging/service-bus-async-messaging)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Azure Service Bus","ko":"Azure Service Bus"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure Data Lake","ko":"Azure Data Lake"},{"label":"C","en":"Azure Traffic Manager","ko":"Azure Traffic Manager"},{"label":"D","en":"Azure Notification Hubs","ko":"Azure Notification Hubs"}],"answers":["A"]},{"n":109,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design data storage solutions","topicKo":"데이터 저장소 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You have an app named App1 that uses an on-premises Microsoft SQL Server database named DB1.\n\nYou plan to migrate DB1 to an Azure SQL managed instance.\n\nYou need to enable customer-managed Transparent Data Encryption (TDE) for the instance. The solution must maximize encryption strength.\n\nWhich encryption-algorithm type and key length should you use for the TDE protector?","stemKo":"You have an app named App1 that uses an on-premises Microsoft SQL Server database named DB1.\n\nYou plan to migrate DB1 to an Azure SQL managed instance.\n\nYou need to enable customer-managed Transparent Data Encryption (TDE) for the instance. The solution must maximize encryption strength.\n\nWhich encryption-algorithm type and key length should you use for the TDE protector?","explanationEn":"For Azure SQL Managed Instance customer-managed TDE, the protector must be an asymmetric RSA or RSA-HSM key. The supported RSA key lengths are 2,048 and 3,072 bits, so RSA 3072 provides the strongest supported option. AES 256 is symmetric and cannot serve as the TDE protector; RSA 4096 is unsupported.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure SQL transparent data encryption with customer-managed key](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/database/transparent-data-encryption-byok-overview?view=azuresql)","explanationKo":"For Azure SQL Managed Instance customer-managed TDE, the protector must be an asymmetric RSA or RSA-HSM key. The supported RSA key lengths are 2,048 and 3,072 bits, so RSA 3072 provides the strongest supported option. AES 256 is symmetric and cannot serve as the TDE protector; RSA 4096 is unsupported.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure SQL transparent data encryption with customer-managed key](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/database/transparent-data-encryption-byok-overview?view=azuresql)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"RSA 3072","ko":"RSA 3072"},{"label":"B","en":"AES 256","ko":"AES 256"},{"label":"C","en":"RSA 4096","ko":"RSA 4096"},{"label":"D","en":"RSA 2048","ko":"RSA 2048"}],"answers":["A"]},{"n":110,"id":null,"type":"dropdown","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You plan to deploy Azure Databricks to support a machine learning application. Data engineers will mount an Azure Data Lake Storage account to the Databricks file system. Folder permissions are assigned directly to the data engineers.\n\nYou need to recommend a design for the planned Databricks deployment. The solution must:\n\n- Ensure that data engineers can access only the folders for which they have permissions.\n- Minimize development effort.\n- Minimize costs.\n\nWhat should the recommendation include?","stemKo":"You plan to deploy Azure Databricks to support a machine learning application. Data engineers will mount an Azure Data Lake Storage account to the Databricks file system. Folder permissions are assigned directly to the data engineers.\n\nYou need to recommend a design for the planned Databricks deployment. The solution must:\n\n- Ensure that data engineers can access only the folders for which they have permissions.\n- Minimize development effort.\n- Minimize costs.\n\nWhat should the recommendation include?","explanationEn":"Microsoft Entra ID credential passthrough uses the signed-in engineer’s identity when accessing Azure Data Lake Storage. This causes the storage account to apply that engineer’s existing folder ACLs, avoiding custom credential handling. Credential passthrough requires an Azure Databricks Premium workspace.\n\n**Learn more:** [Integrate OneLake with Azure Databricks](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/fabric/onelake/onelake-azure-databricks) · [Architecture best practices for Azure Databricks](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/well-architected/service-guides/azure-databricks)","explanationKo":"Microsoft Entra ID credential passthrough uses the signed-in engineer’s identity when accessing Azure Data Lake Storage. This causes the storage account to apply that engineer’s existing folder ACLs, avoiding custom credential handling. Credential passthrough requires an Azure Databricks Premium workspace.\n\n**Learn more:** [Integrate OneLake with Azure Databricks](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/fabric/onelake/onelake-azure-databricks) · [Architecture best practices for Azure Databricks](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/well-architected/service-guides/azure-databricks)","learnMore":[],"blanks":[{"id":"databricks_sku","labelEn":"Databricks SKU:","labelKo":"Databricks SKU:","options":[{"en":"Premium","ko":"Premium"},{"en":"Standard","ko":"Standard"}],"answer":"Premium"},{"id":"cluster_configuration","labelEn":"Cluster configuration:","labelKo":"Cluster configuration:","options":[{"en":"Credential passthrough","ko":"Credential passthrough"},{"en":"Managed identities","ko":"Managed identities"},{"en":"MLflow","ko":"MLflow"},{"en":"A runtime that contains Photon","ko":"A runtime that contains Photon"},{"en":"Secret scope","ko":"Secret scope"}],"answer":"Credential passthrough"}],"template":""},{"n":111,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You must implement Azure RBAC role assignments for the **Network Contributor** role. The solution must satisfy the authentication and authorization requirements.\n\nWhat is the minimum number of assignments you must use?","stemKo":"You must implement Azure RBAC role assignments for the **Network Contributor** role. The solution must satisfy the authentication and authorization requirements.\n\nWhat is the minimum number of assignments you must use?","explanationEn":"Azure RBAC permissions assigned at a management-group scope are inherited by the subscriptions beneath that management group. Because separate Microsoft Entra tenants have separate management-group hierarchies, Network Contributor access across the two tenant hierarchies requires one management-group-scoped assignment in each tenant, for a total of two assignments.\n\n**Learn more:** [Understand scope for Azure RBAC](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/role-based-access-control/scope-overview) · [Steps to assign an Azure role - Azure RBAC](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/role-based-access-control/role-assignments-steps)","explanationKo":"Azure RBAC permissions assigned at a management-group scope are inherited by the subscriptions beneath that management group. Because separate Microsoft Entra tenants have separate management-group hierarchies, Network Contributor access across the two tenant hierarchies requires one management-group-scoped assignment in each tenant, for a total of two assignments.\n\n**Learn more:** [Understand scope for Azure RBAC](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/role-based-access-control/scope-overview) · [Steps to assign an Azure role - Azure RBAC](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/role-based-access-control/role-assignments-steps)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"1","ko":"1"},{"label":"B","en":"2","ko":"2"},{"label":"C","en":"5","ko":"5"},{"label":"D","en":"10","ko":"10"},{"label":"E","en":"15","ko":"15"}],"answers":["B"]},{"n":112,"id":null,"type":"drag_drop","topic":"Design data storage solutions","topicKo":"데이터 저장소 설계","koMissing":true,"images":["assets/1783707658998-0wygkeft.png"],"stemEn":"You plan to import data from your on-premises environment into Azure. The data is listed in the following table.\n\n[[IMG1]]\n\nWhat should you recommend to migrate the data? Each tool can be used once, more than once, or not at all.","stemKo":"You plan to import data from your on-premises environment into Azure. The data is listed in the following table.\n\n[[IMG1]]\n\nWhat should you recommend to migrate the data? Each tool can be used once, more than once, or not at all.","explanationEn":"Data Migration Assistant supports assessing and migrating SQL Server workloads for Azure SQL targets. Azure Cosmos DB Data Migration Tool supports SQL Server as a migration source for Azure Cosmos DB.\n\n**Learn more:** [Migrate SQL Server to Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/data-migration/sql-server/database/guide) · [Migrate data using the Data Migration Tool](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-ca/azure/cosmos-db/how-to-migrate-desktop-tool)","explanationKo":"Data Migration Assistant supports assessing and migrating SQL Server workloads for Azure SQL targets. Azure Cosmos DB Data Migration Tool supports SQL Server as a migration source for Azure Cosmos DB.\n\n**Learn more:** [Migrate SQL Server to Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/data-migration/sql-server/database/guide) · [Migrate data using the Data Migration Tool](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-ca/azure/cosmos-db/how-to-migrate-desktop-tool)","learnMore":[],"items":[{"en":"AzCopy","ko":"AzCopy"},{"en":"Azure Cosmos DB Data Migration Tool","ko":"Azure Cosmos DB Data Migration Tool"},{"en":"Data Management Gateway","ko":"Data Management Gateway"},{"en":"Data Migration Assistant","ko":"Data Migration Assistant"}],"slots":[{"id":"sql2012_to_azuresql","labelEn":"From the SQL Server 2012 database:","labelKo":"From the SQL Server 2012 database:","answer":"Data Migration Assistant"},{"id":"sql2014table_to_cosmos","labelEn":"From the table in the SQL Server 2014 database:","labelKo":"From the table in the SQL Server 2014 database:","answer":"Azure Cosmos DB Data Migration Tool"}],"reuse":true},{"n":113,"id":null,"type":"dropdown","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"HOTSPOT —\n\nDesign an Azure Policy solution that provides the following functionality:\n\n- For new resources, assign tags and values that correspond to the tags and values of the resource group where the resources are deployed.\n- For existing resources, determine whether the tags and values correspond to those of the resource group containing the resources.\n- For noncompliant resources, start automatically generated remediation tasks to add missing tags and values.\n\nThe solution must follow the principle of least privilege.\n\nWhat should the design include?","stemKo":"HOTSPOT —\n\nDesign an Azure Policy solution that provides the following functionality:\n\n- For new resources, assign tags and values that correspond to the tags and values of the resource group where the resources are deployed.\n- For existing resources, determine whether the tags and values correspond to those of the resource group containing the resources.\n- For noncompliant resources, start automatically generated remediation tasks to add missing tags and values.\n\nThe solution must follow the principle of least privilege.\n\nWhat should the design include?","explanationEn":"The Modify effect can add or replace tags on resource creation or update, reports existing resources that do not meet the rule as noncompliant, and supports remediation tasks to correct them. Azure Policy remediation uses the policy assignment’s managed identity. Contributor can modify the affected resources, while User Access Administrator grants unnecessary access-management permissions.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure Policy definition structure - Modify effect](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/governance/policy/concepts/effect-modify) · [Remediate non-compliant resources with Azure Policy](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/governance/policy/how-to/remediate-resources)","explanationKo":"The Modify effect can add or replace tags on resource creation or update, reports existing resources that do not meet the rule as noncompliant, and supports remediation tasks to correct them. Azure Policy remediation uses the policy assignment’s managed identity. Contributor can modify the affected resources, while User Access Administrator grants unnecessary access-management permissions.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure Policy definition structure - Modify effect](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/governance/policy/concepts/effect-modify) · [Remediate non-compliant resources with Azure Policy](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/governance/policy/how-to/remediate-resources)","learnMore":[],"blanks":[{"id":"policy_effect","labelEn":"Azure Policy effect to use:","labelKo":"Azure Policy effect to use:","options":[{"en":"Append","ko":"Append"},{"en":"EnforceOPAConstraint","ko":"EnforceOPAConstraint"},{"en":"EnforceRegoPolicy","ko":"EnforceRegoPolicy"},{"en":"Modify","ko":"Modify"}],"answer":"Modify"},{"id":"remediation_identity","labelEn":"Azure Active Directory (Azure AD) object and role-based access control (RBAC) role to use for the remediation tasks:","labelKo":"Azure Active Directory (Azure AD) object and role-based access control (RBAC) role to use for the remediation tasks:","options":[{"en":"A managed identity with the Contributor role","ko":"A managed identity with the Contributor role"},{"en":"A managed identity with the User Access Administrator role","ko":"A managed identity with the User Access Administrator role"},{"en":"A service principal with the Contributor role","ko":"A service principal with the Contributor role"},{"en":"A service principal with the User Access Administrator role","ko":"A service principal with the User Access Administrator role"}],"answer":"A managed identity with the Contributor role"}],"template":""},{"n":114,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You need to recommend a notification solution for the IT Support distribution group.\n\nWhat should be included in the recommendation?","stemKo":"You need to recommend a notification solution for the IT Support distribution group.\n\nWhat should be included in the recommendation?","explanationEn":"An Azure Monitor action group specifies notification recipients and delivery methods for alerts, including email notifications sent to a distribution group.","explanationKo":"An Azure Monitor action group specifies notification recipients and delivery methods for alerts, including email notifications sent to a distribution group.","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"a SendGrid account with advanced reporting","ko":"a SendGrid account with advanced reporting"},{"label":"B","en":"an action group","ko":"an action group"},{"label":"C","en":"Azure Network Watcher","ko":"Azure Network Watcher"},{"label":"D","en":"Azure AD Connect Health","ko":"Azure AD Connect Health"}],"answers":["B"]},{"n":115,"id":null,"type":"dropdown","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You plan to deploy an Azure web app named App1 that will use Azure Active Directory (Azure AD) authentication.\n\nApp1 will be accessed from the internet by users at your company. All users have Windows 10 computers that are joined to Azure AD.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that ensures users can connect to App1 without an authentication prompt and can access App1 only from company-owned computers.\n\nWhat should you recommend for each requirement?","stemKo":"You plan to deploy an Azure web app named App1 that will use Azure Active Directory (Azure AD) authentication.\n\nApp1 will be accessed from the internet by users at your company. All users have Windows 10 computers that are joined to Azure AD.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that ensures users can connect to App1 without an authentication prompt and can access App1 only from company-owned computers.\n\nWhat should you recommend for each requirement?","explanationEn":"An Azure AD app registration integrates App1 with Microsoft Entra ID for user authentication and single sign-on. Conditional Access evaluates device state at sign-in and can require a compliant or Azure AD-joined device before granting access to App1, restricting the app to organization-managed computers.\n\n**Learn more:** [App sign-in flow with the Microsoft identity platform](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity-platform/app-sign-in-flow) · [Require a compliant device, Microsoft Entra hybrid joined device, or multifactor authentication for all users](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity/conditional-access/policy-alt-all-users-compliant-hybrid-or-mfa)","explanationKo":"An Azure AD app registration integrates App1 with Microsoft Entra ID for user authentication and single sign-on. Conditional Access evaluates device state at sign-in and can require a compliant or Azure AD-joined device before granting access to App1, restricting the app to organization-managed computers.\n\n**Learn more:** [App sign-in flow with the Microsoft identity platform](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity-platform/app-sign-in-flow) · [Require a compliant device, Microsoft Entra hybrid joined device, or multifactor authentication for all users](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity/conditional-access/policy-alt-all-users-compliant-hybrid-or-mfa)","learnMore":[],"blanks":[{"id":"sso","labelEn":"The users can connect to App1 without being prompted for authentication:","labelKo":"The users can connect to App1 without being prompted for authentication:","options":[{"en":"An Azure AD app registration","ko":"An Azure AD app registration"},{"en":"An Azure AD managed identity","ko":"An Azure AD managed identity"},{"en":"Azure AD Application Proxy","ko":"Azure AD Application Proxy"}],"answer":"An Azure AD app registration"},{"id":"company_devices","labelEn":"The users can access App1 only from company-owned computers:","labelKo":"The users can access App1 only from company-owned computers:","options":[{"en":"A Conditional Access policy","ko":"A Conditional Access policy"},{"en":"An Azure AD administrative unit","ko":"An Azure AD administrative unit"},{"en":"Azure Application Gateway","ko":"Azure Application Gateway"},{"en":"Azure Blueprints","ko":"Azure Blueprints"},{"en":"Azure Policy","ko":"Azure Policy"}],"answer":"A Conditional Access policy"}],"template":""},{"n":116,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You have 12 Azure subscriptions and three projects. Each project uses resources in multiple subscriptions.\n\nYou need to use Microsoft Cost Management to monitor costs for each project. The solution must minimize administrative effort.\n\nWhich two components should be included in the solution? Each correct answer presents part of the solution.\n\nNOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.","stemKo":"You have 12 Azure subscriptions and three projects. Each project uses resources in multiple subscriptions.\n\nYou need to use Microsoft Cost Management to monitor costs for each project. The solution must minimize administrative effort.\n\nWhich two components should be included in the solution? Each correct answer presents part of the solution.\n\nNOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.","explanationEn":"Resource tags attach a project identifier to resource usage, allowing Cost Management to group or filter costs by project across subscriptions. Budgets track spending over time and send notifications when configured cost or forecast thresholds are exceeded, providing proactive project-cost monitoring.\n\n**Learn more:** [Group and filter options in Cost Analysis and Budgets](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/cost-management-billing/costs/group-filter) · [What is Microsoft Cost Management](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/cost-management-billing/costs/overview-cost-management)","explanationKo":"Resource tags attach a project identifier to resource usage, allowing Cost Management to group or filter costs by project across subscriptions. Budgets track spending over time and send notifications when configured cost or forecast thresholds are exceeded, providing proactive project-cost monitoring.\n\n**Learn more:** [Group and filter options in Cost Analysis and Budgets](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/cost-management-billing/costs/group-filter) · [What is Microsoft Cost Management](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/cost-management-billing/costs/overview-cost-management)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"budgets","ko":"budgets"},{"label":"B","en":"resource tags","ko":"resource tags"},{"label":"C","en":"custom role-based access control (RBAC) roles","ko":"custom role-based access control (RBAC) roles"},{"label":"D","en":"management groups","ko":"management groups"},{"label":"E","en":"Azure boards","ko":"Azure boards"}],"answers":["AB"]},{"n":117,"id":null,"type":"dropdown","topic":"Design data storage solutions","topicKo":"데이터 저장소 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"HOTSPOT –\n\nYou manage the database environment for Contoso, Ltd., a Microsoft Volume Licensing customer that uses License Mobility through Software Assurance.\n\nYou must deploy 50 databases. The solution must:\n\n- Support automatic scaling.\n- Minimize Microsoft SQL Server licensing costs.\n\nWhat should the solution include?","stemKo":"HOTSPOT –\n\nYou manage the database environment for Contoso, Ltd., a Microsoft Volume Licensing customer that uses License Mobility through Software Assurance.\n\nYou must deploy 50 databases. The solution must:\n\n- Support automatic scaling.\n- Minimize Microsoft SQL Server licensing costs.\n\nWhat should the solution include?","explanationEn":"The vCore purchasing model supports Azure Hybrid Benefit, enabling eligible SQL Server licenses with active Software Assurance to be applied to Azure SQL Database. Azure SQL Database elastic pools are intended for many databases with differing and unpredictable utilization, sharing a scaled pool of resources to lower cost while accommodating changing demand.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure Hybrid Benefit for Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/database/azure-hybrid-benefit?view=azuresql) · [What is an Azure SQL Database elastic pool?](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/database/elastic-pool-overview?view=azuresql)","explanationKo":"The vCore purchasing model supports Azure Hybrid Benefit, enabling eligible SQL Server licenses with active Software Assurance to be applied to Azure SQL Database. Azure SQL Database elastic pools are intended for many databases with differing and unpredictable utilization, sharing a scaled pool of resources to lower cost while accommodating changing demand.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure Hybrid Benefit for Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/database/azure-hybrid-benefit?view=azuresql) · [What is an Azure SQL Database elastic pool?](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/database/elastic-pool-overview?view=azuresql)","learnMore":[],"blanks":[{"id":"purchase_model","labelEn":"Purchase model:","labelKo":"Purchase model:","options":[{"en":"DTU","ko":"DTU"},{"en":"vCore","ko":"vCore"},{"en":"Azure reserved virtual machine instances","ko":"Azure reserved virtual machine instances"}],"answer":"vCore"},{"id":"deployment_option","labelEn":"Deployment option:","labelKo":"Deployment option:","options":[{"en":"An Azure SQL managed instance","ko":"An Azure SQL managed instance"},{"en":"An Azure SQL Database elastic pool","ko":"An Azure SQL Database elastic pool"},{"en":"A SQL Server Always On availability group","ko":"A SQL Server Always On availability group"}],"answer":"An Azure SQL Database elastic pool"}],"template":""},{"n":118,"id":null,"type":"dropdown","topic":"Design infrastructure solutions","topicKo":"인프라 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You plan to migrate App1 to Azure.\n\nYou need to recommend a high-availability solution for App1 that meets the resiliency requirements.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","stemKo":"You plan to migrate App1 to Azure.\n\nYou need to recommend a high-availability solution for App1 that meets the resiliency requirements.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","explanationEn":"A workload that must survive the loss of two availability zones needs deployments in all three zones. Each Azure Dedicated Host group belongs to a single availability zone, so three zones require three host groups. When a scale set uses dedicated hosts, it must use the matching host group and zone configuration; Azure Dedicated Host deployments do not support a zone-spanning scale set. One autoscaling VM scale set is therefore deployed in each zone, requiring three scale sets.\n\n**Learn more:** [Deploy Azure dedicated hosts](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/virtual-machines/dedicated-hosts-how-to) · [Reliability in Azure Virtual Machine Scale Sets](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-au/azure/reliability/reliability-virtual-machine-scale-sets)","explanationKo":"A workload that must survive the loss of two availability zones needs deployments in all three zones. Each Azure Dedicated Host group belongs to a single availability zone, so three zones require three host groups. When a scale set uses dedicated hosts, it must use the matching host group and zone configuration; Azure Dedicated Host deployments do not support a zone-spanning scale set. One autoscaling VM scale set is therefore deployed in each zone, requiring three scale sets.\n\n**Learn more:** [Deploy Azure dedicated hosts](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/virtual-machines/dedicated-hosts-how-to) · [Reliability in Azure Virtual Machine Scale Sets](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-au/azure/reliability/reliability-virtual-machine-scale-sets)","learnMore":[],"blanks":[{"id":"host_groups","labelEn":"Number of host groups:","labelKo":"Number of host groups:","options":[{"en":"1","ko":"1"},{"en":"2","ko":"2"},{"en":"3","ko":"3"},{"en":"6","ko":"6"}],"answer":"3"},{"id":"virtual_machine_scale_sets","labelEn":"Number of virtual machine scale sets:","labelKo":"Number of virtual machine scale sets:","options":[{"en":"0","ko":"0"},{"en":"1","ko":"1"},{"en":"3","ko":"3"}],"answer":"3"}],"template":""},{"n":119,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You are designing a point-of-sale (POS) solution that will be deployed to multiple locations and will use an Azure Databricks workspace in the Standard tier. The solution will contain multiple apps deployed to the on-premises network at each location.\n\nYou need to configure the authentication method that the app will use to access the workspace. The solution must minimize administrative effort related to staff turnover and credential management.\n\nWhat should you configure?","stemKo":"You are designing a point-of-sale (POS) solution that will be deployed to multiple locations and will use an Azure Databricks workspace in the Standard tier. The solution will contain multiple apps deployed to the on-premises network at each location.\n\nYou need to configure the authentication method that the app will use to access the workspace. The solution must minimize administrative effort related to staff turnover and credential management.\n\nWhat should you configure?","explanationEn":"A service principal is a non-user identity for automated tools and applications that provides programmatic access to Azure Databricks without depending on an individual employee’s credentials. Its permissions can be managed independently of users, so staff departures do not disrupt the application. Azure managed identity authentication is supported between Azure Databricks and appropriately configured Azure resources, such as Azure VMs, rather than applications deployed on-premises. Personal access tokens are legacy credentials and require token lifecycle management. [Service principals — Azure Databricks](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/databricks/admin/users-groups/service-principals), [Authenticate with Azure managed identities — Azure Databricks](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/databricks/dev-tools/auth/azure-mi)\n\n**Learn more:** [Service principals — Azure Databricks](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/databricks/admin/users-groups/service-principals) · [Authenticate with Azure managed identities — Azure Databricks](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/databricks/dev-tools/auth/azure-mi)","explanationKo":"A service principal is a non-user identity for automated tools and applications that provides programmatic access to Azure Databricks without depending on an individual employee’s credentials. Its permissions can be managed independently of users, so staff departures do not disrupt the application. Azure managed identity authentication is supported between Azure Databricks and appropriately configured Azure resources, such as Azure VMs, rather than applications deployed on-premises. Personal access tokens are legacy credentials and require token lifecycle management. [Service principals — Azure Databricks](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/databricks/admin/users-groups/service-principals), [Authenticate with Azure managed identities — Azure Databricks](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/databricks/dev-tools/auth/azure-mi)\n\n**Learn more:** [Service principals — Azure Databricks](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/databricks/admin/users-groups/service-principals) · [Authenticate with Azure managed identities — Azure Databricks](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/databricks/dev-tools/auth/azure-mi)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"a managed identity","ko":"a managed identity"},{"label":"B","en":"a service principal","ko":"a service principal"},{"label":"C","en":"a personal access token","ko":"a personal access token"}],"answers":["B"]},{"n":120,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design business continuity solutions","topicKo":"업무 연속성 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You need to design a highly available Azure SQL database that satisfies these requirements:\n\n- Failover between database replicas must occur with no data loss.\n- The database must stay available during a zone outage.\n- Costs must be minimized.\n\nWhich deployment option should you use?","stemKo":"You need to design a highly available Azure SQL database that satisfies these requirements:\n\n- Failover between database replicas must occur with no data loss.\n- The database must stay available during a zone outage.\n- Costs must be minimized.\n\nWhich deployment option should you use?","explanationEn":"Azure SQL Database Business Critical supports zone-redundant replicas across Azure availability zones. During an availability-zone failure, Azure SQL Database can fail over to a synchronized replica with no expected loss of committed data. Azure SQL Database is the more targeted and typically lower-cost deployment choice than Azure SQL Managed Instance when Managed Instance capabilities are not required.\n\n**Learn more:** [Reliability in Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/reliability/reliability-sql-database) · [Availability Through Local and Zone Redundancy - Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/database/high-availability-sla-local-zone-redundancy?view=azuresql-db)","explanationKo":"Azure SQL Database Business Critical supports zone-redundant replicas across Azure availability zones. During an availability-zone failure, Azure SQL Database can fail over to a synchronized replica with no expected loss of committed data. Azure SQL Database is the more targeted and typically lower-cost deployment choice than Azure SQL Managed Instance when Managed Instance capabilities are not required.\n\n**Learn more:** [Reliability in Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/reliability/reliability-sql-database) · [Availability Through Local and Zone Redundancy - Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/database/high-availability-sla-local-zone-redundancy?view=azuresql-db)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Azure SQL Database Basic","ko":"Azure SQL Database Basic"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure SQL Managed Instance General Purpose","ko":"Azure SQL Managed Instance General Purpose"},{"label":"C","en":"Azure SQL Database Business Critical","ko":"Azure SQL Database Business Critical"},{"label":"D","en":"Azure SQL Managed Instance Business Critical","ko":"Azure SQL Managed Instance Business Critical"}],"answers":["C"]},{"n":121,"id":null,"type":"dropdown","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You have an Azure subscription that includes 50 Azure SQL databases.\n\nYou create an Azure Resource Manager (ARM) template named Template1 that enables Transparent Data Encryption (TDE).\n\nYou need to create an Azure Policy definition named Policy1 that uses Template1 to enable TDE for all noncompliant Azure SQL databases.\n\nHow should you configure Policy1?","stemKo":"You have an Azure subscription that includes 50 Azure SQL databases.\n\nYou create an Azure Resource Manager (ARM) template named Template1 that enables Transparent Data Encryption (TDE).\n\nYou need to create an Azure Policy definition named Policy1 that uses Template1 to enable TDE for all noncompliant Azure SQL databases.\n\nHow should you configure Policy1?","explanationEn":"DeployIfNotExists evaluates compliance and deploys the ARM template when the required configuration is absent. A DeployIfNotExists policy definition must include the required RBAC role IDs in roleDefinitionIds. The managed identity that performs remediation belongs to the policy assignment and receives those roles at the assignment scope.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure Policy deployIfNotExists effect](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/governance/policy/concepts/effect-deploy-if-not-exists)","explanationKo":"DeployIfNotExists evaluates compliance and deploys the ARM template when the required configuration is absent. A DeployIfNotExists policy definition must include the required RBAC role IDs in roleDefinitionIds. The managed identity that performs remediation belongs to the policy assignment and receives those roles at the assignment scope.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure Policy deployIfNotExists effect](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/governance/policy/concepts/effect-deploy-if-not-exists)","learnMore":[],"blanks":[{"id":"effect","labelEn":"Set available effects to:","labelKo":"Set available effects to:","options":[{"en":"DeployIfNotExists","ko":"DeployIfNotExists"},{"en":"EnforceRegoPolicy","ko":"EnforceRegoPolicy"},{"en":"Modify","ko":"Modify"}],"answer":"DeployIfNotExists"},{"id":"definition","labelEn":"Include in the definition:","labelKo":"Include in the definition:","options":[{"en":"The identity required to perform the remediation task","ko":"The identity required to perform the remediation task"},{"en":"The scopes of the policy assignments","ko":"The scopes of the policy assignments"},{"en":"The role-based access control (RBAC) roles required to perform the remediation task","ko":"The role-based access control (RBAC) roles required to perform the remediation task"}],"answer":"The role-based access control (RBAC) roles required to perform the remediation task"}],"template":""},{"n":122,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You need to recommend a solution for generating a monthly report of all new Azure Resource Manager (ARM) resource deployments in your Azure subscription.\n\nWhat should the recommendation include?","stemKo":"You need to recommend a solution for generating a monthly report of all new Azure Resource Manager (ARM) resource deployments in your Azure subscription.\n\nWhat should the recommendation include?","explanationEn":"Azure Log Analytics can store exported Azure Activity Log records in the `AzureActivity` table and query them with KQL. Azure Activity Logs record ARM control-plane operations, and `Microsoft.Resources/deployments/write` can be filtered to report new deployments during each month.\n\n**Learn more:** [Activity log in Azure Monitor](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-monitor/platform/activity-log) · [Queries for the AzureActivity table](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-monitor/reference/queries/azureactivity)","explanationKo":"Azure Log Analytics can store exported Azure Activity Log records in the `AzureActivity` table and query them with KQL. Azure Activity Logs record ARM control-plane operations, and `Microsoft.Resources/deployments/write` can be filtered to report new deployments during each month.\n\n**Learn more:** [Activity log in Azure Monitor](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-monitor/platform/activity-log) · [Queries for the AzureActivity table](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-monitor/reference/queries/azureactivity)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Azure Arc","ko":"Azure Arc"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure Log Analytics","ko":"Azure Log Analytics"},{"label":"C","en":"Application insights","ko":"Application insights"},{"label":"D","en":"Azure Monitor action groups","ko":"Azure Monitor action groups"}],"answers":["B"]},{"n":123,"id":null,"type":"dropdown","topic":"Design data storage solutions","topicKo":"데이터 저장소 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"How should the migrated databases DB1 and DB2 be implemented in Azure?","stemKo":"How should the migrated databases DB1 and DB2 be implemented in Azure?","explanationEn":"An Azure SQL Database elastic pool lets multiple databases share provisioned resources, reducing management overhead and cost. A zone-redundant Business Critical elastic pool places replicas across availability zones, supports automatic failover, and uses local SSD storage for low I/O latency.\n\n**Learn more:** [Reliability in Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/reliability/reliability-sql-database) · [Design disaster recovery solutions - Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/database/disaster-recovery-strategies-for-applications-with-elastic-pool)","explanationKo":"An Azure SQL Database elastic pool lets multiple databases share provisioned resources, reducing management overhead and cost. A zone-redundant Business Critical elastic pool places replicas across availability zones, supports automatic failover, and uses local SSD storage for low I/O latency.\n\n**Learn more:** [Reliability in Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/reliability/reliability-sql-database) · [Design disaster recovery solutions - Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/database/disaster-recovery-strategies-for-applications-with-elastic-pool)","learnMore":[],"blanks":[{"id":"database","labelEn":"Database:","labelKo":"Database:","options":[{"en":"A single Azure SQL database","ko":"A single Azure SQL database"},{"en":"Azure SQL Managed Instance","ko":"Azure SQL Managed Instance"},{"en":"An Azure SQL Database elastic pool","ko":"An Azure SQL Database elastic pool"}],"answer":"An Azure SQL Database elastic pool"},{"id":"service_tier","labelEn":"Service tier:","labelKo":"Service tier:","options":[{"en":"Hyperscale","ko":"Hyperscale"},{"en":"Business Critical","ko":"Business Critical"},{"en":"General Purpose","ko":"General Purpose"}],"answer":"Business Critical"}],"template":""},{"n":124,"id":null,"type":"dropdown","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":["assets/1783709612044-cqxxzg70.png"],"stemEn":"You have an Azure subscription containing the resources in the following table:\n\n[[IMG1]]\n\nLog files from App1 are registered to App1Logs. An average of 120 GB of log data is ingested each day.\n\nAn Azure Monitor alert is configured to trigger when the App1 logs contain error messages.\n\nYou need to minimize the Log Analytics costs associated with App1. The solution must meet these requirements:\n\n- Ensure that all log files from App1 are ingested into App1Logs.\n- Minimize the impact on the Azure Monitor alert.\n\nWhich resource should be modified, and which modification should be made?","stemKo":"You have an Azure subscription containing the resources in the following table:\n\n[[IMG1]]\n\nLog files from App1 are registered to App1Logs. An average of 120 GB of log data is ingested each day.\n\nAn Azure Monitor alert is configured to trigger when the App1 logs contain error messages.\n\nYou need to minimize the Log Analytics costs associated with App1. The solution must meet these requirements:\n\n- Ensure that all log files from App1 are ingested into App1Logs.\n- Minimize the impact on the Azure Monitor alert.\n\nWhich resource should be modified, and which modification should be made?","explanationEn":"A Log Analytics workspace commitment tier provides discounted ingestion pricing at an agreed daily volume while retaining Analytics Logs capabilities, including alert-query support. Moving App1Logs to Basic Logs can limit alerting capabilities, and a daily cap can halt further data ingestion after the cap is reached; either conflicts with the stated requirements.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure Monitor Logs cost calculations and options](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-monitor/logs/cost-logs) · [Configure table plans in Azure Monitor Logs](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-monitor/logs/data-platform-logs#table-plans)","explanationKo":"A Log Analytics workspace commitment tier provides discounted ingestion pricing at an agreed daily volume while retaining Analytics Logs capabilities, including alert-query support. Moving App1Logs to Basic Logs can limit alerting capabilities, and a daily cap can halt further data ingestion after the cap is reached; either conflicts with the stated requirements.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure Monitor Logs cost calculations and options](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-monitor/logs/cost-logs) · [Configure table plans in Azure Monitor Logs](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-monitor/logs/data-platform-logs#table-plans)","learnMore":[],"blanks":[{"id":"resource","labelEn":"Resource:","labelKo":"Resource:","options":[{"en":"App1","ko":"App1"},{"en":"App1Logs","ko":"App1Logs"},{"en":"Workspace1","ko":"Workspace1"}],"answer":"Workspace1"},{"id":"modification","labelEn":"Modification:","labelKo":"Modification:","options":[{"en":"Change to a commitment pricing tier","ko":"Change to a commitment pricing tier"},{"en":"Change to the Basic Logs data plan.","ko":"Change to the Basic Logs data plan."},{"en":"Set a daily cap.","ko":"Set a daily cap."}],"answer":"Change to a commitment pricing tier"}],"template":""},{"n":125,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You need to recommend a solution for generating a monthly report of every new Azure Resource Manager (ARM) resource deployment in your Azure subscription.\n\nWhat should the recommendation include?","stemKo":"You need to recommend a solution for generating a monthly report of every new Azure Resource Manager (ARM) resource deployment in your Azure subscription.\n\nWhat should the recommendation include?","explanationEn":"Azure Log Analytics can store Azure Activity Log data in the `AzureActivity` table and query it with KQL. Azure Activity Log records Azure Resource Manager control-plane operations, including deployments, so it can be filtered to report new deployments over each monthly period.\n\n**Learn more:** [Activity log in Azure Monitor](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-monitor/platform/activity-log) · [Example log table queries for AzureActivity](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-monitor/reference/queries/azureactivity)","explanationKo":"Azure Log Analytics can store Azure Activity Log data in the `AzureActivity` table and query it with KQL. Azure Activity Log records Azure Resource Manager control-plane operations, including deployments, so it can be filtered to report new deployments over each monthly period.\n\n**Learn more:** [Activity log in Azure Monitor](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-monitor/platform/activity-log) · [Example log table queries for AzureActivity](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-monitor/reference/queries/azureactivity)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Azure Log Analytics","ko":"Azure Log Analytics"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure Arc","ko":"Azure Arc"},{"label":"C","en":"Azure Analysis Services","ko":"Azure Analysis Services"},{"label":"D","en":"Application Insights","ko":"Application Insights"}],"answers":["A"]},{"n":126,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design infrastructure solutions","topicKo":"인프라 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You are designing an app that will have two components. The components will communicate by sending messages through a queue.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that processes the messages by using a First in, First out (FIFO) pattern.\n\nWhat should be included in the recommendation?","stemKo":"You are designing an app that will have two components. The components will communicate by sending messages through a queue.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that processes the messages by using a First in, First out (FIFO) pattern.\n\nWhat should be included in the recommendation?","explanationEn":"Azure Service Bus sessions provide ordered processing for a sequence of related messages and are the required mechanism for guaranteed FIFO processing. Set the same session ID for messages that belong to the same ordered sequence. Azure Storage queues can occasionally deliver messages out of order, and Service Bus partitioning does not itself provide the FIFO processing guarantee.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure Service Bus message sessions](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/service-bus-messaging/message-sessions) · [Compare Azure Storage queues and Service Bus queues](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-in/azure/service-bus-messaging/service-bus-azure-and-service-bus-queues-compared-contrasted)","explanationKo":"Azure Service Bus sessions provide ordered processing for a sequence of related messages and are the required mechanism for guaranteed FIFO processing. Set the same session ID for messages that belong to the same ordered sequence. Azure Storage queues can occasionally deliver messages out of order, and Service Bus partitioning does not itself provide the FIFO processing guarantee.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure Service Bus message sessions](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/service-bus-messaging/message-sessions) · [Compare Azure Storage queues and Service Bus queues](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-in/azure/service-bus-messaging/service-bus-azure-and-service-bus-queues-compared-contrasted)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"storage queues with a custom metadata setting","ko":"storage queues with a custom metadata setting"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure Service Bus queues with partitioning enabled","ko":"Azure Service Bus queues with partitioning enabled"},{"label":"C","en":"Azure Service Bus queues with sessions enabled","ko":"Azure Service Bus queues with sessions enabled"},{"label":"D","en":"storage queues with a stored access policy","ko":"storage queues with a stored access policy"}],"answers":["C"]},{"n":127,"id":null,"type":"dropdown","topic":"Design infrastructure solutions","topicKo":"인프라 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"HOTSPOT -\n\nYou are assessing whether Azure Traffic Manager and Azure Application Gateway can meet the connection requirements for App1.\n\nWhat is the minimum number of instances needed for each service?","stemKo":"HOTSPOT -\n\nYou are assessing whether Azure Traffic Manager and Azure Application Gateway can meet the connection requirements for App1.\n\nWhat is the minimum number of instances needed for each service?","explanationEn":"One Azure Traffic Manager profile supplies DNS-based routing to the configured endpoints. Two Azure Application Gateway instances provide gateway endpoints in the two required locations.","explanationKo":"One Azure Traffic Manager profile supplies DNS-based routing to the configured endpoints. Two Azure Application Gateway instances provide gateway endpoints in the two required locations.","learnMore":[],"blanks":[{"id":"traffic_manager","labelEn":"Azure Traffic Manager:","labelKo":"Azure Traffic Manager:","options":[{"en":"1","ko":"1"},{"en":"2","ko":"2"},{"en":"3","ko":"3"},{"en":"6","ko":"6"}],"answer":"1"},{"id":"application_gateway","labelEn":"Azure Application Gateway:","labelKo":"Azure Application Gateway:","options":[{"en":"1","ko":"1"},{"en":"2","ko":"2"},{"en":"3","ko":"3"},{"en":"6","ko":"6"}],"answer":"2"}],"template":""},{"n":129,"id":null,"type":"drag_drop","topic":"Design business continuity solutions","topicKo":"업무 연속성 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"Your company identifies these business-continuity and disaster-recovery objectives for virtual machines that host sales, finance, and reporting applications in the on-premises data center:\n\n- The sales application must be able to fail over to a second on-premises data center.\n- The reporting application must be able to recover point-in-time data at daily granularity. The RTO is eight hours.\n- The finance application requires data retention for seven years. If a disaster occurs, the application must be able to run from Azure. The recovery time objective (RTO) is 10 minutes.\n\nYou need to recommend services that meet the business-continuity and disaster-recovery objectives while minimizing costs.\n\nWhat should you recommend for each application?\n\nEach service may be used once, more than once, or not at all.","stemKo":"Your company identifies these business-continuity and disaster-recovery objectives for virtual machines that host sales, finance, and reporting applications in the on-premises data center:\n\n- The sales application must be able to fail over to a second on-premises data center.\n- The reporting application must be able to recover point-in-time data at daily granularity. The RTO is eight hours.\n- The finance application requires data retention for seven years. If a disaster occurs, the application must be able to run from Azure. The recovery time objective (RTO) is 10 minutes.\n\nYou need to recommend services that meet the business-continuity and disaster-recovery objectives while minimizing costs.\n\nWhat should you recommend for each application?\n\nEach service may be used once, more than once, or not at all.","explanationEn":"Azure Site Recovery replicates workloads and orchestrates failover, so it alone is the least-cost fit for sales. Azure Backup creates recovery points and supports scheduled retention, satisfying reporting’s daily point-in-time recovery need. Finance requires both seven-year backup retention and disaster-recovery failover to Azure, so it needs Azure Backup together with Azure Site Recovery.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure Site Recovery documentation](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/site-recovery/) · [Azure Backup service documentation](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/backup/)","explanationKo":"Azure Site Recovery replicates workloads and orchestrates failover, so it alone is the least-cost fit for sales. Azure Backup creates recovery points and supports scheduled retention, satisfying reporting’s daily point-in-time recovery need. Finance requires both seven-year backup retention and disaster-recovery failover to Azure, so it needs Azure Backup together with Azure Site Recovery.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure Site Recovery documentation](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/site-recovery/) · [Azure Backup service documentation](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/backup/)","learnMore":[],"items":[{"en":"Azure Backup only","ko":"Azure Backup only"},{"en":"Azure Site Recovery and Azure Backup","ko":"Azure Site Recovery and Azure Backup"},{"en":"Azure Site Recovery only","ko":"Azure Site Recovery only"}],"slots":[{"id":"sales","labelEn":"Sales:","labelKo":"Sales:","answer":"Azure Site Recovery only"},{"id":"finance","labelEn":"Finance:","labelKo":"Finance:","answer":"Azure Site Recovery and Azure Backup"},{"id":"reporting","labelEn":"Reporting:","labelKo":"Reporting:","answer":"Azure Backup only"}],"reuse":true},{"n":130,"id":null,"type":"dropdown","topic":"Design data storage solutions","topicKo":"데이터 저장소 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You have an Azure subscription.\n\nYou must deploy a solution that provides point-in-time restore for blobs in storage accounts with blob versioning and blob soft delete enabled.\n\nWhich blob type should you create, and what should you enable for the accounts?","stemKo":"You have an Azure subscription.\n\nYou must deploy a solution that provides point-in-time restore for blobs in storage accounts with blob versioning and blob soft delete enabled.\n\nWhich blob type should you create, and what should you enable for the accounts?","explanationEn":"Point-in-time restore supports block blobs only. It requires soft delete, blob versioning, and the change feed; with the first two already enabled, enable the change feed.\n\n**Learn more:** [Point-in-time restore for block blobs - Azure Storage](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/blobs/point-in-time-restore-overview) · [Change feed in Blob Storage - Azure Storage](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/blobs/storage-blob-change-feed)","explanationKo":"Point-in-time restore supports block blobs only. It requires soft delete, blob versioning, and the change feed; with the first two already enabled, enable the change feed.\n\n**Learn more:** [Point-in-time restore for block blobs - Azure Storage](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/blobs/point-in-time-restore-overview) · [Change feed in Blob Storage - Azure Storage](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/blobs/storage-blob-change-feed)","learnMore":[],"blanks":[{"id":"blob_type","labelEn":"Blob type:","labelKo":"Blob type:","options":[{"en":"Append","ko":"Append"},{"en":"Block","ko":"Block"},{"en":"Page","ko":"Page"}],"answer":"Block"},{"id":"enable","labelEn":"Enable:","labelKo":"Enable:","options":[{"en":"A stored access policy","ko":"A stored access policy"},{"en":"Immutable blob storage","ko":"Immutable blob storage"},{"en":"Object replication","ko":"Object replication"},{"en":"The change feed","ko":"The change feed"}],"answer":"The change feed"}],"template":""},{"n":131,"id":null,"type":"dropdown","topic":"Design data storage solutions","topicKo":"데이터 저장소 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You have an Azure subscription containing an Azure SQL Managed Instance that stores employee details, including social security numbers and phone numbers.\n\nYou must configure the managed instance to meet these requirements:\n\n- The helpdesk team can view only the final four digits of an employee’s phone number.\n- Cloud administrators are unable to view employees’ social security numbers.\n\nWhat should you enable for each column in the managed instance?","stemKo":"You have an Azure subscription containing an Azure SQL Managed Instance that stores employee details, including social security numbers and phone numbers.\n\nYou must configure the managed instance to meet these requirements:\n\n- The helpdesk team can view only the final four digits of an employee’s phone number.\n- Cloud administrators are unable to view employees’ social security numbers.\n\nWhat should you enable for each column in the managed instance?","explanationEn":"Dynamic data masking supports a partial mask that exposes only the last four characters to users without unmask permission. Always Encrypted protects sensitive column values from database and cloud administrators unless they possess access to the column master key; encryption and decryption occur in the client driver. TDE protects data at rest, not from administrators querying decrypted data.\n\n**Learn more:** [Dynamic Data Masking - Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/database/dynamic-data-masking-overview?view=azuresql) · [Always Encrypted - Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/database/always-encrypted-overview?view=azuresql)","explanationKo":"Dynamic data masking supports a partial mask that exposes only the last four characters to users without unmask permission. Always Encrypted protects sensitive column values from database and cloud administrators unless they possess access to the column master key; encryption and decryption occur in the client driver. TDE protects data at rest, not from administrators querying decrypted data.\n\n**Learn more:** [Dynamic Data Masking - Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/database/dynamic-data-masking-overview?view=azuresql) · [Always Encrypted - Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/database/always-encrypted-overview?view=azuresql)","learnMore":[],"blanks":[{"id":"phone_numbers","labelEn":"Phone numbers:","labelKo":"Phone numbers:","options":[{"en":"Always Encrypted","ko":"Always Encrypted"},{"en":"Column encryption","ko":"Column encryption"},{"en":"Dynamic data masking","ko":"Dynamic data masking"},{"en":"Transparent Data Encryption (TDE)","ko":"Transparent Data Encryption (TDE)"}],"answer":"Dynamic data masking"},{"id":"social_security_numbers","labelEn":"Social security numbers:","labelKo":"Social security numbers:","options":[{"en":"Always Encrypted","ko":"Always Encrypted"},{"en":"Column encryption","ko":"Column encryption"},{"en":"Dynamic data masking","ko":"Dynamic data masking"},{"en":"Transparent Data Encryption (TDE)","ko":"Transparent Data Encryption (TDE)"}],"answer":"Always Encrypted"}],"template":""},{"n":132,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design business continuity solutions","topicKo":"업무 연속성 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You have an on-premises network and an Azure subscription. The on-premises network includes several branch offices.\n\nA Toronto branch office contains a virtual machine named VM1 that is configured as a file server. Users in all offices access the shared files on VM1.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that ensures users can access the shared files as quickly as possible if the Toronto branch office becomes inaccessible.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","stemKo":"You have an on-premises network and an Azure subscription. The on-premises network includes several branch offices.\n\nA Toronto branch office contains a virtual machine named VM1 that is configured as a file server. Users in all offices access the shared files on VM1.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that ensures users can access the shared files as quickly as possible if the Toronto branch office becomes inaccessible.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","explanationEn":"Azure File Sync synchronizes Windows Server data with an Azure file share, which is the cloud endpoint for the sync group. The Azure file share provides an available cloud copy of the shared data when the Toronto file server cannot be reached, while Azure File Sync can also provide synchronized local server endpoints for branch-office access.\n\n**Learn more:** [Extend Windows File Servers with Azure File Sync](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/file-sync/file-sync-extend-servers) · [Manage Registered Servers with Azure File Sync](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/file-sync/file-sync-server-registration)","explanationKo":"Azure File Sync synchronizes Windows Server data with an Azure file share, which is the cloud endpoint for the sync group. The Azure file share provides an available cloud copy of the shared data when the Toronto file server cannot be reached, while Azure File Sync can also provide synchronized local server endpoints for branch-office access.\n\n**Learn more:** [Extend Windows File Servers with Azure File Sync](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/file-sync/file-sync-extend-servers) · [Manage Registered Servers with Azure File Sync](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/file-sync/file-sync-server-registration)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"a Recovery Services vault and Windows Server Backup","ko":"a Recovery Services vault and Windows Server Backup"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure blob containers and Azure File Sync","ko":"Azure blob containers and Azure File Sync"},{"label":"C","en":"a Recovery Services vault and Azure Backup","ko":"a Recovery Services vault and Azure Backup"},{"label":"D","en":"an Azure file share and Azure File Sync","ko":"an Azure file share and Azure File Sync"}],"answers":["D"]},{"n":133,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design data storage solutions","topicKo":"데이터 저장소 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You must recommend a data storage solution that satisfies these requirements:\n\n- Ensures applications can access the data through a REST connection\n- Hosts 20 independent tables with different sizes and usage patterns\n- Automatically replicates data to a second Azure region\n- Minimizes costs\n\nWhat should you recommend?","stemKo":"You must recommend a data storage solution that satisfies these requirements:\n\n- Ensures applications can access the data through a REST connection\n- Hosts 20 independent tables with different sizes and usage patterns\n- Automatically replicates data to a second Azure region\n- Minimizes costs\n\nWhat should you recommend?","explanationEn":"Azure Table Storage provides a REST API for table data and supports geo-redundant storage (GRS), which asynchronously replicates the storage account’s data to a secondary Azure region. GRS meets the replication requirement at lower cost than RA-GRS because it does not add read access to the secondary region.\n\n**Learn more:** [Table Storage REST API](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/rest/api/storageservices/table-service-rest-api) · [Data redundancy - Azure Storage](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/common/storage-redundancy)","explanationKo":"Azure Table Storage provides a REST API for table data and supports geo-redundant storage (GRS), which asynchronously replicates the storage account’s data to a secondary Azure region. GRS meets the replication requirement at lower cost than RA-GRS because it does not add read access to the secondary region.\n\n**Learn more:** [Table Storage REST API](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/rest/api/storageservices/table-service-rest-api) · [Data redundancy - Azure Storage](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/common/storage-redundancy)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"an Azure SQL Database elastic pool that uses active geo-replication","ko":"an Azure SQL Database elastic pool that uses active geo-replication"},{"label":"B","en":"tables in an Azure Storage account that use geo-redundant storage (GRS)","ko":"tables in an Azure Storage account that use geo-redundant storage (GRS)"},{"label":"C","en":"tables in an Azure Storage account that use read-access geo-redundant storage (RA-GRS)","ko":"tables in an Azure Storage account that use read-access geo-redundant storage (RA-GRS)"},{"label":"D","en":"an Azure SQL database that uses active geo-replication","ko":"an Azure SQL database that uses active geo-replication"}],"answers":["B"]},{"n":134,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design infrastructure solutions","topicKo":"인프라 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You are developing a sales application that will include several Azure cloud services and manage distinct parts of a transaction. Different cloud services will process customer orders, billing, payment, inventory, and shipping.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that lets the cloud services asynchronously exchange transaction information by using XML messages.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","stemKo":"You are developing a sales application that will include several Azure cloud services and manage distinct parts of a transaction. Different cloud services will process customer orders, billing, payment, inventory, and shipping.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that lets the cloud services asynchronously exchange transaction information by using XML messages.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","explanationEn":"Azure Queue Storage provides durable queues that let distributed cloud-service components communicate asynchronously and process transaction messages independently. Queue messages support UTF-8 content compatible with XML requests, making it suitable for XML-based transaction information.\n\n**Learn more:** [Introduction to Azure Queue Storage](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/queues/storage-queues-introduction) · [Azure Queue Storage .NET quickstart](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/queues/storage-quickstart-queues-dotnet)","explanationKo":"Azure Queue Storage provides durable queues that let distributed cloud-service components communicate asynchronously and process transaction messages independently. Queue messages support UTF-8 content compatible with XML requests, making it suitable for XML-based transaction information.\n\n**Learn more:** [Introduction to Azure Queue Storage](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/queues/storage-queues-introduction) · [Azure Queue Storage .NET quickstart](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/queues/storage-quickstart-queues-dotnet)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Azure Application Gateway","ko":"Azure Application Gateway"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure Queue Storage","ko":"Azure Queue Storage"},{"label":"C","en":"Azure Data Lake","ko":"Azure Data Lake"},{"label":"D","en":"Azure Traffic Manager","ko":"Azure Traffic Manager"}],"answers":["B"]},{"n":135,"id":null,"type":"dropdown","topic":"Design data storage solutions","topicKo":"데이터 저장소 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You have an on-premises database that you intend to migrate to Azure.\n\nDesign the database architecture to meet these requirements:\n\n- Support scaling up and down.\n- Support geo-redundant backups.\n- Support a database up to 75 TB.\n- Be optimized for online transaction processing (OLTP).\n\nWhat should the design include?","stemKo":"You have an on-premises database that you intend to migrate to Azure.\n\nDesign the database architecture to meet these requirements:\n\n- Support scaling up and down.\n- Support geo-redundant backups.\n- Support a database up to 75 TB.\n- Be optimized for online transaction processing (OLTP).\n\nWhat should the design include?","explanationEn":"Azure SQL Database Hyperscale supports workloads ranging from OLTP to analytics, can scale compute independently, and supports databases up to 128 TB. Geo-restore is available when geo-redundant storage is chosen, which meets the geo-redundant backup requirement.\n\n**Learn more:** [What is the Hyperscale service tier?](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/database/service-tier-hyperscale?view=azuresql) · [Create a Hyperscale Database - Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/database/hyperscale-database-create-quickstart?view=azuresql)","explanationKo":"Azure SQL Database Hyperscale supports workloads ranging from OLTP to analytics, can scale compute independently, and supports databases up to 128 TB. Geo-restore is available when geo-redundant storage is chosen, which meets the geo-redundant backup requirement.\n\n**Learn more:** [What is the Hyperscale service tier?](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/database/service-tier-hyperscale?view=azuresql) · [Create a Hyperscale Database - Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/database/hyperscale-database-create-quickstart?view=azuresql)","learnMore":[],"blanks":[{"id":"service","labelEn":"Service:","labelKo":"Service:","options":[{"en":"Azure SQL Database","ko":"Azure SQL Database"},{"en":"Azure SQL Managed Instance","ko":"Azure SQL Managed Instance"},{"en":"Azure Synapse Analytics","ko":"Azure Synapse Analytics"},{"en":"SQL Server on Azure Virtual Machines","ko":"SQL Server on Azure Virtual Machines"}],"answer":"Azure SQL Database"},{"id":"service_tier","labelEn":"Service tier:","labelKo":"Service tier:","options":[{"en":"Basic","ko":"Basic"},{"en":"Business Critical","ko":"Business Critical"},{"en":"General Purpose","ko":"General Purpose"},{"en":"Hyperscale","ko":"Hyperscale"},{"en":"Premium","ko":"Premium"},{"en":"Standard","ko":"Standard"}],"answer":"Hyperscale"}],"template":""},{"n":136,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":["assets/1783708623350-sxniuf19.png"],"stemEn":"Your company has the divisions shown in the following table.\n\n[[IMG1]]\n\nSub1 contains an Azure App Service web app named App1. App1 uses Azure AD for single-tenant user authentication. Users from contoso.com can authenticate to App1.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that enables users in the fabrikam.com tenant to authenticate to App1.\n\nWhat should you recommend?","stemKo":"Your company has the divisions shown in the following table.\n\n[[IMG1]]\n\nSub1 contains an Azure App Service web app named App1. App1 uses Azure AD for single-tenant user authentication. Users from contoso.com can authenticate to App1.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that enables users in the fabrikam.com tenant to authenticate to App1.\n\nWhat should you recommend?","explanationEn":"Microsoft Entra entitlement management uses B2B collaboration to grant external users access to resources in another tenant. Fabrikam users can authenticate with their home-tenant identities while being represented as guest users in the Contoso tenant and assigned access to App1.\n\n**Learn more:** [Govern access for external users in entitlement management](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/id-governance/entitlement-management-external-users)","explanationKo":"Microsoft Entra entitlement management uses B2B collaboration to grant external users access to resources in another tenant. Fabrikam users can authenticate with their home-tenant identities while being represented as guest users in the Contoso tenant and assigned access to App1.\n\n**Learn more:** [Govern access for external users in entitlement management](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/id-governance/entitlement-management-external-users)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Configure Azure AD join.","ko":"Configure Azure AD join."},{"label":"B","en":"Configure Azure AD Identity Protection.","ko":"Configure Azure AD Identity Protection."},{"label":"C","en":"Use Azure AD entitlement management to govern external users.","ko":"Use Azure AD entitlement management to govern external users."},{"label":"D","en":"Configure assignments for the fabrikam.com users by using Azure AD Privileged Identity Management (PIM).","ko":"Configure assignments for the fabrikam.com users by using Azure AD Privileged Identity Management (PIM)."}],"answers":["C"]},{"n":137,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design data storage solutions","topicKo":"데이터 저장소 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You have 100 devices that write performance data to Azure Blob Storage.\n\nYou plan to store and analyze the performance data in an Azure SQL database.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that continually copies the performance data to the Azure SQL database.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","stemKo":"You have 100 devices that write performance data to Azure Blob Storage.\n\nYou plan to store and analyze the performance data in an Azure SQL database.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that continually copies the performance data to the Azure SQL database.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","explanationEn":"Azure Data Factory supports scheduled or triggered data-integration pipelines with Copy activity, including copying data from Azure Blob Storage to Azure SQL Database. This makes it suitable for continuously ingesting performance data as it arrives.\n\n**Learn more:** [Copy data from Azure Blob to Azure SQL Database using Azure Data Factory](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/data-factory/tutorial-copy-data-dot-net) · [Copy activity in Azure Data Factory](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/data-factory/copy-activity-overview)","explanationKo":"Azure Data Factory supports scheduled or triggered data-integration pipelines with Copy activity, including copying data from Azure Blob Storage to Azure SQL Database. This makes it suitable for continuously ingesting performance data as it arrives.\n\n**Learn more:** [Copy data from Azure Blob to Azure SQL Database using Azure Data Factory](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/data-factory/tutorial-copy-data-dot-net) · [Copy activity in Azure Data Factory](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/data-factory/copy-activity-overview)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Azure Data Factory","ko":"Azure Data Factory"},{"label":"B","en":"Data Migration Assistant (DMA)","ko":"Data Migration Assistant (DMA)"},{"label":"C","en":"Azure Data Box","ko":"Azure Data Box"},{"label":"D","en":"Azure Database Migration Service","ko":"Azure Database Migration Service"}],"answers":["A"]},{"n":138,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design business continuity solutions","topicKo":"업무 연속성 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You need to design a highly available Azure SQL database that fulfills these requirements:\n\n- Failover between database replicas must take place with no data loss.\n- The database must stay available if a zone outage occurs.\n- Costs must be kept to a minimum.\n\nWhich deployment option should be used?","stemKo":"You need to design a highly available Azure SQL database that fulfills these requirements:\n\n- Failover between database replicas must take place with no data loss.\n- The database must stay available if a zone outage occurs.\n- Costs must be kept to a minimum.\n\nWhich deployment option should be used?","explanationEn":"The Business Critical tier provides several synchronous high-availability replicas. When zone redundancy is enabled, those replicas are distributed across availability zones, so a surviving replica can become primary after a zone failure with zero loss of committed data. Because Business Critical already includes the replicas used for this configuration, enabling zone redundancy does not add a separate charge, unlike zone-redundant Managed Instance General Purpose. [Reliability in Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/reliability/reliability-sql-database)\n\n**Learn more:** [Reliability in Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/reliability/reliability-sql-database) · [Azure SQL Database vCore service tiers](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/database/service-tiers-sql-database-vcore?view=azuresql)","explanationKo":"The Business Critical tier provides several synchronous high-availability replicas. When zone redundancy is enabled, those replicas are distributed across availability zones, so a surviving replica can become primary after a zone failure with zero loss of committed data. Because Business Critical already includes the replicas used for this configuration, enabling zone redundancy does not add a separate charge, unlike zone-redundant Managed Instance General Purpose. [Reliability in Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/reliability/reliability-sql-database)\n\n**Learn more:** [Reliability in Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/reliability/reliability-sql-database) · [Azure SQL Database vCore service tiers](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/database/service-tiers-sql-database-vcore?view=azuresql)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Azure SQL Database Business Critical","ko":"Azure SQL Database Business Critical"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure SQL Database Basic","ko":"Azure SQL Database Basic"},{"label":"C","en":"Azure SQL Managed Instance General Purpose","ko":"Azure SQL Managed Instance General Purpose"},{"label":"D","en":"Azure SQL Database Hyperscale","ko":"Azure SQL Database Hyperscale"}],"answers":["A"]},{"n":139,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":["assets/1783706713371-e9isvnso.png"],"stemEn":"Your company has the infrastructure shown in the following table.\n\n[[IMG1]]\n\nThe on-premises Active Directory domain is synchronized with Azure Active Directory (Azure AD).\n\nServer1 runs an application named App1 that uses LDAP queries to validate user identities in the on-premises Active Directory domain.\n\nYou plan to migrate Server1 to a virtual machine in Subscription1.\n\nA company security policy requires that virtual machines and services deployed to Subscription1 be prevented from accessing the on-premises network.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that ensures App1 continues to function after the migration. The solution must comply with the security policy.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","stemKo":"Your company has the infrastructure shown in the following table.\n\n[[IMG1]]\n\nThe on-premises Active Directory domain is synchronized with Azure Active Directory (Azure AD).\n\nServer1 runs an application named App1 that uses LDAP queries to validate user identities in the on-premises Active Directory domain.\n\nYou plan to migrate Server1 to a virtual machine in Subscription1.\n\nA company security policy requires that virtual machines and services deployed to Subscription1 be prevented from accessing the on-premises network.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that ensures App1 continues to function after the migration. The solution must comply with the security policy.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","explanationEn":"Azure AD Domain Services (now Microsoft Entra Domain Services) supplies managed domain services, including LDAP, to Azure workloads. In a hybrid environment, on-premises AD DS identities synchronize to Microsoft Entra ID and are then automatically synchronized into the managed domain, allowing App1 to perform LDAP queries locally in Azure without access to the on-premises network.\n\n**Learn more:** [LDAP authentication with Microsoft Entra ID](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/architecture/auth-ldap) · [How objects and credentials are synchronized in Microsoft Entra Domain Services](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity/domain-services/synchronization)","explanationKo":"Azure AD Domain Services (now Microsoft Entra Domain Services) supplies managed domain services, including LDAP, to Azure workloads. In a hybrid environment, on-premises AD DS identities synchronize to Microsoft Entra ID and are then automatically synchronized into the managed domain, allowing App1 to perform LDAP queries locally in Azure without access to the on-premises network.\n\n**Learn more:** [LDAP authentication with Microsoft Entra ID](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/architecture/auth-ldap) · [How objects and credentials are synchronized in Microsoft Entra Domain Services](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity/domain-services/synchronization)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Azure AD Application Proxy","ko":"Azure AD Application Proxy"},{"label":"B","en":"the Active Directory Domain Services role on a virtual machine","ko":"the Active Directory Domain Services role on a virtual machine"},{"label":"C","en":"an Azure VPN gateway","ko":"an Azure VPN gateway"},{"label":"D","en":"Azure AD Domain Services (Azure AD DS)","ko":"Azure AD Domain Services (Azure AD DS)"}],"answers":["D"]},{"n":140,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You plan to deploy an application named App1 that will run on five Azure virtual machines. Additional virtual machines will be deployed later to run App1.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that meets the following requirements for the virtual machines running App1:\n\n- Ensure that the virtual machines can authenticate to Azure Active Directory (Azure AD) to access an Azure key vault, Azure Logic Apps instances, and an Azure SQL database.\n- Avoid assigning new roles and permissions for Azure services when additional virtual machines are deployed.\n- Avoid storing secrets and certificates on the virtual machines.\n- Minimize administrative effort for identity management.\n\nWhich type of identity should you include in the recommendation?","stemKo":"You plan to deploy an application named App1 that will run on five Azure virtual machines. Additional virtual machines will be deployed later to run App1.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that meets the following requirements for the virtual machines running App1:\n\n- Ensure that the virtual machines can authenticate to Azure Active Directory (Azure AD) to access an Azure key vault, Azure Logic Apps instances, and an Azure SQL database.\n- Avoid assigning new roles and permissions for Azure services when additional virtual machines are deployed.\n- Avoid storing secrets and certificates on the virtual machines.\n- Minimize administrative effort for identity management.\n\nWhich type of identity should you include in the recommendation?","explanationEn":"A user-assigned managed identity has an independent lifecycle and can be assigned to multiple Azure resources, including all App1 virtual machines. Granting the identity the required access once preserves the same permissions as additional virtual machines are assigned to it. Azure-managed identity tokens eliminate the need to store or manage client secrets and certificates on the virtual machines.\n\n**Learn more:** [Managed identities for Azure resources overview](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity/managed-identities-azure-resources/overview)","explanationKo":"A user-assigned managed identity has an independent lifecycle and can be assigned to multiple Azure resources, including all App1 virtual machines. Granting the identity the required access once preserves the same permissions as additional virtual machines are assigned to it. Azure-managed identity tokens eliminate the need to store or manage client secrets and certificates on the virtual machines.\n\n**Learn more:** [Managed identities for Azure resources overview](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity/managed-identities-azure-resources/overview)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"a system-assigned managed identity","ko":"a system-assigned managed identity"},{"label":"B","en":"a service principal that is configured to use a certificate","ko":"a service principal that is configured to use a certificate"},{"label":"C","en":"a service principal that is configured to use a client secret","ko":"a service principal that is configured to use a client secret"},{"label":"D","en":"a user-assigned managed identity","ko":"a user-assigned managed identity"}],"answers":["D"]},{"n":141,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design business continuity solutions","topicKo":"업무 연속성 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You must design a highly available Azure SQL database that satisfies these requirements:\n\n- Failover between database replicas must happen with no data loss.\n- The database must stay available if an availability zone experiences an outage.\n- Costs must be kept to a minimum.\n\nWhich deployment option should you use?","stemKo":"You must design a highly available Azure SQL database that satisfies these requirements:\n\n- Failover between database replicas must happen with no data loss.\n- The database must stay available if an availability zone experiences an outage.\n- Costs must be kept to a minimum.\n\nWhich deployment option should you use?","explanationEn":"Azure SQL Database Business Critical supports zone-redundant deployments that distribute replicas across availability zones and keep a synchronized replica available for failover. Azure SQL Database Standard does not support zone redundancy. For a database-only workload, Business Critical avoids the additional managed-instance deployment overhead and cost while meeting the required zero-data-loss, zone-resilient availability.\n\n**Learn more:** [Reliability in Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/reliability/reliability-sql-database) · [Availability Through Local and Zone Redundancy - Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/database/high-availability-sla-local-zone-redundancy?view=azuresql-db)","explanationKo":"Azure SQL Database Business Critical supports zone-redundant deployments that distribute replicas across availability zones and keep a synchronized replica available for failover. Azure SQL Database Standard does not support zone redundancy. For a database-only workload, Business Critical avoids the additional managed-instance deployment overhead and cost while meeting the required zero-data-loss, zone-resilient availability.\n\n**Learn more:** [Reliability in Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/reliability/reliability-sql-database) · [Availability Through Local and Zone Redundancy - Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/database/high-availability-sla-local-zone-redundancy?view=azuresql-db)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Azure SQL Database Business Critical","ko":"Azure SQL Database Business Critical"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure SQL Managed Instance Business Critical","ko":"Azure SQL Managed Instance Business Critical"},{"label":"C","en":"Azure SQL Database Standard","ko":"Azure SQL Database Standard"},{"label":"D","en":"Azure SQL Managed Instance General Purpose","ko":"Azure SQL Managed Instance General Purpose"}],"answers":["A"]},{"n":142,"id":null,"type":"dropdown","topic":"Design data storage solutions","topicKo":"데이터 저장소 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You plan to develop a new app that will store business-critical data. The app must meet these requirements:\n\n- Prevent newly stored data from being modified for one year.\n- Maximize data resiliency.\n- Minimize read latency.\n\nWhich storage solution should you recommend for the app?","stemKo":"You plan to develop a new app that will store business-critical data. The app must meet these requirements:\n\n- Prevent newly stored data from being modified for one year.\n- Maximize data resiliency.\n- Minimize read latency.\n\nWhich storage solution should you recommend for the app?","explanationEn":"Immutable (time-based retention) blob storage is supported on both standard and premium performance tiers, so it does not distinguish between the account type options here; the deciding requirement is minimizing read latency. Premium block blob storage accounts are backed by SSD-based hardware optimized for high throughput and low, consistent latency, making Premium block blobs the correct storage account type rather than either standard general-purpose tier. Zone-redundant storage (ZRS) synchronously replicates data across three availability zones in the primary region, maximizing resiliency without the added cost and latency of geo-replicated options, and is supported alongside immutable storage on premium block blob accounts.\n\n**Learn more:** [Store business-critical data with immutable storage](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/blobs/immutable-storage-overview) · [Azure Storage redundancy](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/common/storage-redundancy)","explanationKo":"Immutable (time-based retention) blob storage is supported on both standard and premium performance tiers, so it does not distinguish between the account type options here; the deciding requirement is minimizing read latency. Premium block blob storage accounts are backed by SSD-based hardware optimized for high throughput and low, consistent latency, making Premium block blobs the correct storage account type rather than either standard general-purpose tier. Zone-redundant storage (ZRS) synchronously replicates data across three availability zones in the primary region, maximizing resiliency without the added cost and latency of geo-replicated options, and is supported alongside immutable storage on premium block blob accounts.\n\n**Learn more:** [Store business-critical data with immutable storage](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/blobs/immutable-storage-overview) · [Azure Storage redundancy](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/common/storage-redundancy)","learnMore":[],"blanks":[{"id":"storage_account_type","labelEn":"Storage Account type:","labelKo":"Storage Account type:","options":[{"en":"Premium block blobs","ko":"Premium block blobs"},{"en":"Standard general-purpose v1","ko":"Standard general-purpose v1"},{"en":"Standard general-purpose v2","ko":"Standard general-purpose v2"}],"answer":"Premium block blobs"},{"id":"redundancy","labelEn":"Redundancy:","labelKo":"Redundancy:","options":[{"en":"Zone-redundant storage (ZRS)","ko":"Zone-redundant storage (ZRS)"},{"en":"Locally-redundant storage (LRS)","ko":"Locally-redundant storage (LRS)"}],"answer":"Zone-redundant storage (ZRS)"}],"template":""},{"n":143,"id":null,"type":"dropdown","topic":"Design infrastructure solutions","topicKo":"인프라 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You need to deploy an instance of SQL Server on Azure Virtual Machines. The solution must meet these requirements:\n\n- Support 15,000 disk IOPS.\n- Support SR-IOV.\n- Minimize costs.\n\nWhat should you include in the solution?","stemKo":"You need to deploy an instance of SQL Server on Azure Virtual Machines. The solution must meet these requirements:\n\n- Support 15,000 disk IOPS.\n- Support SR-IOV.\n- Minimize costs.\n\nWhat should you include in the solution?","explanationEn":"DS-series VMs are the cost-effective general-purpose choice and support Accelerated Networking, which enables SR-IOV. Premium SSD can provide the required disk IOPS, whereas Standard SSD is limited to 6,000 IOPS per disk; Ultra Disk is not needed and costs more.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure Accelerated Networking overview](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/virtual-network/accelerated-networking-overview) · [Select a disk type for Azure IaaS VMs](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/virtual-machines/disks-types)","explanationKo":"DS-series VMs are the cost-effective general-purpose choice and support Accelerated Networking, which enables SR-IOV. Premium SSD can provide the required disk IOPS, whereas Standard SSD is limited to 6,000 IOPS per disk; Ultra Disk is not needed and costs more.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure Accelerated Networking overview](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/virtual-network/accelerated-networking-overview) · [Select a disk type for Azure IaaS VMs](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/virtual-machines/disks-types)","learnMore":[],"blanks":[{"id":"virtual_machine_series","labelEn":"Virtual machine series:","labelKo":"Virtual machine series:","options":[{"en":"DS","ko":"DS"},{"en":"NC","ko":"NC"},{"en":"NV","ko":"NV"}],"answer":"DS"},{"id":"disk_type","labelEn":"Disk type:","labelKo":"Disk type:","options":[{"en":"Standard SSD","ko":"Standard SSD"},{"en":"Premium SSD","ko":"Premium SSD"},{"en":"Ultra Disk","ko":"Ultra Disk"}],"answer":"Premium SSD"}],"template":""},{"n":144,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":["assets/1783707484570-jeb2v6ng.jpg"],"stemEn":"Your company has the divisions shown in the following table.\n\n[[IMG1]]\n\nSub1 contains an Azure App Service web app named App1. App1 uses Azure AD for single-tenant user authentication. Users from contoso.com can authenticate to App1.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that enables users in the fabrikam.com tenant to authenticate to App1. What should you recommend?","stemKo":"Your company has the divisions shown in the following table.\n\n[[IMG1]]\n\nSub1 contains an Azure App Service web app named App1. App1 uses Azure AD for single-tenant user authentication. Users from contoso.com can authenticate to App1.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that enables users in the fabrikam.com tenant to authenticate to App1. What should you recommend?","explanationEn":"Azure AD entitlement management uses Microsoft Entra B2B to provide external users with a guest representation in the resource tenant and can assign governed access to enterprise applications through access packages. This enables fabrikam.com users to authenticate with their home tenant identities while receiving access to App1 in the contoso.com tenant.\n\n**Learn more:** [Govern access for external users in entitlement management](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/id-governance/entitlement-management-external-users) · [Create an access package in entitlement management](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/id-governance/entitlement-management-access-package-create)","explanationKo":"Azure AD entitlement management uses Microsoft Entra B2B to provide external users with a guest representation in the resource tenant and can assign governed access to enterprise applications through access packages. This enables fabrikam.com users to authenticate with their home tenant identities while receiving access to App1 in the contoso.com tenant.\n\n**Learn more:** [Govern access for external users in entitlement management](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/id-governance/entitlement-management-external-users) · [Create an access package in entitlement management](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/id-governance/entitlement-management-access-package-create)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Configure the Azure AD provisioning service.","ko":"Configure the Azure AD provisioning service."},{"label":"B","en":"Configure assignments for the fabrikam.com users by using Azure AD Privileged Identity Management (PIM).","ko":"Configure assignments for the fabrikam.com users by using Azure AD Privileged Identity Management (PIM)."},{"label":"C","en":"Use Azure AD entitlement management to govern external users.","ko":"Use Azure AD entitlement management to govern external users."},{"label":"D","en":"Configure Azure AD Identity Protection.","ko":"Configure Azure AD Identity Protection."}],"answers":["C"]},{"n":145,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design data storage solutions","topicKo":"데이터 저장소 설계","koMissing":true,"images":["assets/1783707859616-brfw04sf.png"],"stemEn":"Your company has an app named App1 that uses data from the on-premises Microsoft SQL Server databases shown in the following table.\n\n[[IMG1]]\n\nApp1 and its data are used only on the first day of each month. The data is not expected to grow by more than 3 percent annually.\n\nThe company is rewriting App1 as an Azure web app and plans to migrate all data to Azure.\n\nYou need to migrate the data to Azure SQL Database and ensure that the database is available only on the first day of every month.\n\nWhich service tier should you use?","stemKo":"Your company has an app named App1 that uses data from the on-premises Microsoft SQL Server databases shown in the following table.\n\n[[IMG1]]\n\nApp1 and its data are used only on the first day of each month. The data is not expected to grow by more than 3 percent annually.\n\nThe company is rewriting App1 as an Azure web app and plans to migrate all data to Azure.\n\nYou need to migrate the data to Azure SQL Database and ensure that the database is available only on the first day of every month.\n\nWhich service tier should you use?","explanationEn":"An Azure SQL Database serverless database can automatically pause during inactive periods, leaving only storage billed, and resume when activity returns. Auto-pause and auto-resume are supported only in the vCore-based General Purpose service tier, making it suitable for a workload used only one day per month.\n\n**Learn more:** [Serverless compute tier - Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/database/serverless-tier-overview?view=azuresql)","explanationKo":"An Azure SQL Database serverless database can automatically pause during inactive periods, leaving only storage billed, and resume when activity returns. Auto-pause and auto-resume are supported only in the vCore-based General Purpose service tier, making it suitable for a workload used only one day per month.\n\n**Learn more:** [Serverless compute tier - Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/database/serverless-tier-overview?view=azuresql)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"vCore-based General Purpose","ko":"vCore-based General Purpose"},{"label":"B","en":"DTU-based Standard","ko":"DTU-based Standard"},{"label":"C","en":"vCore-based Business Critical","ko":"vCore-based Business Critical"},{"label":"D","en":"DTU-based Basic","ko":"DTU-based Basic"}],"answers":["A"]},{"n":146,"id":null,"type":"dropdown","topic":"Design infrastructure solutions","topicKo":"인프라 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You have an Azure App Service web app named Webapp1 that connects to an Azure SQL database named DB1. Webapp1 and DB1 are deployed in the East US Azure region.\n\nEnsure that all traffic between Webapp1 and DB1 travels over a private connection.\n\nWhat should you do?","stemKo":"You have an Azure App Service web app named Webapp1 that connects to an Azure SQL database named DB1. Webapp1 and DB1 are deployed in the East US Azure region.\n\nEnsure that all traffic between Webapp1 and DB1 travels over a private connection.\n\nWhat should you do?","explanationEn":"App Service VNet Integration needs a dedicated delegated subnet, and an Azure SQL private endpoint uses another subnet. A private DNS zone linked to the virtual network resolves the Azure SQL private-link hostname to the private endpoint IP address, so database traffic remains private.\n\n**Learn more:** [Integrate your app with an Azure virtual network](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/app-service/overview-vnet-integration) · [Azure Private Endpoint private DNS zone values](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/private-link/private-endpoint-dns)","explanationKo":"App Service VNet Integration needs a dedicated delegated subnet, and an Azure SQL private endpoint uses another subnet. A private DNS zone linked to the virtual network resolves the Azure SQL private-link hostname to the private endpoint IP address, so database traffic remains private.\n\n**Learn more:** [Integrate your app with an Azure virtual network](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/app-service/overview-vnet-integration) · [Azure Private Endpoint private DNS zone values](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/private-link/private-endpoint-dns)","learnMore":[],"blanks":[{"id":"subnets","labelEn":"Create a virtual network that contains at least:","labelKo":"Create a virtual network that contains at least:","options":[{"en":"1 subnet","ko":"1 subnet"},{"en":"2 subnets","ko":"2 subnets"},{"en":"3 subnets","ko":"3 subnets"}],"answer":"2 subnets"},{"id":"dns","labelEn":"From the virtual network, configure name resolution to use:","labelKo":"From the virtual network, configure name resolution to use:","options":[{"en":"A private DNS zone","ko":"A private DNS zone"},{"en":"A public DNS zone","ko":"A public DNS zone"},{"en":"The Azure DNS Private Resolver","ko":"The Azure DNS Private Resolver"}],"answer":"A private DNS zone"}],"template":""},{"n":147,"id":null,"type":"dropdown","topic":"Design data storage solutions","topicKo":"데이터 저장소 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You plan to create an Azure Storage account that will host file shares. The shares will be accessed from transaction-intensive on-premises applications.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that minimizes latency when accessing the file shares and provides the highest level of resiliency for the selected storage tier.","stemKo":"You plan to create an Azure Storage account that will host file shares. The shares will be accessed from transaction-intensive on-premises applications.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that minimizes latency when accessing the file shares and provides the highest level of resiliency for the selected storage tier.","explanationEn":"Premium Azure Files uses SSD media and is recommended for IO-intensive workloads requiring low latency. Premium file shares support LRS or ZRS, not GRS; ZRS synchronously stores replicas across three availability zones, providing greater resiliency than LRS.\n\n**Learn more:** [Reliability in Azure Files](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/reliability/reliability-storage-files) · [Plan for an Azure Files deployment](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/files/storage-files-planning)","explanationKo":"Premium Azure Files uses SSD media and is recommended for IO-intensive workloads requiring low latency. Premium file shares support LRS or ZRS, not GRS; ZRS synchronously stores replicas across three availability zones, providing greater resiliency than LRS.\n\n**Learn more:** [Reliability in Azure Files](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/reliability/reliability-storage-files) · [Plan for an Azure Files deployment](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/files/storage-files-planning)","learnMore":[],"blanks":[{"id":"storage_tier","labelEn":"Storage tier:","labelKo":"Storage tier:","options":[{"en":"Hot","ko":"Hot"},{"en":"Premium","ko":"Premium"},{"en":"Transaction optimized","ko":"Transaction optimized"}],"answer":"Premium"},{"id":"redundancy","labelEn":"Redundancy:","labelKo":"Redundancy:","options":[{"en":"Geo-redundant storage (GRS)","ko":"Geo-redundant storage (GRS)"},{"en":"Zone-redundant storage (ZRS)","ko":"Zone-redundant storage (ZRS)"},{"en":"Locally-redundant storage (LRS)","ko":"Locally-redundant storage (LRS)"}],"answer":"Zone-redundant storage (ZRS)"}],"template":""},{"n":148,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design infrastructure solutions","topicKo":"인프라 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You need to design a solution that executes custom C# code in response to an event routed through Azure Event Grid. The solution must meet the following requirements:\n\n- The executed code must be able to access the private IP address of a Microsoft SQL Server instance running on an Azure virtual machine.\n- Costs must be minimized.\n\nWhat should you include in the solution?","stemKo":"You need to design a solution that executes custom C# code in response to an event routed through Azure Event Grid. The solution must meet the following requirements:\n\n- The executed code must be able to access the private IP address of a Microsoft SQL Server instance running on an Azure virtual machine.\n- Costs must be minimized.\n\nWhat should you include in the solution?","explanationEn":"Azure Functions can execute custom C# code in response to Azure Event Grid events. A function app hosted on the Premium plan supports virtual network integration, allowing outbound communication with resources in the virtual network, including a SQL Server running on an Azure VM by its private IP address. This satisfies the private-connectivity requirement without the higher cost of a dedicated Logic Apps integration service environment.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure Functions Premium plan](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-functions/functions-premium-plan) · [Azure Event Grid trigger for Azure Functions](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-functions/functions-bindings-event-grid-trigger)","explanationKo":"Azure Functions can execute custom C# code in response to Azure Event Grid events. A function app hosted on the Premium plan supports virtual network integration, allowing outbound communication with resources in the virtual network, including a SQL Server running on an Azure VM by its private IP address. This satisfies the private-connectivity requirement without the higher cost of a dedicated Logic Apps integration service environment.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure Functions Premium plan](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-functions/functions-premium-plan) · [Azure Event Grid trigger for Azure Functions](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-functions/functions-bindings-event-grid-trigger)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Azure Logic Apps in the Consumption plan","ko":"Azure Logic Apps in the Consumption plan"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure Functions in the Premium plan","ko":"Azure Functions in the Premium plan"},{"label":"C","en":"Azure Functions in the Consumption plan","ko":"Azure Functions in the Consumption plan"},{"label":"D","en":"Azure Logic Apps in the integrated service environment","ko":"Azure Logic Apps in the integrated service environment"}],"answers":["B"]},{"n":149,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design infrastructure solutions","topicKo":"인프라 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You are developing a sales application that will include several Azure cloud services and handle different components of a transaction. Different cloud services will process customer orders, billing, payment, inventory, and shipping.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that enables the cloud services to asynchronously exchange transaction information by using XML messages.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","stemKo":"You are developing a sales application that will include several Azure cloud services and handle different components of a transaction. Different cloud services will process customer orders, billing, payment, inventory, and shipping.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that enables the cloud services to asynchronously exchange transaction information by using XML messages.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","explanationEn":"Azure Service Bus provides reliable asynchronous messaging between decoupled applications and services through queues and topics. Its messages carry application-defined payloads, so XML transaction data can be sent between the order, billing, payment, inventory, and shipping services.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure Service Bus asynchronous messaging](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/service-bus-messaging/service-bus-async-messaging) · [Azure Service Bus messages, payloads, and serialization](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/service-bus-messaging/service-bus-messages-payloads)","explanationKo":"Azure Service Bus provides reliable asynchronous messaging between decoupled applications and services through queues and topics. Its messages carry application-defined payloads, so XML transaction data can be sent between the order, billing, payment, inventory, and shipping services.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure Service Bus asynchronous messaging](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/service-bus-messaging/service-bus-async-messaging) · [Azure Service Bus messages, payloads, and serialization](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/service-bus-messaging/service-bus-messages-payloads)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Azure Service Fabric","ko":"Azure Service Fabric"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure Notification Hubs","ko":"Azure Notification Hubs"},{"label":"C","en":"Azure Service Bus","ko":"Azure Service Bus"},{"label":"D","en":"Azure Traffic Manager","ko":"Azure Traffic Manager"}],"answers":["C"]},{"n":150,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design infrastructure solutions","topicKo":"인프라 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You plan to deploy an Azure App Service web app with multiple instances in multiple Azure regions.\n\nYou need to recommend a load-balancing service for the planned deployment. The solution must meet these requirements:\n\n- Maintain access to the app if a regional outage occurs.\n- Support Azure Web Application Firewall (WAF).\n- Support cookie-based affinity.\n- Support URL routing.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","stemKo":"You plan to deploy an Azure App Service web app with multiple instances in multiple Azure regions.\n\nYou need to recommend a load-balancing service for the planned deployment. The solution must meet these requirements:\n\n- Maintain access to the app if a regional outage occurs.\n- Support Azure Web Application Firewall (WAF).\n- Support cookie-based affinity.\n- Support URL routing.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","explanationEn":"Azure Front Door provides global HTTP(S) traffic distribution across multiple healthy origins, including automated failover when an origin becomes unavailable. It supports cookie-based session affinity and URL route matching; Azure Front Door Premium provides Web Application Firewall support.\n\n**Learn more:** [Traffic routing methods to origin - Azure Front Door](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/frontdoor/routing-methods) · [Routing architecture - Azure Front Door](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/frontdoor/front-door-routing-architecture)","explanationKo":"Azure Front Door provides global HTTP(S) traffic distribution across multiple healthy origins, including automated failover when an origin becomes unavailable. It supports cookie-based session affinity and URL route matching; Azure Front Door Premium provides Web Application Firewall support.\n\n**Learn more:** [Traffic routing methods to origin - Azure Front Door](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/frontdoor/routing-methods) · [Routing architecture - Azure Front Door](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/frontdoor/front-door-routing-architecture)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Azure Front Door","ko":"Azure Front Door"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure Traffic Manager","ko":"Azure Traffic Manager"},{"label":"C","en":"Azure Application Gateway","ko":"Azure Application Gateway"},{"label":"D","en":"Azure Load Balancer","ko":"Azure Load Balancer"}],"answers":["A"]},{"n":151,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design business continuity solutions","topicKo":"업무 연속성 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You need to design a highly available Azure SQL database that fulfills these requirements:\n\n- Failover between database replicas must occur with no data loss.\n- The database must stay available if an availability zone fails.\n- Costs must be kept to a minimum.\n\nWhich deployment option should you use?","stemKo":"You need to design a highly available Azure SQL database that fulfills these requirements:\n\n- Failover between database replicas must occur with no data loss.\n- The database must stay available if an availability zone fails.\n- Costs must be kept to a minimum.\n\nWhich deployment option should you use?","explanationEn":"Azure SQL Database Business Critical supports zone-redundant deployment, with replicas placed in separate availability zones and synchronous replication that preserves committed data during failover. Its multiple replicas are included, so distributing them across zones has no additional zone-redundancy charge. Azure SQL Database Standard does not support zone redundancy; Hyperscale requires at least one HA secondary replica for zone redundancy.\n\n**Learn more:** [Reliability in Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/reliability/reliability-sql-database) · [Availability Through Local and Zone Redundancy - Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/database/high-availability-sla-local-zone-redundancy?view=azuresql)","explanationKo":"Azure SQL Database Business Critical supports zone-redundant deployment, with replicas placed in separate availability zones and synchronous replication that preserves committed data during failover. Its multiple replicas are included, so distributing them across zones has no additional zone-redundancy charge. Azure SQL Database Standard does not support zone redundancy; Hyperscale requires at least one HA secondary replica for zone redundancy.\n\n**Learn more:** [Reliability in Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/reliability/reliability-sql-database) · [Availability Through Local and Zone Redundancy - Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/database/high-availability-sla-local-zone-redundancy?view=azuresql)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Azure SQL Database Business Critical","ko":"Azure SQL Database Business Critical"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure SQL Database Hyperscale","ko":"Azure SQL Database Hyperscale"},{"label":"C","en":"Azure SQL Managed Instance Business Critical","ko":"Azure SQL Managed Instance Business Critical"},{"label":"D","en":"Azure SQL Database Standard","ko":"Azure SQL Database Standard"}],"answers":["A"]},{"n":152,"id":null,"type":"dropdown","topic":"Design business continuity solutions","topicKo":"업무 연속성 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You have two on-premises Microsoft SQL Server 2017 instances that host an Always On availability group named AG1. AG1 contains one database, DB1.\n\nYour Azure subscription includes a virtual machine named VM1. VM1 runs Linux and hosts a SQL Server 2019 instance.\n\nYou need to migrate DB1 to VM1 while minimizing downtime on DB1. What should you do?","stemKo":"You have two on-premises Microsoft SQL Server 2017 instances that host an Always On availability group named AG1. AG1 contains one database, DB1.\n\nYour Azure subscription includes a virtual machine named VM1. VM1 runs Linux and hosts a SQL Server 2019 instance.\n\nYou need to migrate DB1 to VM1 while minimizing downtime on DB1. What should you do?","explanationEn":"A distributed availability group links separate availability groups and supports low-downtime migration from an existing availability group to SQL Server on an Azure VM. Creating a target availability group on VM1 enables it to participate as the target AG; the distributed AG then synchronizes the database until cutover. This approach supports migration across differing SQL Server versions and underlying platforms, including Windows-to-Linux migration scenarios.\n\n**Learn more:** [Use distributed AG to migrate availability group](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/data-migration/sql-server/virtual-machines/distributed-availability-group-migrate-availability-group) · [Business Continuity and Database Recovery - SQL Server on Linux](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/sql/linux/sql-server-linux-business-continuity-dr?view=sql-server-ver17)","explanationKo":"A distributed availability group links separate availability groups and supports low-downtime migration from an existing availability group to SQL Server on an Azure VM. Creating a target availability group on VM1 enables it to participate as the target AG; the distributed AG then synchronizes the database until cutover. This approach supports migration across differing SQL Server versions and underlying platforms, including Windows-to-Linux migration scenarios.\n\n**Learn more:** [Use distributed AG to migrate availability group](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/data-migration/sql-server/virtual-machines/distributed-availability-group-migrate-availability-group) · [Business Continuity and Database Recovery - SQL Server on Linux](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/sql/linux/sql-server-linux-business-continuity-dr?view=sql-server-ver17)","learnMore":[],"blanks":[{"id":"prepare","labelEn":"Prepare for the migration by:","labelKo":"Prepare for the migration by:","options":[{"en":"Adding a secondary replica to AG1","ko":"Adding a secondary replica to AG1"},{"en":"Creating an Always On availability group on VM1","ko":"Creating an Always On availability group on VM1"},{"en":"Upgrading the on-premises SQL Server instances","ko":"Upgrading the on-premises SQL Server instances"}],"answer":"Creating an Always On availability group on VM1"},{"id":"migrate","labelEn":"Perform the migration by using:","labelKo":"Perform the migration by using:","options":[{"en":"A distributed availability group","ko":"A distributed availability group"},{"en":"Azure Migrate","ko":"Azure Migrate"},{"en":"Log shipping","ko":"Log shipping"}],"answer":"A distributed availability group"}],"template":""},{"n":153,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design infrastructure solutions","topicKo":"인프라 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You are developing a sales application that will include several Azure cloud services and handle different components of a transaction. Different cloud services will process customer orders, billing, payment, inventory, and shipping.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that enables the cloud services to communicate transaction information asynchronously by using XML messages.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","stemKo":"You are developing a sales application that will include several Azure cloud services and handle different components of a transaction. Different cloud services will process customer orders, billing, payment, inventory, and shipping.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that enables the cloud services to communicate transaction information asynchronously by using XML messages.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","explanationEn":"Azure Queue Storage provides reliable, asynchronous message queues for communication between loosely coupled components of distributed applications. Services can enqueue transaction messages for other services to retrieve and process later; queue messages are UTF-8 text compatible with XML requests.\n\n**Learn more:** [Tutorial: Work with Azure Queue Storage queues in .NET](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/queues/storage-tutorial-queues) · [Reliability in Azure Queue Storage](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/reliability/reliability-storage-queue)","explanationKo":"Azure Queue Storage provides reliable, asynchronous message queues for communication between loosely coupled components of distributed applications. Services can enqueue transaction messages for other services to retrieve and process later; queue messages are UTF-8 text compatible with XML requests.\n\n**Learn more:** [Tutorial: Work with Azure Queue Storage queues in .NET](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/queues/storage-tutorial-queues) · [Reliability in Azure Queue Storage](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/reliability/reliability-storage-queue)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Azure Notification Hubs","ko":"Azure Notification Hubs"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure Application Gateway","ko":"Azure Application Gateway"},{"label":"C","en":"Azure Queue Storage","ko":"Azure Queue Storage"},{"label":"D","en":"Azure Traffic Manager","ko":"Azure Traffic Manager"}],"answers":["C"]},{"n":154,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design business continuity solutions","topicKo":"업무 연속성 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You must design a highly available Azure SQL database that meets these requirements:\n\n- Failover between database replicas must take place with no data loss.\n- The database must stay available if an availability zone experiences an outage.\n- Costs must be kept to a minimum.\n\nWhich deployment option should you use?","stemKo":"You must design a highly available Azure SQL database that meets these requirements:\n\n- Failover between database replicas must take place with no data loss.\n- The database must stay available if an availability zone experiences an outage.\n- Costs must be kept to a minimum.\n\nWhich deployment option should you use?","explanationEn":"A zone-redundant Azure SQL Database Premium deployment places synchronous replicas in different availability zones. A transaction is committed only after it is persisted on sufficient secondary replicas, so a fully synchronized replica is available for failover with no loss of committed data. Premium also supports zone redundancy without an additional zone-redundancy charge because it uses its existing replicas.\n\n**Learn more:** [Reliability in Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/reliability/reliability-sql-database)","explanationKo":"A zone-redundant Azure SQL Database Premium deployment places synchronous replicas in different availability zones. A transaction is committed only after it is persisted on sufficient secondary replicas, so a fully synchronized replica is available for failover with no loss of committed data. Premium also supports zone redundancy without an additional zone-redundancy charge because it uses its existing replicas.\n\n**Learn more:** [Reliability in Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/reliability/reliability-sql-database)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Azure SQL Database Standard","ko":"Azure SQL Database Standard"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure SQL Managed Instance General Purpose","ko":"Azure SQL Managed Instance General Purpose"},{"label":"C","en":"Azure SQL Database Serverless","ko":"Azure SQL Database Serverless"},{"label":"D","en":"Azure SQL Database Premium","ko":"Azure SQL Database Premium"}],"answers":["D"]},{"n":155,"id":null,"type":"drag_drop","topic":"Design data storage solutions","topicKo":"데이터 저장소 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You need to recommend a solution that fulfills the file-storage requirements for App2.\n\nWhat should be deployed to the Azure subscription and to the on-premises network? Each service can be used once, more than once, or not at all.","stemKo":"You need to recommend a solution that fulfills the file-storage requirements for App2.\n\nWhat should be deployed to the Azure subscription and to the on-premises network? Each service can be used once, more than once, or not at all.","explanationEn":"Azure Files provides the cloud-hosted file share in the Azure subscription. Azure File Sync uses a Windows Server endpoint on premises to synchronize and locally cache that Azure file share.\n\n**Learn more:** [Introduction to Azure File Sync](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/file-sync/file-sync-introduction) · [Extend Windows file servers with Azure File Sync](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/file-sync/file-sync-extend-servers)","explanationKo":"Azure Files provides the cloud-hosted file share in the Azure subscription. Azure File Sync uses a Windows Server endpoint on premises to synchronize and locally cache that Azure file share.\n\n**Learn more:** [Introduction to Azure File Sync](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/file-sync/file-sync-introduction) · [Extend Windows file servers with Azure File Sync](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/file-sync/file-sync-extend-servers)","learnMore":[],"items":[{"en":"Azure Blob Storage","ko":"Azure Blob Storage"},{"en":"Azure Data Box","ko":"Azure Data Box"},{"en":"Azure Data Box Gateway","ko":"Azure Data Box Gateway"},{"en":"Azure Data Lake Storage","ko":"Azure Data Lake Storage"},{"en":"Azure File Sync","ko":"Azure File Sync"},{"en":"Azure Files","ko":"Azure Files"}],"slots":[{"id":"azure_subscription","labelEn":"Azure subscription:","labelKo":"Azure subscription:","answer":"Azure Files"},{"id":"on_premises_network","labelEn":"On-premises network:","labelKo":"On-premises network:","answer":"Azure File Sync"}],"reuse":true},{"n":156,"id":null,"type":"dropdown","topic":"Design infrastructure solutions","topicKo":"인프라 설계","koMissing":true,"images":["assets/1783707871059-kga3vpj0.png"],"stemEn":"You have the Azure resources shown in the following table.\n\n[[IMG1]]\n\nYou need to design a solution that provides on-premises network connectivity to SQLDB1 through PE1.\n\nHow should name resolution be configured?","stemKo":"You have the Azure resources shown in the following table.\n\n[[IMG1]]\n\nYou need to design a solution that provides on-premises network connectivity to SQLDB1 through PE1.\n\nHow should name resolution be configured?","explanationEn":"Azure-provided DNS resolves the private A record in the private contoso.com zone when the query originates in VNET1. VM1 can act as the DNS forwarder inside VNET1 and forward contoso.com to 168.63.129.16. On-premises DNS must forward that zone to VM1 because Azure-provided DNS is not directly reachable from on premises; this returns PE1’s private endpoint address for SQLDB1.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure Private Endpoint DNS Integration Scenarios](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/private-link/private-endpoint-dns-integration) · [Troubleshoot private endpoint DNS resolution failure in Azure Private Link](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/troubleshoot/azure/private-link/troubleshoot-private-endpoint-dns-resolution)","explanationKo":"Azure-provided DNS resolves the private A record in the private contoso.com zone when the query originates in VNET1. VM1 can act as the DNS forwarder inside VNET1 and forward contoso.com to 168.63.129.16. On-premises DNS must forward that zone to VM1 because Azure-provided DNS is not directly reachable from on premises; this returns PE1’s private endpoint address for SQLDB1.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure Private Endpoint DNS Integration Scenarios](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/private-link/private-endpoint-dns-integration) · [Troubleshoot private endpoint DNS resolution failure in Azure Private Link](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/troubleshoot/azure/private-link/troubleshoot-private-endpoint-dns-resolution)","learnMore":[],"blanks":[{"id":"azure_configuration","labelEn":"Azure configuration","labelKo":"Azure configuration","options":[{"en":"Configure VM1 to forward contoso.com to the public DNS zone","ko":"Configure VM1 to forward contoso.com to the public DNS zone"},{"en":"Configure VM1 to forward contoso.com to the Azure-provided DNS at 168.63.129.16","ko":"Configure VM1 to forward contoso.com to the Azure-provided DNS at 168.63.129.16"},{"en":"In VNet1, configure a custom DNS server set to the Azure-provided DNS at 168.63.129.16","ko":"In VNet1, configure a custom DNS server set to the Azure-provided DNS at 168.63.129.16"}],"answer":"Configure VM1 to forward contoso.com to the Azure-provided DNS at 168.63.129.16"},{"id":"on_premises_dns_configuration","labelEn":"On-premises DNS configuration","labelKo":"On-premises DNS configuration","options":[{"en":"Forward contoso.com to VM1","ko":"Forward contoso.com to VM1"},{"en":"Forward contoso.com to the public DNS zone","ko":"Forward contoso.com to the public DNS zone"},{"en":"Forward contoso.com to the Azure-provisioned DNS at 168.63.129.16","ko":"Forward contoso.com to the Azure-provisioned DNS at 168.63.129.16"}],"answer":"Forward contoso.com to VM1"}],"template":""},{"n":157,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design infrastructure solutions","topicKo":"인프라 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You have an Azure subscription containing two applications named App1 and App2. App1 is a sales-processing application. When an App1 transaction requires shipping, a message is added to an Azure Storage account queue, and App2 then listens to the queue for relevant transactions.\n\nIn the future, additional applications will be added to process some shipping requests based on the specific transaction details.\n\nYou need to recommend a replacement for the storage account queue so that each additional application can read the relevant transactions.\n\nWhat should you recommend?","stemKo":"You have an Azure subscription containing two applications named App1 and App2. App1 is a sales-processing application. When an App1 transaction requires shipping, a message is added to an Azure Storage account queue, and App2 then listens to the queue for relevant transactions.\n\nIn the future, additional applications will be added to process some shipping requests based on the specific transaction details.\n\nYou need to recommend a replacement for the storage account queue so that each additional application can read the relevant transactions.\n\nWhat should you recommend?","explanationEn":"Azure Service Bus topics implement publish/subscribe messaging. Each application can have a separate subscription that receives a copy of published messages, and subscription filters can route only the transactions relevant to that application. Service Bus queues instead deliver each message to a single consumer.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure Service Bus queues, topics, and subscriptions](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/service-bus-messaging/service-bus-queues-topics-subscriptions)","explanationKo":"Azure Service Bus topics implement publish/subscribe messaging. Each application can have a separate subscription that receives a copy of published messages, and subscription filters can route only the transactions relevant to that application. Service Bus queues instead deliver each message to a single consumer.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure Service Bus queues, topics, and subscriptions](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/service-bus-messaging/service-bus-queues-topics-subscriptions)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"one Azure Data Factory pipeline","ko":"one Azure Data Factory pipeline"},{"label":"B","en":"multiple storage account queues","ko":"multiple storage account queues"},{"label":"C","en":"one Azure Service Bus queue","ko":"one Azure Service Bus queue"},{"label":"D","en":"one Azure Service Bus topic","ko":"one Azure Service Bus topic"}],"answers":["D"]},{"n":158,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design infrastructure solutions","topicKo":"인프라 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You are building a sales application that will include several Azure cloud services and manage different parts of a transaction. Separate cloud services will process customer orders, billing, payment, inventory, and shipping.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that lets the cloud services asynchronously exchange transaction information by using XML messages.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","stemKo":"You are building a sales application that will include several Azure cloud services and manage different parts of a transaction. Separate cloud services will process customer orders, billing, payment, inventory, and shipping.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that lets the cloud services asynchronously exchange transaction information by using XML messages.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","explanationEn":"Azure Service Bus provides durable queues and publish/subscribe topics that decouple cloud services for asynchronous messaging. Its message payloads can contain structured data encoded as XML, making it suitable for exchanging transaction data among order, billing, payment, inventory, and shipping components.\n\n**Learn more:** [What is Azure Service Bus?](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/service-bus-messaging/service-bus-messaging-overview) · [Asynchronous messaging patterns and high availability](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/service-bus-messaging/service-bus-async-messaging)","explanationKo":"Azure Service Bus provides durable queues and publish/subscribe topics that decouple cloud services for asynchronous messaging. Its message payloads can contain structured data encoded as XML, making it suitable for exchanging transaction data among order, billing, payment, inventory, and shipping components.\n\n**Learn more:** [What is Azure Service Bus?](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/service-bus-messaging/service-bus-messaging-overview) · [Asynchronous messaging patterns and high availability](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/service-bus-messaging/service-bus-async-messaging)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Azure Notification Hubs","ko":"Azure Notification Hubs"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure Service Bus","ko":"Azure Service Bus"},{"label":"C","en":"Azure Blob Storage","ko":"Azure Blob Storage"},{"label":"D","en":"Azure Service Fabric","ko":"Azure Service Fabric"}],"answers":["B"]},{"n":159,"id":null,"type":"dropdown","topic":"Design business continuity solutions","topicKo":"업무 연속성 설계","koMissing":true,"images":["assets/1783709624644-7j67b19l.png"],"stemEn":"You have the Azure subscriptions shown in the following table.\n\n[[IMG1]]\n\nContoso.onmicrosft.com contains a user named User1.\n\nYou need to deploy a solution to protect against ransomware attacks. The solution must meet these requirements:\n\n- Ensure that all resources in Sub1 are backed up by using Azure Backup.\n- Require User1 to first be assigned a role for Sub2 before the user can make major changes to the backup configuration.\n\nWhat should you create in each subscription?","stemKo":"You have the Azure subscriptions shown in the following table.\n\n[[IMG1]]\n\nContoso.onmicrosft.com contains a user named User1.\n\nYou need to deploy a solution to protect against ransomware attacks. The solution must meet these requirements:\n\n- Ensure that all resources in Sub1 are backed up by using Azure Backup.\n- Require User1 to first be assigned a role for Sub2 before the user can make major changes to the backup configuration.\n\nWhat should you create in each subscription?","explanationEn":"A Recovery Services vault provides Azure Backup backup-policy and recovery-point management for supported Azure workloads. A Resource Guard enables Azure Backup multi-user authorization for critical backup operations. Placing it in the separate Sub2 tenant means User1 needs an applicable role assignment there before making protected backup-configuration changes.\n\n**Learn more:** [Multiuser Authorization Using Resource Guard - Azure Backup](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/backup/multi-user-authorization-concept) · [Create and configure a Recovery Services vault](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/backup/backup-create-recovery-services-vault)","explanationKo":"A Recovery Services vault provides Azure Backup backup-policy and recovery-point management for supported Azure workloads. A Resource Guard enables Azure Backup multi-user authorization for critical backup operations. Placing it in the separate Sub2 tenant means User1 needs an applicable role assignment there before making protected backup-configuration changes.\n\n**Learn more:** [Multiuser Authorization Using Resource Guard - Azure Backup](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/backup/multi-user-authorization-concept) · [Create and configure a Recovery Services vault](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/backup/backup-create-recovery-services-vault)","learnMore":[],"blanks":[{"id":"sub1","labelEn":"Sub1:","labelKo":"Sub1:","options":[{"en":"A Recovery Services vault","ko":"A Recovery Services vault"},{"en":"A Resource Guard","ko":"A Resource Guard"},{"en":"An Azure Site Recovery job","ko":"An Azure Site Recovery job"},{"en":"Microsoft Azure Backup Server (MABS)","ko":"Microsoft Azure Backup Server (MABS)"},{"en":"The Microsoft Azure Recovery Services (MARS) agent","ko":"The Microsoft Azure Recovery Services (MARS) agent"}],"answer":"A Recovery Services vault"},{"id":"sub2","labelEn":"Sub2:","labelKo":"Sub2:","options":[{"en":"A Recovery Services vault","ko":"A Recovery Services vault"},{"en":"A Resource Guard","ko":"A Resource Guard"},{"en":"An Azure Site Recovery job","ko":"An Azure Site Recovery job"},{"en":"Microsoft Azure Backup Server (MABS)","ko":"Microsoft Azure Backup Server (MABS)"},{"en":"The Microsoft Azure Recovery Services (MARS) agent","ko":"The Microsoft Azure Recovery Services (MARS) agent"}],"answer":"A Resource Guard"}],"template":""},{"n":160,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design business continuity solutions","topicKo":"업무 연속성 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You must design a highly available Azure SQL database that satisfies these requirements:\n\n- Failover between database replicas must take place with no data loss.\n- The database must stay available if a zone outage occurs.\n- Costs must be kept to a minimum.\n\nWhich deployment option should you use?","stemKo":"You must design a highly available Azure SQL database that satisfies these requirements:\n\n- Failover between database replicas must take place with no data loss.\n- The database must stay available if a zone outage occurs.\n- Costs must be kept to a minimum.\n\nWhich deployment option should you use?","explanationEn":"A zone-redundant Azure SQL Database Premium deployment places synchronized replicas in separate availability zones. This provides automatic failover during a zone outage with no expected loss of committed data. Basic does not support zone redundancy, while the Business Critical Managed Instance and Hyperscale options provide higher-end capabilities not required for these constraints.\n\n**Learn more:** [Reliability in Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/reliability/reliability-sql-database)","explanationKo":"A zone-redundant Azure SQL Database Premium deployment places synchronized replicas in separate availability zones. This provides automatic failover during a zone outage with no expected loss of committed data. Basic does not support zone redundancy, while the Business Critical Managed Instance and Hyperscale options provide higher-end capabilities not required for these constraints.\n\n**Learn more:** [Reliability in Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/reliability/reliability-sql-database)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Azure SQL Managed Instance Business Critical","ko":"Azure SQL Managed Instance Business Critical"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure SQL Database Premium","ko":"Azure SQL Database Premium"},{"label":"C","en":"Azure SQL Database Basic","ko":"Azure SQL Database Basic"},{"label":"D","en":"Azure SQL Database Hyperscale","ko":"Azure SQL Database Hyperscale"}],"answers":["B"]},{"n":161,"id":null,"type":"dropdown","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":["assets/1783710339237-6vl2qijy.png"],"stemEn":"HOTSPOT -\n\nYou have an Azure subscription that contains the resources shown in the following table.\n\n[[IMG1]]\n\nVNet1, VNet2, and VNet3 each have multiple virtual machines connected. The virtual machines use the Azure DNS service for name resolution.\n\nYou need to recommend an Azure Monitor log-routing solution that meets the following requirements:\n\n- Ensures that logs collected from the virtual machines and sent to Workspace1 are routed over the Microsoft backbone network\n- Minimizes administrative effort\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","stemKo":"HOTSPOT -\n\nYou have an Azure subscription that contains the resources shown in the following table.\n\n[[IMG1]]\n\nVNet1, VNet2, and VNet3 each have multiple virtual machines connected. The virtual machines use the Azure DNS service for name resolution.\n\nYou need to recommend an Azure Monitor log-routing solution that meets the following requirements:\n\n- Ensures that logs collected from the virtual machines and sent to Workspace1 are routed over the Microsoft backbone network\n- Minimizes administrative effort\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","explanationEn":"Microsoft explicitly recommends using a SINGLE Azure Monitor Private Link Scope for all networks that share DNS, because creating multiple AMPLS objects causes the Azure Monitor privatelink DNS zones to override each other and break resolution; one AMPLS also minimizes administrative effort, so the answer is 1 AMPLS. A private endpoint provides connectivity from the VNet where it lives and can be reached by peered VNets. VNet1 and VNet2 are peered and share the contoso.com DNS, so a single private endpoint placed in that pair serves both, while VNet3 is isolated from VNet1/VNet2 and therefore needs its own private endpoint - a minimum of 2 private endpoints. All of them connect to the one shared AMPLS.\n\n**Learn more:** [Design Azure Monitor Private Link configuration](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-monitor/fundamentals/private-link-design) · [Use Azure Private Link to connect networks to Azure Monitor](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-monitor/fundamentals/private-link-security)","explanationKo":"Microsoft explicitly recommends using a SINGLE Azure Monitor Private Link Scope for all networks that share DNS, because creating multiple AMPLS objects causes the Azure Monitor privatelink DNS zones to override each other and break resolution; one AMPLS also minimizes administrative effort, so the answer is 1 AMPLS. A private endpoint provides connectivity from the VNet where it lives and can be reached by peered VNets. VNet1 and VNet2 are peered and share the contoso.com DNS, so a single private endpoint placed in that pair serves both, while VNet3 is isolated from VNet1/VNet2 and therefore needs its own private endpoint - a minimum of 2 private endpoints. All of them connect to the one shared AMPLS.\n\n**Learn more:** [Design Azure Monitor Private Link configuration](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-monitor/fundamentals/private-link-design) · [Use Azure Private Link to connect networks to Azure Monitor](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-monitor/fundamentals/private-link-security)","learnMore":[],"blanks":[{"id":"ampls","labelEn":"Minimum number of Azure Monitor Private Link Scope (AMPLS) objects:","labelKo":"Minimum number of Azure Monitor Private Link Scope (AMPLS) objects:","options":[{"en":"1","ko":"1"},{"en":"2","ko":"2"},{"en":"3","ko":"3"}],"answer":"1"},{"id":"private_endpoints","labelEn":"Minimum number of private endpoints:","labelKo":"Minimum number of private endpoints:","options":[{"en":"1","ko":"1"},{"en":"2","ko":"2"},{"en":"3","ko":"3"}],"answer":"2"}],"template":""},{"n":162,"id":null,"type":"drag_drop","topic":"Design infrastructure solutions","topicKo":"인프라 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You have an on-premises network that uses an IP address space of 172.16.0.0/16.\n\nYou plan to deploy 30 virtual machines to a new Azure subscription.\n\nYou identify the following technical requirements:\n\n- All Azure virtual machines must be placed on the same subnet named Subnet1.\n- All Azure virtual machines must be able to communicate with all on-premises servers.\n- The servers must be able to communicate between the on-premises network and Azure by using a site-to-site VPN.\n\nYou need to recommend a subnet design that meets the technical requirements.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation? Each network address may be used once, more than once, or not at all.","stemKo":"You have an on-premises network that uses an IP address space of 172.16.0.0/16.\n\nYou plan to deploy 30 virtual machines to a new Azure subscription.\n\nYou identify the following technical requirements:\n\n- All Azure virtual machines must be placed on the same subnet named Subnet1.\n- All Azure virtual machines must be able to communicate with all on-premises servers.\n- The servers must be able to communicate between the on-premises network and Azure by using a site-to-site VPN.\n\nYou need to recommend a subnet design that meets the technical requirements.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation? Each network address may be used once, more than once, or not at all.","explanationEn":"A /27 network supplies only 32 addresses, of which Azure reserves five, leaving 27 usable-too few for the 30 planned virtual machines-so Subnet1 must use the larger 192.168.0.0/24 range. The remaining 192.168.1.0/27 range is sized to Azure's recommended minimum for a gateway subnet and is used for the VPN gateway. Both ranges avoid overlapping the on-premises 172.16.0.0/16 address space, which site-to-site VPN connectivity requires.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure VPN Gateway FAQ](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/vpn-gateway/vpn-gateway-vpn-faq#what-are-the-address-range-requirements-for-vpns)","explanationKo":"A /27 network supplies only 32 addresses, of which Azure reserves five, leaving 27 usable-too few for the 30 planned virtual machines-so Subnet1 must use the larger 192.168.0.0/24 range. The remaining 192.168.1.0/27 range is sized to Azure's recommended minimum for a gateway subnet and is used for the VPN gateway. Both ranges avoid overlapping the on-premises 172.16.0.0/16 address space, which site-to-site VPN connectivity requires.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure VPN Gateway FAQ](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/vpn-gateway/vpn-gateway-vpn-faq#what-are-the-address-range-requirements-for-vpns)","learnMore":[],"items":[{"en":"172.16.0.0/16","ko":"172.16.0.0/16"},{"en":"172.16.1.0/27","ko":"172.16.1.0/27"},{"en":"192.168.0.0/24","ko":"192.168.0.0/24"},{"en":"192.168.1.0/27","ko":"192.168.1.0/27"}],"slots":[{"id":"subnet1","labelEn":"Subnet1:","labelKo":"Subnet1:","answer":"192.168.0.0/24"},{"id":"gateway_subnet","labelEn":"Gateway subnet:","labelKo":"Gateway subnet:","answer":"192.168.1.0/27"}],"reuse":true},{"n":163,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design data storage solutions","topicKo":"데이터 저장소 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You have a multi-tier application named App1 and an Azure SQL database named SQL1. App1's backend service writes data to SQL1. Users use the App1 client to read data from SQL1.\n\nDuring times of high utilization, users experience delays when retrieving the data.\n\nYou need to minimize the time required for data requests.\n\nWhat should you include in the solution?","stemKo":"You have a multi-tier application named App1 and an Azure SQL database named SQL1. App1's backend service writes data to SQL1. Users use the App1 client to read data from SQL1.\n\nDuring times of high utilization, users experience delays when retrieving the data.\n\nYou need to minimize the time required for data requests.\n\nWhat should you include in the solution?","explanationEn":"Azure Cache for Redis provides a distributed in-memory data cache for frequently accessed application data. Serving read-heavy requests from the cache reduces Azure SQL Database CPU and read I/O load and provides lower-latency retrieval during periods of high utilization.\n\n**Learn more:** [What is Azure Cache for Redis?](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-cache-for-redis/cache-overview) · [Performance Tuning Guidance for Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/database/performance-guidance?view=azuresql)","explanationKo":"Azure Cache for Redis provides a distributed in-memory data cache for frequently accessed application data. Serving read-heavy requests from the cache reduces Azure SQL Database CPU and read I/O load and provides lower-latency retrieval during periods of high utilization.\n\n**Learn more:** [What is Azure Cache for Redis?](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-cache-for-redis/cache-overview) · [Performance Tuning Guidance for Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/database/performance-guidance?view=azuresql)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Azure Cache for Redis","ko":"Azure Cache for Redis"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure Content Delivery Network (CDN)","ko":"Azure Content Delivery Network (CDN)"},{"label":"C","en":"Azure Data Factory","ko":"Azure Data Factory"},{"label":"D","en":"Azure Synapse Analytics","ko":"Azure Synapse Analytics"}],"answers":["A"]},{"n":164,"id":null,"type":"dropdown","topic":"Design data storage solutions","topicKo":"데이터 저장소 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You need to recommend an Azure Storage account configuration for two applications named Application1 and Application2. The configuration must meet these requirements:\n\n- Storage for Application1 must provide the highest possible transaction rates and the lowest possible latency.\n- Storage for Application2 must provide the lowest possible storage costs per GB.\n- Storage for both applications must remain available if a datacenter fails.\n- Storage for both applications must be optimized for uploads and downloads.\n\nWhat should you recommend?","stemKo":"You need to recommend an Azure Storage account configuration for two applications named Application1 and Application2. The configuration must meet these requirements:\n\n- Storage for Application1 must provide the highest possible transaction rates and the lowest possible latency.\n- Storage for Application2 must provide the lowest possible storage costs per GB.\n- Storage for both applications must remain available if a datacenter fails.\n- Storage for both applications must be optimized for uploads and downloads.\n\nWhat should you recommend?","explanationEn":"Premium block blob storage uses SSDs and is intended for consistently low latency and high transaction rates; ZRS replicates data across availability zones to tolerate a datacenter failure. The Cool tier minimizes per-GB storage cost for infrequently accessed blob data, and GRS replicates to a secondary region without paying for read access to that secondary. Blob storage is designed for upload and download of object data.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure Storage account overview](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/common/storage-account-overview) · [Azure Storage redundancy](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/common/storage-redundancy)","explanationKo":"Premium block blob storage uses SSDs and is intended for consistently low latency and high transaction rates; ZRS replicates data across availability zones to tolerate a datacenter failure. The Cool tier minimizes per-GB storage cost for infrequently accessed blob data, and GRS replicates to a secondary region without paying for read access to that secondary. Blob storage is designed for upload and download of object data.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure Storage account overview](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/common/storage-account-overview) · [Azure Storage redundancy](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/common/storage-redundancy)","learnMore":[],"blanks":[{"id":"application1","labelEn":"Application1:","labelKo":"Application1:","options":[{"en":"BlobStorage with Standard performance, Hot access tier, and Read-access geo-redundant storage (RA-GRS) replication","ko":"BlobStorage with Standard performance, Hot access tier, and Read-access geo-redundant storage (RA-GRS) replication"},{"en":"BlockBlobStorage with Premium performance and Zone-redundant storage (ZRS) replication","ko":"BlockBlobStorage with Premium performance and Zone-redundant storage (ZRS) replication"},{"en":"General purpose v1 with Premium performance and Locally-redundant storage (LRS) replication","ko":"General purpose v1 with Premium performance and Locally-redundant storage (LRS) replication"},{"en":"General purpose v2 with Standard performance, Hot access tier, and Locally-redundant storage (LRS) replication","ko":"General purpose v2 with Standard performance, Hot access tier, and Locally-redundant storage (LRS) replication"}],"answer":"BlockBlobStorage with Premium performance and Zone-redundant storage (ZRS) replication"},{"id":"application2","labelEn":"Application2:","labelKo":"Application2:","options":[{"en":"BlobStorage with Standard performance, Cool access tier, and Geo-redundant storage (GRS) replication","ko":"BlobStorage with Standard performance, Cool access tier, and Geo-redundant storage (GRS) replication"},{"en":"BlockBlobStorage with Premium performance and Zone-redundant storage (ZRS) replication","ko":"BlockBlobStorage with Premium performance and Zone-redundant storage (ZRS) replication"},{"en":"General purpose v1 with Standard performance and Read-access geo-redundant storage (RA-GRS) replication","ko":"General purpose v1 with Standard performance and Read-access geo-redundant storage (RA-GRS) replication"},{"en":"General purpose v2 with Standard performance, Cool access tier, and Read-access geo-redundant storage (RA-GRS) replication","ko":"General purpose v2 with Standard performance, Cool access tier, and Read-access geo-redundant storage (RA-GRS) replication"}],"answer":"BlobStorage with Standard performance, Cool access tier, and Geo-redundant storage (GRS) replication"}],"template":""},{"n":165,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design infrastructure solutions","topicKo":"인프라 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You plan to provision a High Performance Computing (HPC) cluster in Azure that will use a third-party scheduler.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution for provisioning and managing the HPC cluster nodes.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","stemKo":"You plan to provision a High Performance Computing (HPC) cluster in Azure that will use a third-party scheduler.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution for provisioning and managing the HPC cluster nodes.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","explanationEn":"Azure CycleCloud orchestrates and manages HPC environments in Azure, provisions the virtual machines that form cluster nodes, and supports deploying or integrating third-party HPC schedulers.\n\n**Learn more:** [Overview - Azure CycleCloud](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/cyclecloud/overview?view=cyclecloud-8) · [CycleCloud scheduling and autoscaling concepts](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/cyclecloud/concepts/scheduling?view=cyclecloud-8)","explanationKo":"Azure CycleCloud orchestrates and manages HPC environments in Azure, provisions the virtual machines that form cluster nodes, and supports deploying or integrating third-party HPC schedulers.\n\n**Learn more:** [Overview - Azure CycleCloud](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/cyclecloud/overview?view=cyclecloud-8) · [CycleCloud scheduling and autoscaling concepts](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/cyclecloud/concepts/scheduling?view=cyclecloud-8)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Azure Automation","ko":"Azure Automation"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure CycleCloud","ko":"Azure CycleCloud"},{"label":"C","en":"Azure Purview","ko":"Azure Purview"},{"label":"D","en":"Azure Lighthouse","ko":"Azure Lighthouse"}],"answers":["B"]},{"n":166,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":["assets/1783709179904-hvd4270r.png"],"stemEn":"Your company has the divisions shown in the following table.\n\n[[IMG1]]\n\nSub1 contains an Azure App Service web app named App1. App1 uses Azure AD for single-tenant user authentication. Users from contoso.com can authenticate to App1.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that enables users in the fabrikam.com tenant to authenticate to App1.\n\nWhat should you recommend?","stemKo":"Your company has the divisions shown in the following table.\n\n[[IMG1]]\n\nSub1 contains an Azure App Service web app named App1. App1 uses Azure AD for single-tenant user authentication. Users from contoso.com can authenticate to App1.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that enables users in the fabrikam.com tenant to authenticate to App1.\n\nWhat should you recommend?","explanationEn":"A single-tenant Microsoft Entra application accepts users only from its home tenant. To allow users from fabrikam.com to authenticate with their native tenant identities, configure the app registration’s Supported account types for accounts in any organizational directory (multitenant) and use a multitenant sign-in endpoint such as `/common` or `/organizations`.\n\n**Learn more:** [Convert single-tenant app to multitenant on Microsoft Entra ID](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity-platform/howto-convert-app-to-be-multi-tenant)","explanationKo":"A single-tenant Microsoft Entra application accepts users only from its home tenant. To allow users from fabrikam.com to authenticate with their native tenant identities, configure the app registration’s Supported account types for accounts in any organizational directory (multitenant) and use a multitenant sign-in endpoint such as `/common` or `/organizations`.\n\n**Learn more:** [Convert single-tenant app to multitenant on Microsoft Entra ID](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity-platform/howto-convert-app-to-be-multi-tenant)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Configure Azure AD Identity Protection.","ko":"Configure Azure AD Identity Protection."},{"label":"B","en":"Configure assignments for the fabrikam.com users by using Azure AD Privileged Identity Management (PIM).","ko":"Configure assignments for the fabrikam.com users by using Azure AD Privileged Identity Management (PIM)."},{"label":"C","en":"Configure Supported account types in the application registration and update the sign-in endpoint.","ko":"Configure Supported account types in the application registration and update the sign-in endpoint."},{"label":"D","en":"Configure a Conditional Access policy.","ko":"Configure a Conditional Access policy."}],"answers":["C"]},{"n":167,"id":null,"type":"dropdown","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":["assets/1783707483644-8eyrvf8c.png"],"stemEn":"Your company has the divisions shown in the following table.\n\n[[IMG1]]\n\nYou plan to deploy a custom application to every subscription. The application will include:\n\n- A resource group\n- An Azure web app\n- Custom role assignments\n- An Azure Cosmos DB account\n\nYou need to use Azure Blueprints to deploy the application to each subscription.\n\nWhat is the minimum number of objects required to deploy the application?","stemKo":"Your company has the divisions shown in the following table.\n\n[[IMG1]]\n\nYou plan to deploy a custom application to every subscription. The application will include:\n\n- A resource group\n- An Azure web app\n- Custom role assignments\n- An Azure Cosmos DB account\n\nYou need to use Azure Blueprints to deploy the application to each subscription.\n\nWhat is the minimum number of objects required to deploy the application?","explanationEn":"Management groups are scoped within an Azure AD tenant, so two tenants require two management groups. A management-group blueprint definition is available to subscriptions beneath that management group, which requires one definition in each tenant. Blueprint assignments are created on subscriptions, requiring one assignment for each of the four subscriptions.\n\n**Learn more:** [Overview of Azure Blueprints](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/governance/blueprints/overview) · [Azure management groups overview](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/governance/management-groups/overview)","explanationKo":"Management groups are scoped within an Azure AD tenant, so two tenants require two management groups. A management-group blueprint definition is available to subscriptions beneath that management group, which requires one definition in each tenant. Blueprint assignments are created on subscriptions, requiring one assignment for each of the four subscriptions.\n\n**Learn more:** [Overview of Azure Blueprints](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/governance/blueprints/overview) · [Azure management groups overview](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/governance/management-groups/overview)","learnMore":[],"blanks":[{"id":"management_groups","labelEn":"Management groups:","labelKo":"Management groups:","options":[{"en":"1","ko":"1"},{"en":"2","ko":"2"},{"en":"3","ko":"3"},{"en":"4","ko":"4"}],"answer":"2"},{"id":"blueprint_definitions","labelEn":"Blueprint definitions:","labelKo":"Blueprint definitions:","options":[{"en":"1","ko":"1"},{"en":"2","ko":"2"},{"en":"3","ko":"3"},{"en":"4","ko":"4"}],"answer":"2"},{"id":"blueprint_assignments","labelEn":"Blueprint assignments:","labelKo":"Blueprint assignments:","options":[{"en":"1","ko":"1"},{"en":"2","ko":"2"},{"en":"3","ko":"3"},{"en":"4","ko":"4"}],"answer":"4"}],"template":""},{"n":168,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design business continuity solutions","topicKo":"업무 연속성 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You must design a highly available Azure SQL database that satisfies these requirements:\n\n- Failover between database replicas must occur with no data loss.\n- The database must stay available during an availability-zone outage.\n- Costs must be minimized.\n\nWhich deployment option should you choose?","stemKo":"You must design a highly available Azure SQL database that satisfies these requirements:\n\n- Failover between database replicas must occur with no data loss.\n- The database must stay available during an availability-zone outage.\n- Costs must be minimized.\n\nWhich deployment option should you choose?","explanationEn":"Azure SQL Database Premium supports zone redundancy by placing its existing high-availability replicas in separate availability zones. Transactions are committed only after sufficient replicas are synchronized, so a synchronized replica is available for failover without loss of committed data. Premium incurs no additional charge to enable zone redundancy because it uses its existing replicas; Basic does not support zone redundancy, and Hyperscale is unnecessary for these requirements.\n\n**Learn more:** [Reliability in Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/reliability/reliability-sql-database)","explanationKo":"Azure SQL Database Premium supports zone redundancy by placing its existing high-availability replicas in separate availability zones. Transactions are committed only after sufficient replicas are synchronized, so a synchronized replica is available for failover without loss of committed data. Premium incurs no additional charge to enable zone redundancy because it uses its existing replicas; Basic does not support zone redundancy, and Hyperscale is unnecessary for these requirements.\n\n**Learn more:** [Reliability in Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/reliability/reliability-sql-database)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Azure SQL Database Hyperscale","ko":"Azure SQL Database Hyperscale"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure SQL Database Premium","ko":"Azure SQL Database Premium"},{"label":"C","en":"Azure SQL Database Basic","ko":"Azure SQL Database Basic"},{"label":"D","en":"Azure SQL Database Serverless","ko":"Azure SQL Database Serverless"}],"answers":["B"]},{"n":169,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design data storage solutions","topicKo":"데이터 저장소 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You have data files stored in Azure Blob Storage.\n\nYou plan to transform the files and move them to Azure Data Lake Storage.\n\nYou need to use mapping data flow to transform the data.\n\nWhich service should you use?","stemKo":"You have data files stored in Azure Blob Storage.\n\nYou plan to transform the files and move them to Azure Data Lake Storage.\n\nYou need to use mapping data flow to transform the data.\n\nWhich service should you use?","explanationEn":"Azure Data Factory provides mapping data flows for visually designed, code-free data transformations. Its pipelines can use Blob Storage as a source and Azure Data Lake Storage as a destination.\n\n**Learn more:** [Mapping data flows in Azure Data Factory](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/data-factory/concepts-data-flow-overview)","explanationKo":"Azure Data Factory provides mapping data flows for visually designed, code-free data transformations. Its pipelines can use Blob Storage as a source and Azure Data Lake Storage as a destination.\n\n**Learn more:** [Mapping data flows in Azure Data Factory](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/data-factory/concepts-data-flow-overview)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Azure Databricks","ko":"Azure Databricks"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure Storage Sync","ko":"Azure Storage Sync"},{"label":"C","en":"Azure Data Factory","ko":"Azure Data Factory"},{"label":"D","en":"Azure Data Box Gateway","ko":"Azure Data Box Gateway"}],"answers":["C"]},{"n":170,"id":null,"type":"dropdown","topic":"Design infrastructure solutions","topicKo":"인프라 설계","koMissing":true,"images":["assets/1783708071335-15np9yqc.png"],"stemEn":"You have the resources shown in the following table.\n\n[[IMG1]]\n\nYou create a new Azure resource group named RG2.\n\nYou need to move the virtual machines to RG2. What should you use for each virtual machine?","stemKo":"You have the resources shown in the following table.\n\n[[IMG1]]\n\nYou create a new Azure resource group named RG2.\n\nYou need to move the virtual machines to RG2. What should you use for each virtual machine?","explanationEn":"An Azure resource move operation moves an existing Azure VM between resource groups; Azure Resource Mover is the applicable listed relocation service for VM1. Azure Migrate is designed to discover, assess, and migrate on-premises machines into Azure, allowing VM2 to be created in RG2. Azure Arc manages on-premises servers as Azure-connected resources but does not migrate the VM workload to Azure.\n\n**Learn more:** [Move Azure resources to a new resource group or subscription](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-resource-manager/management/move-resource-group-and-subscription) · [Migrate on-premises machines to Azure with Azure Migrate](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/site-recovery/migrate-tutorial-on-premises-azure)","explanationKo":"An Azure resource move operation moves an existing Azure VM between resource groups; Azure Resource Mover is the applicable listed relocation service for VM1. Azure Migrate is designed to discover, assess, and migrate on-premises machines into Azure, allowing VM2 to be created in RG2. Azure Arc manages on-premises servers as Azure-connected resources but does not migrate the VM workload to Azure.\n\n**Learn more:** [Move Azure resources to a new resource group or subscription](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-resource-manager/management/move-resource-group-and-subscription) · [Migrate on-premises machines to Azure with Azure Migrate](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/site-recovery/migrate-tutorial-on-premises-azure)","learnMore":[],"blanks":[{"id":"vm1","labelEn":"VM1","labelKo":"VM1","options":[{"en":"Azure Arc","ko":"Azure Arc"},{"en":"Azure Lighthouse","ko":"Azure Lighthouse"},{"en":"Azure Migrate","ko":"Azure Migrate"},{"en":"Azure Resource Mover","ko":"Azure Resource Mover"},{"en":"The Data Migration Assistant (DMA)","ko":"The Data Migration Assistant (DMA)"}],"answer":"Azure Resource Mover"},{"id":"vm2","labelEn":"VM2","labelKo":"VM2","options":[{"en":"Azure Arc","ko":"Azure Arc"},{"en":"Azure Lighthouse","ko":"Azure Lighthouse"},{"en":"Azure Migrate","ko":"Azure Migrate"},{"en":"Azure Resource Mover","ko":"Azure Resource Mover"},{"en":"The Data Migration Assistant (DMA)","ko":"The Data Migration Assistant (DMA)"}],"answer":"Azure Migrate"}],"template":""},{"n":171,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":["assets/1783709015917-3isgry20.png"],"stemEn":"Your company has the divisions shown in the following table.\n\n[[IMG1]]\n\nSub1 contains an Azure App Service web app named App1. App1 uses Azure AD for single-tenant user authentication. Users from contoso.com can authenticate to App1.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that enables users in the fabrikam.com tenant to authenticate to App1.\n\nWhat should you recommend?","stemKo":"Your company has the divisions shown in the following table.\n\n[[IMG1]]\n\nSub1 contains an Azure App Service web app named App1. App1 uses Azure AD for single-tenant user authentication. Users from contoso.com can authenticate to App1.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that enables users in the fabrikam.com tenant to authenticate to App1.\n\nWhat should you recommend?","explanationEn":"A single-tenant Microsoft Entra ID application accepts identities only from its home tenant. Changing the application registration's Supported account types to an organizational multitenant audience allows users from other Microsoft Entra tenants, including fabrikam.com, to sign in. The application must use a multitenant authority such as the `/common` sign-in endpoint so Microsoft Entra ID can discover and authenticate the user's home tenant. [Convert single-tenant app to multitenant on Microsoft Entra ID](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity-platform/howto-convert-app-to-be-multi-tenant)\n\n**Learn more:** [Convert single-tenant app to multitenant on Microsoft Entra ID](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity-platform/howto-convert-app-to-be-multi-tenant)","explanationKo":"A single-tenant Microsoft Entra ID application accepts identities only from its home tenant. Changing the application registration's Supported account types to an organizational multitenant audience allows users from other Microsoft Entra tenants, including fabrikam.com, to sign in. The application must use a multitenant authority such as the `/common` sign-in endpoint so Microsoft Entra ID can discover and authenticate the user's home tenant. [Convert single-tenant app to multitenant on Microsoft Entra ID](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity-platform/howto-convert-app-to-be-multi-tenant)\n\n**Learn more:** [Convert single-tenant app to multitenant on Microsoft Entra ID](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity-platform/howto-convert-app-to-be-multi-tenant)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Configure the Azure AD provisioning service.","ko":"Configure the Azure AD provisioning service."},{"label":"B","en":"Enable Azure AD pass-through authentication and update the sign-in endpoint.","ko":"Enable Azure AD pass-through authentication and update the sign-in endpoint."},{"label":"C","en":"Configure Supported account types in the application registration and update the sign-in endpoint.","ko":"Configure Supported account types in the application registration and update the sign-in endpoint."},{"label":"D","en":"Configure Azure AD join.","ko":"Configure Azure AD join."}],"answers":["C"]},{"n":172,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design business continuity solutions","topicKo":"업무 연속성 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You must design a highly available Azure SQL database that satisfies these requirements:\n\n- Failover between database replicas must take place with no data loss.\n- The database must stay available if an availability zone has an outage.\n- Costs must be minimized.\n\nWhich deployment option should you choose?","stemKo":"You must design a highly available Azure SQL database that satisfies these requirements:\n\n- Failover between database replicas must take place with no data loss.\n- The database must stay available if an availability zone has an outage.\n- Costs must be minimized.\n\nWhich deployment option should you choose?","explanationEn":"Azure SQL Database Premium supports zone redundancy, distributing database replicas across availability zones. Its high-availability replicas are synchronized, allowing failover without loss of committed data. Standard does not support zone redundancy, while a Business Critical managed instance is a more expensive deployment model than the Premium single-database option for these requirements. [Reliability in Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/reliability/reliability-sql-database)\n\n**Learn more:** [Reliability in Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/reliability/reliability-sql-database)","explanationKo":"Azure SQL Database Premium supports zone redundancy, distributing database replicas across availability zones. Its high-availability replicas are synchronized, allowing failover without loss of committed data. Standard does not support zone redundancy, while a Business Critical managed instance is a more expensive deployment model than the Premium single-database option for these requirements. [Reliability in Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/reliability/reliability-sql-database)\n\n**Learn more:** [Reliability in Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/reliability/reliability-sql-database)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Azure SQL Database Standard","ko":"Azure SQL Database Standard"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure SQL Managed Instance Business Critical","ko":"Azure SQL Managed Instance Business Critical"},{"label":"C","en":"Azure SQL Database Serverless","ko":"Azure SQL Database Serverless"},{"label":"D","en":"Azure SQL Database Premium","ko":"Azure SQL Database Premium"}],"answers":["D"]},{"n":173,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design infrastructure solutions","topicKo":"인프라 설계","koMissing":true,"images":["assets/1783708890226-vo5ctawj.png"],"stemEn":"You have an Azure subscription containing the resources shown in the following table.\n\n[[IMG1]]\n\nYou create peering between VNet1 and VNet2, and between VNet1 and VNet3.\n\nThe virtual machines host an HTTPS-based client/server application and are reachable only through each virtual machine's private IP address.\n\nYou need to implement a load-balancing solution for VM2 and VM3. The solution must ensure that if VM2 fails, requests are automatically routed to VM3, and if VM3 fails, requests are automatically routed to VM2.\n\nWhat should you include in the solution?","stemKo":"You have an Azure subscription containing the resources shown in the following table.\n\n[[IMG1]]\n\nYou create peering between VNet1 and VNet2, and between VNet1 and VNet3.\n\nThe virtual machines host an HTTPS-based client/server application and are reachable only through each virtual machine's private IP address.\n\nYou need to implement a load-balancing solution for VM2 and VM3. The solution must ensure that if VM2 fails, requests are automatically routed to VM3, and if VM3 fails, requests are automatically routed to VM2.\n\nWhat should you include in the solution?","explanationEn":"Azure Application Gateway v2 provides HTTP/HTTPS request routing and health-based backend selection. Its backend pool can contain private IP addresses, and a private frontend IP can serve the client in VNet1. VNet peering enables the gateway to reach VM2 and VM3, so unhealthy backend instances are removed from request routing.\n\n**Learn more:** [How an application gateway works](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/application-gateway/how-application-gateway-works) · [Azure Application Gateway frontend IP address configuration](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/application-gateway/configuration-frontend-ip)","explanationKo":"Azure Application Gateway v2 provides HTTP/HTTPS request routing and health-based backend selection. Its backend pool can contain private IP addresses, and a private frontend IP can serve the client in VNet1. VNet peering enables the gateway to reach VM2 and VM3, so unhealthy backend instances are removed from request routing.\n\n**Learn more:** [How an application gateway works](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/application-gateway/how-application-gateway-works) · [Azure Application Gateway frontend IP address configuration](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/application-gateway/configuration-frontend-ip)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Azure Firewall Premium","ko":"Azure Firewall Premium"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure Application Gateway v2","ko":"Azure Application Gateway v2"},{"label":"C","en":"a cross-region load balancer","ko":"a cross-region load balancer"},{"label":"D","en":"Azure Front Door Premium","ko":"Azure Front Door Premium"}],"answers":["B"]},{"n":174,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design infrastructure solutions","topicKo":"인프라 설계","koMissing":true,"images":["assets/1783709613159-0zt2qmpl.png"],"stemEn":"You have an Azure subscription that includes the resources shown in the following table.\n\n[[IMG1]]\n\nYou need to recommend a load-balancing solution that distributes incoming traffic for VMSS1 across NVA1 and NVA2. The solution must minimize administrative effort.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","stemKo":"You have an Azure subscription that includes the resources shown in the following table.\n\n[[IMG1]]\n\nYou need to recommend a load-balancing solution that distributes incoming traffic for VMSS1 across NVA1 and NVA2. The solution must minimize administrative effort.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","explanationEn":"Gateway Load Balancer transparently inserts network virtual appliances into the data path and distributes traffic across NVA instances in its backend pool. It can be chained to a supported Standard Load Balancer frontend, providing symmetric traffic flows without requiring manual user-defined routes or other additional routing configuration. [Gateway Load Balancer — Microsoft Learn](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/load-balancer/gateway-overview)\n\n**Learn more:** [Gateway Load Balancer — Microsoft Learn](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/load-balancer/gateway-overview)","explanationKo":"Gateway Load Balancer transparently inserts network virtual appliances into the data path and distributes traffic across NVA instances in its backend pool. It can be chained to a supported Standard Load Balancer frontend, providing symmetric traffic flows without requiring manual user-defined routes or other additional routing configuration. [Gateway Load Balancer — Microsoft Learn](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/load-balancer/gateway-overview)\n\n**Learn more:** [Gateway Load Balancer — Microsoft Learn](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/load-balancer/gateway-overview)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Gateway Load Balancer","ko":"Gateway Load Balancer"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure Front Door","ko":"Azure Front Door"},{"label":"C","en":"Azure Application Gateway","ko":"Azure Application Gateway"},{"label":"D","en":"Azure Traffic Manager","ko":"Azure Traffic Manager"}],"answers":["A"]},{"n":175,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You need to recommend a solution for producing a monthly report of all new Azure Resource Manager (ARM) resource deployments in your Azure subscription.\n\nWhat should the recommendation include?","stemKo":"You need to recommend a solution for producing a monthly report of all new Azure Resource Manager (ARM) resource deployments in your Azure subscription.\n\nWhat should the recommendation include?","explanationEn":"Azure Activity Log Administrative events record Resource Manager create, update, delete, and action operations. Exporting these events to a Log Analytics workspace makes them queryable in the `AzureActivity` table, enabling a monthly report of new ARM resource deployments and retention beyond the default Activity Log period.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure Monitor activity log](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-monitor/platform/activity-log) · [Azure Activity Log event schema](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-monitor/platform/activity-log-schema)","explanationKo":"Azure Activity Log Administrative events record Resource Manager create, update, delete, and action operations. Exporting these events to a Log Analytics workspace makes them queryable in the `AzureActivity` table, enabling a monthly report of new ARM resource deployments and retention beyond the default Activity Log period.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure Monitor activity log](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-monitor/platform/activity-log) · [Azure Activity Log event schema](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-monitor/platform/activity-log-schema)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Azure Arc","ko":"Azure Arc"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure Monitor metrics","ko":"Azure Monitor metrics"},{"label":"C","en":"Azure Advisor","ko":"Azure Advisor"},{"label":"D","en":"Azure Log Analytics","ko":"Azure Log Analytics"}],"answers":["D"]},{"n":176,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You are building an app that will use Azure Functions to read activity logs for an Azure subscription.\n\nYou need to recommend an authentication solution for Azure Functions. The solution must minimize administrative effort.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","stemKo":"You are building an app that will use Azure Functions to read activity logs for an Azure subscription.\n\nYou need to recommend an authentication solution for Azure Functions. The solution must minimize administrative effort.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","explanationEn":"A system-assigned managed identity is managed by Azure and is tied to the lifecycle of the Azure Function App. It can be granted the required Azure RBAC permissions to read subscription activity logs without creating, storing, rotating, or managing application secrets or certificates.\n\n**Learn more:** [Use managed identities for App Service and Azure Functions](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/app-service/overview-managed-identity) · [Managed identities for Azure resources](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity/managed-identities-azure-resources/overview)","explanationKo":"A system-assigned managed identity is managed by Azure and is tied to the lifecycle of the Azure Function App. It can be granted the required Azure RBAC permissions to read subscription activity logs without creating, storing, rotating, or managing application secrets or certificates.\n\n**Learn more:** [Use managed identities for App Service and Azure Functions](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/app-service/overview-managed-identity) · [Managed identities for Azure resources](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity/managed-identities-azure-resources/overview)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"an enterprise application in Azure AD","ko":"an enterprise application in Azure AD"},{"label":"B","en":"system-assigned managed identities","ko":"system-assigned managed identities"},{"label":"C","en":"shared access signatures (SAS)","ko":"shared access signatures (SAS)"},{"label":"D","en":"application registration in Azure AD","ko":"application registration in Azure AD"}],"answers":["B"]},{"n":177,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"Contoso, Ltd. has an Azure Active Directory (Azure AD) tenant integrated with Microsoft 365 and an Azure subscription.\n\nContoso has an on-premises identity infrastructure that includes servers running Active Directory Domain Services (AD DS) and Azure AD Connect.\n\nContoso has a partnership with Fabrikam, Inc. Fabrikam has an Active Directory forest and a Microsoft 365 tenant. Fabrikam has the same on-premises identity infrastructure components as Contoso.\n\nA team of 10 Fabrikam developers will work on an Azure solution hosted in Contoso's Azure subscription. The developers must be added to the Contributor role for a resource group in the Contoso subscription.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that enables Contoso to assign the role to the 10 Fabrikam developers. The solution must ensure that the Fabrikam developers use their existing credentials to access resources.\n\nWhat should you recommend?","stemKo":"Contoso, Ltd. has an Azure Active Directory (Azure AD) tenant integrated with Microsoft 365 and an Azure subscription.\n\nContoso has an on-premises identity infrastructure that includes servers running Active Directory Domain Services (AD DS) and Azure AD Connect.\n\nContoso has a partnership with Fabrikam, Inc. Fabrikam has an Active Directory forest and a Microsoft 365 tenant. Fabrikam has the same on-premises identity infrastructure components as Contoso.\n\nA team of 10 Fabrikam developers will work on an Azure solution hosted in Contoso's Azure subscription. The developers must be added to the Contributor role for a resource group in the Contoso subscription.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that enables Contoso to assign the role to the 10 Fabrikam developers. The solution must ensure that the Fabrikam developers use their existing credentials to access resources.\n\nWhat should you recommend?","explanationEn":"Microsoft Entra B2B collaboration lets Contoso create guest accounts for Fabrikam users in the Contoso tenant. The guest users continue to authenticate with their existing Fabrikam credentials, and Azure RBAC can assign them only the required Contributor permissions at the resource-group scope.\n\n**Learn more:** [Assign Azure roles to external users using the Azure portal](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/role-based-access-control/role-assignments-external-users) · [Quickstart: Add a guest user and send an invitation](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/external-id/b2b-quickstart-add-guest-users-portal)","explanationKo":"Microsoft Entra B2B collaboration lets Contoso create guest accounts for Fabrikam users in the Contoso tenant. The guest users continue to authenticate with their existing Fabrikam credentials, and Azure RBAC can assign them only the required Contributor permissions at the resource-group scope.\n\n**Learn more:** [Assign Azure roles to external users using the Azure portal](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/role-based-access-control/role-assignments-external-users) · [Quickstart: Add a guest user and send an invitation](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/external-id/b2b-quickstart-add-guest-users-portal)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"In the Azure AD tenant of Contoso. create cloud-only user accounts for the Fabrikam developers.","ko":"In the Azure AD tenant of Contoso. create cloud-only user accounts for the Fabrikam developers."},{"label":"B","en":"Configure a forest trust between the on-premises Active Directory forests of Contoso and Fabrikam.","ko":"Configure a forest trust between the on-premises Active Directory forests of Contoso and Fabrikam."},{"label":"C","en":"Configure an organization relationship between the Microsoft 365 tenants of Fabrikam and Contoso.","ko":"Configure an organization relationship between the Microsoft 365 tenants of Fabrikam and Contoso."},{"label":"D","en":"In the Azure AD tenant of Contoso, create guest accounts for the Fabnkam developers.","ko":"In the Azure AD tenant of Contoso, create guest accounts for the Fabnkam developers."}],"answers":["D"]},{"n":178,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design infrastructure solutions","topicKo":"인프라 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You have a .NET web service called Service1 that performs the following tasks:\n\n- Reads and writes temporary files on the local file system.\n- Writes to the Application event log.\n\nYou need to recommend an Azure hosting solution for Service1. The solution must meet these requirements:\n\n- Minimize maintenance overhead.\n- Minimize costs.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","stemKo":"You have a .NET web service called Service1 that performs the following tasks:\n\n- Reads and writes temporary files on the local file system.\n- Writes to the Application event log.\n\nYou need to recommend an Azure hosting solution for Service1. The solution must meet these requirements:\n\n- Minimize maintenance overhead.\n- Minimize costs.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","explanationEn":"Windows Azure virtual machine scale set instances provide local temporary disks and can use Windows Application event logs. Azure App Service blocks application code from accessing common Windows event logs, including the Application log; this limitation also rules out an App Service Environment and Azure Functions app. A VM scale set can automate instance management and scaling while meeting the required operating-system capabilities.\n\n**Learn more:** [Operating System Functionality in Azure App Service](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-ca/azure/app-service/operating-system-functionality) · [FAQ for Azure Virtual Machine Scale Sets](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/virtual-machine-scale-sets/virtual-machine-scale-sets-faq)","explanationKo":"Windows Azure virtual machine scale set instances provide local temporary disks and can use Windows Application event logs. Azure App Service blocks application code from accessing common Windows event logs, including the Application log; this limitation also rules out an App Service Environment and Azure Functions app. A VM scale set can automate instance management and scaling while meeting the required operating-system capabilities.\n\n**Learn more:** [Operating System Functionality in Azure App Service](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-ca/azure/app-service/operating-system-functionality) · [FAQ for Azure Virtual Machine Scale Sets](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/virtual-machine-scale-sets/virtual-machine-scale-sets-faq)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"an Azure App Service web app","ko":"an Azure App Service web app"},{"label":"B","en":"an Azure virtual machine scale set","ko":"an Azure virtual machine scale set"},{"label":"C","en":"an App Service Environment (ASE)","ko":"an App Service Environment (ASE)"},{"label":"D","en":"an Azure Functions app","ko":"an Azure Functions app"}],"answers":["B"]},{"n":179,"id":null,"type":"dropdown","topic":"Design data storage solutions","topicKo":"데이터 저장소 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You are designing a storage solution to ingest, store, and analyze petabytes (PBs) of structured, semi-structured, and unstructured text data. The analyzed data will be offloaded to Azure Data Lake Storage Gen2 for long-term retention.\n\nYou need to recommend a storage and analytics solution that:\n\n- Stores the processed data\n- Provides interactive analytics\n- Supports manual scaling, built-in autoscaling, and custom autoscaling\n\nWhat should the recommendation include?","stemKo":"You are designing a storage solution to ingest, store, and analyze petabytes (PBs) of structured, semi-structured, and unstructured text data. The analyzed data will be offloaded to Azure Data Lake Storage Gen2 for long-term retention.\n\nYou need to recommend a storage and analytics solution that:\n\n- Stores the processed data\n- Provides interactive analytics\n- Supports manual scaling, built-in autoscaling, and custom autoscaling\n\nWhat should the recommendation include?","explanationEn":"Azure Data Explorer is designed for fast, interactive analysis of large volumes of structured, semi-structured, and unstructured data. It supports Manual scale, Optimized autoscale, and Custom autoscale for clusters, and its query language is Kusto Query Language (KQL).\n\n**Learn more:** [Manage cluster horizontal scaling in Azure Data Explorer](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/data-explorer/manage-cluster-horizontal-scaling) · [Write Kusto Query Language queries in the Azure Data Explorer web UI](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/data-explorer/web-ui-kql)","explanationKo":"Azure Data Explorer is designed for fast, interactive analysis of large volumes of structured, semi-structured, and unstructured data. It supports Manual scale, Optimized autoscale, and Custom autoscale for clusters, and its query language is Kusto Query Language (KQL).\n\n**Learn more:** [Manage cluster horizontal scaling in Azure Data Explorer](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/data-explorer/manage-cluster-horizontal-scaling) · [Write Kusto Query Language queries in the Azure Data Explorer web UI](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/data-explorer/web-ui-kql)","learnMore":[],"blanks":[{"id":"storage_analytics","labelEn":"For storage and interactive analytics:","labelKo":"For storage and interactive analytics:","options":[{"en":"Azure Data Explorer","ko":"Azure Data Explorer"},{"en":"Azure Data Lake Analytics","ko":"Azure Data Lake Analytics"},{"en":"Log Analytics","ko":"Log Analytics"}],"answer":"Azure Data Explorer"},{"id":"query_language","labelEn":"Query language:","labelKo":"Query language:","options":[{"en":"KQL","ko":"KQL"},{"en":"Transact-SQL","ko":"Transact-SQL"},{"en":"U-SQL","ko":"U-SQL"}],"answer":"KQL"}],"template":""},{"n":180,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design infrastructure solutions","topicKo":"인프라 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You must recommend a solution that fulfills the application development requirements.\n\nWhat should the recommendation include?","stemKo":"You must recommend a solution that fulfills the application development requirements.\n\nWhat should the recommendation include?","explanationEn":"Azure App Service deployment slots provide a separate live staging environment where application changes can be validated before being swapped into production. Slot swapping warms the target instances and supports a seamless deployment without dropped requests or deployment downtime. [Set up staging environments in Azure App Service](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/app-service/deploy-staging-slots)\n\n**Learn more:** [Set up staging environments in Azure App Service](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/app-service/deploy-staging-slots)","explanationKo":"Azure App Service deployment slots provide a separate live staging environment where application changes can be validated before being swapped into production. Slot swapping warms the target instances and supports a seamless deployment without dropped requests or deployment downtime. [Set up staging environments in Azure App Service](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/app-service/deploy-staging-slots)\n\n**Learn more:** [Set up staging environments in Azure App Service](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/app-service/deploy-staging-slots)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"the Azure App Configuration service","ko":"the Azure App Configuration service"},{"label":"B","en":"an Azure Container Registry instance","ko":"an Azure Container Registry instance"},{"label":"C","en":"deployment slots","ko":"deployment slots"},{"label":"D","en":"Continuous Integration/Continuous Deployment (CI/CD) sources","ko":"Continuous Integration/Continuous Deployment (CI/CD) sources"}],"answers":["C"]},{"n":181,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design infrastructure solutions","topicKo":"인프라 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You are developing a sales application that will include several Azure cloud services and manage different components of a transaction. Different cloud services will process customer orders, billing, payment, inventory, and shipping.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that enables the cloud services to communicate transaction information asynchronously by using XML messages.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","stemKo":"You are developing a sales application that will include several Azure cloud services and manage different components of a transaction. Different cloud services will process customer orders, billing, payment, inventory, and shipping.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that enables the cloud services to communicate transaction information asynchronously by using XML messages.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","explanationEn":"Azure Service Bus is a managed enterprise message broker that decouples services through queues and publish-subscribe topics, enabling reliable asynchronous processing. Service Bus messages can carry structured payloads in XML, making it suitable for exchanging transaction information among independently operating services.\n\n**Learn more:** [What is Azure Service Bus?](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/service-bus-messaging/service-bus-messaging-overview) · [Asynchronous messaging patterns and high availability](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/service-bus-messaging/service-bus-async-messaging)","explanationKo":"Azure Service Bus is a managed enterprise message broker that decouples services through queues and publish-subscribe topics, enabling reliable asynchronous processing. Service Bus messages can carry structured payloads in XML, making it suitable for exchanging transaction information among independently operating services.\n\n**Learn more:** [What is Azure Service Bus?](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/service-bus-messaging/service-bus-messaging-overview) · [Asynchronous messaging patterns and high availability](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/service-bus-messaging/service-bus-async-messaging)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Azure Service Fabric","ko":"Azure Service Fabric"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure Data Lake","ko":"Azure Data Lake"},{"label":"C","en":"Azure Service Bus","ko":"Azure Service Bus"},{"label":"D","en":"Azure Traffic Manager","ko":"Azure Traffic Manager"}],"answers":["C"]},{"n":182,"id":null,"type":"dropdown","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You need to recommend a solution that ensures App1 can access the third-party credentials and access strings while meeting the security requirements. What should the recommendation include?","stemKo":"You need to recommend a solution that ensures App1 can access the third-party credentials and access strings while meeting the security requirements. What should the recommendation include?","explanationEn":"A system-assigned managed identity is tied exclusively to the App Service resource, so it avoids sharing an application credential with another service. Assigning the managed identity an Azure Key Vault data-plane role, such as Key Vault Secrets User, authorizes it to retrieve secrets through Azure RBAC.\n\n**Learn more:** [Use managed identities for App Service and Azure Functions](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/app-service/overview-managed-identity) · [Provide access to Key Vault keys, certificates, and secrets with Azure RBAC](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/key-vault/general/rbac-guide)","explanationKo":"A system-assigned managed identity is tied exclusively to the App Service resource, so it avoids sharing an application credential with another service. Assigning the managed identity an Azure Key Vault data-plane role, such as Key Vault Secrets User, authorizes it to retrieve secrets through Azure RBAC.\n\n**Learn more:** [Use managed identities for App Service and Azure Functions](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/app-service/overview-managed-identity) · [Provide access to Key Vault keys, certificates, and secrets with Azure RBAC](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/key-vault/general/rbac-guide)","learnMore":[],"blanks":[{"id":"authenticate","labelEn":"Authenticate App1 by using:","labelKo":"Authenticate App1 by using:","options":[{"en":"A certificate","ko":"A certificate"},{"en":"A system-assigned managed identity","ko":"A system-assigned managed identity"},{"en":"A user-assigned managed identity","ko":"A user-assigned managed identity"}],"answer":"A system-assigned managed identity"},{"id":"authorize","labelEn":"Authorize App1 to retrieve Key Vault secrets by using:","labelKo":"Authorize App1 to retrieve Key Vault secrets by using:","options":[{"en":"An access policy","ko":"An access policy"},{"en":"A connected service","ko":"A connected service"},{"en":"A private link","ko":"A private link"},{"en":"A role assignment","ko":"A role assignment"}],"answer":"A role assignment"}],"template":""},{"n":183,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":["assets/1783707656398-lxde47n9.jpg"],"stemEn":"Your company has the divisions shown in the following table.\n\n[[IMG1]]\n\nSub1 contains an Azure App Service web app named App1. App1 uses Azure AD for single-tenant user authentication. Users from contoso.com can authenticate to App1.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that enables users in the fabrikam.com tenant to authenticate to App1.\n\nWhat should you recommend?","stemKo":"Your company has the divisions shown in the following table.\n\n[[IMG1]]\n\nSub1 contains an Azure App Service web app named App1. App1 uses Azure AD for single-tenant user authentication. Users from contoso.com can authenticate to App1.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that enables users in the fabrikam.com tenant to authenticate to App1.\n\nWhat should you recommend?","explanationEn":"A single-tenant Microsoft Entra application can be accessed by guest users in its home tenant. Microsoft Entra entitlement management governs external-user access through access packages and can invite users from another organization as B2B guests, allowing Fabrikam users to authenticate to the application in the Contoso tenant.\n\n**Learn more:** [Single and multitenant apps in Microsoft Entra ID](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity-platform/single-and-multi-tenant-apps) · [What is entitlement management?](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/id-governance/entitlement-management-overview)","explanationKo":"A single-tenant Microsoft Entra application can be accessed by guest users in its home tenant. Microsoft Entra entitlement management governs external-user access through access packages and can invite users from another organization as B2B guests, allowing Fabrikam users to authenticate to the application in the Contoso tenant.\n\n**Learn more:** [Single and multitenant apps in Microsoft Entra ID](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity-platform/single-and-multi-tenant-apps) · [What is entitlement management?](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/id-governance/entitlement-management-overview)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Configure the Azure AD provisioning service.","ko":"Configure the Azure AD provisioning service."},{"label":"B","en":"Enable Azure AD pass-through authentication and update the sign-in endpoint.","ko":"Enable Azure AD pass-through authentication and update the sign-in endpoint."},{"label":"C","en":"Use Azure AD entitlement management to govern external users.","ko":"Use Azure AD entitlement management to govern external users."},{"label":"D","en":"Configure Azure AD join.","ko":"Configure Azure AD join."}],"answers":["C"]},{"n":184,"id":null,"type":"dropdown","topic":"Design infrastructure solutions","topicKo":"인프라 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You are designing a cost-optimized Azure Batch solution to run two types of jobs on Linux nodes. The first job type consists of short-running tasks for a development environment. The second job type consists of long-running Message Passing Interface (MPI) applications for a production environment that requires timely job completion.\n\nRecommend the pool type and node type for each job type. The solution must minimize compute charges and use Azure Hybrid Benefit whenever possible.\n\nWhat should you recommend?","stemKo":"You are designing a cost-optimized Azure Batch solution to run two types of jobs on Linux nodes. The first job type consists of short-running tasks for a development environment. The second job type consists of long-running Message Passing Interface (MPI) applications for a production environment that requires timely job completion.\n\nRecommend the pool type and node type for each job type. The solution must minimize compute charges and use Azure Hybrid Benefit whenever possible.\n\nWhat should you recommend?","explanationEn":"Low-priority nodes minimize compute cost for the short, interruptible development tasks, and pairing them with the user subscription pool allocation mode lets Azure Hybrid Benefit be applied. The production MPI job needs guaranteed, uninterrupted compute so it can finish in a timely manner, so it must use dedicated nodes rather than preemptible low-priority nodes; Microsoft's guidance provisions these dedicated nodes through the batch service allocation mode for this pairing.\n\n**Learn more:** [Nodes and pools in Azure Batch](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/batch/nodes-and-pools)","explanationKo":"Low-priority nodes minimize compute cost for the short, interruptible development tasks, and pairing them with the user subscription pool allocation mode lets Azure Hybrid Benefit be applied. The production MPI job needs guaranteed, uninterrupted compute so it can finish in a timely manner, so it must use dedicated nodes rather than preemptible low-priority nodes; Microsoft's guidance provisions these dedicated nodes through the batch service allocation mode for this pairing.\n\n**Learn more:** [Nodes and pools in Azure Batch](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/batch/nodes-and-pools)","learnMore":[],"blanks":[{"id":"first_job","labelEn":"First job:","labelKo":"First job:","options":[{"en":"Batch service and dedicated virtual machines","ko":"Batch service and dedicated virtual machines"},{"en":"User subscription and dedicated virtual machines","ko":"User subscription and dedicated virtual machines"},{"en":"User subscription and low-priority virtual machines","ko":"User subscription and low-priority virtual machines"}],"answer":"User subscription and low-priority virtual machines"},{"id":"second_job","labelEn":"Second job:","labelKo":"Second job:","options":[{"en":"Batch service and dedicated virtual machines","ko":"Batch service and dedicated virtual machines"},{"en":"User subscription and dedicated virtual machines","ko":"User subscription and dedicated virtual machines"},{"en":"User subscription and low-priority virtual machines","ko":"User subscription and low-priority virtual machines"}],"answer":"Batch service and dedicated virtual machines"}],"template":""},{"n":185,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":["assets/1783709177179-qcnmj7h7.png"],"stemEn":"Your company has the divisions shown in the following table.\n\n[[IMG1]]\n\nSub1 contains an Azure App Service web app named App1. App1 uses Azure AD for single-tenant user authentication. Users from contoso.com can authenticate to App1.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that enables users in the fabrikam.com tenant to authenticate to App1.\n\nWhat should you recommend?","stemKo":"Your company has the divisions shown in the following table.\n\n[[IMG1]]\n\nSub1 contains an Azure App Service web app named App1. App1 uses Azure AD for single-tenant user authentication. Users from contoso.com can authenticate to App1.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that enables users in the fabrikam.com tenant to authenticate to App1.\n\nWhat should you recommend?","explanationEn":"Azure AD entitlement management uses Microsoft Entra B2B collaboration to let external users authenticate through their home directory while creating a guest representation in the resource tenant. That guest identity can be assigned access to App1 in the contoso.com tenant, enabling fabrikam.com users to sign in to the single-tenant app.\n\n**Learn more:** [Govern access for external users in entitlement management](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/id-governance/entitlement-management-external-users) · [Add and manage B2B collaboration users in the Microsoft Entra admin center](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/external-id/add-users-administrator)","explanationKo":"Azure AD entitlement management uses Microsoft Entra B2B collaboration to let external users authenticate through their home directory while creating a guest representation in the resource tenant. That guest identity can be assigned access to App1 in the contoso.com tenant, enabling fabrikam.com users to sign in to the single-tenant app.\n\n**Learn more:** [Govern access for external users in entitlement management](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/id-governance/entitlement-management-external-users) · [Add and manage B2B collaboration users in the Microsoft Entra admin center](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/external-id/add-users-administrator)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Use Azure AD entitlement management to govern external users.","ko":"Use Azure AD entitlement management to govern external users."},{"label":"B","en":"Enable Azure AD pass-through authentication and update the sign-in endpoint.","ko":"Enable Azure AD pass-through authentication and update the sign-in endpoint."},{"label":"C","en":"Configure a Conditional Access policy.","ko":"Configure a Conditional Access policy."},{"label":"D","en":"Configure assignments for the fabrikam.com users by using Azure AD Privileged Identity Management (PIM).","ko":"Configure assignments for the fabrikam.com users by using Azure AD Privileged Identity Management (PIM)."}],"answers":["A"]},{"n":186,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design infrastructure solutions","topicKo":"인프라 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You are building a sales application that will include several Azure cloud services and manage different transaction components. Different cloud services will process customer orders, billing, payment, inventory, and shipping.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that allows the cloud services to asynchronously exchange transaction information by using XML messages.\n\nWhat should be included in the recommendation?","stemKo":"You are building a sales application that will include several Azure cloud services and manage different transaction components. Different cloud services will process customer orders, billing, payment, inventory, and shipping.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that allows the cloud services to asynchronously exchange transaction information by using XML messages.\n\nWhat should be included in the recommendation?","explanationEn":"Azure Queue Storage provides durable queues for asynchronous communication between loosely coupled components of a distributed application. Queue messages must be compatible with UTF-8 XML requests, making it suitable for exchanging XML transaction information.\n\n**Learn more:** [What is Azure Queue Storage?](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/queues/storage-queues-introduction) · [Quickstart: Azure Queue Storage client library for .NET](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/queues/storage-quickstart-queues-dotnet)","explanationKo":"Azure Queue Storage provides durable queues for asynchronous communication between loosely coupled components of a distributed application. Queue messages must be compatible with UTF-8 XML requests, making it suitable for exchanging XML transaction information.\n\n**Learn more:** [What is Azure Queue Storage?](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/queues/storage-queues-introduction) · [Quickstart: Azure Queue Storage client library for .NET](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/queues/storage-quickstart-queues-dotnet)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Azure Service Fabric","ko":"Azure Service Fabric"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure Traffic Manager","ko":"Azure Traffic Manager"},{"label":"C","en":"Azure Queue Storage","ko":"Azure Queue Storage"},{"label":"D","en":"Azure Notification Hubs","ko":"Azure Notification Hubs"}],"answers":["C"]},{"n":187,"id":null,"type":"dropdown","topic":"Design business continuity solutions","topicKo":"업무 연속성 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You have 10 on-premises servers that run Windows Server.\n\nYou need to back up the servers daily to a Recovery Services vault. The solution must meet these requirements:\n\n- Back up every file and folder on the servers.\n- Keep three backup copies in Azure.\n- Minimize cost.\n\nWhat should you configure?","stemKo":"You have 10 on-premises servers that run Windows Server.\n\nYou need to back up the servers daily to a Recovery Services vault. The solution must meet these requirements:\n\n- Back up every file and folder on the servers.\n- Keep three backup copies in Azure.\n- Minimize cost.\n\nWhat should you configure?","explanationEn":"The MARS agent backs up files and folders from on-premises Windows Server directly to an Azure Recovery Services vault. LRS stores three synchronous copies within one Azure datacenter and is less expensive than ZRS or GRS, satisfying the three-copy and cost-minimization requirements.\n\n**Learn more:** [Back up files and folders by using the Azure Backup agent](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/backup/backup-windows-with-mars-agent) · [Azure Storage redundancy](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/common/storage-redundancy)","explanationKo":"The MARS agent backs up files and folders from on-premises Windows Server directly to an Azure Recovery Services vault. LRS stores three synchronous copies within one Azure datacenter and is less expensive than ZRS or GRS, satisfying the three-copy and cost-minimization requirements.\n\n**Learn more:** [Back up files and folders by using the Azure Backup agent](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/backup/backup-windows-with-mars-agent) · [Azure Storage redundancy](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/common/storage-redundancy)","learnMore":[],"blanks":[{"id":"servers","labelEn":"On the servers:","labelKo":"On the servers:","options":[{"en":"The Azure Site Recovery Mobility service","ko":"The Azure Site Recovery Mobility service"},{"en":"The Microsoft Azure Recovery Services (MARS) agent","ko":"The Microsoft Azure Recovery Services (MARS) agent"},{"en":"Volume Shadow Copy Service (VSS)","ko":"Volume Shadow Copy Service (VSS)"}],"answer":"The Microsoft Azure Recovery Services (MARS) agent"},{"id":"storage","labelEn":"For the storage:","labelKo":"For the storage:","options":[{"en":"Geo-redundant storage (GRS)","ko":"Geo-redundant storage (GRS)"},{"en":"Locally-redundant storage (LRS)","ko":"Locally-redundant storage (LRS)"},{"en":"Zone-redundant storage (ZRS)","ko":"Zone-redundant storage (ZRS)"}],"answer":"Locally-redundant storage (LRS)"}],"template":""},{"n":188,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design data storage solutions","topicKo":"데이터 저장소 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You have 100 servers running Windows Server 2012 R2 that host Microsoft SQL Server 2014 instances. The instances contain databases with these characteristics:\n\n- Stored procedures are implemented by using CLR.\n- The largest database is currently 3 TB, and no database will ever be larger than 4 TB.\n\nYou plan to migrate all data from SQL Server to Azure.\n\nYou need to recommend a service to host the databases. The solution must meet these requirements:\n\n- Whenever possible, minimize management overhead for the migrated databases.\n- Ensure users can authenticate by using Azure Active Directory (Azure AD) credentials.\n- Minimize the number of database changes needed to facilitate the migration.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","stemKo":"You have 100 servers running Windows Server 2012 R2 that host Microsoft SQL Server 2014 instances. The instances contain databases with these characteristics:\n\n- Stored procedures are implemented by using CLR.\n- The largest database is currently 3 TB, and no database will ever be larger than 4 TB.\n\nYou plan to migrate all data from SQL Server to Azure.\n\nYou need to recommend a service to host the databases. The solution must meet these requirements:\n\n- Whenever possible, minimize management overhead for the migrated databases.\n- Ensure users can authenticate by using Azure Active Directory (Azure AD) credentials.\n- Minimize the number of database changes needed to facilitate the migration.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","explanationEn":"Azure SQL Managed Instance is a fully managed PaaS service designed for SQL Server migrations with minimal application or database changes. It supports CLR functionality, Microsoft Entra ID (Azure AD) authentication, and storage configurations sufficient for a 4-TB database, while eliminating the operating-system and SQL Server instance management required for SQL Server on Azure virtual machines.\n\n**Learn more:** [SQL Server to Azure SQL Managed Instance: Migration Overview](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/data-migration/sql-server/managed-instance/overview) · [T-SQL differences between SQL Server and Azure SQL Managed Instance](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/managed-instance/transact-sql-tsql-differences-sql-server?view=azuresql)","explanationKo":"Azure SQL Managed Instance is a fully managed PaaS service designed for SQL Server migrations with minimal application or database changes. It supports CLR functionality, Microsoft Entra ID (Azure AD) authentication, and storage configurations sufficient for a 4-TB database, while eliminating the operating-system and SQL Server instance management required for SQL Server on Azure virtual machines.\n\n**Learn more:** [SQL Server to Azure SQL Managed Instance: Migration Overview](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/data-migration/sql-server/managed-instance/overview) · [T-SQL differences between SQL Server and Azure SQL Managed Instance](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/managed-instance/transact-sql-tsql-differences-sql-server?view=azuresql)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Azure SQL Database elastic pools","ko":"Azure SQL Database elastic pools"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure SQL Managed Instance","ko":"Azure SQL Managed Instance"},{"label":"C","en":"Azure SQL Database single databases","ko":"Azure SQL Database single databases"},{"label":"D","en":"SQL Server 2016 on Azure virtual machines","ko":"SQL Server 2016 on Azure virtual machines"}],"answers":["B"]},{"n":189,"id":null,"type":"dropdown","topic":"Design business continuity solutions","topicKo":"업무 연속성 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"HOTSPOT –\n\nYou plan to migrate on-premises Microsoft SQL Server databases to Azure.\n\nYou need to recommend a deployment and resiliency solution that meets these requirements:\n\n- Supports user-initiated backups\n- Supports multiple automatically replicated instances across Azure regions\n- Minimizes the administrative effort required to implement and maintain business continuity\n\nWhat should you recommend?","stemKo":"HOTSPOT –\n\nYou plan to migrate on-premises Microsoft SQL Server databases to Azure.\n\nYou need to recommend a deployment and resiliency solution that meets these requirements:\n\n- Supports user-initiated backups\n- Supports multiple automatically replicated instances across Azure regions\n- Minimizes the administrative effort required to implement and maintain business continuity\n\nWhat should you recommend?","explanationEn":"Azure SQL Managed Instance supports user-initiated copy-only backups for user databases. Its failover groups automatically replicate all user databases to a secondary managed instance in another Azure region and support managed failover, providing cross-region business continuity with less administration than maintaining SQL Server virtual machines and their replication infrastructure. Zone redundancy protects only within one region.\n\n**Learn more:** [Reliability in Azure SQL Managed Instance](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/reliability/reliability-sql-managed-instance) · [Failover groups overview and best practices - Azure SQL Managed Instance](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/managed-instance/failover-group-sql-mi?view=azuresql)","explanationKo":"Azure SQL Managed Instance supports user-initiated copy-only backups for user databases. Its failover groups automatically replicate all user databases to a secondary managed instance in another Azure region and support managed failover, providing cross-region business continuity with less administration than maintaining SQL Server virtual machines and their replication infrastructure. Zone redundancy protects only within one region.\n\n**Learn more:** [Reliability in Azure SQL Managed Instance](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/reliability/reliability-sql-managed-instance) · [Failover groups overview and best practices - Azure SQL Managed Instance](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/managed-instance/failover-group-sql-mi?view=azuresql)","learnMore":[],"blanks":[{"id":"deployment_solution","labelEn":"Deployment solution:","labelKo":"Deployment solution:","options":[{"en":"Azure SQL Managed Instance","ko":"Azure SQL Managed Instance"},{"en":"SQL Server on Azure Virtual Machines","ko":"SQL Server on Azure Virtual Machines"},{"en":"An Azure SQL Database single database","ko":"An Azure SQL Database single database"}],"answer":"Azure SQL Managed Instance"},{"id":"resiliency_solution","labelEn":"Resiliency solution:","labelKo":"Resiliency solution:","options":[{"en":"Auto-failover group","ko":"Auto-failover group"},{"en":"Active geo-replication","ko":"Active geo-replication"},{"en":"Zone-redundant deployment","ko":"Zone-redundant deployment"}],"answer":"Auto-failover group"}],"template":""},{"n":190,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design business continuity solutions","topicKo":"업무 연속성 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You plan to deploy an Azure Database for MySQL flexible server named Server1 in the East US Azure region.\n\nYou need to implement a business-continuity solution for Server1. The solution must minimize downtime if a failover to a paired region occurs.\n\nWhat should you do?","stemKo":"You plan to deploy an Azure Database for MySQL flexible server named Server1 in the East US Azure region.\n\nYou need to implement a business-continuity solution for Server1. The solution must minimize downtime if a failover to a paired region occurs.\n\nWhat should you do?","explanationEn":"A cross-region read replica provides a pre-created copy of the server that can be promoted to an independent read-write server and receive redirected application traffic during a regional failure. This avoids the variable recovery time required to create and restore a new server from geo-redundant backups. Microsoft documents read replicas as a disaster-recovery option and describes geo-redundant backup recovery as deploying a new server with variable RTO.\n\n**Learn more:** [Overview of business continuity with Azure Database for MySQL - Flexible Server](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/mysql/flexible-server/concepts-business-continuity) · [Backup and restore in Azure Database for MySQL](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/mysql/flexible-server/concepts-backup-restore)","explanationKo":"A cross-region read replica provides a pre-created copy of the server that can be promoted to an independent read-write server and receive redirected application traffic during a regional failure. This avoids the variable recovery time required to create and restore a new server from geo-redundant backups. Microsoft documents read replicas as a disaster-recovery option and describes geo-redundant backup recovery as deploying a new server with variable RTO.\n\n**Learn more:** [Overview of business continuity with Azure Database for MySQL - Flexible Server](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/mysql/flexible-server/concepts-business-continuity) · [Backup and restore in Azure Database for MySQL](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/mysql/flexible-server/concepts-backup-restore)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Create a read replica.","ko":"Create a read replica."},{"label":"B","en":"Store the database files in Azure premium file shares.","ko":"Store the database files in Azure premium file shares."},{"label":"C","en":"Implement Geo-redundant backup.","ko":"Implement Geo-redundant backup."},{"label":"D","en":"Configure native MySQL replication.","ko":"Configure native MySQL replication."}],"answers":["A"]},{"n":191,"id":null,"type":"dropdown","topic":"Design infrastructure solutions","topicKo":"인프라 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"Your company operates two on-premises sites in New York and Los Angeles, plus Azure virtual networks in the East US and West US Azure regions. Each on-premises site has ExpressRoute Global Reach circuits to both regions.\n\nRecommend a solution that meets these requirements:\n\n- Outbound internet traffic from workloads in the virtual networks must be routed through the nearest available on-premises site.\n- If an on-premises site fails, internet-bound traffic from the virtual-network workloads must automatically reroute through the other site.\n\nWhat should the recommendation include?","stemKo":"Your company operates two on-premises sites in New York and Los Angeles, plus Azure virtual networks in the East US and West US Azure regions. Each on-premises site has ExpressRoute Global Reach circuits to both regions.\n\nRecommend a solution that meets these requirements:\n\n- Outbound internet traffic from workloads in the virtual networks must be routed through the nearest available on-premises site.\n- If an on-premises site fails, internet-bound traffic from the virtual-network workloads must automatically reroute through the other site.\n\nWhat should the recommendation include?","explanationEn":"Forcing outbound internet traffic from the VNets through on-premises over ExpressRoute is achieved by having the on-premises sites advertise a default route (0.0.0.0/0) into Azure over the ExpressRoute BGP peering sessions - ExpressRoute forced tunneling cannot be done with user-defined routes, so BGP is how routing to the on-premises locations is configured. Because BGP is a dynamic routing protocol, Azure automatically selects the nearest advertised path and, when a site fails and stops advertising its route, BGP reconverges and reroutes traffic through the surviving site with no manual change. HSRP and VRRP are first-hop gateway-redundancy protocols used inside an on-premises LAN, not for Azure/ExpressRoute path selection, so they are wrong for the failover blank. Both blanks are therefore BGP.\n\n**Learn more:** [ExpressRoute with VPN failover reference architecture](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/architecture/reference-architectures/hybrid-networking/expressroute-vpn-failover)","explanationKo":"Forcing outbound internet traffic from the VNets through on-premises over ExpressRoute is achieved by having the on-premises sites advertise a default route (0.0.0.0/0) into Azure over the ExpressRoute BGP peering sessions - ExpressRoute forced tunneling cannot be done with user-defined routes, so BGP is how routing to the on-premises locations is configured. Because BGP is a dynamic routing protocol, Azure automatically selects the nearest advertised path and, when a site fails and stops advertising its route, BGP reconverges and reroutes traffic through the surviving site with no manual change. HSRP and VRRP are first-hop gateway-redundancy protocols used inside an on-premises LAN, not for Azure/ExpressRoute path selection, so they are wrong for the failover blank. Both blanks are therefore BGP.\n\n**Learn more:** [ExpressRoute with VPN failover reference architecture](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/architecture/reference-architectures/hybrid-networking/expressroute-vpn-failover)","learnMore":[],"blanks":[{"id":"routing","labelEn":"Routing from the virtual networks to the on-premises locations must be configured by using:","labelKo":"Routing from the virtual networks to the on-premises locations must be configured by using:","options":[{"en":"Azure default routes","ko":"Azure default routes"},{"en":"Border Gateway Protocol (BGP)","ko":"Border Gateway Protocol (BGP)"},{"en":"User-defined routes","ko":"User-defined routes"}],"answer":"Border Gateway Protocol (BGP)"},{"id":"failover","labelEn":"The automatic routing configuration following a failover must be handled by using:","labelKo":"The automatic routing configuration following a failover must be handled by using:","options":[{"en":"Border Gateway Protocol (BGP)","ko":"Border Gateway Protocol (BGP)"},{"en":"Hot Standby Routing Protocol (HSRP)","ko":"Hot Standby Routing Protocol (HSRP)"},{"en":"Virtual Router Redundancy Protocol (VRRP)","ko":"Virtual Router Redundancy Protocol (VRRP)"}],"answer":"Border Gateway Protocol (BGP)"}],"template":""},{"n":192,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You have an Azure subscription that includes a storage account.\n\nAn application occasionally writes duplicate files to the storage account. You have a PowerShell script that detects and deletes duplicate files in the storage account. At present, the script is run manually only after the operations manager grants approval.\n\nYou need to recommend a serverless solution that performs these actions:\n\n- Runs the script every hour to determine whether duplicate files exist.\n- Sends the operations manager an email notification requesting approval to delete the duplicate files.\n- Processes an email reply from the operations manager indicating whether deletion is approved.\n- Runs the script when deletion is approved.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","stemKo":"You have an Azure subscription that includes a storage account.\n\nAn application occasionally writes duplicate files to the storage account. You have a PowerShell script that detects and deletes duplicate files in the storage account. At present, the script is run manually only after the operations manager grants approval.\n\nYou need to recommend a serverless solution that performs these actions:\n\n- Runs the script every hour to determine whether duplicate files exist.\n- Sends the operations manager an email notification requesting approval to delete the duplicate files.\n- Processes an email reply from the operations manager indicating whether deletion is approved.\n- Runs the script when deletion is approved.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","explanationEn":"Azure Logic Apps can run a recurring workflow, send and receive email through connectors, and coordinate the approval response. Azure Functions provides serverless execution for the PowerShell script, allowing the workflow to invoke it only after approval is received.\n\n**Learn more:** [Schedule and run recurring workflows with the Recurrence trigger in Azure Logic Apps](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/connectors/connectors-native-recurrence) · [Create a function in Azure that runs on a schedule](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-functions/functions-create-scheduled-function)","explanationKo":"Azure Logic Apps can run a recurring workflow, send and receive email through connectors, and coordinate the approval response. Azure Functions provides serverless execution for the PowerShell script, allowing the workflow to invoke it only after approval is received.\n\n**Learn more:** [Schedule and run recurring workflows with the Recurrence trigger in Azure Logic Apps](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/connectors/connectors-native-recurrence) · [Create a function in Azure that runs on a schedule](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-functions/functions-create-scheduled-function)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Azure Logic Apps and Azure Event Grid","ko":"Azure Logic Apps and Azure Event Grid"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure Logic Apps and Azure Functions","ko":"Azure Logic Apps and Azure Functions"},{"label":"C","en":"Azure Pipelines and Azure Service Fabric","ko":"Azure Pipelines and Azure Service Fabric"},{"label":"D","en":"Azure Functions and Azure Batch","ko":"Azure Functions and Azure Batch"}],"answers":["B"]},{"n":193,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design infrastructure solutions","topicKo":"인프라 설계","koMissing":true,"images":["assets/1783708073129-oaflmmou.png"],"stemEn":"You are designing a microservices architecture to support a web application.\n\nThe solution must satisfy the following requirements:\n\n- Deploy the solution both on-premises and in Azure.\n- Support low-latency and hyper-scale operations.\n\n[[IMG1]]\n\n- Permit independent upgrades for every microservice.\n- Define policies that perform automatic microservice repairs.\n\nYou need to recommend a technology. What should you recommend?","stemKo":"You are designing a microservices architecture to support a web application.\n\nThe solution must satisfy the following requirements:\n\n- Deploy the solution both on-premises and in Azure.\n- Support low-latency and hyper-scale operations.\n\n[[IMG1]]\n\n- Permit independent upgrades for every microservice.\n- Define policies that perform automatic microservice repairs.\n\nYou need to recommend a technology. What should you recommend?","explanationEn":"Azure Service Fabric is a distributed-systems platform for scalable, reliable microservices that can run both in Azure and in standalone on-premises clusters. It supports services being independently versioned, deployed, upgraded, and scaled, and it provides health monitoring plus detection and restart of failed services. Its stateful services are intended for high-throughput, low-latency workloads at large scale.\n\n**Learn more:** [Overview of Azure Service Fabric](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/service-fabric/service-fabric-overview) · [Introduction to microservices on Azure](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/service-fabric/service-fabric-overview-microservices)","explanationKo":"Azure Service Fabric is a distributed-systems platform for scalable, reliable microservices that can run both in Azure and in standalone on-premises clusters. It supports services being independently versioned, deployed, upgraded, and scaled, and it provides health monitoring plus detection and restart of failed services. Its stateful services are intended for high-throughput, low-latency workloads at large scale.\n\n**Learn more:** [Overview of Azure Service Fabric](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/service-fabric/service-fabric-overview) · [Introduction to microservices on Azure](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/service-fabric/service-fabric-overview-microservices)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Azure Container Instance","ko":"Azure Container Instance"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure Logic App","ko":"Azure Logic App"},{"label":"C","en":"Azure Service Fabric","ko":"Azure Service Fabric"},{"label":"D","en":"Azure virtual machine scale set","ko":"Azure virtual machine scale set"}],"answers":["C"]},{"n":194,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design infrastructure solutions","topicKo":"인프라 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You have an Azure subscription containing an Azure Kubernetes Service (AKS) instance named AKS1. AKS1 hosts microservice-based APIs configured to listen on nondefault HTTP ports.\n\nYou plan to deploy a Standard-tier Azure API Management instance named APIM1 to make the APIs available to external users.\n\nYou need to ensure that the AKS1 APIs can be accessed by APIM1. The solution must meet these requirements:\n\n- Implement mTLS authentication between APIM1 and AKS1.\n- Minimize development effort.\n- Minimize costs.\n\nWhat should you do?","stemKo":"You have an Azure subscription containing an Azure Kubernetes Service (AKS) instance named AKS1. AKS1 hosts microservice-based APIs configured to listen on nondefault HTTP ports.\n\nYou plan to deploy a Standard-tier Azure API Management instance named APIM1 to make the APIs available to external users.\n\nYou need to ensure that the AKS1 APIs can be accessed by APIM1. The solution must meet these requirements:\n\n- Implement mTLS authentication between APIM1 and AKS1.\n- Minimize development effort.\n- Minimize costs.\n\nWhat should you do?","explanationEn":"An ingress controller supplies a centralized Layer-7 entry point for HTTP APIs, routes requests to Kubernetes services on their configured ports, and can enforce mTLS at the cluster edge. Azure API Management natively supports mTLS, and Microsoft’s AKS/API Management guidance states that Kubernetes can enable this pattern by installing an ingress controller. This centralizes authentication and routing instead of requiring every microservice to implement them or exposing separate load balancers.\n\n**Learn more:** [Use Azure API Management with microservices deployed in Azure Kubernetes Service](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/api-management/api-management-kubernetes) · [Best practices for network resources in Azure Kubernetes Service](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/aks/operator-best-practices-network)","explanationKo":"An ingress controller supplies a centralized Layer-7 entry point for HTTP APIs, routes requests to Kubernetes services on their configured ports, and can enforce mTLS at the cluster edge. Azure API Management natively supports mTLS, and Microsoft’s AKS/API Management guidance states that Kubernetes can enable this pattern by installing an ingress controller. This centralizes authentication and routing instead of requiring every microservice to implement them or exposing separate load balancers.\n\n**Learn more:** [Use Azure API Management with microservices deployed in Azure Kubernetes Service](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/api-management/api-management-kubernetes) · [Best practices for network resources in Azure Kubernetes Service](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/aks/operator-best-practices-network)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Implement an external load balancer on AKS1.","ko":"Implement an external load balancer on AKS1."},{"label":"B","en":"Redeploy APIM1 to the virtual network that contains AKS1.","ko":"Redeploy APIM1 to the virtual network that contains AKS1."},{"label":"C","en":"Implement an ExternalName service on AKS1.","ko":"Implement an ExternalName service on AKS1."},{"label":"D","en":"Deploy an ingress controller to AKS1.","ko":"Deploy an ingress controller to AKS1."}],"answers":["D"]},{"n":195,"id":null,"type":"dropdown","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"HOTSPOT -\n\nYour company has 20 web APIs developed in-house. It is developing 10 web apps that will use those APIs. Both the web apps and APIs are registered in the company’s Azure Active Directory (Azure AD) tenant, and the web APIs are published through Azure API Management.\n\nRecommend a solution that blocks unauthorized requests originating from the web apps before they reach the web APIs. The solution must:\n\n- Use Azure AD-generated claims.\n- Minimize configuration and management effort.\n\nWhat should be included in the recommendation?","stemKo":"HOTSPOT -\n\nYour company has 20 web APIs developed in-house. It is developing 10 web apps that will use those APIs. Both the web apps and APIs are registered in the company’s Azure Active Directory (Azure AD) tenant, and the web APIs are published through Azure API Management.\n\nRecommend a solution that blocks unauthorized requests originating from the web apps before they reach the web APIs. The solution must:\n\n- Use Azure AD-generated claims.\n- Minimize configuration and management effort.\n\nWhat should be included in the recommendation?","explanationEn":"Azure AD app registrations expose API permissions and issue access tokens with claims for authorized client applications. Azure API Management’s validate-jwt policy validates those Azure AD tokens at the gateway, so unauthorized requests are rejected before they reach the backend web APIs. This centralizes enforcement across the APIs and minimizes per-API configuration.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure API Management validate-jwt policy](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/api-management/validate-jwt-policy) · [Configure an application to expose a web API](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity-platform/quickstart-configure-app-expose-web-apis)","explanationKo":"Azure AD app registrations expose API permissions and issue access tokens with claims for authorized client applications. Azure API Management’s validate-jwt policy validates those Azure AD tokens at the gateway, so unauthorized requests are rejected before they reach the backend web APIs. This centralizes enforcement across the APIs and minimizes per-API configuration.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure API Management validate-jwt policy](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/api-management/validate-jwt-policy) · [Configure an application to expose a web API](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity-platform/quickstart-configure-app-expose-web-apis)","learnMore":[],"blanks":[{"id":"grant_permissions","labelEn":"Grant permissions to allow the web apps to access the web APIs by using:","labelKo":"Grant permissions to allow the web apps to access the web APIs by using:","options":[{"en":"Azure AD","ko":"Azure AD"},{"en":"Azure API Management","ko":"Azure API Management"},{"en":"The web APIs","ko":"The web APIs"}],"answer":"Azure AD"},{"id":"jwt_validation_policy","labelEn":"Configure a JSON Web Token (JWT) validation policy by using:","labelKo":"Configure a JSON Web Token (JWT) validation policy by using:","options":[{"en":"Azure AD","ko":"Azure AD"},{"en":"Azure API Management","ko":"Azure API Management"},{"en":"The web APIs","ko":"The web APIs"}],"answer":"Azure API Management"}],"template":""},{"n":196,"id":null,"type":"dropdown","topic":"Design data storage solutions","topicKo":"데이터 저장소 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You are designing an Azure Storage solution for sensitive data. The data will be accessed daily, and the dataset is under 10 GB.\n\nRecommend a storage solution that meets these requirements:\n\n- Retain all data written to storage for five years.\n- After it is written, data must be read-only; modifications and deletion must be prevented.\n- After five years, data may be deleted but must never be modified.\n- Minimize data-access charges.\n\nWhat should you recommend?","stemKo":"You are designing an Azure Storage solution for sensitive data. The data will be accessed daily, and the dataset is under 10 GB.\n\nRecommend a storage solution that meets these requirements:\n\n- Retain all data written to storage for five years.\n- After it is written, data must be read-only; modifications and deletion must be prevented.\n- After five years, data may be deleted but must never be modified.\n- Minimize data-access charges.\n\nWhat should you recommend?","explanationEn":"The Hot tier is intended for frequently accessed data and has the lowest access costs. A container-level time-based retention immutability policy provides write-once, read-many protection: blobs cannot be modified or deleted during the five-year retention interval; once it expires, they can be deleted but not overwritten.\n\n**Learn more:** [Access tiers for blob data - Azure Storage](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/blobs/access-tiers-overview) · [Overview of immutable storage for blob data - Azure Storage](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/blobs/immutable-storage-overview)","explanationKo":"The Hot tier is intended for frequently accessed data and has the lowest access costs. A container-level time-based retention immutability policy provides write-once, read-many protection: blobs cannot be modified or deleted during the five-year retention interval; once it expires, they can be deleted but not overwritten.\n\n**Learn more:** [Access tiers for blob data - Azure Storage](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/blobs/access-tiers-overview) · [Overview of immutable storage for blob data - Azure Storage](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/blobs/immutable-storage-overview)","learnMore":[],"blanks":[{"id":"storage_account_type","labelEn":"Storage account type:","labelKo":"Storage account type:","options":[{"en":"General purpose v2 with Archive access tier for blobs","ko":"General purpose v2 with Archive access tier for blobs"},{"en":"General purpose v2 with Cool access tier for blobs","ko":"General purpose v2 with Cool access tier for blobs"},{"en":"General purpose v2 with Hot access tier for blobs","ko":"General purpose v2 with Hot access tier for blobs"}],"answer":"General purpose v2 with Hot access tier for blobs"},{"id":"configuration","labelEn":"Configuration to prevent modifications and deletions:","labelKo":"Configuration to prevent modifications and deletions:","options":[{"en":"Container access level","ko":"Container access level"},{"en":"Container access policy","ko":"Container access policy"},{"en":"Storage account resource lock","ko":"Storage account resource lock"}],"answer":"Container access policy"}],"template":""},{"n":197,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design business continuity solutions","topicKo":"업무 연속성 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You must design a highly available Azure SQL database that fulfills these requirements:\n\n- Failover between database replicas must take place with no data loss.\n- The database must stay available if an availability zone fails.\n- Costs must be kept to a minimum.\n\nWhich deployment option should you use?","stemKo":"You must design a highly available Azure SQL database that fulfills these requirements:\n\n- Failover between database replicas must take place with no data loss.\n- The database must stay available if an availability zone fails.\n- Costs must be kept to a minimum.\n\nWhich deployment option should you use?","explanationEn":"A zone-redundant Azure SQL Database Premium deployment distributes fully synchronized replicas across availability zones. A synchronized replica can become primary during a zone failure without loss of committed data. Premium supports zone redundancy, whereas the Standard tier does not; Premium also has no additional charge for enabling zone redundancy because it already uses multiple database replicas.\n\n**Learn more:** [Reliability in Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/reliability/reliability-sql-database) · [Availability through local and zone redundancy for Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/database/high-availability-sla-local-zone-redundancy)","explanationKo":"A zone-redundant Azure SQL Database Premium deployment distributes fully synchronized replicas across availability zones. A synchronized replica can become primary during a zone failure without loss of committed data. Premium supports zone redundancy, whereas the Standard tier does not; Premium also has no additional charge for enabling zone redundancy because it already uses multiple database replicas.\n\n**Learn more:** [Reliability in Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/reliability/reliability-sql-database) · [Availability through local and zone redundancy for Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/database/high-availability-sla-local-zone-redundancy)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Azure SQL Database Hyperscale","ko":"Azure SQL Database Hyperscale"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure SQL Database Premium","ko":"Azure SQL Database Premium"},{"label":"C","en":"Azure SQL Database Standard","ko":"Azure SQL Database Standard"},{"label":"D","en":"Azure SQL Managed Instance General Purpose","ko":"Azure SQL Managed Instance General Purpose"}],"answers":["B"]},{"n":198,"id":null,"type":"statements","topic":"Design infrastructure solutions","topicKo":"인프라 설계","koMissing":true,"images":["assets/1783708086417-fa0j5pk3.jpg"],"stemEn":"You design a solution for the web tier of WebApp1, as shown in the exhibit.\n\n[[IMG1]]\n\nFor each statement, select **Yes** when it is true. Otherwise, select **No**.","stemKo":"You design a solution for the web tier of WebApp1, as shown in the exhibit.\n\n[[IMG1]]\n\nFor each statement, select **Yes** when it is true. Otherwise, select **No**.","explanationEn":"Azure Traffic Manager continuously monitors public endpoints and automatically fails over DNS responses to a healthy regional endpoint. Two Azure App Service web apps in separate regions therefore provide regional redundancy without manual failover configuration. App Service supports scale-out/autoscale when configured on a supported App Service plan.\n\n**Learn more:** [How Azure Traffic Manager Works](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/traffic-manager/traffic-manager-how-it-works) · [Automatic scaling in Azure App Service](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/app-service/manage-automatic-scaling)","explanationKo":"Azure Traffic Manager continuously monitors public endpoints and automatically fails over DNS responses to a healthy regional endpoint. Two Azure App Service web apps in separate regions therefore provide regional redundancy without manual failover configuration. App Service supports scale-out/autoscale when configured on a supported App Service plan.\n\n**Learn more:** [How Azure Traffic Manager Works](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/traffic-manager/traffic-manager-how-it-works) · [Automatic scaling in Azure App Service](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/app-service/manage-automatic-scaling)","learnMore":[],"statements":[{"en":"The design supports the technical requirements for redundancy.","ko":"The design supports the technical requirements for redundancy.","answer":"Yes"},{"en":"The design supports autoscaling.","ko":"The design supports autoscaling.","answer":"Yes"},{"en":"The design requires a manual configuration if an Azure region fails.","ko":"The design requires a manual configuration if an Azure region fails.","answer":"No"}],"columns":["Yes","No"]},{"n":199,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design infrastructure solutions","topicKo":"인프라 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You have an Azure subscription.\n\nYou need to deploy an Azure Kubernetes Service (AKS) solution that uses Windows Server 2019 nodes. The solution must meet these requirements:\n\n- Minimize the time required to provision compute resources during scale-out operations.\n- Support autoscaling for Windows Server containers.\n\nWhich scaling option should you recommend?","stemKo":"You have an Azure subscription.\n\nYou need to deploy an Azure Kubernetes Service (AKS) solution that uses Windows Server 2019 nodes. The solution must meet these requirements:\n\n- Minimize the time required to provision compute resources during scale-out operations.\n- Support autoscaling for Windows Server containers.\n\nWhich scaling option should you recommend?","explanationEn":"Virtual nodes with Virtual Kubelet and Azure Container Instances (ACI) provide rapid pod provisioning, avoiding the wait for the cluster autoscaler to deploy VM compute nodes. Windows Server containers can be scheduled to ACI by manually installing the open-source Virtual Kubelet ACI provider. [Microsoft Learn: Use virtual nodes with AKS](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/aks/virtual-nodes)\n\n**Learn more:** [Use virtual nodes with Azure Kubernetes Service (AKS)](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/aks/virtual-nodes)","explanationKo":"Virtual nodes with Virtual Kubelet and Azure Container Instances (ACI) provide rapid pod provisioning, avoiding the wait for the cluster autoscaler to deploy VM compute nodes. Windows Server containers can be scheduled to ACI by manually installing the open-source Virtual Kubelet ACI provider. [Microsoft Learn: Use virtual nodes with AKS](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/aks/virtual-nodes)\n\n**Learn more:** [Use virtual nodes with Azure Kubernetes Service (AKS)](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/aks/virtual-nodes)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Kubernetes version 1.20.2 or newer","ko":"Kubernetes version 1.20.2 or newer"},{"label":"B","en":"Virtual nodes with Virtual Kubelet ACI","ko":"Virtual nodes with Virtual Kubelet ACI"},{"label":"C","en":"cluster autoscaler","ko":"cluster autoscaler"},{"label":"D","en":"horizontal pod autoscaler","ko":"horizontal pod autoscaler"}],"answers":["B"]},{"n":200,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design infrastructure solutions","topicKo":"인프라 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You are building an app that will use Azure Functions to process events from Azure Event Hubs. Request processing is expected to take between five and 20 minutes.\n\nYou need to recommend a hosting solution that meets these requirements:\n\n- Supports the estimated request-processing runtimes\n- Supports event-driven autoscaling for the app\n\nWhich hosting plan should you recommend?","stemKo":"You are building an app that will use Azure Functions to process events from Azure Event Hubs. Request processing is expected to take between five and 20 minutes.\n\nYou need to recommend a hosting solution that meets these requirements:\n\n- Supports the estimated request-processing runtimes\n- Supports event-driven autoscaling for the app\n\nWhich hosting plan should you recommend?","explanationEn":"Azure Functions Premium supports event-driven scaling and allows the function timeout to be configured without a maximum enforced duration. Consumption is limited to 10 minutes per execution, while Dedicated/App Service plans do not use Azure Functions event-driven scaling.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure Functions scale and hosting](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-functions/functions-scale) · [Event-driven scaling in Azure Functions](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-functions/event-driven-scaling)","explanationKo":"Azure Functions Premium supports event-driven scaling and allows the function timeout to be configured without a maximum enforced duration. Consumption is limited to 10 minutes per execution, while Dedicated/App Service plans do not use Azure Functions event-driven scaling.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure Functions scale and hosting](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-functions/functions-scale) · [Event-driven scaling in Azure Functions](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-functions/event-driven-scaling)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Dedicated","ko":"Dedicated"},{"label":"B","en":"Consumption","ko":"Consumption"},{"label":"C","en":"App Service","ko":"App Service"},{"label":"D","en":"Premium","ko":"Premium"}],"answers":["D"]},{"n":201,"id":null,"type":"dropdown","topic":"Design business continuity solutions","topicKo":"업무 연속성 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You are designing an Azure App Service web app.\n\nYou plan to deploy the web app to the North Europe Azure region and the West Europe Azure region.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution for the web app. The solution must meet these requirements:\n\n- Users must always access the web app from the North Europe region, unless that region fails.\n- The web app must remain available to users if an Azure region is unavailable.\n- Deployment costs must be minimized.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","stemKo":"You are designing an Azure App Service web app.\n\nYou plan to deploy the web app to the North Europe Azure region and the West Europe Azure region.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution for the web app. The solution must meet these requirements:\n\n- Users must always access the web app from the North Europe region, unless that region fails.\n- The web app must remain available to users if an Azure region is unavailable.\n- Deployment costs must be minimized.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","explanationEn":"Azure Traffic Manager provides DNS-based routing, endpoint health monitoring, and failover across Azure regions. With the Priority routing method, North Europe is the primary endpoint and West Europe receives traffic only when the primary endpoint is unhealthy, satisfying the primary-region and availability requirements with minimal added deployment infrastructure.\n\n**Learn more:** [Traffic Manager routing methods](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/traffic-manager/traffic-manager-routing-methods) · [Azure Traffic Manager overview](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/traffic-manager/traffic-manager-overview)","explanationKo":"Azure Traffic Manager provides DNS-based routing, endpoint health monitoring, and failover across Azure regions. With the Priority routing method, North Europe is the primary endpoint and West Europe receives traffic only when the primary endpoint is unhealthy, satisfying the primary-region and availability requirements with minimal added deployment infrastructure.\n\n**Learn more:** [Traffic Manager routing methods](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/traffic-manager/traffic-manager-routing-methods) · [Azure Traffic Manager overview](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/traffic-manager/traffic-manager-overview)","learnMore":[],"blanks":[{"id":"request_routing_method","labelEn":"Request routing method:","labelKo":"Request routing method:","options":[{"en":"A Traffic Manager profile","ko":"A Traffic Manager profile"},{"en":"Azure Application Gateway","ko":"Azure Application Gateway"},{"en":"Azure Load Balancer","ko":"Azure Load Balancer"}],"answer":"A Traffic Manager profile"},{"id":"request_routing_configuration","labelEn":"Request routing configuration:","labelKo":"Request routing configuration:","options":[{"en":"Cookie-based session affinity","ko":"Cookie-based session affinity"},{"en":"Performance traffic routing","ko":"Performance traffic routing"},{"en":"Priority traffic routing","ko":"Priority traffic routing"},{"en":"Weighted traffic routing","ko":"Weighted traffic routing"}],"answer":"Priority traffic routing"}],"template":""},{"n":202,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design infrastructure solutions","topicKo":"인프라 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"Your on-premises datacenter has a server running Linux that hosts a Java app named App1. App1 has the following characteristics:\n\n- App1 is an interactive application that users access through HTTPS connections.\n- The number of connections to App1 varies significantly during the day.\n- App1 runs multiple concurrent instances.\n- App1 requires major changes to run in a container.\n\nYou plan to migrate App1 to Azure.\n\nYou need to recommend a compute solution for App1. The solution must meet these requirements:\n\n- The solution must run multiple App1 instances.\n- The instance count must be managed automatically based on load.\n- Administrative effort must be minimized.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","stemKo":"Your on-premises datacenter has a server running Linux that hosts a Java app named App1. App1 has the following characteristics:\n\n- App1 is an interactive application that users access through HTTPS connections.\n- The number of connections to App1 varies significantly during the day.\n- App1 runs multiple concurrent instances.\n- App1 requires major changes to run in a container.\n\nYou plan to migrate App1 to Azure.\n\nYou need to recommend a compute solution for App1. The solution must meet these requirements:\n\n- The solution must run multiple App1 instances.\n- The instance count must be managed automatically based on load.\n- Administrative effort must be minimized.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","explanationEn":"Azure App Service is a fully managed HTTP-based hosting service for Java web applications. It supports built-in load balancing and automatic scale-out for multiple instances based on incoming HTTP traffic, while allowing Java applications to be deployed as code or JAR/WAR packages rather than requiring containerization. This satisfies variable HTTPS demand with minimal administrative management.\n\n**Learn more:** [Deploy and configure a Java SE, Tomcat, or JBoss EAP app in Azure App Service](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/app-service/configure-language-java-deploy-run) · [Automatic scaling in Azure App Service](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/app-service/manage-automatic-scaling)","explanationKo":"Azure App Service is a fully managed HTTP-based hosting service for Java web applications. It supports built-in load balancing and automatic scale-out for multiple instances based on incoming HTTP traffic, while allowing Java applications to be deployed as code or JAR/WAR packages rather than requiring containerization. This satisfies variable HTTPS demand with minimal administrative management.\n\n**Learn more:** [Deploy and configure a Java SE, Tomcat, or JBoss EAP app in Azure App Service](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/app-service/configure-language-java-deploy-run) · [Automatic scaling in Azure App Service](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/app-service/manage-automatic-scaling)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Azure Batch","ko":"Azure Batch"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure App Service","ko":"Azure App Service"},{"label":"C","en":"Azure Kubernetes Service (AKS)","ko":"Azure Kubernetes Service (AKS)"},{"label":"D","en":"Azure Virtual Machine Scale Sets","ko":"Azure Virtual Machine Scale Sets"}],"answers":["B"]},{"n":203,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design data storage solutions","topicKo":"데이터 저장소 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You have an on-premises application that consumes data from multiple databases. The application code refers to database tables by using a combination of the server, database, and table names.\n\nYou need to migrate the application data to Azure.\n\nTo which two services can you migrate the application data to meet the goal? Each correct answer provides a complete solution.\n\n**NOTE:** Each correct selection is worth one point.","stemKo":"You have an on-premises application that consumes data from multiple databases. The application code refers to database tables by using a combination of the server, database, and table names.\n\nYou need to migrate the application data to Azure.\n\nTo which two services can you migrate the application data to meet the goal? Each correct answer provides a complete solution.\n\n**NOTE:** Each correct selection is worth one point.","explanationEn":"SQL Server on an Azure virtual machine preserves the full SQL Server instance model, including multi-database and server-qualified object references. Azure SQL Managed Instance is designed for migrating on-premises SQL Server applications with minimal application or database changes and supports instance-level SQL Server capabilities. Azure SQL Database does not preserve this multi-database, server-qualified reference model without application changes, and Stretch Database is not a complete migration target.\n\n**Learn more:** [Migration overview: SQL Server to SQL Server on Azure VMs](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/data-migration/sql-server/virtual-machines/overview) · [Migration overview: SQL Server to Azure SQL Managed Instance](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/data-migration/sql-server/managed-instance/overview)","explanationKo":"SQL Server on an Azure virtual machine preserves the full SQL Server instance model, including multi-database and server-qualified object references. Azure SQL Managed Instance is designed for migrating on-premises SQL Server applications with minimal application or database changes and supports instance-level SQL Server capabilities. Azure SQL Database does not preserve this multi-database, server-qualified reference model without application changes, and Stretch Database is not a complete migration target.\n\n**Learn more:** [Migration overview: SQL Server to SQL Server on Azure VMs](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/data-migration/sql-server/virtual-machines/overview) · [Migration overview: SQL Server to Azure SQL Managed Instance](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/data-migration/sql-server/managed-instance/overview)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"SQL Server Stretch Database","ko":"SQL Server Stretch Database"},{"label":"B","en":"SQL Server on an Azure virtual machine","ko":"SQL Server on an Azure virtual machine"},{"label":"C","en":"Azure SQL Database","ko":"Azure SQL Database"},{"label":"D","en":"Azure SQL Managed Instance","ko":"Azure SQL Managed Instance"}],"answers":["BD"]},{"n":204,"id":null,"type":"dropdown","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You have an Azure subscription containing an Azure key vault named KV1 and a virtual machine named VM1. VM1 runs Windows Server 2022: Azure Edition.\n\nYou plan to deploy an ASP.NET Core-based application named App1 to VM1.\n\nYou must configure App1 to use a system-assigned managed identity to retrieve secrets from KV1 while minimizing development effort.\n\nWhat should you do?","stemKo":"You have an Azure subscription containing an Azure key vault named KV1 and a virtual machine named VM1. VM1 runs Windows Server 2022: Azure Edition.\n\nYou plan to deploy an ASP.NET Core-based application named App1 to VM1.\n\nYou must configure App1 to use a system-assigned managed identity to retrieve secrets from KV1 while minimizing development effort.\n\nWhat should you do?","explanationEn":"A system-assigned managed identity running on an Azure VM obtains Microsoft Entra access tokens through the VM's Azure Instance Metadata Service endpoint. It represents a non-interactive client-credentials flow; authorization-code and implicit flows require interactive user sign-in and are not suitable for this workload identity.\n\n**Learn more:** [Use managed identities on a virtual machine to acquire access tokens](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity/managed-identities-azure-resources/how-to-use-vm-token) · [OAuth 2.0 client credentials grant flow](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity-platform/v2-oauth2-client-creds-grant-flow)","explanationKo":"A system-assigned managed identity running on an Azure VM obtains Microsoft Entra access tokens through the VM's Azure Instance Metadata Service endpoint. It represents a non-interactive client-credentials flow; authorization-code and implicit flows require interactive user sign-in and are not suitable for this workload identity.\n\n**Learn more:** [Use managed identities on a virtual machine to acquire access tokens](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity/managed-identities-azure-resources/how-to-use-vm-token) · [OAuth 2.0 client credentials grant flow](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity-platform/v2-oauth2-client-creds-grant-flow)","learnMore":[],"blanks":[{"id":"oauth_flow","labelEn":"Configure App1 to use OAuth 2.0:","labelKo":"Configure App1 to use OAuth 2.0:","options":[{"en":"Authorization code grant flows","ko":"Authorization code grant flows"},{"en":"Client credentials grant flows","ko":"Client credentials grant flows"},{"en":"Implicit grant flows","ko":"Implicit grant flows"}],"answer":"Client credentials grant flows"},{"id":"token_endpoint","labelEn":"Configure App1 to use a REST API call to retrieve an authentication token from the:","labelKo":"Configure App1 to use a REST API call to retrieve an authentication token from the:","options":[{"en":"Azure Instance Metadata Service (IMDS) endpoint","ko":"Azure Instance Metadata Service (IMDS) endpoint"},{"en":"OAuth 2.0 access token endpoint of Azure AD","ko":"OAuth 2.0 access token endpoint of Azure AD"},{"en":"OAuth 2.0 access token endpoint of Microsoft Identity Platform","ko":"OAuth 2.0 access token endpoint of Microsoft Identity Platform"}],"answer":"Azure Instance Metadata Service (IMDS) endpoint"}],"template":""},{"n":205,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design business continuity solutions","topicKo":"업무 연속성 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You must design a highly available Azure SQL database that satisfies these requirements:\n\n- Failover between database replicas must happen with no data loss.\n- The database must stay available if an availability zone has an outage.\n- Costs must be kept to a minimum.\n\nWhich deployment option should you choose?","stemKo":"You must design a highly available Azure SQL database that satisfies these requirements:\n\n- Failover between database replicas must happen with no data loss.\n- The database must stay available if an availability zone has an outage.\n- Costs must be kept to a minimum.\n\nWhich deployment option should you choose?","explanationEn":"Azure SQL Database Premium supports zone redundancy, which distributes database replicas across availability zones and provides a zero-loss recovery point objective for a zone failure. Basic and Standard do not support zone redundancy. Premium meets the required availability and data-loss objectives without the additional high-availability replica requirement of a zone-redundant Hyperscale deployment, making it the cost-minimizing suitable option.\n\n**Learn more:** [Reliability in Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/reliability/reliability-sql-database) · [Availability Through Local and Zone Redundancy - Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/database/high-availability-sla-local-zone-redundancy?view=azuresql-db)","explanationKo":"Azure SQL Database Premium supports zone redundancy, which distributes database replicas across availability zones and provides a zero-loss recovery point objective for a zone failure. Basic and Standard do not support zone redundancy. Premium meets the required availability and data-loss objectives without the additional high-availability replica requirement of a zone-redundant Hyperscale deployment, making it the cost-minimizing suitable option.\n\n**Learn more:** [Reliability in Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/reliability/reliability-sql-database) · [Availability Through Local and Zone Redundancy - Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/database/high-availability-sla-local-zone-redundancy?view=azuresql-db)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Azure SQL Database Hyperscale","ko":"Azure SQL Database Hyperscale"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure SQL Database Premium","ko":"Azure SQL Database Premium"},{"label":"C","en":"Azure SQL Database Basic","ko":"Azure SQL Database Basic"},{"label":"D","en":"Azure SQL Database Standard","ko":"Azure SQL Database Standard"}],"answers":["B"]},{"n":206,"id":null,"type":"statements","topic":"Design data storage solutions","topicKo":"데이터 저장소 설계","koMissing":true,"images":["assets/1783706727700-ws75vqcv.png","assets/1783706730589-axaakm83.png","assets/1783706733105-6e2yg1ic.png"],"stemEn":"HOTSPOT -\n\nYou have an Azure subscription containing the Azure SQL servers shown in the following table.\n\n[[IMG1]]\n\nThe subscription has the storage accounts shown in the following table.\n\n[[IMG2]]\n\nYou create the Azure SQL databases shown in the following table.\n\n[[IMG3]]\n\nFor each of the following statements, select Yes if the statement is true. Otherwise, select No.","stemKo":"HOTSPOT -\n\nYou have an Azure subscription containing the Azure SQL servers shown in the following table.\n\n[[IMG1]]\n\nThe subscription has the storage accounts shown in the following table.\n\n[[IMG2]]\n\nYou create the Azure SQL databases shown in the following table.\n\n[[IMG3]]\n\nFor each of the following statements, select Yes if the statement is true. Otherwise, select No.","explanationEn":"Azure SQL Database auditing can write audit logs to an Azure Storage account. When configuring auditing in the Azure portal, the storage account must be in the same region as the database and logical server. SQLdb1 and storage1 are both in East US, so that pairing is valid. SQLdb2 is on an East US server and SQLdb3 is on a West US server, whereas storage2 is in Central US, so neither can use storage2 through the portal.\n\n**Learn more:** [Set up Auditing - Azure SQL Database & Azure Synapse Analytics](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/database/auditing-setup?view=azuresql)","explanationKo":"Azure SQL Database auditing can write audit logs to an Azure Storage account. When configuring auditing in the Azure portal, the storage account must be in the same region as the database and logical server. SQLdb1 and storage1 are both in East US, so that pairing is valid. SQLdb2 is on an East US server and SQLdb3 is on a West US server, whereas storage2 is in Central US, so neither can use storage2 through the portal.\n\n**Learn more:** [Set up Auditing - Azure SQL Database & Azure Synapse Analytics](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/database/auditing-setup?view=azuresql)","learnMore":[],"statements":[{"en":"When you enable auditing for SQLdb1, you can store the audit information to storage1.","ko":"When you enable auditing for SQLdb1, you can store the audit information to storage1.","answer":"Yes"},{"en":"When you enable auditing for SQLdb2, you can store the audit information to storage2.","ko":"When you enable auditing for SQLdb2, you can store the audit information to storage2.","answer":"No"},{"en":"When you enable auditing for SQLdb3, you can store the audit information to storage2.","ko":"When you enable auditing for SQLdb3, you can store the audit information to storage2.","answer":"No"}],"columns":["Yes","No"]},{"n":207,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You must recommend a solution for generating a monthly report of all new Azure Resource Manager (ARM) resource deployments in your Azure subscription.\n\nWhat should the recommendation include?","stemKo":"You must recommend a solution for generating a monthly report of all new Azure Resource Manager (ARM) resource deployments in your Azure subscription.\n\nWhat should the recommendation include?","explanationEn":"The Azure Activity Log captures subscription-level control-plane events. Its Administrative category records Azure Resource Manager create, update, delete, and action operations, providing the audit data needed to identify new resource deployments during each month.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure Activity Log event schema](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-monitor/platform/activity-log-schema) · [Activity log in Azure Monitor](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-monitor/platform/activity-log)","explanationKo":"The Azure Activity Log captures subscription-level control-plane events. Its Administrative category records Azure Resource Manager create, update, delete, and action operations, providing the audit data needed to identify new resource deployments during each month.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure Activity Log event schema](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-monitor/platform/activity-log-schema) · [Activity log in Azure Monitor](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-monitor/platform/activity-log)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Azure Monitor action groups","ko":"Azure Monitor action groups"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure Arc","ko":"Azure Arc"},{"label":"C","en":"Azure Monitor metrics","ko":"Azure Monitor metrics"},{"label":"D","en":"Azure Activity Log","ko":"Azure Activity Log"}],"answers":["D"]},{"n":208,"id":null,"type":"dropdown","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You have an Azure App Service web app that uses a system-assigned managed identity.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution for storing the web app’s settings as secrets in an Azure Key Vault. The solution must meet these requirements:\n\n- Minimize changes to the app code.\n- Apply the principle of least privilege.\n\nWhat should the recommendation include?","stemKo":"You have an Azure App Service web app that uses a system-assigned managed identity.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution for storing the web app’s settings as secrets in an Azure Key Vault. The solution must meet these requirements:\n\n- Minimize changes to the app code.\n- Apply the principle of least privilege.\n\nWhat should the recommendation include?","explanationEn":"Azure App Service Key Vault references are configured in application settings and resolve secret values through the app’s managed identity, so application code does not need to call Key Vault. The identity needs only secret read access (`secrets/get`), corresponding to the `Secrets: Get` permission; granting list access is unnecessary when the reference specifies the secret name.\n\n**Learn more:** [Use Key Vault references as app settings in Azure App Service](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/app-service/app-service-key-vault-references) · [Azure Key Vault built-in RBAC roles](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/key-vault/general/rbac-guide?tabs=azure-cli)","explanationKo":"Azure App Service Key Vault references are configured in application settings and resolve secret values through the app’s managed identity, so application code does not need to call Key Vault. The identity needs only secret read access (`secrets/get`), corresponding to the `Secrets: Get` permission; granting list access is unnecessary when the reference specifies the secret name.\n\n**Learn more:** [Use Key Vault references as app settings in Azure App Service](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/app-service/app-service-key-vault-references) · [Azure Key Vault built-in RBAC roles](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/key-vault/general/rbac-guide?tabs=azure-cli)","learnMore":[],"blanks":[{"id":"key_vault_integration_method","labelEn":"Key Vault integration method:","labelKo":"Key Vault integration method:","options":[{"en":"Key Vault references in Application settings","ko":"Key Vault references in Application settings"},{"en":"Key Vault references in Appsettings.json","ko":"Key Vault references in Appsettings.json"},{"en":"Key Vault references in Web.config","ko":"Key Vault references in Web.config"},{"en":"Key Vault SDK","ko":"Key Vault SDK"}],"answer":"Key Vault references in Application settings"},{"id":"key_vault_permissions_for_managed_identity","labelEn":"Key Vault permissions for the managed identity:","labelKo":"Key Vault permissions for the managed identity:","options":[{"en":"Keys: Get","ko":"Keys: Get"},{"en":"Keys: List and Get","ko":"Keys: List and Get"},{"en":"Secrets: Get","ko":"Secrets: Get"},{"en":"Secrets: List and Get","ko":"Secrets: List and Get"}],"answer":"Secrets: Get"}],"template":""},{"n":209,"id":null,"type":"dropdown","topic":"Design infrastructure solutions","topicKo":"인프라 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You have an Azure subscription named Subscription1 that is connected to a hybrid Azure Active Directory (Azure AD) tenant.\n\nAn on-premises datacenter has no VPN connection to Subscription1. The datacenter includes a computer named Server1 with Microsoft SQL Server 2016 installed. Server1 is blocked from accessing the internet.\n\nAn Azure logic app resource named LogicApp1 needs write access to a database on Server1.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that enables LogicApp1 to access Server1.\n\nWhat should you recommend deploying on-premises and in Azure?","stemKo":"You have an Azure subscription named Subscription1 that is connected to a hybrid Azure Active Directory (Azure AD) tenant.\n\nAn on-premises datacenter has no VPN connection to Subscription1. The datacenter includes a computer named Server1 with Microsoft SQL Server 2016 installed. Server1 is blocked from accessing the internet.\n\nAn Azure logic app resource named LogicApp1 needs write access to a database on Server1.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that enables LogicApp1 to access Server1.\n\nWhat should you recommend deploying on-premises and in Azure?","explanationEn":"The on-premises data gateway enables Logic Apps to reach on-premises SQL Server through an outbound connection from the gateway host, so no VPN or inbound internet access to Server1 is required. The gateway is registered in Azure as a connection gateway resource and used by the Logic Apps SQL connection.","explanationKo":"The on-premises data gateway enables Logic Apps to reach on-premises SQL Server through an outbound connection from the gateway host, so no VPN or inbound internet access to Server1 is required. The gateway is registered in Azure as a connection gateway resource and used by the Logic Apps SQL connection.","learnMore":[],"blanks":[{"id":"on_premises","labelEn":"On-premises:","labelKo":"On-premises:","options":[{"en":"A Web Application Proxy for Windows Server","ko":"A Web Application Proxy for Windows Server"},{"en":"An Azure AD Application Proxy connector","ko":"An Azure AD Application Proxy connector"},{"en":"An On-premises data gateway","ko":"An On-premises data gateway"},{"en":"Hybrid Connection Manager","ko":"Hybrid Connection Manager"}],"answer":"An On-premises data gateway"},{"id":"azure","labelEn":"Azure:","labelKo":"Azure:","options":[{"en":"A connection gateway resource","ko":"A connection gateway resource"},{"en":"An Azure Application Gateway","ko":"An Azure Application Gateway"},{"en":"An Azure Event Grid domain","ko":"An Azure Event Grid domain"},{"en":"An enterprise application","ko":"An enterprise application"}],"answer":"A connection gateway resource"}],"template":""},{"n":210,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design business continuity solutions","topicKo":"업무 연속성 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You need to design a highly available Azure SQL database that satisfies these requirements:\n\n- Failover between database replicas must occur with no data loss.\n- The database must stay available during a zone outage.\n- Costs must be kept to a minimum.\n\nWhich deployment option should you use?","stemKo":"You need to design a highly available Azure SQL database that satisfies these requirements:\n\n- Failover between database replicas must occur with no data loss.\n- The database must stay available during a zone outage.\n- Costs must be kept to a minimum.\n\nWhich deployment option should you use?","explanationEn":"A zone-redundant Azure SQL Database provides replicas across availability zones and a zero-loss recovery point objective for committed data when a zone fails. The Premium tier supports zone redundancy, whereas Basic does not. Premium provides the required zonal high availability at lower cost than the Business Critical and Hyperscale options.\n\n**Learn more:** [Reliability in Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/reliability/reliability-sql-database)","explanationKo":"A zone-redundant Azure SQL Database provides replicas across availability zones and a zero-loss recovery point objective for committed data when a zone fails. The Premium tier supports zone redundancy, whereas Basic does not. Premium provides the required zonal high availability at lower cost than the Business Critical and Hyperscale options.\n\n**Learn more:** [Reliability in Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/reliability/reliability-sql-database)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Azure SQL Database Business Critical","ko":"Azure SQL Database Business Critical"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure SQL Database Premium","ko":"Azure SQL Database Premium"},{"label":"C","en":"Azure SQL Database Basic","ko":"Azure SQL Database Basic"},{"label":"D","en":"Azure SQL Database Hyperscale","ko":"Azure SQL Database Hyperscale"}],"answers":["B"]},{"n":211,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design infrastructure solutions","topicKo":"인프라 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You are building a sales application that will include several Azure cloud services and manage different parts of a transaction. Different cloud services will process customer orders, billing, payment, inventory, and shipping.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that enables the cloud services to communicate transaction information asynchronously by using XML messages.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","stemKo":"You are building a sales application that will include several Azure cloud services and manage different parts of a transaction. Different cloud services will process customer orders, billing, payment, inventory, and shipping.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that enables the cloud services to communicate transaction information asynchronously by using XML messages.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","explanationEn":"Azure Queue Storage provides reliable, asynchronous message delivery between loosely coupled components of a distributed application. Queue messages are UTF-8 text compatible with XML requests, allowing the transaction-processing services to exchange XML message content without synchronous dependencies.\n\n**Learn more:** [Introduction to Azure Queue Storage](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/queues/storage-queues-introduction) · [Quickstart: Azure Queue Storage client library for .NET](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/queues/storage-quickstart-queues-dotnet)","explanationKo":"Azure Queue Storage provides reliable, asynchronous message delivery between loosely coupled components of a distributed application. Queue messages are UTF-8 text compatible with XML requests, allowing the transaction-processing services to exchange XML message content without synchronous dependencies.\n\n**Learn more:** [Introduction to Azure Queue Storage](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/queues/storage-queues-introduction) · [Quickstart: Azure Queue Storage client library for .NET](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/queues/storage-quickstart-queues-dotnet)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Azure Service Fabric","ko":"Azure Service Fabric"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure Queue Storage","ko":"Azure Queue Storage"},{"label":"C","en":"Azure Traffic Manager","ko":"Azure Traffic Manager"},{"label":"D","en":"Azure Application Gateway","ko":"Azure Application Gateway"}],"answers":["B"]},{"n":212,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design infrastructure solutions","topicKo":"인프라 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You are developing a sales application that will include several Azure cloud services and process different parts of a transaction. Various cloud services will handle customer orders, billing, payment, inventory, and shipping.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that enables the cloud services to asynchronously exchange transaction information by using XML messages.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","stemKo":"You are developing a sales application that will include several Azure cloud services and process different parts of a transaction. Various cloud services will handle customer orders, billing, payment, inventory, and shipping.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that enables the cloud services to asynchronously exchange transaction information by using XML messages.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","explanationEn":"Azure Queue Storage enables loosely coupled components of a distributed application to exchange messages for later, asynchronous processing. Queue messages support UTF-8/XML-compatible content, making the service suitable for passing transaction information among order, billing, payment, inventory, and shipping services.\n\n**Learn more:** [Introduction to Azure Queue Storage](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-sg/azure/storage/queues/storage-queues-introduction) · [Tutorial: Work with Azure Queue Storage queues in .NET](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/queues/storage-tutorial-queues)","explanationKo":"Azure Queue Storage enables loosely coupled components of a distributed application to exchange messages for later, asynchronous processing. Queue messages support UTF-8/XML-compatible content, making the service suitable for passing transaction information among order, billing, payment, inventory, and shipping services.\n\n**Learn more:** [Introduction to Azure Queue Storage](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-sg/azure/storage/queues/storage-queues-introduction) · [Tutorial: Work with Azure Queue Storage queues in .NET](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/queues/storage-tutorial-queues)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Azure Notification Hubs","ko":"Azure Notification Hubs"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure Service Fabric","ko":"Azure Service Fabric"},{"label":"C","en":"Azure Queue Storage","ko":"Azure Queue Storage"},{"label":"D","en":"Azure Application Gateway","ko":"Azure Application Gateway"}],"answers":["C"]},{"n":213,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design data storage solutions","topicKo":"데이터 저장소 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You are designing an Azure IoT Hub solution that will contain 50,000 IoT devices.\n\nEach device will stream data that includes temperature, device ID, and time data. About 50,000 records will be written per second, and the data will be visualized in near real time.\n\nYou need to recommend a service for storing and querying the data.\n\nWhich two services can you recommend? Each correct answer provides a complete solution.\n\nNOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.","stemKo":"You are designing an Azure IoT Hub solution that will contain 50,000 IoT devices.\n\nEach device will stream data that includes temperature, device ID, and time data. About 50,000 records will be written per second, and the data will be visualized in near real time.\n\nYou need to recommend a service for storing and querying the data.\n\nWhich two services can you recommend? Each correct answer provides a complete solution.\n\nNOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.","explanationEn":"For the same IoT scenario (50,000 devices, 50,000 records/sec, near-real-time visualization and querying), Azure Cosmos DB for NoSQL provides globally distributed, high-throughput storage with query capability, and Azure Time Series Insights was designed specifically for time-series data ingestion, storage, querying, and visualization. Both services independently provide complete solutions for storing and querying the telemetry data.","explanationKo":"For the same IoT scenario (50,000 devices, 50,000 records/sec, near-real-time visualization and querying), Azure Cosmos DB for NoSQL provides globally distributed, high-throughput storage with query capability, and Azure Time Series Insights was designed specifically for time-series data ingestion, storage, querying, and visualization. Both services independently provide complete solutions for storing and querying the telemetry data.","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Azure Table Storage","ko":"Azure Table Storage"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure Event Grid","ko":"Azure Event Grid"},{"label":"C","en":"Azure Cosmos DB for NoSQL","ko":"Azure Cosmos DB for NoSQL"},{"label":"D","en":"Azure Time Series Insights","ko":"Azure Time Series Insights"}],"answers":["CD"]},{"n":214,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You have an Azure subscription.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that lets developers provision Azure virtual machines. The solution must satisfy these requirements:\n\n- Allow virtual machines to be created only in specified regions.\n- Allow virtual machines to be created only in specified sizes.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","stemKo":"You have an Azure subscription.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that lets developers provision Azure virtual machines. The solution must satisfy these requirements:\n\n- Allow virtual machines to be created only in specified regions.\n- Allow virtual machines to be created only in specified sizes.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","explanationEn":"Azure Policy can deny deployments outside an allowed list of regions and deny virtual machines whose size SKU is not in an approved list. Its built-in policies include **Allowed locations** and **Allowed virtual machine size SKUs**, so policy assignments can enforce both restrictions across the applicable scope.\n\n**Learn more:** [Overview of Azure Policy](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/governance/policy/overview) · [Built-in policy definitions for Azure Virtual Machines](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/virtual-machines/policy-reference)","explanationKo":"Azure Policy can deny deployments outside an allowed list of regions and deny virtual machines whose size SKU is not in an approved list. Its built-in policies include **Allowed locations** and **Allowed virtual machine size SKUs**, so policy assignments can enforce both restrictions across the applicable scope.\n\n**Learn more:** [Overview of Azure Policy](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/governance/policy/overview) · [Built-in policy definitions for Azure Virtual Machines](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/virtual-machines/policy-reference)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Azure Resource Manager (ARM) templates","ko":"Azure Resource Manager (ARM) templates"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure Policy","ko":"Azure Policy"},{"label":"C","en":"Conditional Access policies","ko":"Conditional Access policies"},{"label":"D","en":"role-based access control (RBAC)","ko":"role-based access control (RBAC)"}],"answers":["B"]},{"n":215,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You have an Azure subscription containing a custom application named Application1. Application1 was developed by an external company, Fabrikam, Ltd. Fabrikam developers were assigned role-based access control (RBAC) permissions to the Application1 components. All users have Microsoft 365 E5 licenses.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution to verify whether the Fabrikam developers still need permissions to Application1. The solution must meet these requirements:\n\n- Send the developers’ manager a monthly email message listing the access permissions to Application1.\n- Automatically revoke an access permission if the manager does not verify it.\n- Minimize development effort.\n\nWhat should you recommend?","stemKo":"You have an Azure subscription containing a custom application named Application1. Application1 was developed by an external company, Fabrikam, Ltd. Fabrikam developers were assigned role-based access control (RBAC) permissions to the Application1 components. All users have Microsoft 365 E5 licenses.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution to verify whether the Fabrikam developers still need permissions to Application1. The solution must meet these requirements:\n\n- Send the developers’ manager a monthly email message listing the access permissions to Application1.\n- Automatically revoke an access permission if the manager does not verify it.\n- Minimize development effort.\n\nWhat should you recommend?","explanationEn":"Microsoft Entra access reviews provide a built-in review process for Azure resource-role assignments. A review can recur monthly, assign each user’s manager as reviewer, send review notifications, and automatically apply results so unreviewed or denied role assignments are removed. This meets the access-governance requirements without custom automation.\n\n**Learn more:** [Create an access review of Azure resource and Microsoft Entra roles in PIM](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/id-governance/privileged-identity-management/pim-create-roles-and-resource-roles-review) · [Plan a Microsoft Entra access reviews deployment](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/id-governance/deploy-access-reviews)","explanationKo":"Microsoft Entra access reviews provide a built-in review process for Azure resource-role assignments. A review can recur monthly, assign each user’s manager as reviewer, send review notifications, and automatically apply results so unreviewed or denied role assignments are removed. This meets the access-governance requirements without custom automation.\n\n**Learn more:** [Create an access review of Azure resource and Microsoft Entra roles in PIM](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/id-governance/privileged-identity-management/pim-create-roles-and-resource-roles-review) · [Plan a Microsoft Entra access reviews deployment](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/id-governance/deploy-access-reviews)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"In Azure Active Directory (Azure AD), create an access review of Application1.","ko":"In Azure Active Directory (Azure AD), create an access review of Application1."},{"label":"B","en":"Create an Azure Automation runbook that runs the Get-AzRoleAssignment cmdlet.","ko":"Create an Azure Automation runbook that runs the Get-AzRoleAssignment cmdlet."},{"label":"C","en":"In Azure Active Directory (Azure AD) Privileged Identity Management, create a custom role assignment for the Application1 resources.","ko":"In Azure Active Directory (Azure AD) Privileged Identity Management, create a custom role assignment for the Application1 resources."},{"label":"D","en":"Create an Azure Automation runbook that runs the Get-AzureADUserAppRoleAssignment cmdlet.","ko":"Create an Azure Automation runbook that runs the Get-AzureADUserAppRoleAssignment cmdlet."}],"answers":["A"]},{"n":216,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design infrastructure solutions","topicKo":"인프라 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You need to recommend a solution for the App1 maintenance task. The solution must minimize costs.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","stemKo":"You need to recommend a solution for the App1 maintenance task. The solution must minimize costs.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","explanationEn":"Azure App Service WebJobs run background programs or scripts alongside an App Service app, using the same App Service environment. WebJobs are supported by all App Service plans at no extra charge, making them appropriate for a maintenance task when minimizing additional cost is required.\n\n**Learn more:** [Run background tasks with WebJobs - Azure App Service](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/app-service/webjobs-create)","explanationKo":"Azure App Service WebJobs run background programs or scripts alongside an App Service app, using the same App Service environment. WebJobs are supported by all App Service plans at no extra charge, making them appropriate for a maintenance task when minimizing additional cost is required.\n\n**Learn more:** [Run background tasks with WebJobs - Azure App Service](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/app-service/webjobs-create)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"an Azure logic app","ko":"an Azure logic app"},{"label":"B","en":"an Azure function","ko":"an Azure function"},{"label":"C","en":"an Azure virtual machine","ko":"an Azure virtual machine"},{"label":"D","en":"an App Service WebJob","ko":"an App Service WebJob"}],"answers":["D"]},{"n":217,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design infrastructure solutions","topicKo":"인프라 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You are developing a sales application that will include several Azure cloud services and manage different components of a transaction. Different cloud services will process customer orders, billing, payment, inventory, and shipping.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that enables the cloud services to asynchronously communicate transaction information by using XML messages.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","stemKo":"You are developing a sales application that will include several Azure cloud services and manage different components of a transaction. Different cloud services will process customer orders, billing, payment, inventory, and shipping.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that enables the cloud services to asynchronously communicate transaction information by using XML messages.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","explanationEn":"Azure Queue Storage provides durable queues for messages exchanged between distributed application components, enabling services to process transaction information asynchronously and independently. Queue messages can contain XML payloads.\n\n**Learn more:** [Introduction to Azure Queue Storage](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/queues/storage-queues-introduction) · [Reliability in Azure Queue Storage](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/reliability/reliability-storage-queue)","explanationKo":"Azure Queue Storage provides durable queues for messages exchanged between distributed application components, enabling services to process transaction information asynchronously and independently. Queue messages can contain XML payloads.\n\n**Learn more:** [Introduction to Azure Queue Storage](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/queues/storage-queues-introduction) · [Reliability in Azure Queue Storage](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/reliability/reliability-storage-queue)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Azure Application Gateway","ko":"Azure Application Gateway"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure Data Lake","ko":"Azure Data Lake"},{"label":"C","en":"Azure Queue Storage","ko":"Azure Queue Storage"},{"label":"D","en":"Azure Blob Storage","ko":"Azure Blob Storage"}],"answers":["C"]},{"n":218,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design infrastructure solutions","topicKo":"인프라 설계","koMissing":true,"images":["assets/1783706735069-tn1invw3.png"],"stemEn":"You have the Azure resources shown in the following table.\n\n[[IMG1]]\n\nYou need to deploy a new Azure Firewall policy that contains mandatory rules for every Azure Firewall deployment. The new policy will be configured as a parent policy for the existing policies.\n\nWhat is the minimum number of additional Azure Firewall policies that you should create?","stemKo":"You have the Azure resources shown in the following table.\n\n[[IMG1]]\n\nYou need to deploy a new Azure Firewall policy that contains mandatory rules for every Azure Firewall deployment. The new policy will be configured as a parent policy for the existing policies.\n\nWhat is the minimum number of additional Azure Firewall policies that you should create?","explanationEn":"Azure Firewall Policy hierarchy requires the parent policy and its child policy to be in the same region. Because the existing child policies are in Central US, East US, and West Europe, a separate parent policy is required for each of those three regions. [What is Azure Firewall Manager? | Microsoft Learn](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/firewall/central-management)\n\n**Learn more:** [What is Azure Firewall Manager? | Microsoft Learn](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/firewall/central-management) · [Use Azure Firewall policy to define a rule hierarchy | Microsoft Learn](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/firewall-manager/rule-hierarchy)","explanationKo":"Azure Firewall Policy hierarchy requires the parent policy and its child policy to be in the same region. Because the existing child policies are in Central US, East US, and West Europe, a separate parent policy is required for each of those three regions. [What is Azure Firewall Manager? | Microsoft Learn](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/firewall/central-management)\n\n**Learn more:** [What is Azure Firewall Manager? | Microsoft Learn](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/firewall/central-management) · [Use Azure Firewall policy to define a rule hierarchy | Microsoft Learn](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/firewall-manager/rule-hierarchy)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"0","ko":"0"},{"label":"B","en":"1","ko":"1"},{"label":"C","en":"2","ko":"2"},{"label":"D","en":"3","ko":"3"}],"answers":["D"]},{"n":219,"id":null,"type":"dropdown","topic":"Design data storage solutions","topicKo":"데이터 저장소 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You plan to move App1 to Azure.\n\nYou need to recommend a storage solution for App1 that meets the security and compliance requirements.\n\nWhich storage type should you recommend, and how should you configure the storage?","stemKo":"You plan to move App1 to Azure.\n\nYou need to recommend a storage solution for App1 that meets the security and compliance requirements.\n\nWhich storage type should you recommend, and how should you configure the storage?","explanationEn":"Standard general-purpose v2 supports Azure Blob Storage immutable-storage policies, which keep data in a write-once, read-many state so it cannot be modified or deleted for the configured retention period. Enabling a hierarchical namespace provides Azure Data Lake Storage capabilities, including file and directory hierarchy and ACL-based access control. NFSv3 is not appropriate because immutable storage policies are unsupported on accounts with NFSv3 enabled.\n\n**Learn more:** [Create a storage account for Azure Data Lake Storage](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/blobs/create-data-lake-storage-account) · [Azure Data Lake Storage hierarchical namespace](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/blobs/data-lake-storage-namespace)","explanationKo":"Standard general-purpose v2 supports Azure Blob Storage immutable-storage policies, which keep data in a write-once, read-many state so it cannot be modified or deleted for the configured retention period. Enabling a hierarchical namespace provides Azure Data Lake Storage capabilities, including file and directory hierarchy and ACL-based access control. NFSv3 is not appropriate because immutable storage policies are unsupported on accounts with NFSv3 enabled.\n\n**Learn more:** [Create a storage account for Azure Data Lake Storage](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/blobs/create-data-lake-storage-account) · [Azure Data Lake Storage hierarchical namespace](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/blobs/data-lake-storage-namespace)","learnMore":[],"blanks":[{"id":"storage_account_type","labelEn":"Storage account type:","labelKo":"Storage account type:","options":[{"en":"Premium page blobs","ko":"Premium page blobs"},{"en":"Premium file shares","ko":"Premium file shares"},{"en":"Standard general-purpose v2","ko":"Standard general-purpose v2"}],"answer":"Standard general-purpose v2"},{"id":"configuration","labelEn":"Configuration:","labelKo":"Configuration:","options":[{"en":"NFSv3","ko":"NFSv3"},{"en":"Large file shares","ko":"Large file shares"},{"en":"Hierarchical namespace","ko":"Hierarchical namespace"}],"answer":"Hierarchical namespace"}],"template":""},{"n":220,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design data storage solutions","topicKo":"데이터 저장소 설계","koMissing":true,"images":["assets/1783706737032-wf280om4.png"],"stemEn":"You are designing a SQL database solution. The solution will contain 20 databases, each 20 GB, with varying usage patterns.\n\nYou need to recommend a database platform to host the databases. The solution must satisfy the following requirements:\n\n- Meet a Service Level Agreement (SLA) of 99.99% uptime.\n- Dynamically scale the compute resources assigned to the databases.\n- Include reserved capacity.\n\nCompute charges must be minimized.\n\n[[IMG1]]\n\nWhat should be included in the recommendation?","stemKo":"You are designing a SQL database solution. The solution will contain 20 databases, each 20 GB, with varying usage patterns.\n\nYou need to recommend a database platform to host the databases. The solution must satisfy the following requirements:\n\n- Meet a Service Level Agreement (SLA) of 99.99% uptime.\n- Dynamically scale the compute resources assigned to the databases.\n- Include reserved capacity.\n\nCompute charges must be minimized.\n\n[[IMG1]]\n\nWhat should be included in the recommendation?","explanationEn":"Azure SQL Database elastic pools let databases with varying and unpredictable usage patterns share a provisioned pool of compute resources, avoiding the cost of independently sizing all 20 databases for peak demand. Pool compute can be scaled as workload needs change, and provisioned Azure SQL Database compute can receive reserved-capacity discounts. Azure SQL Database serverless automatically scales compute but is ineligible for reservation discounts.\n\n**Learn more:** [Resource Management in Dense Elastic Pools - Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/database/elastic-pool-resource-management?view=azuresql) · [How a reservation discount is applied to Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/cost-management-billing/reservations/understand-reservation-charges)","explanationKo":"Azure SQL Database elastic pools let databases with varying and unpredictable usage patterns share a provisioned pool of compute resources, avoiding the cost of independently sizing all 20 databases for peak demand. Pool compute can be scaled as workload needs change, and provisioned Azure SQL Database compute can receive reserved-capacity discounts. Azure SQL Database serverless automatically scales compute but is ineligible for reservation discounts.\n\n**Learn more:** [Resource Management in Dense Elastic Pools - Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/database/elastic-pool-resource-management?view=azuresql) · [How a reservation discount is applied to Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/cost-management-billing/reservations/understand-reservation-charges)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"an elastic pool that contains 20 Azure SQL databases","ko":"an elastic pool that contains 20 Azure SQL databases"},{"label":"B","en":"20 databases on a Microsoft SQL server that runs on an Azure virtual machine in an availability set","ko":"20 databases on a Microsoft SQL server that runs on an Azure virtual machine in an availability set"},{"label":"C","en":"20 databases on a Microsoft SQL server that runs on an Azure virtual machine","ko":"20 databases on a Microsoft SQL server that runs on an Azure virtual machine"},{"label":"D","en":"20 instances of Azure SQL Database serverless","ko":"20 instances of Azure SQL Database serverless"}],"answers":["A"]},{"n":221,"id":null,"type":"dropdown","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You have an Azure subscription containing 300 virtual machines that run Windows Server 2019.\n\nYou need to centrally monitor all warning events in the virtual machines' System logs.\n\nWhat should the solution include?","stemKo":"You have an Azure subscription containing 300 virtual machines that run Windows Server 2019.\n\nYou need to centrally monitor all warning events in the virtual machines' System logs.\n\nWhat should the solution include?","explanationEn":"A Log Analytics workspace is the Azure Monitor Logs data store used for centralized querying and monitoring. The Azure Monitor agent collects Windows System event-log data from each virtual machine when configured through a data collection rule, enabling central monitoring of warning events.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure Monitor Agent overview](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-monitor/agents/azure-monitor-agent-overview) · [Collect Windows event log data sources with Azure Monitor Agent](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-monitor/vm/data-collection-windows-events)","explanationKo":"A Log Analytics workspace is the Azure Monitor Logs data store used for centralized querying and monitoring. The Azure Monitor agent collects Windows System event-log data from each virtual machine when configured through a data collection rule, enabling central monitoring of warning events.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure Monitor Agent overview](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-monitor/agents/azure-monitor-agent-overview) · [Collect Windows event log data sources with Azure Monitor Agent](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-monitor/vm/data-collection-windows-events)","learnMore":[],"blanks":[{"id":"resource","labelEn":"Resource to create in Azure:","labelKo":"Resource to create in Azure:","options":[{"en":"An event hub","ko":"An event hub"},{"en":"A log analytics workspace","ko":"A log analytics workspace"},{"en":"A search service","ko":"A search service"},{"en":"A storage account","ko":"A storage account"}],"answer":"A log analytics workspace"},{"id":"vm_configuration","labelEn":"Configuration to perform on the virtual machines:","labelKo":"Configuration to perform on the virtual machines:","options":[{"en":"Create event subscriptions","ko":"Create event subscriptions"},{"en":"Configure Continuous delivery","ko":"Configure Continuous delivery"},{"en":"Install the Azure Monitor agent","ko":"Install the Azure Monitor agent"},{"en":"Modify the membership of the Event Log Readers group","ko":"Modify the membership of the Event Log Readers group"}],"answer":"Install the Azure Monitor agent"}],"template":""},{"n":222,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design business continuity solutions","topicKo":"업무 연속성 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You plan to migrate a web app named App1 from an on-premises datacenter to Azure.\n\nApp1 relies on a custom COM component installed on the host server.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution to host App1 in Azure. The solution must meet the following requirements:\n\n- App1 must remain available to users if an Azure datacenter becomes unavailable.\n- Costs must be minimized.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","stemKo":"You plan to migrate a web app named App1 from an on-premises datacenter to Azure.\n\nApp1 relies on a custom COM component installed on the host server.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution to host App1 in Azure. The solution must meet the following requirements:\n\n- App1 must remain available to users if an Azure datacenter becomes unavailable.\n- Costs must be minimized.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","explanationEn":"A virtual machine scale set provides servers on which the custom COM component can be installed, and an Azure Load Balancer distributes traffic among the instances. Availability zones are physically separate groups of datacenters within an Azure region with independent power, cooling, and networking; distributing the scale set across two zones protects the application from a datacenter/zone outage. This meets the stated availability scope without the additional cost of duplicating the solution in a second region.\n\n**Learn more:** [What are Azure availability zones?](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-ie/azure/reliability/availability-zones-overview) · [Azure Virtual Machine Scale Sets overview](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/virtual-machine-scale-sets/overview)","explanationKo":"A virtual machine scale set provides servers on which the custom COM component can be installed, and an Azure Load Balancer distributes traffic among the instances. Availability zones are physically separate groups of datacenters within an Azure region with independent power, cooling, and networking; distributing the scale set across two zones protects the application from a datacenter/zone outage. This meets the stated availability scope without the additional cost of duplicating the solution in a second region.\n\n**Learn more:** [What are Azure availability zones?](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-ie/azure/reliability/availability-zones-overview) · [Azure Virtual Machine Scale Sets overview](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/virtual-machine-scale-sets/overview)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"In two Azure regions, deploy a load balancer and a web app.","ko":"In two Azure regions, deploy a load balancer and a web app."},{"label":"B","en":"In two Azure regions, deploy a load balancer and a virtual machine scale set.","ko":"In two Azure regions, deploy a load balancer and a virtual machine scale set."},{"label":"C","en":"Deploy a load balancer and a virtual machine scale set across two availability zones.","ko":"Deploy a load balancer and a virtual machine scale set across two availability zones."},{"label":"D","en":"In two Azure regions, deploy an Azure Traffic Manager profile and a web app.","ko":"In two Azure regions, deploy an Azure Traffic Manager profile and a web app."}],"answers":["C"]},{"n":223,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":["assets/1783709017229-ebflhgly.png"],"stemEn":"Your company has the divisions displayed in the following table.\n\n[[IMG1]]\n\nSub1 contains an Azure App Service web app named App1. App1 uses Azure AD for single-tenant user authentication. Users from contoso.com can authenticate to App1.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that enables users in the fabrikam.com tenant to authenticate to App1.\n\nWhat should you recommend?","stemKo":"Your company has the divisions displayed in the following table.\n\n[[IMG1]]\n\nSub1 contains an Azure App Service web app named App1. App1 uses Azure AD for single-tenant user authentication. Users from contoso.com can authenticate to App1.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that enables users in the fabrikam.com tenant to authenticate to App1.\n\nWhat should you recommend?","explanationEn":"Azure AD entitlement management uses Microsoft Entra B2B to govern access for users from external organizations. A fabrikam.com user can authenticate through their home tenant while being represented as an external user in the contoso.com resource tenant and assigned access to the application through an access package. Pass-through authentication, Privileged Identity Management, and Identity Protection do not provide external-user onboarding and application access governance.\n\n**Learn more:** [Govern access for external users in entitlement management](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/id-governance/entitlement-management-external-users) · [Onboard external users to line of business applications using Microsoft Entra B2B](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/architecture/11-onboard-external-user)","explanationKo":"Azure AD entitlement management uses Microsoft Entra B2B to govern access for users from external organizations. A fabrikam.com user can authenticate through their home tenant while being represented as an external user in the contoso.com resource tenant and assigned access to the application through an access package. Pass-through authentication, Privileged Identity Management, and Identity Protection do not provide external-user onboarding and application access governance.\n\n**Learn more:** [Govern access for external users in entitlement management](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/id-governance/entitlement-management-external-users) · [Onboard external users to line of business applications using Microsoft Entra B2B](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/architecture/11-onboard-external-user)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Enable Azure AD pass-through authentication and update the sign-in endpoint.","ko":"Enable Azure AD pass-through authentication and update the sign-in endpoint."},{"label":"B","en":"Use Azure AD entitlement management to govern external users.","ko":"Use Azure AD entitlement management to govern external users."},{"label":"C","en":"Configure assignments for the fabrikam.com users by using Azure AD Privileged Identity Management (PIM).","ko":"Configure assignments for the fabrikam.com users by using Azure AD Privileged Identity Management (PIM)."},{"label":"D","en":"Configure Azure AD Identity Protection.","ko":"Configure Azure AD Identity Protection."}],"answers":["B"]},{"n":224,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design data storage solutions","topicKo":"데이터 저장소 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You have an Azure subscription.\n\nYour on-premises network includes a file server named Server1. Server1 holds 5 ׀¢׀’ of company files that are rarely accessed.\n\nYou plan to copy the files to Azure Storage.\n\nYou need to implement a storage solution for these files that meets the following requirements:\n\n- The files must be available within 24 hours after they are requested.\n- Storage costs must be minimized.\n\nWhich two possible storage solutions meet this goal? Each correct answer provides a complete solution.\n\nNOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.","stemKo":"You have an Azure subscription.\n\nYour on-premises network includes a file server named Server1. Server1 holds 5 ׀¢׀’ of company files that are rarely accessed.\n\nYou plan to copy the files to Azure Storage.\n\nYou need to implement a storage solution for these files that meets the following requirements:\n\n- The files must be available within 24 hours after they are requested.\n- Storage costs must be minimized.\n\nWhich two possible storage solutions meet this goal? Each correct answer provides a complete solution.\n\nNOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.","explanationEn":"The Archive access tier is the lowest-cost tier for blob data that is rarely accessed. An archived blob can be rehydrated to an online tier in up to 15 hours, which meets a 24-hour availability requirement. Both Blob Storage accounts and general-purpose v2 accounts support explicitly setting eligible blobs to the Archive tier; the account’s Hot or Cool default tier applies only when a blob does not have an explicitly assigned tier.\n\n**Learn more:** [Access tiers for blob data - Azure Storage](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/blobs/access-tiers-overview) · [Archive a blob - Azure Storage](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/blobs/archive-blob)","explanationKo":"The Archive access tier is the lowest-cost tier for blob data that is rarely accessed. An archived blob can be rehydrated to an online tier in up to 15 hours, which meets a 24-hour availability requirement. Both Blob Storage accounts and general-purpose v2 accounts support explicitly setting eligible blobs to the Archive tier; the account’s Hot or Cool default tier applies only when a blob does not have an explicitly assigned tier.\n\n**Learn more:** [Access tiers for blob data - Azure Storage](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/blobs/access-tiers-overview) · [Archive a blob - Azure Storage](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/blobs/archive-blob)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Create an Azure Blob Storage account that is configured for the Cool default access tier. Create a blob container, copy the files to the blob container, and set each file to the Archive access tier.","ko":"Create an Azure Blob Storage account that is configured for the Cool default access tier. Create a blob container, copy the files to the blob container, and set each file to the Archive access tier."},{"label":"B","en":"Create a general-purpose v1 storage account. Create a blob container and copy the files to the blob container.","ko":"Create a general-purpose v1 storage account. Create a blob container and copy the files to the blob container."},{"label":"C","en":"Create a general-purpose v2 storage account that is configured for the Cool default access tier. Create a file share in the storage account and copy the files to the file share.","ko":"Create a general-purpose v2 storage account that is configured for the Cool default access tier. Create a file share in the storage account and copy the files to the file share."},{"label":"D","en":"Create a general-purpose v2 storage account that is configured for the Hot default access tier. Create a blob container, copy the files to the blob container, and set each file to the Archive access tier.","ko":"Create a general-purpose v2 storage account that is configured for the Hot default access tier. Create a blob container, copy the files to the blob container, and set each file to the Archive access tier."},{"label":"E","en":"Create a general-purpose v1 storage account. Create a fie share in the storage account and copy the files to the file share.","ko":"Create a general-purpose v1 storage account. Create a fie share in the storage account and copy the files to the file share."}],"answers":["AD"]},{"n":225,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design business continuity solutions","topicKo":"업무 연속성 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You need to design a highly available Azure SQL database that satisfies these requirements:\n\n- Failover between database replicas must take place with no data loss.\n- The database must stay available if a zone outage occurs.\n- Costs must be minimized.\n\nWhich deployment option should you use?","stemKo":"You need to design a highly available Azure SQL database that satisfies these requirements:\n\n- Failover between database replicas must take place with no data loss.\n- The database must stay available if a zone outage occurs.\n- Costs must be minimized.\n\nWhich deployment option should you use?","explanationEn":"Azure SQL Database Business Critical supports zone redundancy, distributing its existing synchronous replicas across availability zones. This provides zero expected loss of committed data during a zone failure and keeps the database available through automatic failover. Unlike General Purpose zone redundancy, enabling zone redundancy in the Business Critical tier has no additional charge; Basic and Standard tiers do not support zone redundancy.\n\n**Learn more:** [Reliability in Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/reliability/reliability-sql-database)","explanationKo":"Azure SQL Database Business Critical supports zone redundancy, distributing its existing synchronous replicas across availability zones. This provides zero expected loss of committed data during a zone failure and keeps the database available through automatic failover. Unlike General Purpose zone redundancy, enabling zone redundancy in the Business Critical tier has no additional charge; Basic and Standard tiers do not support zone redundancy.\n\n**Learn more:** [Reliability in Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/reliability/reliability-sql-database)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Azure SQL Database Basic","ko":"Azure SQL Database Basic"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure SQL Database Business Critical","ko":"Azure SQL Database Business Critical"},{"label":"C","en":"Azure SQL Database Standard","ko":"Azure SQL Database Standard"},{"label":"D","en":"Azure SQL Managed Instance General Purpose","ko":"Azure SQL Managed Instance General Purpose"}],"answers":["B"]},{"n":226,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design data storage solutions","topicKo":"데이터 저장소 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You need to design a highly available Azure SQL database that satisfies these requirements:\n\n- Failover between database replicas must occur with no data loss.\n- The database must stay available if a zone outage occurs.\n- Costs must be minimized.\n\nWhich deployment option should you use?","stemKo":"You need to design a highly available Azure SQL database that satisfies these requirements:\n\n- Failover between database replicas must occur with no data loss.\n- The database must stay available if a zone outage occurs.\n- Costs must be minimized.\n\nWhich deployment option should you use?","explanationEn":"Azure SQL Database Business Critical supports zone-redundant replicas across availability zones. A zone failure can fail over to a fully synchronized replica with no loss of committed data. In the Business Critical tier, zone redundancy uses existing replicas and incurs no extra charge for enabling it, making it more cost-effective than a Business Critical managed instance for these requirements.\n\n**Learn more:** [Reliability in Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/reliability/reliability-sql-database) · [Availability through local and zone redundancy - Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/database/high-availability-sla-local-zone-redundancy?view=azuresql-db)","explanationKo":"Azure SQL Database Business Critical supports zone-redundant replicas across availability zones. A zone failure can fail over to a fully synchronized replica with no loss of committed data. In the Business Critical tier, zone redundancy uses existing replicas and incurs no extra charge for enabling it, making it more cost-effective than a Business Critical managed instance for these requirements.\n\n**Learn more:** [Reliability in Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/reliability/reliability-sql-database) · [Availability through local and zone redundancy - Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/database/high-availability-sla-local-zone-redundancy?view=azuresql-db)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Azure SQL Managed Instance Business Critical","ko":"Azure SQL Managed Instance Business Critical"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure SQL Database Business Critical","ko":"Azure SQL Database Business Critical"},{"label":"C","en":"Azure SQL Database Basic","ko":"Azure SQL Database Basic"},{"label":"D","en":"Azure SQL Database Standard","ko":"Azure SQL Database Standard"}],"answers":["B"]},{"n":227,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"Contoso, Ltd. implements several Azure logic apps with HTTP triggers. The logic apps provide access to an on-premises web service.\n\nContoso establishes a partnership with Fabrikam, Inc. Fabrikam has no existing Azure Active Directory (Azure AD) tenant and uses third-party OAuth 2.0 identity management to authenticate its users.\n\nFabrikam developers plan to use a subset of the logic apps to build applications that integrate with Contoso's on-premises web service.\n\nYou need to design a solution that gives the Fabrikam developers access to the logic apps. The solution must meet these requirements:\n\n- Requests to the logic apps from the developers must be limited to lower rates than requests from Contoso users.\n- The developers must be able to use their existing OAuth 2.0 provider to access the logic apps.\n- The solution must **NOT** require changes to the logic apps.\n- The solution must **NOT** use Azure AD guest accounts.\n\nWhat should you include in the solution?","stemKo":"Contoso, Ltd. implements several Azure logic apps with HTTP triggers. The logic apps provide access to an on-premises web service.\n\nContoso establishes a partnership with Fabrikam, Inc. Fabrikam has no existing Azure Active Directory (Azure AD) tenant and uses third-party OAuth 2.0 identity management to authenticate its users.\n\nFabrikam developers plan to use a subset of the logic apps to build applications that integrate with Contoso's on-premises web service.\n\nYou need to design a solution that gives the Fabrikam developers access to the logic apps. The solution must meet these requirements:\n\n- Requests to the logic apps from the developers must be limited to lower rates than requests from Contoso users.\n- The developers must be able to use their existing OAuth 2.0 provider to access the logic apps.\n- The solution must **NOT** require changes to the logic apps.\n- The solution must **NOT** use Azure AD guest accounts.\n\nWhat should you include in the solution?","explanationEn":"Azure API Management can front the HTTP-triggered logic apps without changing their implementation. Its rate-limit policies can enforce a lower request rate for Fabrikam callers, and its `validate-jwt` policy can validate JWTs from a supported third-party OAuth 2.0/OpenID Connect identity provider. This avoids requiring Microsoft Entra ID guest accounts.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure API Management rate-limit policy](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/api-management/rate-limit-policy) · [Azure API Management validate-jwt policy](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/api-management/validate-jwt-policy)","explanationKo":"Azure API Management can front the HTTP-triggered logic apps without changing their implementation. Its rate-limit policies can enforce a lower request rate for Fabrikam callers, and its `validate-jwt` policy can validate JWTs from a supported third-party OAuth 2.0/OpenID Connect identity provider. This avoids requiring Microsoft Entra ID guest accounts.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure API Management rate-limit policy](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/api-management/rate-limit-policy) · [Azure API Management validate-jwt policy](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/api-management/validate-jwt-policy)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Azure Front Door","ko":"Azure Front Door"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure AD Application Proxy","ko":"Azure AD Application Proxy"},{"label":"C","en":"Azure AD business-to-business (B2B)","ko":"Azure AD business-to-business (B2B)"},{"label":"D","en":"Azure API Management","ko":"Azure API Management"}],"answers":["D"]},{"n":228,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design infrastructure solutions","topicKo":"인프라 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You have an Azure subscription that includes an Azure Cosmos DB for NoSQL account named account1 and an Azure Synapse Analytics workspace named Workspace1. The account1 account has a container named Contained with the analytical store enabled.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that processes the data stored in Contained in near-real-time (NRT) and writes the results to a data warehouse in Workspace1 by using a runtime engine in the workspace. The solution must minimize data movement.\n\nWhich pool in Workspace1 should you use?","stemKo":"You have an Azure subscription that includes an Azure Cosmos DB for NoSQL account named account1 and an Azure Synapse Analytics workspace named Workspace1. The account1 account has a container named Contained with the analytical store enabled.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that processes the data stored in Contained in near-real-time (NRT) and writes the results to a data warehouse in Workspace1 by using a runtime engine in the workspace. The solution must minimize data movement.\n\nWhich pool in Workspace1 should you use?","explanationEn":"Apache Spark directly reads the Azure Cosmos DB analytical store for near-real-time analysis, performs transformations and aggregations in Spark, and loads the resulting data into a dedicated SQL pool data warehouse. This uses the analytical-store integration rather than first copying the source data through an intermediate store.\n\n**Learn more:** [Copy data from Azure Cosmos DB into a dedicated SQL pool using Apache Spark](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/synapse-analytics/synapse-link/how-to-copy-to-sql-pool) · [Interact with Azure Cosmos DB using Apache Spark 3 in Azure Synapse Link](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/synapse-analytics/synapse-link/how-to-query-analytical-store-spark-3)","explanationKo":"Apache Spark directly reads the Azure Cosmos DB analytical store for near-real-time analysis, performs transformations and aggregations in Spark, and loads the resulting data into a dedicated SQL pool data warehouse. This uses the analytical-store integration rather than first copying the source data through an intermediate store.\n\n**Learn more:** [Copy data from Azure Cosmos DB into a dedicated SQL pool using Apache Spark](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/synapse-analytics/synapse-link/how-to-copy-to-sql-pool) · [Interact with Azure Cosmos DB using Apache Spark 3 in Azure Synapse Link](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/synapse-analytics/synapse-link/how-to-query-analytical-store-spark-3)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Apache Spark","ko":"Apache Spark"},{"label":"B","en":"serverless SQL","ko":"serverless SQL"},{"label":"C","en":"dedicated SQL","ko":"dedicated SQL"},{"label":"D","en":"Data Explorer","ko":"Data Explorer"}],"answers":["A"]},{"n":229,"id":null,"type":"drag_drop","topic":"Design infrastructure solutions","topicKo":"인프라 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"Your company has an existing web app running on Azure virtual machines.\n\nYou must ensure that the app is protected from SQL injection attempts and uses a Layer 7 load balancer. The solution must minimize disruptions to the app's code.\n\nWhat should you recommend? Each service may be used once, more than once, or not at all.","stemKo":"Your company has an existing web app running on Azure virtual machines.\n\nYou must ensure that the app is protected from SQL injection attempts and uses a Layer 7 load balancer. The solution must minimize disruptions to the app's code.\n\nWhat should you recommend? Each service may be used once, more than once, or not at all.","explanationEn":"Azure Application Gateway is a Layer 7 load balancer. Its Web Application Firewall (WAF) feature provides centralized protection against common web exploits, including SQL injection, without requiring application-code changes.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure Application Gateway overview](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/application-gateway/overview) · [What is Azure Web Application Firewall on Azure Application Gateway?](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/web-application-firewall/ag/ag-overview)","explanationKo":"Azure Application Gateway is a Layer 7 load balancer. Its Web Application Firewall (WAF) feature provides centralized protection against common web exploits, including SQL injection, without requiring application-code changes.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure Application Gateway overview](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/application-gateway/overview) · [What is Azure Web Application Firewall on Azure Application Gateway?](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/web-application-firewall/ag/ag-overview)","learnMore":[],"items":[{"en":"Web Application Firewall (WAF)","ko":"Web Application Firewall (WAF)"},{"en":"Azure Application Gateway","ko":"Azure Application Gateway"},{"en":"Azure Load Balancer","ko":"Azure Load Balancer"},{"en":"Azure Traffic Manager","ko":"Azure Traffic Manager"},{"en":"SSL offloading","ko":"SSL offloading"},{"en":"URL-based content routing","ko":"URL-based content routing"}],"slots":[{"id":"azure_service","labelEn":"Azure service:","labelKo":"Azure service:","answer":"Azure Application Gateway"},{"id":"feature","labelEn":"Feature:","labelKo":"Feature:","answer":"Web Application Firewall (WAF)"}],"reuse":true},{"n":230,"id":null,"type":"dropdown","topic":"Design infrastructure solutions","topicKo":"인프라 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You have an Azure subscription.\n\nYou are designing a solution for containerized apps. The solution must meet these requirements:\n\n- Automatically scale the apps by creating additional instances.\n- Minimize administrative effort required to maintain nodes and clusters.\n- Ensure that containerized apps are highly available across multiple availability zones.\n- Provide a central location for lifecycle management and storage of container images.\n\nWhat should the solution include?","stemKo":"You have an Azure subscription.\n\nYou are designing a solution for containerized apps. The solution must meet these requirements:\n\n- Automatically scale the apps by creating additional instances.\n- Minimize administrative effort required to maintain nodes and clusters.\n- Ensure that containerized apps are highly available across multiple availability zones.\n- Provide a central location for lifecycle management and storage of container images.\n\nWhat should the solution include?","explanationEn":"Azure Container Apps is a fully managed platform for containerized applications that supports automatic scaling while avoiding direct node and cluster management; it can be deployed with zone redundancy for high availability. Azure Container Registry centrally stores container images and provides image lifecycle capabilities.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure Container Apps overview](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/container-apps/overview) · [Azure Container Registry documentation](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/container-registry/)","explanationKo":"Azure Container Apps is a fully managed platform for containerized applications that supports automatic scaling while avoiding direct node and cluster management; it can be deployed with zone redundancy for high availability. Azure Container Registry centrally stores container images and provides image lifecycle capabilities.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure Container Apps overview](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/container-apps/overview) · [Azure Container Registry documentation](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/container-registry/)","learnMore":[],"blanks":[{"id":"run_apps","labelEn":"To run the containerized apps:","labelKo":"To run the containerized apps:","options":[{"en":"Azure Container Apps","ko":"Azure Container Apps"},{"en":"Azure Container Instances","ko":"Azure Container Instances"},{"en":"Azure Container Registry","ko":"Azure Container Registry"},{"en":"Azure Kubernetes Service (AKS)","ko":"Azure Kubernetes Service (AKS)"}],"answer":"Azure Container Apps"},{"id":"image_lifecycle","labelEn":"For the lifecycle management and storage of container images:","labelKo":"For the lifecycle management and storage of container images:","options":[{"en":"Azure Container Apps","ko":"Azure Container Apps"},{"en":"Azure Container Instances","ko":"Azure Container Instances"},{"en":"Azure Container Registry","ko":"Azure Container Registry"},{"en":"Azure Service Fabric","ko":"Azure Service Fabric"}],"answer":"Azure Container Registry"}],"template":""},{"n":231,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design data storage solutions","topicKo":"데이터 저장소 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You have an on-premises Microsoft SQL Server 2008 instance that hosts a 50-GB database.\n\nYou need to migrate the database to an Azure SQL Managed Instance. The solution must minimize downtime.\n\nWhat should you use?","stemKo":"You have an on-premises Microsoft SQL Server 2008 instance that hosts a 50-GB database.\n\nYou need to migrate the database to an Azure SQL Managed Instance. The solution must minimize downtime.\n\nWhat should you use?","explanationEn":"Azure Data Studio supports the Azure SQL migration workflow for moving SQL Server databases to Azure SQL Managed Instance. Its online migration capability uses continuous data synchronization during migration, so downtime is limited to the final cutover rather than the full transfer of the 50-GB database.\n\n**Learn more:** [Migration overview: SQL Server to Azure SQL Managed Instance](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/data-migration/sql-server/managed-instance/overview)","explanationKo":"Azure Data Studio supports the Azure SQL migration workflow for moving SQL Server databases to Azure SQL Managed Instance. Its online migration capability uses continuous data synchronization during migration, so downtime is limited to the final cutover rather than the full transfer of the 50-GB database.\n\n**Learn more:** [Migration overview: SQL Server to Azure SQL Managed Instance](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/data-migration/sql-server/managed-instance/overview)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Azure Migrate","ko":"Azure Migrate"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure Data Studio","ko":"Azure Data Studio"},{"label":"C","en":"WANdisco LiveData Platform for Azure","ko":"WANdisco LiveData Platform for Azure"},{"label":"D","en":"SQL Server Management Studio (SSMS)","ko":"SQL Server Management Studio (SSMS)"}],"answers":["B"]},{"n":232,"id":null,"type":"dropdown","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"Your on-premises network contains an Active Directory Domain Services (AD DS) domain. The domain includes Server1, which hosts App1 using AD DS authentication. Remote users access App1 through a VPN connection to the on-premises network.\n\nYou have an Azure AD tenant that synchronizes with the AD DS domain by using Azure AD Connect.\n\nYou need to enable remote users to access App1 without using a VPN. The solution must meet the following requirements:\n\n- Ensure users authenticate by using Azure Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA).\n- Minimize administrative effort.\n\nWhat should you include in the solution?","stemKo":"Your on-premises network contains an Active Directory Domain Services (AD DS) domain. The domain includes Server1, which hosts App1 using AD DS authentication. Remote users access App1 through a VPN connection to the on-premises network.\n\nYou have an Azure AD tenant that synchronizes with the AD DS domain by using Azure AD Connect.\n\nYou need to enable remote users to access App1 without using a VPN. The solution must meet the following requirements:\n\n- Ensure users authenticate by using Azure Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA).\n- Minimize administrative effort.\n\nWhat should you include in the solution?","explanationEn":"Microsoft Entra Application Proxy securely publishes on-premises web applications for remote access. The published application is an enterprise application, and its connector is a lightweight agent installed on a Windows Server in the private network. Azure AD preauthentication supports Conditional Access and MFA before requests reach the on-premises application, avoiding VPN access and minimizing infrastructure administration.\n\n**Learn more:** [Microsoft Entra application proxy](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity/app-proxy/overview-what-is-app-proxy) · [Microsoft Entra Private Network Connectors](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/global-secure-access/concept-connectors)","explanationKo":"Microsoft Entra Application Proxy securely publishes on-premises web applications for remote access. The published application is an enterprise application, and its connector is a lightweight agent installed on a Windows Server in the private network. Azure AD preauthentication supports Conditional Access and MFA before requests reach the on-premises application, avoiding VPN access and minimizing infrastructure administration.\n\n**Learn more:** [Microsoft Entra application proxy](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity/app-proxy/overview-what-is-app-proxy) · [Microsoft Entra Private Network Connectors](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/global-secure-access/concept-connectors)","learnMore":[],"blanks":[{"id":"azure_ad","labelEn":"In Azure AD:","labelKo":"In Azure AD:","options":[{"en":"A managed identity","ko":"A managed identity"},{"en":"An access package","ko":"An access package"},{"en":"An app registration","ko":"An app registration"},{"en":"An enterprise application","ko":"An enterprise application"}],"answer":"An enterprise application"},{"id":"on_premises","labelEn":"On-premises:","labelKo":"On-premises:","options":[{"en":"A server that runs Windows Server and has the Azure AD Application Proxy connector installed","ko":"A server that runs Windows Server and has the Azure AD Application Proxy connector installed"},{"en":"A server that runs Windows Server and has the on-premises data gateway (standard mode) installed","ko":"A server that runs Windows Server and has the on-premises data gateway (standard mode) installed"},{"en":"A server that runs Windows Server and has the Web Application Proxy role service installed","ko":"A server that runs Windows Server and has the Web Application Proxy role service installed"}],"answer":"A server that runs Windows Server and has the Azure AD Application Proxy connector installed"}],"template":""},{"n":233,"id":null,"type":"drag_drop","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"Your on-premises network has a server named Server1 that hosts an ASP.NET application named App1.\n\nYou use a hybrid Azure Active Directory (Azure AD) deployment.\n\nRecommend a solution that ensures users authenticate with their Azure AD account and Azure Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA) when connecting to App1 from the internet.\n\nWhich three features should be deployed and configured, in order?","stemKo":"Your on-premises network has a server named Server1 that hosts an ASP.NET application named App1.\n\nYou use a hybrid Azure Active Directory (Azure AD) deployment.\n\nRecommend a solution that ensures users authenticate with their Azure AD account and Azure Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA) when connecting to App1 from the internet.\n\nWhich three features should be deployed and configured, in order?","explanationEn":"Azure AD Application Proxy securely publishes the on-premises web application and supports Azure AD preauthentication. Publishing creates/configures the application’s enterprise application (service principal), which is the target for Conditional Access. A Conditional Access policy can then require Azure MFA for users accessing that enterprise application.\n\n**Learn more:** [Microsoft Entra application proxy overview](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity/app-proxy/overview-what-is-app-proxy) · [Microsoft Entra Conditional Access: Cloud apps, actions, and authentication context](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity/conditional-access/concept-conditional-access-cloud-apps)","explanationKo":"Azure AD Application Proxy securely publishes the on-premises web application and supports Azure AD preauthentication. Publishing creates/configures the application’s enterprise application (service principal), which is the target for Conditional Access. A Conditional Access policy can then require Azure MFA for users accessing that enterprise application.\n\n**Learn more:** [Microsoft Entra application proxy overview](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity/app-proxy/overview-what-is-app-proxy) · [Microsoft Entra Conditional Access: Cloud apps, actions, and authentication context](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity/conditional-access/concept-conditional-access-cloud-apps)","learnMore":[],"items":[{"en":"a public Azure Load Balancer","ko":"a public Azure Load Balancer"},{"en":"a managed identity","ko":"a managed identity"},{"en":"an internal Azure Load Balancer","ko":"an internal Azure Load Balancer"},{"en":"a Conditional Access policy","ko":"a Conditional Access policy"},{"en":"an Azure App Service plan","ko":"an Azure App Service plan"},{"en":"Azure AD Application Proxy","ko":"Azure AD Application Proxy"},{"en":"an Azure AD enterprise application","ko":"an Azure AD enterprise application"}],"slots":[{"id":"step1","labelEn":"항목 step1","labelKo":"항목 step1","answer":"Azure AD Application Proxy"},{"id":"step2","labelEn":"항목 step2","labelKo":"항목 step2","answer":"an Azure AD enterprise application"},{"id":"step3","labelEn":"항목 step3","labelKo":"항목 step3","answer":"a Conditional Access policy"}],"reuse":false},{"n":234,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You have an Azure Active Directory (Azure AD) tenant named contoso.com that contains a security group named Group1. Group1 is configured for assigned membership. Group1 has 50 members, including 20 guest users.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution to evaluate Group1 membership. The solution must meet these requirements:\n\n- The evaluation must automatically recur every three months.\n- Every member must be able to state whether they need to remain in Group1.\n- Users who state that they do not need to be in Group1 must be removed from Group1 automatically.\n- Users who do not state whether they need to be in Group1 must be removed from Group1 automatically.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","stemKo":"You have an Azure Active Directory (Azure AD) tenant named contoso.com that contains a security group named Group1. Group1 is configured for assigned membership. Group1 has 50 members, including 20 guest users.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution to evaluate Group1 membership. The solution must meet these requirements:\n\n- The evaluation must automatically recur every three months.\n- Every member must be able to state whether they need to remain in Group1.\n- Users who state that they do not need to be in Group1 must be removed from Group1 automatically.\n- Users who do not state whether they need to be in Group1 must be removed from Group1 automatically.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","explanationEn":"Microsoft Entra access reviews support recurring reviews of group membership, self-review by group members, automatic application of denied decisions, and automatic removal of access for reviewers who do not respond when that outcome is configured.\n\n**Learn more:** [Create an access review of groups and applications](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/id-governance/create-access-review) · [Plan a Microsoft Entra access reviews deployment](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/id-governance/deploy-access-reviews)","explanationKo":"Microsoft Entra access reviews support recurring reviews of group membership, self-review by group members, automatic application of denied decisions, and automatic removal of access for reviewers who do not respond when that outcome is configured.\n\n**Learn more:** [Create an access review of groups and applications](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/id-governance/create-access-review) · [Plan a Microsoft Entra access reviews deployment](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/id-governance/deploy-access-reviews)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Implement Azure AD Identity Protection.","ko":"Implement Azure AD Identity Protection."},{"label":"B","en":"Change the Membership type of Group1 to Dynamic User.","ko":"Change the Membership type of Group1 to Dynamic User."},{"label":"C","en":"Create an access review.","ko":"Create an access review."},{"label":"D","en":"Implement Azure AD Privileged Identity Management (PIM).","ko":"Implement Azure AD Privileged Identity Management (PIM)."}],"answers":["C"]},{"n":235,"id":null,"type":"dropdown","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"To meet Fabrikam's authentication requirements, what should you include in the solution?","stemKo":"To meet Fabrikam's authentication requirements, what should you include in the solution?","explanationEn":"A single Entra tenant can host the required hybrid identities, and corp.fabrikam.com must be added and verified to use that UPN suffix. One Conditional Access policy requires MFA for Azure portal administrative access; a separate policy blocks access from outside the company, since a block control cannot be combined with an MFA grant requirement in the same policy.\n\n**Learn more:** [Manage custom domain names in Microsoft Entra ID](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity/users/domains-manage) · [Conditional Access policy components](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity/conditional-access/concept-conditional-access-policies)","explanationKo":"A single Entra tenant can host the required hybrid identities, and corp.fabrikam.com must be added and verified to use that UPN suffix. One Conditional Access policy requires MFA for Azure portal administrative access; a separate policy blocks access from outside the company, since a block control cannot be combined with an MFA grant requirement in the same policy.\n\n**Learn more:** [Manage custom domain names in Microsoft Entra ID](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity/users/domains-manage) · [Conditional Access policy components](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity/conditional-access/concept-conditional-access-policies)","learnMore":[],"blanks":[{"id":"azure_ad_tenants","labelEn":"Minimum number of Azure AD tenants:","labelKo":"Minimum number of Azure AD tenants:","options":[{"en":"0","ko":"0"},{"en":"1","ko":"1"},{"en":"2","ko":"2"},{"en":"3","ko":"3"},{"en":"4","ko":"4"}],"answer":"1"},{"id":"custom_domains","labelEn":"Minimum number of custom domains to add:","labelKo":"Minimum number of custom domains to add:","options":[{"en":"0","ko":"0"},{"en":"1","ko":"1"},{"en":"2","ko":"2"},{"en":"3","ko":"3"},{"en":"4","ko":"4"}],"answer":"1"},{"id":"conditional_access_policies","labelEn":"Minimum number of conditional access policies to create:","labelKo":"Minimum number of conditional access policies to create:","options":[{"en":"0","ko":"0"},{"en":"1","ko":"1"},{"en":"2","ko":"2"},{"en":"3","ko":"3"},{"en":"4","ko":"4"}],"answer":"2"}],"template":""},{"n":236,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You have an Azure AD tenant named contoso.com that contains a security group named Group1. Group1 is configured with assigned memberships and has 50 members, including 20 guest users.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution to evaluate Group1 membership. The solution must meet these requirements:\n\n- The evaluation must recur automatically every three months.\n- Each member must be able to indicate whether they still need to belong to Group1.\n- Members who indicate that they no longer need to be in Group1 must be removed automatically.\n- Members who do not indicate whether they still need to be in Group1 must be removed automatically.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","stemKo":"You have an Azure AD tenant named contoso.com that contains a security group named Group1. Group1 is configured with assigned memberships and has 50 members, including 20 guest users.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution to evaluate Group1 membership. The solution must meet these requirements:\n\n- The evaluation must recur automatically every three months.\n- Each member must be able to indicate whether they still need to belong to Group1.\n- Members who indicate that they no longer need to be in Group1 must be removed automatically.\n- Members who do not indicate whether they still need to be in Group1 must be removed automatically.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","explanationEn":"Microsoft Entra access reviews support recurring quarterly reviews of security-group members and self-review by each member. With automatic application of results enabled, denied membership is removed automatically; setting nonresponses to remove access also removes members who do not respond.\n\n**Learn more:** [What are access reviews? - Microsoft Entra](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/id-governance/access-reviews-overview) · [Create an access review of groups and applications](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/id-governance/create-access-review)","explanationKo":"Microsoft Entra access reviews support recurring quarterly reviews of security-group members and self-review by each member. With automatic application of results enabled, denied membership is removed automatically; setting nonresponses to remove access also removes members who do not respond.\n\n**Learn more:** [What are access reviews? - Microsoft Entra](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/id-governance/access-reviews-overview) · [Create an access review of groups and applications](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/id-governance/create-access-review)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Implement Azure AD Identity Protection.","ko":"Implement Azure AD Identity Protection."},{"label":"B","en":"Change the Membership type of Group1 to Dynamic User.","ko":"Change the Membership type of Group1 to Dynamic User."},{"label":"C","en":"Create an access review.","ko":"Create an access review."},{"label":"D","en":"Implement Azure AD Privileged Identity Management (PIM).","ko":"Implement Azure AD Privileged Identity Management (PIM)."}],"answers":["C"]},{"n":237,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design infrastructure solutions","topicKo":"인프라 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You have an app named App1 that uses two on-premises Microsoft SQL Server databases named DB1 and DB2.\n\nYou plan to migrate DB1 and DB2 to Azure.\n\nYou need to recommend an Azure solution to host DB1 and DB2. The solution must meet these requirements:\n\n- Support server-side transactions across DB1 and DB2.\n- Minimize the administrative effort required to update the solution.\n\nWhat should you recommend?","stemKo":"You have an app named App1 that uses two on-premises Microsoft SQL Server databases named DB1 and DB2.\n\nYou plan to migrate DB1 and DB2 to Azure.\n\nYou need to recommend an Azure solution to host DB1 and DB2. The solution must meet these requirements:\n\n- Support server-side transactions across DB1 and DB2.\n- Minimize the administrative effort required to update the solution.\n\nWhat should you recommend?","explanationEn":"Azure SQL Managed Instance supports server-side distributed transactions written in Transact-SQL across databases. As a managed PaaS service, it also reduces operating-system and SQL Server update administration compared with SQL Server hosted on an Azure virtual machine.\n\n**Learn more:** [Distributed transactions across cloud databases](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/database/elastic-transactions-overview?view=azuresql) · [Distributed Transaction Coordinator (DTC) for Azure SQL Managed Instance](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/managed-instance/distributed-transaction-coordinator-dtc?view=azuresql)","explanationKo":"Azure SQL Managed Instance supports server-side distributed transactions written in Transact-SQL across databases. As a managed PaaS service, it also reduces operating-system and SQL Server update administration compared with SQL Server hosted on an Azure virtual machine.\n\n**Learn more:** [Distributed transactions across cloud databases](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/database/elastic-transactions-overview?view=azuresql) · [Distributed Transaction Coordinator (DTC) for Azure SQL Managed Instance](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/managed-instance/distributed-transaction-coordinator-dtc?view=azuresql)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"two Azure SQL databases in an elastic pool","ko":"two Azure SQL databases in an elastic pool"},{"label":"B","en":"two databases on the same Azure SQL managed instance","ko":"two databases on the same Azure SQL managed instance"},{"label":"C","en":"two databases on the same SQL Server instance on an Azure virtual machine","ko":"two databases on the same SQL Server instance on an Azure virtual machine"},{"label":"D","en":"two Azure SQL databases on different Azure SQL Database servers","ko":"two Azure SQL databases on different Azure SQL Database servers"}],"answers":["B"]},{"n":238,"id":null,"type":"dropdown","topic":"Design data storage solutions","topicKo":"데이터 저장소 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"Your on-premises datacenter contains Server1, which runs Microsoft SQL Server 2022. Server1 hosts a 30-TB customer-data database named DB1. It also runs App1, a custom application that validates DB1 record compliance. App1 must run on the same server as DB1.\n\nYou have an Azure subscription.\n\nYou need to migrate DB1 to Azure while minimizing administrative effort.\n\nChoose the service for DB1 and the migration tool.","stemKo":"Your on-premises datacenter contains Server1, which runs Microsoft SQL Server 2022. Server1 hosts a 30-TB customer-data database named DB1. It also runs App1, a custom application that validates DB1 record compliance. App1 must run on the same server as DB1.\n\nYou have an Azure subscription.\n\nYou need to migrate DB1 to Azure while minimizing administrative effort.\n\nChoose the service for DB1 and the migration tool.","explanationEn":"SQL Server on Azure Virtual Machines allows the custom application and SQL Server database to be co-hosted on the same server. Azure Database Migration Service provides a managed workflow for migrating on-premises SQL Server databases to SQL Server on Azure virtual machines.\n\n**Learn more:** [Tutorial: Migrate SQL Server to SQL Server on an Azure Virtual Machine with Azure DMS (online)](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/data-migration/sql-server/virtual-machines/database-migration-service-online) · [Azure Database Migration Service documentation](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/dms/)","explanationKo":"SQL Server on Azure Virtual Machines allows the custom application and SQL Server database to be co-hosted on the same server. Azure Database Migration Service provides a managed workflow for migrating on-premises SQL Server databases to SQL Server on Azure virtual machines.\n\n**Learn more:** [Tutorial: Migrate SQL Server to SQL Server on an Azure Virtual Machine with Azure DMS (online)](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/data-migration/sql-server/virtual-machines/database-migration-service-online) · [Azure Database Migration Service documentation](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/dms/)","learnMore":[],"blanks":[{"id":"migrate_to","labelEn":"Migrate to:","labelKo":"Migrate to:","options":[{"en":"Azure SQL Database","ko":"Azure SQL Database"},{"en":"Azure SQL Managed Instance","ko":"Azure SQL Managed Instance"},{"en":"SQL Server on Azure Virtual Machines","ko":"SQL Server on Azure Virtual Machines"}],"answer":"SQL Server on Azure Virtual Machines"},{"id":"by_using","labelEn":"By using:","labelKo":"By using:","options":[{"en":"Azure Database Migration Service","ko":"Azure Database Migration Service"},{"en":"Azure Migrate","ko":"Azure Migrate"},{"en":"The Azure SQL Migration extension for Azure Data Studio","ko":"The Azure SQL Migration extension for Azure Data Studio"}],"answer":"Azure Database Migration Service"}],"template":""},{"n":239,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design infrastructure solutions","topicKo":"인프라 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"Solution: An Azure virtual machine scale set that uses autoscaling is deployed.\n\nDoes this satisfy the goal?","stemKo":"Solution: An Azure virtual machine scale set that uses autoscaling is deployed.\n\nDoes this satisfy the goal?","explanationEn":"Autoscaling a Virtual Machine Scale Set adjusts instance capacity within its deployment region; it does not create a second regional deployment or configure cross-region failover. Therefore, the solution does not provide redundancy when an Azure region fails, even though virtual machines allow operating-system administration and can run the full .NET Framework.\n\n**Learn more:** [Reliability in Azure Virtual Machine Scale Sets](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/reliability/reliability-virtual-machine-scale-sets) · [Azure Virtual Machine Scale Sets overview](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/virtual-machine-scale-sets/overview)","explanationKo":"Autoscaling a Virtual Machine Scale Set adjusts instance capacity within its deployment region; it does not create a second regional deployment or configure cross-region failover. Therefore, the solution does not provide redundancy when an Azure region fails, even though virtual machines allow operating-system administration and can run the full .NET Framework.\n\n**Learn more:** [Reliability in Azure Virtual Machine Scale Sets](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/reliability/reliability-virtual-machine-scale-sets) · [Azure Virtual Machine Scale Sets overview](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/virtual-machine-scale-sets/overview)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Yes","ko":"Yes"},{"label":"B","en":"No","ko":"No"}],"answers":["B"]},{"n":240,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design infrastructure solutions","topicKo":"인프라 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"Solution: You deploy two Azure virtual machines across two Azure regions and deploy an Azure Application Gateway.\n\nDoes this satisfy the goal?","stemKo":"Solution: You deploy two Azure virtual machines across two Azure regions and deploy an Azure Application Gateway.\n\nDoes this satisfy the goal?","explanationEn":"Azure Application Gateway v2 is a single-region service and becomes unavailable if its region fails. Multi-region resilience requires separate gateways in the target regions and a global load-balancing service, such as Azure Traffic Manager or Azure Front Door, to route and fail over traffic between them.\n\n**Learn more:** [Reliability in Azure Application Gateway v2](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/reliability/reliability-application-gateway-v2)","explanationKo":"Azure Application Gateway v2 is a single-region service and becomes unavailable if its region fails. Multi-region resilience requires separate gateways in the target regions and a global load-balancing service, such as Azure Traffic Manager or Azure Front Door, to route and fail over traffic between them.\n\n**Learn more:** [Reliability in Azure Application Gateway v2](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/reliability/reliability-application-gateway-v2)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Yes","ko":"Yes"},{"label":"B","en":"No","ko":"No"}],"answers":["B"]},{"n":241,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design infrastructure solutions","topicKo":"인프라 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"Solution: Deploy two Azure virtual machines in two Azure regions and create an Azure Traffic Manager profile.\n\nDoes this satisfy the goal?","stemKo":"Solution: Deploy two Azure virtual machines in two Azure regions and create an Azure Traffic Manager profile.\n\nDoes this satisfy the goal?","explanationEn":"Azure virtual machines provide control of the guest operating system and can host applications that require the full .NET Framework. With one VM in each of two regions, Azure Traffic Manager can monitor the endpoints and route traffic to the healthy regional instance during a regional outage, providing the required regional redundancy.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure Traffic Manager FAQ](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/traffic-manager/traffic-manager-faqs) · [Quickstart: Create a Traffic Manager profile using the Azure portal](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/traffic-manager/quickstart-create-traffic-manager-profile)","explanationKo":"Azure virtual machines provide control of the guest operating system and can host applications that require the full .NET Framework. With one VM in each of two regions, Azure Traffic Manager can monitor the endpoints and route traffic to the healthy regional instance during a regional outage, providing the required regional redundancy.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure Traffic Manager FAQ](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/traffic-manager/traffic-manager-faqs) · [Quickstart: Create a Traffic Manager profile using the Azure portal](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/traffic-manager/quickstart-create-traffic-manager-profile)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Yes","ko":"Yes"},{"label":"B","en":"No","ko":"No"}],"answers":["A"]},{"n":242,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design infrastructure solutions","topicKo":"인프라 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"Solution: You deploy a web app by using an Isolated App Service plan.\n\nDoes this satisfy the goal?","stemKo":"Solution: You deploy a web app by using an Isolated App Service plan.\n\nDoes this satisfy the goal?","explanationEn":"An Isolated App Service plan is still a managed Azure App Service platform, rather than administrator-controlled operating-system infrastructure. It therefore does not provide administrators with OS access to install custom application dependencies, and a single regional deployment does not provide redundancy against an Azure region failure. A multi-region design on infrastructure with the required operating-system control is needed.\n\n**Learn more:** [What are Azure App Service plans?](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/app-service/overview-hosting-plans) · [Reliability in Azure App Service Environment](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/reliability/reliability-app-service-environment)","explanationKo":"An Isolated App Service plan is still a managed Azure App Service platform, rather than administrator-controlled operating-system infrastructure. It therefore does not provide administrators with OS access to install custom application dependencies, and a single regional deployment does not provide redundancy against an Azure region failure. A multi-region design on infrastructure with the required operating-system control is needed.\n\n**Learn more:** [What are Azure App Service plans?](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/app-service/overview-hosting-plans) · [Reliability in Azure App Service Environment](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/reliability/reliability-app-service-environment)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Yes","ko":"Yes"},{"label":"B","en":"No","ko":"No"}],"answers":["B"]},{"n":243,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design business continuity solutions","topicKo":"업무 연속성 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You must design a highly available Azure SQL database that meets these requirements:\n\n- Failover between database replicas must take place with no data loss.\n- The database must stay available if a zone outage occurs.\n- Costs must be kept to a minimum.\n\nWhich deployment option should you use?","stemKo":"You must design a highly available Azure SQL database that meets these requirements:\n\n- Failover between database replicas must take place with no data loss.\n- The database must stay available if a zone outage occurs.\n- Costs must be kept to a minimum.\n\nWhich deployment option should you use?","explanationEn":"Azure SQL Database Premium supports zone redundancy, distributing synchronous database replicas across availability zones. Synchronous replication preserves committed data during failover, and zone redundancy keeps the database resilient to an availability-zone outage. Azure SQL Database Standard does not support zone redundancy, while a Business Critical managed instance provides capabilities beyond those required at a higher cost.\n\n**Learn more:** [Reliability in Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/reliability/reliability-sql-database)","explanationKo":"Azure SQL Database Premium supports zone redundancy, distributing synchronous database replicas across availability zones. Synchronous replication preserves committed data during failover, and zone redundancy keeps the database resilient to an availability-zone outage. Azure SQL Database Standard does not support zone redundancy, while a Business Critical managed instance provides capabilities beyond those required at a higher cost.\n\n**Learn more:** [Reliability in Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/reliability/reliability-sql-database)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Azure SQL Managed Instance Business Critical","ko":"Azure SQL Managed Instance Business Critical"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure SQL Managed Instance General Purpose","ko":"Azure SQL Managed Instance General Purpose"},{"label":"C","en":"Azure SQL Database Standard","ko":"Azure SQL Database Standard"},{"label":"D","en":"Azure SQL Database Premium","ko":"Azure SQL Database Premium"}],"answers":["D"]},{"n":244,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"Solution: You recommend using an Azure Policy initiative to enforce the location restriction.\n\nDoes this meet the goal?","stemKo":"Solution: You recommend using an Azure Policy initiative to enforce the location restriction.\n\nDoes this meet the goal?","explanationEn":"An Azure Policy initiative can include the built-in **Allowed locations** policy and assign the permitted region values. That policy uses a deny effect to prevent deployment of resources outside the approved locations, enforcing geo-compliance requirements for the App Service instances.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure Policy overview](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/governance/policy/overview) · [Tutorial: Create and manage policies to enforce compliance](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/governance/policy/tutorials/create-and-manage)","explanationKo":"An Azure Policy initiative can include the built-in **Allowed locations** policy and assign the permitted region values. That policy uses a deny effect to prevent deployment of resources outside the approved locations, enforcing geo-compliance requirements for the App Service instances.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure Policy overview](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/governance/policy/overview) · [Tutorial: Create and manage policies to enforce compliance](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/governance/policy/tutorials/create-and-manage)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Yes","ko":"Yes"},{"label":"B","en":"No","ko":"No"}],"answers":["A"]},{"n":245,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"Solution: You recommend creating resource groups based on location and applying resource locks to those resource groups.\n\nDoes this meet the goal?","stemKo":"Solution: You recommend creating resource groups based on location and applying resource locks to those resource groups.\n\nDoes this meet the goal?","explanationEn":"Azure resource locks protect resources from deletion or modification; they do not limit the Azure regions in which resources can be created. Enforcing deployment only to approved regions requires an Azure Policy assignment that restricts allowed locations.\n\n**Learn more:** [Lock your Azure resources to protect your infrastructure](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-resource-manager/management/lock-resources) · [Tutorial: Disallow resource types in your cloud environment](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/governance/policy/tutorials/disallowed-resources)","explanationKo":"Azure resource locks protect resources from deletion or modification; they do not limit the Azure regions in which resources can be created. Enforcing deployment only to approved regions requires an Azure Policy assignment that restricts allowed locations.\n\n**Learn more:** [Lock your Azure resources to protect your infrastructure](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-resource-manager/management/lock-resources) · [Tutorial: Disallow resource types in your cloud environment](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/governance/policy/tutorials/disallowed-resources)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Yes","ko":"Yes"},{"label":"B","en":"No","ko":"No"}],"answers":["B"]},{"n":246,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"Solution: You recommend using the Regulatory compliance dashboard in Microsoft Defender for Cloud.\n\nDoes this satisfy the goal?","stemKo":"Solution: You recommend using the Regulatory compliance dashboard in Microsoft Defender for Cloud.\n\nDoes this satisfy the goal?","explanationEn":"The Regulatory compliance dashboard continuously assesses resources against compliance controls and reports their compliance state, but it does not prevent deployments outside specified regions. Azure Policy can enforce that Azure resources are deployed only to allowed regions.\n\n**Learn more:** [Regulatory compliance standards in Microsoft Defender for Cloud](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-ie/azure/defender-for-cloud/concept-regulatory-compliance-standards) · [What is Azure Policy?](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/governance/policy/overview)","explanationKo":"The Regulatory compliance dashboard continuously assesses resources against compliance controls and reports their compliance state, but it does not prevent deployments outside specified regions. Azure Policy can enforce that Azure resources are deployed only to allowed regions.\n\n**Learn more:** [Regulatory compliance standards in Microsoft Defender for Cloud](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-ie/azure/defender-for-cloud/concept-regulatory-compliance-standards) · [What is Azure Policy?](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/governance/policy/overview)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Yes","ko":"Yes"},{"label":"B","en":"No","ko":"No"}],"answers":["B"]},{"n":247,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"Solution: You recommend using an Azure Policy initiative that enforces the location of resource groups.\n\nDoes this meet the goal?","stemKo":"Solution: You recommend using an Azure Policy initiative that enforces the location of resource groups.\n\nDoes this meet the goal?","explanationEn":"Resource-group location enforcement does not control the deployment locations of the resources contained in those groups. Azure Policy must evaluate and restrict the locations of the App Service resources themselves to enforce approved regions and regional co-location. Microsoft documents that policies enforcing location on resource groups specifically target the `Microsoft.Resources/subscriptions/resourceGroups` resource type, while the built-in **Allowed locations** policy restricts locations for new resources.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure Policy definition structure basics](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/governance/policy/concepts/definition-structure-basics) · [Azure Policy overview](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/governance/policy/overview)","explanationKo":"Resource-group location enforcement does not control the deployment locations of the resources contained in those groups. Azure Policy must evaluate and restrict the locations of the App Service resources themselves to enforce approved regions and regional co-location. Microsoft documents that policies enforcing location on resource groups specifically target the `Microsoft.Resources/subscriptions/resourceGroups` resource type, while the built-in **Allowed locations** policy restricts locations for new resources.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure Policy definition structure basics](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/governance/policy/concepts/definition-structure-basics) · [Azure Policy overview](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/governance/policy/overview)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Yes","ko":"Yes"},{"label":"B","en":"No","ko":"No"}],"answers":["B"]},{"n":248,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design data storage solutions","topicKo":"데이터 저장소 설계","koMissing":true,"images":["assets/1783707860428-t3uny355.png"],"stemEn":"You have the resources shown in the following table:\n\n[[IMG1]]\n\nCDB1 hosts a container that stores operational data that is continuously updated.\n\nYou are designing a solution that will use AS1 to analyze the operational data each day.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that analyzes the data without affecting the performance of the operational data store.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","stemKo":"You have the resources shown in the following table:\n\n[[IMG1]]\n\nCDB1 hosts a container that stores operational data that is continuously updated.\n\nYou are designing a solution that will use AS1 to analyze the operational data each day.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that analyzes the data without affecting the performance of the operational data store.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","explanationEn":"Azure Synapse Link for Azure Cosmos DB exposes an isolated analytical store to Azure Synapse Analytics. Analytical queries run independently of the Cosmos DB transactional workload and do not consume the throughput provisioned for the operational data store.\n\n**Learn more:** [What is Azure Synapse Link for Azure Cosmos DB?](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/cosmos-db/synapse-link) · [What is Azure Cosmos DB analytical store?](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/cosmos-db/analytical-store-introduction)","explanationKo":"Azure Synapse Link for Azure Cosmos DB exposes an isolated analytical store to Azure Synapse Analytics. Analytical queries run independently of the Cosmos DB transactional workload and do not consume the throughput provisioned for the operational data store.\n\n**Learn more:** [What is Azure Synapse Link for Azure Cosmos DB?](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/cosmos-db/synapse-link) · [What is Azure Cosmos DB analytical store?](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/cosmos-db/analytical-store-introduction)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Azure Cosmos DB change feed","ko":"Azure Cosmos DB change feed"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure Data Factory with Azure Cosmos DB and Azure Synapse Analytics connectors","ko":"Azure Data Factory with Azure Cosmos DB and Azure Synapse Analytics connectors"},{"label":"C","en":"Azure Synapse Link for Azure Cosmos DB","ko":"Azure Synapse Link for Azure Cosmos DB"},{"label":"D","en":"Azure Synapse Analytics with PolyBase data loading","ko":"Azure Synapse Analytics with PolyBase data loading"}],"answers":["C"]},{"n":249,"id":null,"type":"dropdown","topic":"Design data storage solutions","topicKo":"데이터 저장소 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You are planning an Azure Storage solution for sensitive data. The data will be accessed daily, and the dataset is less than 10 GB.\n\nRecommend a storage solution that meets these requirements:\n\n- All data written to storage must be retained for five years.\n- Once written, data can only be read; modifications and deletions must be prevented.\n- After five years, data may be deleted but must never be modified.\n- Data-access charges must be minimized.","stemKo":"You are planning an Azure Storage solution for sensitive data. The data will be accessed daily, and the dataset is less than 10 GB.\n\nRecommend a storage solution that meets these requirements:\n\n- All data written to storage must be retained for five years.\n- Once written, data can only be read; modifications and deletions must be prevented.\n- After five years, data may be deleted but must never be modified.\n- Data-access charges must be minimized.","explanationEn":"The Hot tier is optimized for frequently accessed data and has lower access and transaction charges than the Cool tier. A container-level time-based immutability policy provides WORM protection: blobs cannot be modified or deleted during retention, then can be deleted but not overwritten after retention expires. An Azure Resource Manager lock does not protect blobs from data-plane deletion or overwrite operations.\n\n**Learn more:** [Access tiers for blob data - Azure Storage](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/blobs/access-tiers-overview) · [Store business-critical blob data with immutable storage in a write once, read many (WORM) state](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/blobs/immutable-storage-overview)","explanationKo":"The Hot tier is optimized for frequently accessed data and has lower access and transaction charges than the Cool tier. A container-level time-based immutability policy provides WORM protection: blobs cannot be modified or deleted during retention, then can be deleted but not overwritten after retention expires. An Azure Resource Manager lock does not protect blobs from data-plane deletion or overwrite operations.\n\n**Learn more:** [Access tiers for blob data - Azure Storage](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/blobs/access-tiers-overview) · [Store business-critical blob data with immutable storage in a write once, read many (WORM) state](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/blobs/immutable-storage-overview)","learnMore":[],"blanks":[{"id":"storage_account_type","labelEn":"Storage account type:","labelKo":"Storage account type:","options":[{"en":"Premium block blobs","ko":"Premium block blobs"},{"en":"General purpose v2 with Cool access tier for blobs","ko":"General purpose v2 with Cool access tier for blobs"},{"en":"General purpose v2 with Hot access tier for blobs","ko":"General purpose v2 with Hot access tier for blobs"}],"answer":"General purpose v2 with Hot access tier for blobs"},{"id":"configuration_to_prevent_modifications_and_deletions","labelEn":"Configuration to prevent modifications and deletions:","labelKo":"Configuration to prevent modifications and deletions:","options":[{"en":"Container access level","ko":"Container access level"},{"en":"Container access policy","ko":"Container access policy"},{"en":"Storage account resource lock","ko":"Storage account resource lock"}],"answer":"Container access policy"}],"template":""},{"n":250,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design business continuity solutions","topicKo":"업무 연속성 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You must design a highly available Azure SQL database that satisfies these requirements:\n\n- Failover between database replicas must take place with no data loss.\n- The database must stay available if a zone outage occurs.\n- Costs must be kept to a minimum.\n\nWhich deployment option should you use?","stemKo":"You must design a highly available Azure SQL database that satisfies these requirements:\n\n- Failover between database replicas must take place with no data loss.\n- The database must stay available if a zone outage occurs.\n- Costs must be kept to a minimum.\n\nWhich deployment option should you use?","explanationEn":"Azure SQL Database Premium can be configured for zone redundancy, placing replicas in separate availability zones. Its primary replica persists changes to synchronized secondary replicas before committing transactions, ensuring a fully synchronized replica is available for failover; Azure documents no expected data loss during a zone failover. Premium already provides multiple replicas, so distributing them across zones incurs no additional zone-redundancy charge.\n\n**Learn more:** [Reliability in Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/reliability/reliability-sql-database)","explanationKo":"Azure SQL Database Premium can be configured for zone redundancy, placing replicas in separate availability zones. Its primary replica persists changes to synchronized secondary replicas before committing transactions, ensuring a fully synchronized replica is available for failover; Azure documents no expected data loss during a zone failover. Premium already provides multiple replicas, so distributing them across zones incurs no additional zone-redundancy charge.\n\n**Learn more:** [Reliability in Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/reliability/reliability-sql-database)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Azure SQL Managed Instance General Purpose","ko":"Azure SQL Managed Instance General Purpose"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure SQL Database Hyperscale","ko":"Azure SQL Database Hyperscale"},{"label":"C","en":"Azure SQL Database Premium","ko":"Azure SQL Database Premium"},{"label":"D","en":"Azure SQL Managed Instance Business Critical","ko":"Azure SQL Managed Instance Business Critical"}],"answers":["C"]},{"n":251,"id":null,"type":"drag_drop","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You need to configure an Azure Policy that ensures Azure SQL databases have Transparent Data Encryption (TDE) enabled and meets the security and compliance requirements.\n\nWhich three actions should you perform, in order?","stemKo":"You need to configure an Azure Policy that ensures Azure SQL databases have Transparent Data Encryption (TDE) enabled and meets the security and compliance requirements.\n\nWhich three actions should you perform, in order?","explanationEn":"TDE is enforced by deploying the Azure SQL Database transparentDataEncryption configuration when it is missing or noncompliant, which is the purpose of a deployIfNotExists policy. Remediating existing resources requires the policy assignment’s managed identity; the assignment can use a system-assigned identity, so a separate user-assigned identity is unnecessary. A remediation task then deploys the policy’s configuration to the existing noncompliant databases.\n\n**Learn more:** [Remediate non-compliant resources - Azure Policy](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/governance/policy/how-to/remediate-resources) · [Azure Policy deployIfNotExists effect](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/governance/policy/concepts/effect-deploy-if-not-exists)","explanationKo":"TDE is enforced by deploying the Azure SQL Database transparentDataEncryption configuration when it is missing or noncompliant, which is the purpose of a deployIfNotExists policy. Remediating existing resources requires the policy assignment’s managed identity; the assignment can use a system-assigned identity, so a separate user-assigned identity is unnecessary. A remediation task then deploys the policy’s configuration to the existing noncompliant databases.\n\n**Learn more:** [Remediate non-compliant resources - Azure Policy](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/governance/policy/how-to/remediate-resources) · [Azure Policy deployIfNotExists effect](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/governance/policy/concepts/effect-deploy-if-not-exists)","learnMore":[],"items":[{"en":"Create an Azure policy definition that uses the deployIfNotExists effect.","ko":"Create an Azure policy definition that uses the deployIfNotExists effect."},{"en":"Invoke a remediation task.","ko":"Invoke a remediation task."},{"en":"Create an Azure policy definition that uses the Modify effect","ko":"Create an Azure policy definition that uses the Modify effect"},{"en":"Create an Azure policy assignment.","ko":"Create an Azure policy assignment."},{"en":"Create a user-assigned managed identity.","ko":"Create a user-assigned managed identity."}],"slots":[{"id":"step1","labelEn":"항목 step1","labelKo":"항목 step1","answer":"Create an Azure policy definition that uses the deployIfNotExists effect."},{"id":"step2","labelEn":"항목 step2","labelKo":"항목 step2","answer":"Create an Azure policy assignment."},{"id":"step3","labelEn":"항목 step3","labelKo":"항목 step3","answer":"Invoke a remediation task."}],"reuse":false},{"n":252,"id":null,"type":"dropdown","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You have an Azure subscription named Sub1 linked to an Azure AD tenant named contoso.com.\n\nYou plan to deploy two ASP.NET Core apps, App1 and App2, to 100 virtual machines in Sub1. Users will sign in to both apps by using their contoso.com credentials.\n\nApp1 needs read permission to access the signed-in user's calendar. App2 needs write permission to access the signed-in user's calendar.\n\nRecommend an authentication and authorization solution that uses least privilege and minimizes administrative effort.","stemKo":"You have an Azure subscription named Sub1 linked to an Azure AD tenant named contoso.com.\n\nYou plan to deploy two ASP.NET Core apps, App1 and App2, to 100 virtual machines in Sub1. Users will sign in to both apps by using their contoso.com credentials.\n\nApp1 needs read permission to access the signed-in user's calendar. App2 needs write permission to access the signed-in user's calendar.\n\nRecommend an authentication and authorization solution that uses least privilege and minimizes administrative effort.","explanationEn":"An Azure AD application registration configures an ASP.NET Core app to sign in Microsoft Entra users and obtain tokens. Delegated Microsoft Graph permissions let each app access the signed-in user's calendar on that user's behalf. They can be least-privilege scoped, such as Calendars.Read for App1 and Calendars.ReadWrite for App2; application permissions are app-only access, and Azure RBAC does not grant Microsoft Graph calendar access.\n\n**Learn more:** [Overview of Microsoft Graph permissions](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/graph/permissions-overview) · [How to register an app in Microsoft Entra ID](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity-platform/quickstart-register-app)","explanationKo":"An Azure AD application registration configures an ASP.NET Core app to sign in Microsoft Entra users and obtain tokens. Delegated Microsoft Graph permissions let each app access the signed-in user's calendar on that user's behalf. They can be least-privilege scoped, such as Calendars.Read for App1 and Calendars.ReadWrite for App2; application permissions are app-only access, and Azure RBAC does not grant Microsoft Graph calendar access.\n\n**Learn more:** [Overview of Microsoft Graph permissions](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/graph/permissions-overview) · [How to register an app in Microsoft Entra ID](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity-platform/quickstart-register-app)","learnMore":[],"blanks":[{"id":"authentication","labelEn":"Authentication:","labelKo":"Authentication:","options":[{"en":"Application registration in Azure AD","ko":"Application registration in Azure AD"},{"en":"A system-assigned managed identity","ko":"A system-assigned managed identity"},{"en":"A user-assigned managed identity","ko":"A user-assigned managed identity"}],"answer":"Application registration in Azure AD"},{"id":"authorization","labelEn":"Authorization:","labelKo":"Authorization:","options":[{"en":"Application permissions","ko":"Application permissions"},{"en":"Azure role-based access control (Azure RBAC)","ko":"Azure role-based access control (Azure RBAC)"},{"en":"Delegated permissions","ko":"Delegated permissions"}],"answer":"Delegated permissions"}],"template":""},{"n":253,"id":null,"type":"dropdown","topic":"Design infrastructure solutions","topicKo":"인프라 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You have an Azure subscription that contains 100 virtual machines running Windows Server 2022 with the Azure Monitor Agent installed.\n\nRecommend a solution that meets these requirements:\n\n- Forward JSON-formatted logs from the virtual machines to a Log Analytics workspace.\n- Transform the logs and store the data in a table in the Log Analytics workspace.\n\nWhat should be included in the recommendation?","stemKo":"You have an Azure subscription that contains 100 virtual machines running Windows Server 2022 with the Azure Monitor Agent installed.\n\nRecommend a solution that meets these requirements:\n\n- Forward JSON-formatted logs from the virtual machines to a Log Analytics workspace.\n- Transform the logs and store the data in a table in the Log Analytics workspace.\n\nWhat should be included in the recommendation?","explanationEn":"An Azure Monitor data collection endpoint provides endpoints for log ingestion and Azure Monitor Agent configuration. Transformations are KQL statements in a data collection rule that modify incoming records before Azure Monitor sends them to the destination Log Analytics workspace and table.\n\n**Learn more:** [Data collection endpoints in Azure Monitor](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-monitor/data-collection/data-collection-endpoint-overview) · [Transformations in Azure Monitor](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-monitor/data-collection/data-collection-transformations)","explanationKo":"An Azure Monitor data collection endpoint provides endpoints for log ingestion and Azure Monitor Agent configuration. Transformations are KQL statements in a data collection rule that modify incoming records before Azure Monitor sends them to the destination Log Analytics workspace and table.\n\n**Learn more:** [Data collection endpoints in Azure Monitor](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-monitor/data-collection/data-collection-endpoint-overview) · [Transformations in Azure Monitor](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-monitor/data-collection/data-collection-transformations)","learnMore":[],"blanks":[{"id":"forward_logs","labelEn":"To forward the logs:","labelKo":"To forward the logs:","options":[{"en":"A linked storage account for the Log Analytics workspace","ko":"A linked storage account for the Log Analytics workspace"},{"en":"An Azure Monitor data collection endpoint","ko":"An Azure Monitor data collection endpoint"},{"en":"A service endpoint","ko":"A service endpoint"}],"answer":"An Azure Monitor data collection endpoint"},{"id":"transform_store","labelEn":"To transform the logs and store the data:","labelKo":"To transform the logs and store the data:","options":[{"en":"A KQL query","ko":"A KQL query"},{"en":"A WQL query","ko":"A WQL query"},{"en":"An XPath query","ko":"An XPath query"}],"answer":"A KQL query"}],"template":""},{"n":254,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You plan to deploy an Azure SQL database that will store Personally Identifiable Information (PII).\n\nYou need to ensure that only privileged users are able to view the PII. What should you include in the solution?","stemKo":"You plan to deploy an Azure SQL database that will store Personally Identifiable Information (PII).\n\nYou need to ensure that only privileged users are able to view the PII. What should you include in the solution?","explanationEn":"Dynamic data masking limits exposure of sensitive columns by returning masked values to nonprivileged users while privileged users can be granted permission to view the unmasked data. Transparent Data Encryption protects data at rest, Data Discovery & Classification identifies and labels sensitive data, and Azure RBAC does not provide column-level masking of query results. [Microsoft Learn: Dynamic data masking](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/database/dynamic-data-masking-overview?view=azuresql)\n\n**Learn more:** [Microsoft Learn — Dynamic data masking](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/database/dynamic-data-masking-overview?view=azuresql)","explanationKo":"Dynamic data masking limits exposure of sensitive columns by returning masked values to nonprivileged users while privileged users can be granted permission to view the unmasked data. Transparent Data Encryption protects data at rest, Data Discovery & Classification identifies and labels sensitive data, and Azure RBAC does not provide column-level masking of query results. [Microsoft Learn: Dynamic data masking](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/database/dynamic-data-masking-overview?view=azuresql)\n\n**Learn more:** [Microsoft Learn — Dynamic data masking](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/database/dynamic-data-masking-overview?view=azuresql)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"dynamic data masking","ko":"dynamic data masking"},{"label":"B","en":"role-based access control (RBAC)","ko":"role-based access control (RBAC)"},{"label":"C","en":"Data Discovery & Classification","ko":"Data Discovery & Classification"},{"label":"D","en":"Transparent Data Encryption (TDE)","ko":"Transparent Data Encryption (TDE)"}],"answers":["A"]},{"n":255,"id":null,"type":"dropdown","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":["assets/1783707502059-t2mym6qv.png"],"stemEn":"You have several Azure App Service web apps that use Azure Key Vault to hold data-encryption keys. Several departments have the following requests to support the web apps:\n\n[[IMG1]]\n\nWhich service should be recommended for each department’s request?","stemKo":"You have several Azure App Service web apps that use Azure Key Vault to hold data-encryption keys. Several departments have the following requests to support the web apps:\n\n[[IMG1]]\n\nWhich service should be recommended for each department’s request?","explanationEn":"Azure AD Privileged Identity Management supports just-in-time and approval-based privileged-role activation, activation justification, role-assignment alerts, access reviews, and audit history. Azure Managed Identity lets an App Service app obtain Microsoft Entra tokens for Azure Key Vault; grant that identity an appropriate Key Vault role to retrieve keys. Azure AD Connect synchronizes identities, while Azure AD Identity Protection detects and remediates identity risks, so neither fulfills these requested access-management functions.\n\n**Learn more:** [What is Microsoft Entra Privileged Identity Management?](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/id-governance/privileged-identity-management/pim-configure) · [Use managed identities for App Service and Azure Functions](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/app-service/overview-managed-identity)","explanationKo":"Azure AD Privileged Identity Management supports just-in-time and approval-based privileged-role activation, activation justification, role-assignment alerts, access reviews, and audit history. Azure Managed Identity lets an App Service app obtain Microsoft Entra tokens for Azure Key Vault; grant that identity an appropriate Key Vault role to retrieve keys. Azure AD Connect synchronizes identities, while Azure AD Identity Protection detects and remediates identity risks, so neither fulfills these requested access-management functions.\n\n**Learn more:** [What is Microsoft Entra Privileged Identity Management?](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/id-governance/privileged-identity-management/pim-configure) · [Use managed identities for App Service and Azure Functions](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/app-service/overview-managed-identity)","learnMore":[],"blanks":[{"id":"security","labelEn":"Security:","labelKo":"Security:","options":[{"en":"Azure AD Privileged Identity Management","ko":"Azure AD Privileged Identity Management"},{"en":"Azure Managed Identity","ko":"Azure Managed Identity"},{"en":"Azure AD Connect","ko":"Azure AD Connect"},{"en":"Azure AD Identity Protection","ko":"Azure AD Identity Protection"}],"answer":"Azure AD Privileged Identity Management"},{"id":"development","labelEn":"Development:","labelKo":"Development:","options":[{"en":"Azure AD Privileged Identity Management","ko":"Azure AD Privileged Identity Management"},{"en":"Azure Managed Identity","ko":"Azure Managed Identity"},{"en":"Azure AD Connect","ko":"Azure AD Connect"},{"en":"Azure AD Identity Protection","ko":"Azure AD Identity Protection"}],"answer":"Azure Managed Identity"},{"id":"quality_assurance","labelEn":"Quality Assurance:","labelKo":"Quality Assurance:","options":[{"en":"Azure AD Privileged Identity Management","ko":"Azure AD Privileged Identity Management"},{"en":"Azure Managed Identity","ko":"Azure Managed Identity"},{"en":"Azure AD Connect","ko":"Azure AD Connect"},{"en":"Azure AD Identity Protection","ko":"Azure AD Identity Protection"}],"answer":"Azure AD Privileged Identity Management"}],"template":""},{"n":256,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You are designing a governance solution for Azure.\n\nAll Azure resources must be readily identifiable by the following operational information: environment, owner, department, and cost center.\n\nYou need to ensure that the operational information can be used when generating reports for the Azure resources.\n\nWhat should you include in the solution?","stemKo":"You are designing a governance solution for Azure.\n\nAll Azure resources must be readily identifiable by the following operational information: environment, owner, department, and cost center.\n\nYou need to ensure that the operational information can be used when generating reports for the Azure resources.\n\nWhat should you include in the solution?","explanationEn":"Azure tags provide resource metadata for operational classification and reporting, including values such as environment, owner, department, and cost center. Azure Policy can enforce consistent tag rules, including requiring or adding tags to resources at scale.\n\n**Learn more:** [Overview of Azure Policy](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/governance/policy/overview) · [Tutorial: Manage tag governance with Azure Policy](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/governance/policy/tutorials/govern-tags)","explanationKo":"Azure tags provide resource metadata for operational classification and reporting, including values such as environment, owner, department, and cost center. Azure Policy can enforce consistent tag rules, including requiring or adding tags to resources at scale.\n\n**Learn more:** [Overview of Azure Policy](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/governance/policy/overview) · [Tutorial: Manage tag governance with Azure Policy](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/governance/policy/tutorials/govern-tags)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"an Azure data catalog that uses the Azure REST API as a data source","ko":"an Azure data catalog that uses the Azure REST API as a data source"},{"label":"B","en":"an Azure management group that uses parent groups to create a hierarchy","ko":"an Azure management group that uses parent groups to create a hierarchy"},{"label":"C","en":"an Azure policy that enforces tagging rules","ko":"an Azure policy that enforces tagging rules"},{"label":"D","en":"Azure Active Directory (Azure AD) administrative units","ko":"Azure Active Directory (Azure AD) administrative units"}],"answers":["C"]},{"n":257,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design infrastructure solutions","topicKo":"인프라 설계","koMissing":true,"images":["assets/1783708094177-s6nxdupd.png"],"stemEn":"You have an on-premises line-of-business (LOB) application that uses a Microsoft SQL Server instance for its backend.\n\nYou plan to migrate the on-premises SQL Server instance to Azure virtual machines.\n\nYou need to recommend a highly available SQL Server deployment that meets these requirements:\n\n- Minimizes costs\n- Minimizes failover time if a single server fails\n\n[[IMG1]]\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","stemKo":"You have an on-premises line-of-business (LOB) application that uses a Microsoft SQL Server instance for its backend.\n\nYou plan to migrate the on-premises SQL Server instance to Azure virtual machines.\n\nYou need to recommend a highly available SQL Server deployment that meets these requirements:\n\n- Minimizes costs\n- Minimizes failover time if a single server fails\n\n[[IMG1]]\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","explanationEn":"An Always On availability group with a distributed network name (DNN) listener avoids the Azure Load Balancer required by a virtual network name (VNN) listener in a single-subnet deployment. Removing that dependency lowers deployment and management overhead and avoids the load balancer’s health-probe delay, making failover faster. Availability groups protect at the database level without the shared storage required for a failover cluster instance. [Configure a DNN listener for an availability group](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/virtual-machines/windows/availability-group-distributed-network-name-dnn-listener-configure?view=azuresql)\n\n**Learn more:** [Configure a DNN listener for an availability group](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/virtual-machines/windows/availability-group-distributed-network-name-dnn-listener-configure?view=azuresql) · [Always On availability groups on SQL Server on Azure VMs](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/virtual-machines/windows/availability-group-overview?view=azuresql-vm)","explanationKo":"An Always On availability group with a distributed network name (DNN) listener avoids the Azure Load Balancer required by a virtual network name (VNN) listener in a single-subnet deployment. Removing that dependency lowers deployment and management overhead and avoids the load balancer’s health-probe delay, making failover faster. Availability groups protect at the database level without the shared storage required for a failover cluster instance. [Configure a DNN listener for an availability group](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/virtual-machines/windows/availability-group-distributed-network-name-dnn-listener-configure?view=azuresql)\n\n**Learn more:** [Configure a DNN listener for an availability group](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/virtual-machines/windows/availability-group-distributed-network-name-dnn-listener-configure?view=azuresql) · [Always On availability groups on SQL Server on Azure VMs](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/virtual-machines/windows/availability-group-overview?view=azuresql-vm)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"an Always On availability group that has premium storage disks and a virtual network name (VNN)","ko":"an Always On availability group that has premium storage disks and a virtual network name (VNN)"},{"label":"B","en":"an Always On Failover Cluster Instance that has a virtual network name (VNN) and a standard file share","ko":"an Always On Failover Cluster Instance that has a virtual network name (VNN) and a standard file share"},{"label":"C","en":"an Always On availability group that has premium storage disks and a distributed network name (DNN)","ko":"an Always On availability group that has premium storage disks and a distributed network name (DNN)"},{"label":"D","en":"an Always On Failover Cluster Instance that has a virtual network name (VNN) and a premium file share","ko":"an Always On Failover Cluster Instance that has a virtual network name (VNN) and a premium file share"}],"answers":["C"]},{"n":258,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"Solution: Use Azure Advisor for network-traffic analysis.\n\nDoes this satisfy the goal?","stemKo":"Solution: Use Azure Advisor for network-traffic analysis.\n\nDoes this satisfy the goal?","explanationEn":"Azure Advisor does not determine whether specific packets to or from virtual machines are allowed or denied. Azure Network Watcher IP flow verify performs that diagnostic by evaluating the configured security and admin rules and returning an allowed or denied result.\n\n**Learn more:** [IP flow verify overview — Azure Network Watcher](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/network-watcher/ip-flow-verify-overview)","explanationKo":"Azure Advisor does not determine whether specific packets to or from virtual machines are allowed or denied. Azure Network Watcher IP flow verify performs that diagnostic by evaluating the configured security and admin rules and returning an allowed or denied result.\n\n**Learn more:** [IP flow verify overview — Azure Network Watcher](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/network-watcher/ip-flow-verify-overview)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Yes","ko":"Yes"},{"label":"B","en":"No","ko":"No"}],"answers":["B"]},{"n":259,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design infrastructure solutions","topicKo":"인프라 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"Solution: Use Azure Traffic Analytics in Azure Network Watcher to analyze network traffic.\n\nDoes this satisfy the goal?","stemKo":"Solution: Use Azure Traffic Analytics in Azure Network Watcher to analyze network traffic.\n\nDoes this satisfy the goal?","explanationEn":"Azure Traffic Analytics analyzes Azure Network Watcher flow logs and provides visibility into allowed and blocked traffic, including the rules that block flows. It can therefore identify whether traffic to Azure virtual machines is allowed or denied.\n\n**Learn more:** [Traffic Analytics Overview - Azure Network Watcher](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/network-watcher/traffic-analytics)","explanationKo":"Azure Traffic Analytics analyzes Azure Network Watcher flow logs and provides visibility into allowed and blocked traffic, including the rules that block flows. It can therefore identify whether traffic to Azure virtual machines is allowed or denied.\n\n**Learn more:** [Traffic Analytics Overview - Azure Network Watcher](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/network-watcher/traffic-analytics)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Yes","ko":"Yes"},{"label":"B","en":"No","ko":"No"}],"answers":["A"]},{"n":260,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design infrastructure solutions","topicKo":"인프라 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"Solution: Use Azure Network Watcher to run IP flow verify for network-traffic analysis.\n\nDoes this satisfy the goal?","stemKo":"Solution: Use Azure Network Watcher to run IP flow verify for network-traffic analysis.\n\nDoes this satisfy the goal?","explanationEn":"Azure Network Watcher IP flow verify tests a specified TCP or UDP flow to or from an Azure virtual machine against the applicable security and admin rules. It returns whether access is allowed or denied and identifies the rule responsible, enabling diagnosis of virtual-machine traffic-filtering issues.\n\n**Learn more:** [IP Flow Verify Overview - Azure Network Watcher](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/network-watcher/ip-flow-verify-overview) · [Diagnose a virtual machine network traffic filter problem](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/virtual-network/diagnose-network-traffic-filter-problem)","explanationKo":"Azure Network Watcher IP flow verify tests a specified TCP or UDP flow to or from an Azure virtual machine against the applicable security and admin rules. It returns whether access is allowed or denied and identifies the rule responsible, enabling diagnosis of virtual-machine traffic-filtering issues.\n\n**Learn more:** [IP Flow Verify Overview - Azure Network Watcher](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/network-watcher/ip-flow-verify-overview) · [Diagnose a virtual machine network traffic filter problem](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/virtual-network/diagnose-network-traffic-filter-problem)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Yes","ko":"Yes"},{"label":"B","en":"No","ko":"No"}],"answers":["A"]},{"n":261,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design infrastructure solutions","topicKo":"인프라 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"Solution: Install and configure the Azure Monitor Agent and the Dependency Agent on every virtual machine. Use VM insights in Azure Monitor to analyze network traffic.\n\nDoes this satisfy the goal?","stemKo":"Solution: Install and configure the Azure Monitor Agent and the Dependency Agent on every virtual machine. Use VM insights in Azure Monitor to analyze network traffic.\n\nDoes this satisfy the goal?","explanationEn":"VM insights uses the Dependency Agent for process and connection-dependency data; it does not determine whether a packet is permitted or blocked by network security rules. Azure Network Watcher IP flow verify evaluates the applicable security and admin rules for a virtual machine and reports whether the specified traffic is allowed or denied.\n\n**Learn more:** [IP flow verify overview - Azure Network Watcher](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/network-watcher/ip-flow-verify-overview) · [Dependency Agent in Azure Monitor VM insights](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-monitor/vm/vminsights-dependency-agent)","explanationKo":"VM insights uses the Dependency Agent for process and connection-dependency data; it does not determine whether a packet is permitted or blocked by network security rules. Azure Network Watcher IP flow verify evaluates the applicable security and admin rules for a virtual machine and reports whether the specified traffic is allowed or denied.\n\n**Learn more:** [IP flow verify overview - Azure Network Watcher](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/network-watcher/ip-flow-verify-overview) · [Dependency Agent in Azure Monitor VM insights](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-monitor/vm/vminsights-dependency-agent)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Yes","ko":"Yes"},{"label":"B","en":"No","ko":"No"}],"answers":["B"]},{"n":262,"id":null,"type":"dropdown","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You have 100 Azure Storage accounts.\n\nAccess to the accounts is restricted by using Azure role-based access control (Azure RBAC) assignments.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that uses role-assignment conditions based on the tags assigned to individual resources within the storage accounts.\n\nWhat should the recommendation include?","stemKo":"You have 100 Azure Storage accounts.\n\nAccess to the accounts is restricted by using Azure role-based access control (Azure RBAC) assignments.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that uses role-assignment conditions based on the tags assigned to individual resources within the storage accounts.\n\nWhat should the recommendation include?","explanationEn":"Azure RBAC conditions are Azure attribute-based access control (ABAC) conditions. For Azure Storage, blob authorization conditions can evaluate blob resource attributes, including blob index tags, so permissions can be scoped to blobs with particular tags.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure role assignment conditions for Azure Storage](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/blobs/storage-auth-abac) · [What is Azure attribute-based access control (Azure ABAC)?](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/role-based-access-control/conditions-overview)","explanationKo":"Azure RBAC conditions are Azure attribute-based access control (ABAC) conditions. For Azure Storage, blob authorization conditions can evaluate blob resource attributes, including blob index tags, so permissions can be scoped to blobs with particular tags.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure role assignment conditions for Azure Storage](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/blobs/storage-auth-abac) · [What is Azure attribute-based access control (Azure ABAC)?](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/role-based-access-control/conditions-overview)","learnMore":[],"blanks":[{"id":"condition_method","labelEn":"Implement role assignment conditions by using:","labelKo":"Implement role assignment conditions by using:","options":[{"en":"Access control lists (ACLs)","ko":"Access control lists (ACLs)"},{"en":"Attribute-based access control (ABAC)","ko":"Attribute-based access control (ABAC)"},{"en":"Shared access signatures (SAS)","ko":"Shared access signatures (SAS)"}],"answer":"Attribute-based access control (ABAC)"},{"id":"resource_type","labelEn":"Assign permissions to:","labelKo":"Assign permissions to:","options":[{"en":"Blobs","ko":"Blobs"},{"en":"Files","ko":"Files"},{"en":"Tables","ko":"Tables"}],"answer":"Blobs"}],"template":""},{"n":263,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":["assets/1783708622840-yqxe1eay.png"],"stemEn":"Your company has the divisions shown in the following table.\n\n[[IMG1]]\n\nSub1 contains an Azure App Service web app named App1. App1 uses Azure AD for single-tenant user authentication. Users from contoso.com can authenticate to App1.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that enables users in the fabrikam.com tenant to authenticate to App1.\n\nWhat should you recommend?","stemKo":"Your company has the divisions shown in the following table.\n\n[[IMG1]]\n\nSub1 contains an Azure App Service web app named App1. App1 uses Azure AD for single-tenant user authentication. Users from contoso.com can authenticate to App1.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that enables users in the fabrikam.com tenant to authenticate to App1.\n\nWhat should you recommend?","explanationEn":"Microsoft Entra entitlement management can govern external users through access packages that grant access to applications and manage the related B2B guest-user lifecycle. This enables Fabrikam users to be represented as external users in the Contoso tenant and access the single-tenant application. Conditional Access and Identity Protection control sign-in conditions or risk, while provisioning synchronizes identities; none alone grants governed external-user access.\n\n**Learn more:** [Govern access for external users in entitlement management](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/id-governance/entitlement-management-external-users) · [What is Microsoft Entra B2B collaboration?](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/external-id/what-is-b2b?azure-portal=true)","explanationKo":"Microsoft Entra entitlement management can govern external users through access packages that grant access to applications and manage the related B2B guest-user lifecycle. This enables Fabrikam users to be represented as external users in the Contoso tenant and access the single-tenant application. Conditional Access and Identity Protection control sign-in conditions or risk, while provisioning synchronizes identities; none alone grants governed external-user access.\n\n**Learn more:** [Govern access for external users in entitlement management](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/id-governance/entitlement-management-external-users) · [What is Microsoft Entra B2B collaboration?](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/external-id/what-is-b2b?azure-portal=true)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Configure a Conditional Access policy.","ko":"Configure a Conditional Access policy."},{"label":"B","en":"Use Azure AD entitlement management to govern external users.","ko":"Use Azure AD entitlement management to govern external users."},{"label":"C","en":"Configure the Azure AD provisioning service.","ko":"Configure the Azure AD provisioning service."},{"label":"D","en":"Configure Azure AD Identity Protection.","ko":"Configure Azure AD Identity Protection."}],"answers":["B"]},{"n":264,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design infrastructure solutions","topicKo":"인프라 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You are developing a sales application that will include several Azure cloud services and handle different transaction components. Various cloud services will process customer orders, billing, payment, inventory, and shipping.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that lets the cloud services asynchronously exchange transaction information by using XML messages.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","stemKo":"You are developing a sales application that will include several Azure cloud services and handle different transaction components. Various cloud services will process customer orders, billing, payment, inventory, and shipping.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that lets the cloud services asynchronously exchange transaction information by using XML messages.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","explanationEn":"Azure Queue Storage provides durable queues for asynchronous communication between distributed application components, allowing transaction-processing services to be decoupled. Queue messages must be compatible with UTF-8 XML requests, which meets the XML-message requirement.\n\n**Learn more:** [What is Azure Queue Storage?](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/queues/storage-queues-introduction) · [Quickstart: Azure Queue Storage client library for .NET](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/queues/storage-quickstart-queues-dotnet)","explanationKo":"Azure Queue Storage provides durable queues for asynchronous communication between distributed application components, allowing transaction-processing services to be decoupled. Queue messages must be compatible with UTF-8 XML requests, which meets the XML-message requirement.\n\n**Learn more:** [What is Azure Queue Storage?](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/queues/storage-queues-introduction) · [Quickstart: Azure Queue Storage client library for .NET](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/queues/storage-quickstart-queues-dotnet)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Azure Notification Hubs","ko":"Azure Notification Hubs"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure Service Fabric","ko":"Azure Service Fabric"},{"label":"C","en":"Azure Queue Storage","ko":"Azure Queue Storage"},{"label":"D","en":"Azure Data Lake","ko":"Azure Data Lake"}],"answers":["C"]},{"n":265,"id":null,"type":"drag_drop","topic":"Design data storage solutions","topicKo":"데이터 저장소 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You have an on-premises application named App1 that customers use to manage digital images. You plan to migrate App1 to Azure.\n\nRecommend a data-storage solution that meets these image-storage requirements:\n\n- Encrypt images at rest.\n- Allow files up to 50 MB.\n- Manage image access by using Azure Web Application Firewall (WAF) on Azure Front Door.\n\nThe solution must also meet these customer-account requirements:\n\n- Support automatic storage scale-out.\n- Keep App1 available if a datacenter fails.\n- Support reading and writing data from multiple Azure regions.\n\nWhich service should be included for each data type? Each service can be used once, more than once, or not at all.","stemKo":"You have an on-premises application named App1 that customers use to manage digital images. You plan to migrate App1 to Azure.\n\nRecommend a data-storage solution that meets these image-storage requirements:\n\n- Encrypt images at rest.\n- Allow files up to 50 MB.\n- Manage image access by using Azure Web Application Firewall (WAF) on Azure Front Door.\n\nThe solution must also meet these customer-account requirements:\n\n- Support automatic storage scale-out.\n- Keep App1 available if a datacenter fails.\n- Support reading and writing data from multiple Azure regions.\n\nWhich service should be included for each data type? Each service can be used once, more than once, or not at all.","explanationEn":"Azure Blob storage is appropriate for image objects: Azure Storage encrypts data at rest by default, and Blob Storage can serve as an Azure Front Door origin protected by WAF. Azure Cosmos DB provides autoscale throughput and supports geographically distributed, multi-region read and write workloads with high availability.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure Storage encryption for data at rest](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/common/storage-service-encryption) · [Azure Front Door frequently asked questions](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/frontdoor/front-door-faq)","explanationKo":"Azure Blob storage is appropriate for image objects: Azure Storage encrypts data at rest by default, and Blob Storage can serve as an Azure Front Door origin protected by WAF. Azure Cosmos DB provides autoscale throughput and supports geographically distributed, multi-region read and write workloads with high availability.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure Storage encryption for data at rest](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/common/storage-service-encryption) · [Azure Front Door frequently asked questions](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/frontdoor/front-door-faq)","learnMore":[],"items":[{"en":"Azure Blob storage","ko":"Azure Blob storage"},{"en":"Azure Cosmos DB","ko":"Azure Cosmos DB"},{"en":"Azure SQL Database","ko":"Azure SQL Database"},{"en":"Azure Table storage","ko":"Azure Table storage"}],"slots":[{"id":"image_storage","labelEn":"Image storage:","labelKo":"Image storage:","answer":"Azure Blob storage"},{"id":"customer_accounts","labelEn":"Customer accounts:","labelKo":"Customer accounts:","answer":"Azure Cosmos DB"}],"reuse":true},{"n":266,"id":null,"type":"dropdown","topic":"Design data storage solutions","topicKo":"데이터 저장소 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You are designing an application that will use Azure Linux virtual machines to analyze video files. The files will be uploaded from corporate offices that connect to Azure by using ExpressRoute.\n\nYou plan to provision an Azure Storage account to host the files. You must ensure that the storage account meets these requirements:\n\n- Supports video files of up to 7 TB\n- Provides the highest possible availability\n- Optimizes storage for the large video files\n- Ensures files from the on-premises network are uploaded by using ExpressRoute\n\nHow should you configure the storage account?","stemKo":"You are designing an application that will use Azure Linux virtual machines to analyze video files. The files will be uploaded from corporate offices that connect to Azure by using ExpressRoute.\n\nYou plan to provision an Azure Storage account to host the files. You must ensure that the storage account meets these requirements:\n\n- Supports video files of up to 7 TB\n- Provides the highest possible availability\n- Optimizes storage for the large video files\n- Ensures files from the on-premises network are uploaded by using ExpressRoute\n\nHow should you configure the storage account?","explanationEn":"A standard general-purpose v2 account supports Blob storage, including block blobs that can exceed 7 TB and are appropriate for large video objects. GRS replicates data to a geographically separate secondary region, providing more availability and disaster resilience than LRS or ZRS among the listed choices. A private endpoint enables private access to the storage account from on-premises networks connected to the virtual network through ExpressRoute private peering.\n\n**Learn more:** [Scalability and performance targets for Blob storage](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/blobs/scalability-targets) · [Data redundancy - Azure Storage](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/common/storage-redundancy)","explanationKo":"A standard general-purpose v2 account supports Blob storage, including block blobs that can exceed 7 TB and are appropriate for large video objects. GRS replicates data to a geographically separate secondary region, providing more availability and disaster resilience than LRS or ZRS among the listed choices. A private endpoint enables private access to the storage account from on-premises networks connected to the virtual network through ExpressRoute private peering.\n\n**Learn more:** [Scalability and performance targets for Blob storage](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/blobs/scalability-targets) · [Data redundancy - Azure Storage](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/common/storage-redundancy)","learnMore":[],"blanks":[{"id":"storage_account_type","labelEn":"Storage account type:","labelKo":"Storage account type:","options":[{"en":"Premium files shares","ko":"Premium files shares"},{"en":"Premium page blobs","ko":"Premium page blobs"},{"en":"Standard general-purpose v2","ko":"Standard general-purpose v2"}],"answer":"Standard general-purpose v2"},{"id":"data_redundancy","labelEn":"Data redundancy:","labelKo":"Data redundancy:","options":[{"en":"Zone-redundant storage (ZRS)","ko":"Zone-redundant storage (ZRS)"},{"en":"Locally-redundant storage (LRS)","ko":"Locally-redundant storage (LRS)"},{"en":"Geo-redundant storage (GRS)","ko":"Geo-redundant storage (GRS)"}],"answer":"Geo-redundant storage (GRS)"},{"id":"networking","labelEn":"Networking:","labelKo":"Networking:","options":[{"en":"Azure Route Server","ko":"Azure Route Server"},{"en":"A private endpoint","ko":"A private endpoint"},{"en":"A service endpoint","ko":"A service endpoint"}],"answer":"A private endpoint"}],"template":""},{"n":267,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You need to recommend a solution for producing a monthly report of every new Azure Resource Manager (ARM) resource deployment in your Azure subscription.\n\nWhat should the recommendation include?","stemKo":"You need to recommend a solution for producing a monthly report of every new Azure Resource Manager (ARM) resource deployment in your Azure subscription.\n\nWhat should the recommendation include?","explanationEn":"Azure Activity Log records Azure Resource Manager control-plane operations, including resource creation and deployment events. Exporting the activity log to an Azure Log Analytics workspace stores the events in the `AzureActivity` table, where KQL can filter new deployment operations over each monthly reporting period. [Activity log in Azure Monitor](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-monitor/platform/activity-log)\n\n**Learn more:** [Activity log in Azure Monitor](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-monitor/platform/activity-log)","explanationKo":"Azure Activity Log records Azure Resource Manager control-plane operations, including resource creation and deployment events. Exporting the activity log to an Azure Log Analytics workspace stores the events in the `AzureActivity` table, where KQL can filter new deployment operations over each monthly reporting period. [Activity log in Azure Monitor](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-monitor/platform/activity-log)\n\n**Learn more:** [Activity log in Azure Monitor](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-monitor/platform/activity-log)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Azure Log Analytics","ko":"Azure Log Analytics"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure Arc","ko":"Azure Arc"},{"label":"C","en":"Azure Analysis Services","ko":"Azure Analysis Services"},{"label":"D","en":"Azure Monitor action groups","ko":"Azure Monitor action groups"}],"answers":["A"]},{"n":268,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design infrastructure solutions","topicKo":"인프라 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You are developing a sales application that will include several Azure cloud services and manage different parts of a transaction. Separate cloud services will process customer orders, billing, payment, inventory, and shipping.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that lets the cloud services asynchronously exchange transaction information by using XML messages.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","stemKo":"You are developing a sales application that will include several Azure cloud services and manage different parts of a transaction. Separate cloud services will process customer orders, billing, payment, inventory, and shipping.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that lets the cloud services asynchronously exchange transaction information by using XML messages.\n\nWhat should you include in the recommendation?","explanationEn":"Azure Queue Storage provides durable queues that decouple distributed application components: services can place transaction messages on a queue for later retrieval and processing by other services. Queue messages must be compatible with an XML request using UTF-8 encoding, which supports XML-based transaction messaging.\n\n**Learn more:** [Tutorial: Work with Azure Queue Storage queues in .NET](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/queues/storage-tutorial-queues)","explanationKo":"Azure Queue Storage provides durable queues that decouple distributed application components: services can place transaction messages on a queue for later retrieval and processing by other services. Queue messages must be compatible with an XML request using UTF-8 encoding, which supports XML-based transaction messaging.\n\n**Learn more:** [Tutorial: Work with Azure Queue Storage queues in .NET](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/queues/storage-tutorial-queues)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Azure Blob Storage","ko":"Azure Blob Storage"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure Data Lake","ko":"Azure Data Lake"},{"label":"C","en":"Azure Queue Storage","ko":"Azure Queue Storage"},{"label":"D","en":"Azure Service Fabric","ko":"Azure Service Fabric"}],"answers":["C"]},{"n":269,"id":null,"type":"drag_drop","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You have an Azure subscription containing Azure virtual machines running Windows Server 2016 and Linux.\n\nYou need to use Azure Monitor to create an alerting strategy for security-related events. Identify the Azure Monitor Logs tables to query for each log type.\n\nEach table can be used once, more than once, or not at all.","stemKo":"You have an Azure subscription containing Azure virtual machines running Windows Server 2016 and Linux.\n\nYou need to use Azure Monitor to create an alerting strategy for security-related events. Identify the Azure Monitor Logs tables to query for each log type.\n\nEach table can be used once, more than once, or not at all.","explanationEn":"The Event table contains records collected from Windows Event Log on Windows computers. Linux system log records are collected into the Syslog table, which can be queried for security-relevant syslog events.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure Monitor Logs reference - Event](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-monitor/reference/tables/event) · [Azure Monitor Logs reference - Syslog](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-monitor/reference/tables/syslog)","explanationKo":"The Event table contains records collected from Windows Event Log on Windows computers. Linux system log records are collected into the Syslog table, which can be queried for security-relevant syslog events.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure Monitor Logs reference - Event](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-monitor/reference/tables/event) · [Azure Monitor Logs reference - Syslog](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-monitor/reference/tables/syslog)","learnMore":[],"items":[{"en":"AzureActivity","ko":"AzureActivity"},{"en":"AzureDiagnostics","ko":"AzureDiagnostics"},{"en":"Event","ko":"Event"},{"en":"Syslog","ko":"Syslog"}],"slots":[{"id":"windows_event_logs","labelEn":"Events from Windows event logs:","labelKo":"Events from Windows event logs:","answer":"Event"},{"id":"linux_system_logging","labelEn":"Events from Linux system logging:","labelKo":"Events from Linux system logging:","answer":"Syslog"}],"reuse":true},{"n":270,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":["assets/1783708886651-c7csf8is.png"],"stemEn":"Your company has the divisions shown in the following table.\n\n[[IMG1]]\n\nSub1 contains an Azure App Service web app named App1. App1 uses Azure AD for single-tenant user authentication. Users from contoso.com can authenticate to App1.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that enables users in the fabrikam.com tenant to authenticate to App1.\n\nWhat should you recommend?","stemKo":"Your company has the divisions shown in the following table.\n\n[[IMG1]]\n\nSub1 contains an Azure App Service web app named App1. App1 uses Azure AD for single-tenant user authentication. Users from contoso.com can authenticate to App1.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that enables users in the fabrikam.com tenant to authenticate to App1.\n\nWhat should you recommend?","explanationEn":"A multitenant Microsoft Entra application allows organizational users from other tenants to sign in. Changing the app registration’s Supported account types to allow accounts in any organizational directory and using a multitenant sign-in authority endpoint enables fabrikam.com users to authenticate to the app.\n\n**Learn more:** [Convert single-tenant app to multitenant on Microsoft Entra ID](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity-platform/howto-convert-app-to-be-multi-tenant) · [Identity and account types for single- and multitenant apps](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/security/zero-trust/develop/identity-supported-account-types)","explanationKo":"A multitenant Microsoft Entra application allows organizational users from other tenants to sign in. Changing the app registration’s Supported account types to allow accounts in any organizational directory and using a multitenant sign-in authority endpoint enables fabrikam.com users to authenticate to the app.\n\n**Learn more:** [Convert single-tenant app to multitenant on Microsoft Entra ID](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity-platform/howto-convert-app-to-be-multi-tenant) · [Identity and account types for single- and multitenant apps](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/security/zero-trust/develop/identity-supported-account-types)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Configure Azure AD join.","ko":"Configure Azure AD join."},{"label":"B","en":"Configure Azure AD Identity Protection.","ko":"Configure Azure AD Identity Protection."},{"label":"C","en":"Configure a Conditional Access policy.","ko":"Configure a Conditional Access policy."},{"label":"D","en":"Configure Supported account types in the application registration and update the sign-in endpoint.","ko":"Configure Supported account types in the application registration and update the sign-in endpoint."}],"answers":["D"]},{"n":271,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":["assets/1783708621309-ingiz9db.png"],"stemEn":"Your company has the divisions shown in the following table.\n\n[[IMG1]]\n\nSub1 contains an Azure App Service web app named App1. App1 uses Azure AD for single-tenant user authentication. Users from contoso.com can authenticate to App1.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that enables users in the fabrikam.com tenant to authenticate to App1.\n\nWhat should you recommend?","stemKo":"Your company has the divisions shown in the following table.\n\n[[IMG1]]\n\nSub1 contains an Azure App Service web app named App1. App1 uses Azure AD for single-tenant user authentication. Users from contoso.com can authenticate to App1.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that enables users in the fabrikam.com tenant to authenticate to App1.\n\nWhat should you recommend?","explanationEn":"Microsoft Entra entitlement management uses B2B collaboration to provide external users with guest representations in the resource directory and assign them access to resources. An access package can govern Fabrikam users' lifecycle and application access while they authenticate through their home tenant.\n\n**Learn more:** [Govern access for external users in entitlement management](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/id-governance/entitlement-management-external-users) · [Manage connected organizations in entitlement management](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/id-governance/entitlement-management-organization)","explanationKo":"Microsoft Entra entitlement management uses B2B collaboration to provide external users with guest representations in the resource directory and assign them access to resources. An access package can govern Fabrikam users' lifecycle and application access while they authenticate through their home tenant.\n\n**Learn more:** [Govern access for external users in entitlement management](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/id-governance/entitlement-management-external-users) · [Manage connected organizations in entitlement management](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/id-governance/entitlement-management-organization)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Configure Azure AD join.","ko":"Configure Azure AD join."},{"label":"B","en":"Use Azure AD entitlement management to govern external users.","ko":"Use Azure AD entitlement management to govern external users."},{"label":"C","en":"Enable Azure AD pass-through authentication and update the sign-in endpoint.","ko":"Enable Azure AD pass-through authentication and update the sign-in endpoint."},{"label":"D","en":"Configure assignments for the fabrikam.com users by using Azure AD Privileged Identity Management (PIM).","ko":"Configure assignments for the fabrikam.com users by using Azure AD Privileged Identity Management (PIM)."}],"answers":["B"]},{"n":272,"id":null,"type":"dropdown","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You have an Azure subscription containing multiple storage accounts, and Azure Policy definitions are assigned to those storage accounts.\n\nRecommend a solution that meets these requirements:\n\n- Trigger Azure Policy compliance scans on demand.\n- Generate Azure Monitor alerts for non-compliance by querying logs collected in Log Analytics.\n\nWhat should you recommend for each requirement?","stemKo":"You have an Azure subscription containing multiple storage accounts, and Azure Policy definitions are assigned to those storage accounts.\n\nRecommend a solution that meets these requirements:\n\n- Trigger Azure Policy compliance scans on demand.\n- Generate Azure Monitor alerts for non-compliance by querying logs collected in Log Analytics.\n\nWhat should you recommend for each requirement?","explanationEn":"`az policy state trigger-scan` starts an on-demand Azure Policy compliance evaluation. Azure activity logs can be exported through diagnostic settings to a Log Analytics workspace, where log queries can drive Azure Monitor log alerts for policy non-compliance events.\n\n**Learn more:** [Get policy compliance data - Azure Policy](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/governance/policy/how-to/get-compliance-data) · [Azure Monitor activity log](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-monitor/platform/activity-log)","explanationKo":"`az policy state trigger-scan` starts an on-demand Azure Policy compliance evaluation. Azure activity logs can be exported through diagnostic settings to a Log Analytics workspace, where log queries can drive Azure Monitor log alerts for policy non-compliance events.\n\n**Learn more:** [Get policy compliance data - Azure Policy](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/governance/policy/how-to/get-compliance-data) · [Azure Monitor activity log](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-monitor/platform/activity-log)","learnMore":[],"blanks":[{"id":"compliance_scans","labelEn":"To trigger the compliance scans, use:","labelKo":"To trigger the compliance scans, use:","options":[{"en":"An Azure template","ko":"An Azure template"},{"en":"The Azure Command-Line Interface (CLI)","ko":"The Azure Command-Line Interface (CLI)"},{"en":"The Azure portal","ko":"The Azure portal"}],"answer":"The Azure Command-Line Interface (CLI)"},{"id":"noncompliance_alerts","labelEn":"To generate the non-compliance alerts, configure diagnostic settings for the:","labelKo":"To generate the non-compliance alerts, configure diagnostic settings for the:","options":[{"en":"Azure activity logs","ko":"Azure activity logs"},{"en":"Log Analytics workspace","ko":"Log Analytics workspace"},{"en":"Storage accounts","ko":"Storage accounts"}],"answer":"Azure activity logs"}],"template":""},{"n":273,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design infrastructure solutions","topicKo":"인프라 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You plan to migrate on-premises MySQL databases to Azure Database for MySQL Flexible Server.\n\nYou need to recommend a configuration solution for Azure Database for MySQL Flexible Server. The solution must meet the following requirements:\n\n- The databases must remain accessible if a datacenter fails.\n- Costs must be minimized.\n\nWhich compute tier should you recommend?","stemKo":"You plan to migrate on-premises MySQL databases to Azure Database for MySQL Flexible Server.\n\nYou need to recommend a configuration solution for Azure Database for MySQL Flexible Server. The solution must meet the following requirements:\n\n- The databases must remain accessible if a datacenter fails.\n- Costs must be minimized.\n\nWhich compute tier should you recommend?","explanationEn":"Zone-redundant high availability provides resilience to an availability-zone/datacenter failure by using a standby server in another zone. The Burstable tier does not support high availability. General Purpose supports production workloads and high availability without the additional memory-focused capacity and cost of the Memory Optimized tier.\n\n**Learn more:** [High availability concepts in Azure Database for MySQL - Flexible Server](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/mysql/flexible-server/concepts-high-availability) · [Azure Database for MySQL - Flexible Server service tiers](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/mysql/flexible-server/concepts-service-tiers-storage)","explanationKo":"Zone-redundant high availability provides resilience to an availability-zone/datacenter failure by using a standby server in another zone. The Burstable tier does not support high availability. General Purpose supports production workloads and high availability without the additional memory-focused capacity and cost of the Memory Optimized tier.\n\n**Learn more:** [High availability concepts in Azure Database for MySQL - Flexible Server](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/mysql/flexible-server/concepts-high-availability) · [Azure Database for MySQL - Flexible Server service tiers](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/mysql/flexible-server/concepts-service-tiers-storage)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Burstable","ko":"Burstable"},{"label":"B","en":"General Purpose","ko":"General Purpose"},{"label":"C","en":"Memory Optimized","ko":"Memory Optimized"}],"answers":["B"]},{"n":274,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You need to recommend a solution that produces a monthly report of all new Azure Resource Manager (ARM) resource deployments in your Azure subscription.\n\nWhat should the recommendation include?","stemKo":"You need to recommend a solution that produces a monthly report of all new Azure Resource Manager (ARM) resource deployments in your Azure subscription.\n\nWhat should the recommendation include?","explanationEn":"Azure Activity Log records Azure Resource Manager control-plane deployment operations. Sending the activity log to a Log Analytics workspace stores the events in the `AzureActivity` table, where they can be queried and used to produce a monthly deployment report.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure Monitor activity log](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-monitor/platform/activity-log)","explanationKo":"Azure Activity Log records Azure Resource Manager control-plane deployment operations. Sending the activity log to a Log Analytics workspace stores the events in the `AzureActivity` table, where they can be queried and used to produce a monthly deployment report.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure Monitor activity log](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-monitor/platform/activity-log)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Application Insights","ko":"Application Insights"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure Analysis Services","ko":"Azure Analysis Services"},{"label":"C","en":"Azure Advisor","ko":"Azure Advisor"},{"label":"D","en":"Azure Log Analytics","ko":"Azure Log Analytics"}],"answers":["D"]},{"n":275,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design data storage solutions","topicKo":"데이터 저장소 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You must recommend a solution that fulfills the database retention requirements.\n\nWhat should you recommend?","stemKo":"You must recommend a solution that fulfills the database retention requirements.\n\nWhat should you recommend?","explanationEn":"An Azure SQL Database long-term retention (LTR) policy automatically retains database backups in separate Azure Blob storage for the configured weekly, monthly, and yearly periods, for up to 10 years. This directly satisfies long-term database-retention requirements.\n\n**Learn more:** [Manage Azure SQL Database long-term backup retention](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/database/long-term-backup-retention-configure?view=azuresql)","explanationKo":"An Azure SQL Database long-term retention (LTR) policy automatically retains database backups in separate Azure Blob storage for the configured weekly, monthly, and yearly periods, for up to 10 years. This directly satisfies long-term database-retention requirements.\n\n**Learn more:** [Manage Azure SQL Database long-term backup retention](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/database/long-term-backup-retention-configure?view=azuresql)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Configure a long-term retention policy for the database.","ko":"Configure a long-term retention policy for the database."},{"label":"B","en":"Configure Azure Site Recovery.","ko":"Configure Azure Site Recovery."},{"label":"C","en":"Use automatic Azure SQL Database backups.","ko":"Use automatic Azure SQL Database backups."},{"label":"D","en":"Configure geo-replication of the database.","ko":"Configure geo-replication of the database."}],"answers":["A"]},{"n":276,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design infrastructure solutions","topicKo":"인프라 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You are building a sales application that will include several Azure cloud services and manage different parts of a transaction. Separate cloud services will process customer orders, billing, payment, inventory, and shipping.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that lets the cloud services asynchronously exchange transaction information by using XML messages.\n\nWhat should be included in the recommendation?","stemKo":"You are building a sales application that will include several Azure cloud services and manage different parts of a transaction. Separate cloud services will process customer orders, billing, payment, inventory, and shipping.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that lets the cloud services asynchronously exchange transaction information by using XML messages.\n\nWhat should be included in the recommendation?","explanationEn":"Azure Service Bus is a managed enterprise message broker that decouples services through queues and publish-subscribe topics. It supports asynchronous, store-and-forward communication, and its message payloads can contain structured data encoded as XML.\n\n**Learn more:** [What is Azure Service Bus?](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-gb/azure/service-bus-messaging/service-bus-messaging-overview) · [Asynchronous messaging patterns and high availability](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/service-bus-messaging/service-bus-async-messaging)","explanationKo":"Azure Service Bus is a managed enterprise message broker that decouples services through queues and publish-subscribe topics. It supports asynchronous, store-and-forward communication, and its message payloads can contain structured data encoded as XML.\n\n**Learn more:** [What is Azure Service Bus?](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-gb/azure/service-bus-messaging/service-bus-messaging-overview) · [Asynchronous messaging patterns and high availability](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/service-bus-messaging/service-bus-async-messaging)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Azure Service Bus","ko":"Azure Service Bus"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure Data Lake","ko":"Azure Data Lake"},{"label":"C","en":"Azure Traffic Manager","ko":"Azure Traffic Manager"},{"label":"D","en":"Azure Blob Storage","ko":"Azure Blob Storage"}],"answers":["A"]},{"n":277,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design infrastructure solutions","topicKo":"인프라 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You have an Azure subscription.\n\nYou need to recommend an Azure Kubernetes Service (AKS) solution that uses Linux nodes. The solution must meet the following requirements:\n\n- Minimize the time required to provision compute resources during scale-out operations.\n- Support autoscaling for Linux containers.\n- Minimize administrative effort.\n\nWhich scaling option should you recommend?","stemKo":"You have an Azure subscription.\n\nYou need to recommend an Azure Kubernetes Service (AKS) solution that uses Linux nodes. The solution must meet the following requirements:\n\n- Minimize the time required to provision compute resources during scale-out operations.\n- Support autoscaling for Linux containers.\n- Minimize administrative effort.\n\nWhich scaling option should you recommend?","explanationEn":"AKS virtual nodes use Azure Container Instances to provision pods rapidly, without waiting for the cluster autoscaler to deploy VM compute nodes. They are supported for Linux pods and nodes, and the serverless container infrastructure reduces node-administration overhead.\n\n**Learn more:** [Use virtual nodes with Azure Kubernetes Service (AKS)](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/aks/virtual-nodes)","explanationKo":"AKS virtual nodes use Azure Container Instances to provision pods rapidly, without waiting for the cluster autoscaler to deploy VM compute nodes. They are supported for Linux pods and nodes, and the serverless container infrastructure reduces node-administration overhead.\n\n**Learn more:** [Use virtual nodes with Azure Kubernetes Service (AKS)](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/aks/virtual-nodes)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"horizontal pod autoscaler","ko":"horizontal pod autoscaler"},{"label":"B","en":"cluster autoscaler","ko":"cluster autoscaler"},{"label":"C","en":"virtual nodes","ko":"virtual nodes"},{"label":"D","en":"Virtual Kubelet","ko":"Virtual Kubelet"}],"answers":["C"]},{"n":278,"id":null,"type":"dropdown","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"A company plans to implement an HTTP-based API for a web app that enables customers to check their order status.\n\nThe API must:\n\n- Use Azure Functions.\n- Offer public, read-only operations.\n- Block write operations.\n\nRecommend the HTTP methods and authorization level to configure.","stemKo":"A company plans to implement an HTTP-based API for a web app that enables customers to check their order status.\n\nThe API must:\n\n- Use Azure Functions.\n- Offer public, read-only operations.\n- Block write operations.\n\nRecommend the HTTP methods and authorization level to configure.","explanationEn":"An Azure Functions HTTP trigger can restrict the methods to GET, allowing read-only requests while excluding write operations. The Anonymous authorization level requires no access key, making the endpoint publicly accessible.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure Functions HTTP trigger](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-functions/functions-bindings-http-webhook-trigger)","explanationKo":"An Azure Functions HTTP trigger can restrict the methods to GET, allowing read-only requests while excluding write operations. The Anonymous authorization level requires no access key, making the endpoint publicly accessible.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure Functions HTTP trigger](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-functions/functions-bindings-http-webhook-trigger)","learnMore":[],"blanks":[{"id":"http_methods","labelEn":"HTTP methods:","labelKo":"HTTP methods:","options":[{"en":"API methods","ko":"API methods"},{"en":"GET only","ko":"GET only"},{"en":"GET and POST only","ko":"GET and POST only"},{"en":"GET, POST, and OPTIONS only","ko":"GET, POST, and OPTIONS only"}],"answer":"GET only"},{"id":"authorization_level","labelEn":"Authorization level:","labelKo":"Authorization level:","options":[{"en":"Function","ko":"Function"},{"en":"Anonymous","ko":"Anonymous"},{"en":"Admin","ko":"Admin"}],"answer":"Anonymous"}],"template":""},{"n":279,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You have an Azure subscription that contains a blob container with multiple blobs.\n\nTen users in your company's finance department plan to access the blobs during April.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that enables access to the blobs only for the month of April.\n\nWhich security solution should be included in the recommendation?","stemKo":"You have an Azure subscription that contains a blob container with multiple blobs.\n\nTen users in your company's finance department plan to access the blobs during April.\n\nYou need to recommend a solution that enables access to the blobs only for the month of April.\n\nWhich security solution should be included in the recommendation?","explanationEn":"A shared access signature (SAS) provides delegated, granular access to Azure Storage resources, including blob containers and blobs. Its permissions and validity interval can be set so access begins and expires during April only.\n\n**Learn more:** [Grant limited access to Azure Storage resources using shared access signatures (SAS)](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/common/storage-sas-overview)","explanationKo":"A shared access signature (SAS) provides delegated, granular access to Azure Storage resources, including blob containers and blobs. Its permissions and validity interval can be set so access begins and expires during April only.\n\n**Learn more:** [Grant limited access to Azure Storage resources using shared access signatures (SAS)](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/common/storage-sas-overview)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"shared access signatures (SAS)","ko":"shared access signatures (SAS)"},{"label":"B","en":"Conditional Access policies","ko":"Conditional Access policies"},{"label":"C","en":"certificates","ko":"certificates"},{"label":"D","en":"access keys","ko":"access keys"}],"answers":["A"]},{"n":280,"id":null,"type":"dropdown","topic":"Design data storage solutions","topicKo":"데이터 저장소 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You have an Azure subscription.\n\nYou need to deploy a relational database that meets these requirements:\n\n- Support multiple read-only replicas.\n- Automatically load-balance read-only requests across all read-only replicas.\n- Minimize administrative effort.\n\nWhat should you use?","stemKo":"You have an Azure subscription.\n\nYou need to deploy a relational database that meets these requirements:\n\n- Support multiple read-only replicas.\n- Automatically load-balance read-only requests across all read-only replicas.\n- Minimize administrative effort.\n\nWhat should you use?","explanationEn":"Azure SQL Database Hyperscale supports multiple named replicas for read scale-out and can distribute read-only workloads across them. A single Azure SQL database in the Hyperscale service tier is therefore the managed, low-administration option that satisfies the replica and read-only load-balancing requirements.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure SQL Database Hyperscale service tier overview](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/database/service-tier-hyperscale?view=azuresql) · [Scale out with read-only replicas - Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/database/read-scale-out?view=azuresql)","explanationKo":"Azure SQL Database Hyperscale supports multiple named replicas for read scale-out and can distribute read-only workloads across them. A single Azure SQL database in the Hyperscale service tier is therefore the managed, low-administration option that satisfies the replica and read-only load-balancing requirements.\n\n**Learn more:** [Azure SQL Database Hyperscale service tier overview](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/database/service-tier-hyperscale?view=azuresql) · [Scale out with read-only replicas - Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/database/read-scale-out?view=azuresql)","learnMore":[],"blanks":[{"id":"service","labelEn":"Service","labelKo":"Service","options":[{"en":"A single Azure SQL database","ko":"A single Azure SQL database"},{"en":"An Azure SQL Database elastic pool","ko":"An Azure SQL Database elastic pool"},{"en":"Azure SQL Managed Instances","ko":"Azure SQL Managed Instances"}],"answer":"A single Azure SQL database"},{"id":"service_tier","labelEn":"Service tier","labelKo":"Service tier","options":[{"en":"Business Critical","ko":"Business Critical"},{"en":"Hyperscale","ko":"Hyperscale"},{"en":"Premium","ko":"Premium"}],"answer":"Hyperscale"}],"template":""},{"n":281,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design data storage solutions","topicKo":"데이터 저장소 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You are designing an application that will be hosted in Azure.\n\nThe application will store video files ranging from 50 MB to 12 GB. It will use certificate-based authentication and be available to users on the internet.\n\nYou need to recommend a storage option for the video files. The solution must deliver the fastest read performance while minimizing storage costs.\n\nWhat should you recommend?","stemKo":"You are designing an application that will be hosted in Azure.\n\nThe application will store video files ranging from 50 MB to 12 GB. It will use certificate-based authentication and be available to users on the internet.\n\nYou need to recommend a storage option for the video files. The solution must deliver the fastest read performance while minimizing storage costs.\n\nWhat should you recommend?","explanationEn":"Azure Blob Storage is optimized for massive amounts of unstructured data and is designed for distributed file access and streaming video and audio over HTTP/HTTPS. Block blobs support access tiers, enabling storage costs to be optimized for the files’ access pattern while online tiers provide immediate retrieval.\n\n**Learn more:** [Introduction to Azure Blob Storage](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/blobs/storage-blobs-introduction) · [Access tiers for blob data](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/blobs/access-tiers-overview)","explanationKo":"Azure Blob Storage is optimized for massive amounts of unstructured data and is designed for distributed file access and streaming video and audio over HTTP/HTTPS. Block blobs support access tiers, enabling storage costs to be optimized for the files’ access pattern while online tiers provide immediate retrieval.\n\n**Learn more:** [Introduction to Azure Blob Storage](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/blobs/storage-blobs-introduction) · [Access tiers for blob data](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/blobs/access-tiers-overview)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Azure Files","ko":"Azure Files"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure Data Lake Storage Gen2","ko":"Azure Data Lake Storage Gen2"},{"label":"C","en":"Azure Blob Storage","ko":"Azure Blob Storage"},{"label":"D","en":"Azure SQL Database","ko":"Azure SQL Database"}],"answers":["C"]},{"n":282,"id":null,"type":"dropdown","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"Fabrikam, Inc. is an engineering company with a main office in London and branch offices in Amsterdam, Berlin, and Rome.\n\nThe network has two Active Directory forests: `corp.fabrikam.com`, a production forest for internal user and computer authentication, and `rd.fabrikam.com`, which is used only by R&amp;D and is restricted to on-premises resources. No trust relationship exists between the forests.\n\nFabrikam plans to move most production workloads to Azure and establish a hybrid identity model for a forthcoming Microsoft 365 deployment. R&amp;D operations will remain on-premises.\n\nThe technical requirements state that users must always authenticate with their `corp.fabrikam.com` UPN identity. Directory synchronization between Azure AD and `corp.fabrikam.com` must continue despite a failed link between Azure and the on-premises network.\n\nSecurity requirements state that company information, including policies, templates, and data, must be inaccessible to people outside the company. Administrators must be able to authenticate to the Azure portal using their `corp.fabrikam.com` credentials, and every administrative Azure portal access must use multi-factor authentication (MFA).\n\nTo meet Fabrikam’s authentication requirements, include the following in the solution:","stemKo":"Fabrikam, Inc. is an engineering company with a main office in London and branch offices in Amsterdam, Berlin, and Rome.\n\nThe network has two Active Directory forests: `corp.fabrikam.com`, a production forest for internal user and computer authentication, and `rd.fabrikam.com`, which is used only by R&amp;D and is restricted to on-premises resources. No trust relationship exists between the forests.\n\nFabrikam plans to move most production workloads to Azure and establish a hybrid identity model for a forthcoming Microsoft 365 deployment. R&amp;D operations will remain on-premises.\n\nThe technical requirements state that users must always authenticate with their `corp.fabrikam.com` UPN identity. Directory synchronization between Azure AD and `corp.fabrikam.com` must continue despite a failed link between Azure and the on-premises network.\n\nSecurity requirements state that company information, including policies, templates, and data, must be inaccessible to people outside the company. Administrators must be able to authenticate to the Azure portal using their `corp.fabrikam.com` credentials, and every administrative Azure portal access must use multi-factor authentication (MFA).\n\nTo meet Fabrikam’s authentication requirements, include the following in the solution:","explanationEn":"A single Microsoft Entra ID tenant can provide the hybrid identity for the `corp.fabrikam.com` production forest and Microsoft 365. The R&D forest remains on-premises, so it does not require a tenant. One Conditional Access policy can require MFA for administrative roles accessing Azure management, while a separate policy restricts access to company cloud information from outside the company.\n\n**Learn more:** [Hybrid identity documentation](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity/hybrid/) · [Require MFA for administrators with Conditional Access](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity/conditional-access/policy-old-require-mfa-admin)","explanationKo":"A single Microsoft Entra ID tenant can provide the hybrid identity for the `corp.fabrikam.com` production forest and Microsoft 365. The R&D forest remains on-premises, so it does not require a tenant. One Conditional Access policy can require MFA for administrative roles accessing Azure management, while a separate policy restricts access to company cloud information from outside the company.\n\n**Learn more:** [Hybrid identity documentation](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity/hybrid/) · [Require MFA for administrators with Conditional Access](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity/conditional-access/policy-old-require-mfa-admin)","learnMore":[],"blanks":[{"id":"azure_ad_tenants","labelEn":"Minimum number of Azure AD tenants:","labelKo":"Minimum number of Azure AD tenants:","options":[{"en":"0","ko":"0"},{"en":"1","ko":"1"},{"en":"2","ko":"2"},{"en":"3","ko":"3"},{"en":"4","ko":"4"}],"answer":"1"},{"id":"conditional_access_policies","labelEn":"Minimum number of conditional access policies to create:","labelKo":"Minimum number of conditional access policies to create:","options":[{"en":"0","ko":"0"},{"en":"1","ko":"1"},{"en":"2","ko":"2"},{"en":"3","ko":"3"},{"en":"4","ko":"4"}],"answer":"2"}],"template":""},{"n":283,"id":null,"type":"statements","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":["assets/1783709176390-52jz297l.png","assets/1783709178734-sbh9tdl6.png","assets/1783709180700-5bgw172h.png","assets/1783709183091-ons041pu.png"],"stemEn":"You have an Azure AD tenant that includes a management group named MG1.\n\nYou have the Azure subscriptions shown in the following table.\n\n[[IMG1]]\n\nThe subscriptions contain the resource groups shown in the following table.\n\n[[IMG2]]\n\nThe subscription contains the Azure AD security groups shown in the following table.\n\n[[IMG3]]\n\nThe subscription contains the user accounts shown in the following table.\n\n[[IMG4]]\n\nYou perform these actions:\n\n- Assign User3 the Contributor role for Sub1.\n- Assign Group1 the Virtual Machine Contributor role for MG1.\n- Assign Group3 the Contributor role for the Tenant Root Group.\n\nFor each of the following statements, select Yes if the statement is true. Otherwise, select No.","stemKo":"You have an Azure AD tenant that includes a management group named MG1.\n\nYou have the Azure subscriptions shown in the following table.\n\n[[IMG1]]\n\nThe subscriptions contain the resource groups shown in the following table.\n\n[[IMG2]]\n\nThe subscription contains the Azure AD security groups shown in the following table.\n\n[[IMG3]]\n\nThe subscription contains the user accounts shown in the following table.\n\n[[IMG4]]\n\nYou perform these actions:\n\n- Assign User3 the Contributor role for Sub1.\n- Assign Group1 the Virtual Machine Contributor role for MG1.\n- Assign Group3 the Contributor role for the Tenant Root Group.\n\nFor each of the following statements, select Yes if the statement is true. Otherwise, select No.","explanationEn":"Azure RBAC permissions assigned at a management group or Tenant Root Group are inherited by child scopes, and role assignments through nested groups are transitive. User1 inherits Virtual Machine Contributor access through Group1 at MG1, so can create a virtual machine in RG1. User2 inherits Contributor through Group2’s membership in Group3, but Contributor cannot create Azure RBAC role assignments. User3 also inherits Contributor through Group3 at the Tenant Root Group, so can create a storage account in RG2.\n\n**Learn more:** [What is Azure role-based access control (Azure RBAC)?](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/role-based-access-control/overview) · [Understand scope for Azure RBAC](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/role-based-access-control/scope-overview)","explanationKo":"Azure RBAC permissions assigned at a management group or Tenant Root Group are inherited by child scopes, and role assignments through nested groups are transitive. User1 inherits Virtual Machine Contributor access through Group1 at MG1, so can create a virtual machine in RG1. User2 inherits Contributor through Group2’s membership in Group3, but Contributor cannot create Azure RBAC role assignments. User3 also inherits Contributor through Group3 at the Tenant Root Group, so can create a storage account in RG2.\n\n**Learn more:** [What is Azure role-based access control (Azure RBAC)?](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/role-based-access-control/overview) · [Understand scope for Azure RBAC](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/role-based-access-control/scope-overview)","learnMore":[],"statements":[{"en":"User1 can create a new virtual machine in RG1.","ko":"User1 can create a new virtual machine in RG1.","answer":"Yes"},{"en":"User2 can grant permissions to Group2.","ko":"User2 can grant permissions to Group2.","answer":"No"},{"en":"User3 can create a storage account in RG2.","ko":"User3 can create a storage account in RG2.","answer":"Yes"}],"columns":["Yes","No"]},{"n":284,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design identity, governance, and monitoring solutions","topicKo":"ID·거버넌스·모니터링 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You need to recommend a solution that generates a monthly report covering all new Azure Resource Manager (ARM) resource deployments in your Azure subscription.\n\nWhat should the recommendation include?","stemKo":"You need to recommend a solution that generates a monthly report covering all new Azure Resource Manager (ARM) resource deployments in your Azure subscription.\n\nWhat should the recommendation include?","explanationEn":"Azure Activity Log records Azure Resource Manager control-plane operations, including resource creation and deployment-related events. Routing that data to an Azure Log Analytics workspace allows it to be queried over a monthly period to produce a report of new deployments.\n\n**Learn more:** [Activity log in Azure Monitor](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-monitor/platform/activity-log) · [Monitor Azure Resource Manager](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-resource-manager/management/monitor-resource-manager)","explanationKo":"Azure Activity Log records Azure Resource Manager control-plane operations, including resource creation and deployment-related events. Routing that data to an Azure Log Analytics workspace allows it to be queried over a monthly period to produce a report of new deployments.\n\n**Learn more:** [Activity log in Azure Monitor](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-monitor/platform/activity-log) · [Monitor Azure Resource Manager](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-resource-manager/management/monitor-resource-manager)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Azure Log Analytics","ko":"Azure Log Analytics"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure Arc","ko":"Azure Arc"},{"label":"C","en":"Azure Monitor metrics","ko":"Azure Monitor metrics"},{"label":"D","en":"Azure Monitor action groups","ko":"Azure Monitor action groups"}],"answers":["A"]},{"n":285,"id":null,"type":"multiple_choice","topic":"Design data storage solutions","topicKo":"데이터 저장소 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You have an on-premises application named App1 that uses an Oracle database.\n\nYou plan to use Azure Databricks to transform and load data from App1 into an Azure Synapse Analytics instance.\n\nYou need to ensure that App1 data is available to Databricks.\n\nWhich two Azure services should you include in the solution? Each correct answer represents part of the solution.\n\nNOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.","stemKo":"You have an on-premises application named App1 that uses an Oracle database.\n\nYou plan to use Azure Databricks to transform and load data from App1 into an Azure Synapse Analytics instance.\n\nYou need to ensure that App1 data is available to Databricks.\n\nWhich two Azure services should you include in the solution? Each correct answer represents part of the solution.\n\nNOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.","explanationEn":"Azure Data Factory can copy data from an Oracle database; for an on-premises data store, it uses a self-hosted integration runtime to establish connectivity. Azure Data Lake Storage provides the scalable storage layer from which Azure Databricks can access and transform the copied data before it is loaded into Azure Synapse Analytics.\n\n**Learn more:** [Copy data from and to Oracle by using Azure Data Factory or Azure Synapse Analytics](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/data-factory/connector-oracle) · [Connect to Azure Data Lake Storage and Blob Storage](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/databricks/connect/storage/azure-storage)","explanationKo":"Azure Data Factory can copy data from an Oracle database; for an on-premises data store, it uses a self-hosted integration runtime to establish connectivity. Azure Data Lake Storage provides the scalable storage layer from which Azure Databricks can access and transform the copied data before it is loaded into Azure Synapse Analytics.\n\n**Learn more:** [Copy data from and to Oracle by using Azure Data Factory or Azure Synapse Analytics](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/data-factory/connector-oracle) · [Connect to Azure Data Lake Storage and Blob Storage](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/databricks/connect/storage/azure-storage)","learnMore":[],"choices":[{"label":"A","en":"Azure Data Box Gateway","ko":"Azure Data Box Gateway"},{"label":"B","en":"Azure Import/Export service","ko":"Azure Import/Export service"},{"label":"C","en":"Azure Data Lake Storage","ko":"Azure Data Lake Storage"},{"label":"D","en":"Azure Data Box Edge","ko":"Azure Data Box Edge"},{"label":"E","en":"Azure Data Factory","ko":"Azure Data Factory"}],"answers":["CE"]},{"n":286,"id":null,"type":"dropdown","topic":"Design data storage solutions","topicKo":"데이터 저장소 설계","koMissing":true,"images":[],"stemEn":"You have an on-premises Microsoft SQL Server database named SQL1.\n\nYou plan to migrate SQL1 to Azure.\n\nRecommend a hosting solution for SQL1 that meets these requirements:\n\n- Supports deployment of multiple secondary, read-only replicas.\n- Supports automatic replication between primary and secondary replicas.\n- Supports failover between primary and secondary replicas within a 15-minute recovery time objective (RTO).\n\nWhat should the solution include?","stemKo":"You have an on-premises Microsoft SQL Server database named SQL1.\n\nYou plan to migrate SQL1 to Azure.\n\nRecommend a hosting solution for SQL1 that meets these requirements:\n\n- Supports deployment of multiple secondary, read-only replicas.\n- Supports automatic replication between primary and secondary replicas.\n- Supports failover between primary and secondary replicas within a 15-minute recovery time objective (RTO).\n\nWhat should the solution include?","explanationEn":"Hyperscale provides read-only secondary replicas. Active geo-replication continuously and asynchronously replicates the primary database to readable geo-secondary replicas, supports up to four geo-secondaries, and allows failover to a secondary replica.\n\n**Learn more:** [Active geo-replication - Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/database/active-geo-replication-overview?view=azuresql) · [Hyperscale secondary replicas - Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/database/service-tier-hyperscale-replicas?view=azuresql)","explanationKo":"Hyperscale provides read-only secondary replicas. Active geo-replication continuously and asynchronously replicates the primary database to readable geo-secondary replicas, supports up to four geo-secondaries, and allows failover to a secondary replica.\n\n**Learn more:** [Active geo-replication - Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/database/active-geo-replication-overview?view=azuresql) · [Hyperscale secondary replicas - Azure SQL Database](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-sql/database/service-tier-hyperscale-replicas?view=azuresql)","learnMore":[],"blanks":[{"id":"azure_service_or_service_tier","labelEn":"Azure service or service tier:","labelKo":"Azure service or service tier:","options":[{"en":"Azure SQL Database","ko":"Azure SQL Database"},{"en":"Azure SQL managed Instance","ko":"Azure SQL managed Instance"},{"en":"The Hyperscale service tier","ko":"The Hyperscale service tier"}],"answer":"The Hyperscale service tier"},{"id":"replication_mechanism","labelEn":"Replication mechanism:","labelKo":"Replication mechanism:","options":[{"en":"Active geo-replication","ko":"Active geo-replication"},{"en":"Auto-failover groups","ko":"Auto-failover groups"},{"en":"Standard geo-replication","ko":"Standard geo-replication"}],"answer":"Active geo-replication"}],"template":""}],"sets":[],"series":[{"id":"az305-series-1","no":1,"title":"솔루션 시리즈 Q28~Q31","members":[28,29,30,31]},{"id":"az305-series-2","no":2,"title":"솔루션 시리즈 Q239~Q242","members":[239,240,241,242]},{"id":"az305-series-3","no":3,"title":"솔루션 시리즈 Q244~Q247","members":[244,245,246,247]},{"id":"az305-series-4","no":4,"title":"솔루션 시리즈 Q258~Q261","members":[258,259,260,261]}]};
